const e={P2800:["Transmission Range Sensor B Circuit (PRNDL Input)","P2800 is the general circuit code for the second signal path that tells the modules which selector position (P, R, N, D, L) is engaged. It applies when that signal is unusable without a clear low, high or frequency pattern. Ford's 2019 hybrid OBD summary lists it for the eCVT range sensor with the wrench lamp and no MIL, judged in under a second;",["Water entry or corrosion in connectors along the sensor circuit","Chafed or broken wiring between sensor and module","Failed transmission range sensor","Invalid gear position message from another module over CAN"],["Wrench lamp or MIL on, gear display missing or wrong","Engine does not start in Park or Neutral","Trouble selecting a drive position"],2,3,["P0705","P2801","P2802","P2803","P2804","P2805","P26C3"],""],P2801:["Transmission Range Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","Here the B signal of the range sensor is electrically present but its content does not make sense. On sensors with a pulse-width output, Ford checks the carrier frequency: its 2024 summary sets P2801 (UDS P2800_38) on the 6R80, 6R140, 10R60 and 10R80 automatics when the frequency leaves 125 Hz plus or minus 25 Hz, while the 2012 summary applies the same test to the 250 Hz signal of the DPS6 dual-clutch box.",["Range sensor electronics producing a wrong signal frequency","Damaged or loose pins at the transmission connector","Sensor shifted on its shaft so the angles disagree"],["Warning lamp with shift quality or gear display issues","Transmission uses a fixed substitute range strategy"],2,3,["P0706","P2800","P2802","P2803","P2805"],"חיישן טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2802:["Transmission Range Sensor B Circuit Low","P2802 means the B signal of the range sensor sits too low, usually a ground short or a duty cycle collapsing toward zero. GM's tables for 2020 and 2025 place the check in the engine module, which reads internal range sensor B on its own wire: a circuit impedance under 0.5 ohm to ground for 0.5 s within a one-second window sets the code as Type A, MIL in the first trip.",["Signal wire of sensor B shorted to ground","Water or corrosion in a connector of the circuit","Range sensor output stage failed low"],["MIL or wrench lamp on","No start in Park, missing gear indication","Stop-start or shift functions restricted"],2,3,["P2803","P0707","P2800","P2805"],"חיישן טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2803:["Transmission Range Sensor B Circuit High","P2803 is stored when the output of range sensor B reads too high, which typically points to an open circuit or a short to supply voltage. In GM's 2020 and 2025 tables the engine module watches its own range sensor input for this: either under 0.5 ohm to the voltage source or above 200 kilohms to ground for 0.5 s sets a Type A fault. Ford's 2024 summary flags a duty cycle over 92 % (P2800_85).",["Open signal circuit or pushed-out connector pin","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source","Module calibration misreading the signal, fixed by software","Range sensor output stuck high"],["MIL on, often with transmission temperature codes","Shift system warning in the instrument cluster","Wrong or missing gear display"],2,3,["P2802","P0708","P2804","P2800"],"חיישן טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2804:["Transmission Range Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","P2804 points to a B signal that drops out or jumps for short moments instead of failing permanently. Ford is the main user: its 2024 OBD summary books it as the general electrical fault of TRS B (UDS P2800_01), checked continuously, with up to 30 s allowed for pattern recognition and 2 s for analog faults.",["Connector not fully seated or pin pushed back","Harness chafing that opens the circuit under vibration","Worn contacts or electronics inside the range sensor"],["MIL comes and goes, often with several transmission codes","Gear display flickers","Occasional shift system warning"],2,3,["P2803","P0709","P2800","P0708"],"חיישן טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2805:["Transmission Range Sensor A/B Correlation","Both range sensor signals are valid on their own, yet they do not agree. Many designs output two complementary pulse-width signals whose duty cycles must add up to 100 %. GM reads signal A in the transmission module and signal B in the engine module and sets P2805 as Type A when the sum is off by more than 4.849 % (2020 table) or 5.2 % (2025) for 1 s of 1.5 s.",["Range sensor with one drifting output","Added resistance or poor ground in one of the two signal paths","Fault in the reading control module"],["MIL and gearbox warning on","Engine will not start or selector position not accepted","Substitute gear or limp operation"],4,3,["P0705","P2800","P0706","P2801","P26C3"],"חיישן טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2806:["Transmission Range Sensor Alignment","P2806 says that the selector position reported by the range sensor and the actual mechanical position of the gearbox do not line up. Ford is the only public user found. Its 2019 hybrid OBD summary lists the code for the eCVT with the wrench lamp and without the MIL; one section defines a park pawl check behind it: if the park motor turns more than 9 radians while the pawl should already be engaged, the code is set.",["Range sensor not aligned correctly after transmission work","Stretched selector cable or worn linkage","Park pawl or park motor mechanism damaged"],["Wrench lamp, gear display differs from lever position","Vehicle may roll in Park","Start refused in Park or Neutral"],2,2,["P0705","P0706","P2800","P2805","P280A"],""],P2807:["Pressure Control Solenoid G","P2807 is the umbrella code for pressure control solenoid G; the fault type follows in the extra byte. Which hydraulic function G controls is set by each maker. Toyota uses it on its eight-speed automatics: bulletin T-SB-0160-18 lists P28077F (actuator stuck off) on 2017-2018 Highlander and Sienna together with other solenoid codes, whine, harsh shifts and reduced power, and supplies a remanufactured transaxle.",["Debris or wear particles jamming the valve","Internal transmission damage producing particles","Solenoid G worn or electrically weak"],["MIL on with harsh or delayed shifts","Whine noise from the transmission","Reduced power or limp mode"],4,3,["P2808","P2809","P2810","P2812","P27AD","P2816","P0745"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ G"],P2808:["Pressure Control Solenoid G Performance/Stuck Off","P2808 means valve G does not deliver the pressure or effect it is commanded to give. GM documents two very different applications. In the 2016 eight-speed table G is the converter clutch valve: with at least 750 kPa commanded, slip of 130 rpm or more in lock mode for 4 s, counted three times, sets the code, and the MIL needs two trips.",["Valve G stuck by contamination so pressure stays low","Worn converter clutch lining that slips despite pressure","Low fluid level or internal leak in the circuit"],["MIL on, engine speed higher than expected at cruise","Higher fuel consumption and transmission heat","Limited-slip function inactive on Corvette"],4,3,["P2809","P2807","P2812","P0741","P2817"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ G — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2809:["Pressure Control Solenoid G Stuck On","P2809 is the reverse case: valve G keeps acting although it should have released. On GM's 2016 eight-speed automatics, where G operates the converter lockup clutch, the converter shows almost no slip, between minus 50 and plus 30 rpm, while the clutch is commanded off; after 1.5 s and six fail counts the controller stores the code, with the MIL lit in the first trip.",["Valve G held open by debris","Contaminated or degraded transmission fluid","Mechanical fault inside solenoid G"],["Engine stalls or shudders when coming to a stop","MIL on","Differential stays locked on Corvette, tyre scrub in tight turns"],4,3,["P2808","P2807","P0742","P2818"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ G — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P280A:["Transmission Range Sensor A Circuit Not Learned","P280A means the module holds no valid learned reference for range sensor A, so it cannot translate the raw signal into a reliable selector position. This is typical after replacing the sensor, the gearbox or the control module, after a software update, or when a learn run was aborted. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 only requires that transmission inputs are checked.",["Learn procedure skipped after replacing sensor, gearbox or module","Learn run aborted, for example by low battery voltage","Learned values cleared by a software update","Sensor signal outside the learnable window"],["Warning lamp right after a repair or update","Engine does not start or gear display missing"],2,3,["P280B","P0705","P0706","P2806"],"מעגל חיישן טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ A — לא בוצע לימוד"],P280B:["Transmission Range Sensor B Circuit Not Learned","P280B flags missing or invalid adaptation values for the second range sensor signal. Where a design reads A and B in different modules, as GM does with sensor A in the TCM and sensor B in the engine module, a replaced or reprogrammed engine controller can lose the B reference while A is still learned.",["Module reading sensor B replaced or reprogrammed without learn","Learn procedure interrupted","Open circuit faults on sensor B preventing the learn"],["Warning lamp after module replacement","Gear position checks disabled, possible start refusal"],2,3,["P280A","P2800","P2805","P2806"],"מעגל חיישן טווח תיבת הילוכים‏ B — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2810:["Pressure Control Solenoid G Electrical","P2810 is a collective electrical code for solenoid G: the control unit sees a fault in coil or wiring but does not split it into open, low or high. No manufacturer documents P2810 publicly. The makers that do use valve G report electrical faults more precisely.",["Coil of solenoid G open or shorted internally","Damaged internal harness or lead frame","Corroded or loose transmission connector","Faulty output stage in the control module"],["MIL on and harsh shifts","Transmission in default pressure or limp mode"],4,3,["P2812","P2814","P2815","P2811","P2807"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ G"],P2811:["Pressure Control Solenoid G Intermittent","With P2811 the module records that valve G misbehaved only for moments, electrically or in effect, and then recovered. No maker publishes a description of this exact code. GM's preliminary information PIP5799 for 2019-2021 vehicles with 10L60 to 10L1000 automatics shows where such faults usually hide: G there is solenoid valve 7, the line pressure valve, and electrical faults on it (P2812 or P2814) are cured by a…",["Loose terminal or fretting corrosion in the gearbox connector","Intermittent contact inside the valve body solenoid assembly","Coil that fails only when hot"],["Occasional harsh shift, then normal again","MIL that comes and goes"],4,3,["P2810","P2812","P2814","P2807"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ G — תקלה לסירוגין"],P2812:["Pressure Control Solenoid G Control Circuit/Open","P2812 signals an open control circuit of solenoid G. GM uses it widely: on the 2016 eight-speed (TCC valve) the hardware open flag must stand for 0.3 s of 0.5 s, one trip; the 2020 table, now with the ten-speed line pressure valve as well, asks for 0.6 s of 0.65 s and rates it Type B;",["Open coil in solenoid G or in the valve body assembly","Open terminal or corroded pin in the transmission connector","Broken wire between module and solenoid","Faulty output driver in the control module"],["Check engine light on","Harsh shifts on line pressure designs","No converter lockup or limited-slip function"],4,3,["P2814","P2815","P2813","P2810","P2807","P0960"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ G — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2813:["Pressure Control Solenoid G Control Circuit Range/Performance","On paper P2813 is a plausibility fault in the control circuit of solenoid G, but its main real-world use is hydraulic. Nissan-built CVTs label it as the select solenoid, which applies the forward and reverse clutches.",["Select solenoid valve sticking in the valve body","CVT wear with belt slip or clutch damage","Degraded or contaminated CVT fluid","Added resistance in the solenoid circuit"],["Strong shock when selecting D or R","Slow start and weak acceleration","MIL after the second trip"],4,3,["P2812","P2814","P2815","P0776","P0841"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ G — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2814:["Pressure Control Solenoid G Control Circuit Low","P2814 reports that the drive line of solenoid G is pulled toward ground, typically a chafed wire or a coil shorted to ground. GM's 2020 tables name G as the line pressure valve on nine- and ten-speed boxes and the converter clutch valve on the eight-speed; a resistance of about 0.5 ohm to ground, present for 0.3 s out of a 0.5 s sample, sets a Type A fault.",["Solenoid G control wire chafed through to ground in the gearbox harness","Solenoid G coil with internal short to its housing","Fault inside the valve body assembly (GM 10-speed, PIP5799)","Damaged output stage in the transmission control module"],["MIL or transmission warning on, often with a fault message","Firm shifts because line pressure falls back to a fixed value","Converter clutch no longer locks up (eight-speed applications)","Limited-slip differential inactive on dual-clutch Corvettes"],3,3,["P2815","P2812","P2810","P2807","P281D"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ G — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2815:["Pressure Control Solenoid G Control Circuit High","P2815 is the opposite electrical case: the driver of solenoid G sees battery voltage where the load should pull the pin down. In GM's 2016 eight-speed table, where G is the converter clutch pressure valve, the flag must stand for 0.3 s of a 0.5 s window and one trip is enough.",["Control wire of solenoid G touching a supply voltage wire","Solenoid coil with shorted turns drawing too much current","Two solenoid outputs shorted together inside the harness or valve body","Faulty driver stage in the transmission module"],["MIL lit and transmission in a substitute program","Harsh engagement or missing converter lockup","Code may appear only after the next engine start (shutdown test)"],3,3,["P2814","P2812","P2810","P2807","P281E"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ G — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2816:["Pressure Control Solenoid H","P2816 is the general code for pressure control solenoid H; a fault type byte usually narrows it down. The valve H stands for depends on the maker. Toyota uses the code on its eight-speed automatics: bulletin T-SB-0160-18 lists P28167F (actuator stuck off) for 2017-2018 Highlander and Sienna together with whine, harsh shifts and reduced power, and offers a remanufactured transaxle, while T-SB-0076-24 for the 2024…",["Internal transmission damage leaving debris in the hydraulics (Toyota eight-speed)","Valve H sticking in its bore","Solenoid H itself defective"],["MIL on, sometimes reduced engine power","Harsh or erratic shifts","Whining noise from the transmission"],4,3,["P2817","P2818","P2819","P281B","P2807"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ H"],P2817:["Pressure Control Solenoid H Performance/Stuck Off","P2817 means valve H fails to produce the effect it is commanded to give. On GM nine- and ten-speed automatics H is the converter clutch valve: too much slip in lock mode (130 rpm) or a large slip error in controlled mode, counted three times, sets a Type A fault.",["Valve H stuck or hydraulically unable to apply","Damaged turbine shaft seal letting converter clutch pressure escape (GM 8T65)","Misjudged pressure signal in older control software (Honda CVT)","Low or degraded transmission fluid"],["MIL on or flashing D indicator","Converter clutch slips, engine speed higher than usual at cruise","Increased fuel consumption"],4,3,["P2818","P2816","P2808","P0741","P281B"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ H — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2818:["Pressure Control Solenoid H Stuck On","P2818 reports that valve H stays effective when it should be released. In GM's eight-speed table for the 8L90, H is the default valve: in Park at 400-900 rpm, with fluid between 0 and 40 °C and a converter clutch test pressure of 600 kPa, slip of 6 rpm or less for 0.5 s counts as a fail, and the MIL follows after two trips.",["Valve in the valve body sticking in the applied position","Early TCM calibration (GM 8L90 2015, reprogramming)","Internal transmission fault that persists when cold (PI1405)","Contaminated fluid holding the valve"],["Engine stalls when coming to a stop or when D or R is selected","Firm upshifts or downshifts, shudder","MIL on, code may set only at low fluid temperature"],4,3,["P2817","P2816","P2809","P0742","P0606"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ H — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2819:["Pressure Control Solenoid H Electrical","P2819 is a collective electrical code for solenoid H: the module knows that coil or wiring is faulty but does not say whether the circuit is open or shorted. Mercedes-Benz uses it on the 8G-DCT dual-clutch gearbox (transmission 724.1 in the A-Class, CLA and GLA/GLB families): P281900, an electrical fault of pressure regulating valve 8, is one of the codes its guided diagnosis tool in XENTRY handles, alongside…",["Coil of valve H open or shorted","Poor contact between valve and mechatronic or module board","Damaged transmission wiring or connector"],["MIL or transmission warning on","Limp-home mode with restricted gears","Jerky starts or rough shifts"],4,3,["P2816","P281B","P281D","P281E","P2810"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ H"],P281A:["Pressure Control Solenoid H Intermittent","P281A marks a fault at valve H that comes and goes, either electrically or in its hydraulic effect. There is no public manufacturer description of P281A. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 calls for monitoring of such actuators but does not prescribe an intermittent code.",["Loose or corroded terminal at the transmission connector","Coil of valve H failing only at operating temperature","Cracked solder joint in an integrated mechatronic unit"],["Occasional harsh or delayed shift","Warning lamp that comes and goes","Short spells of limp-home mode"],3,3,["P2819","P281B","P281D","P281E","P2811"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ H — תקלה לסירוגין"],P281B:["Pressure Control Solenoid H Control Circuit/Open","P281B stands for an open control circuit of solenoid H. GM's 2020 tables apply it to the converter clutch valve of nine- and ten-speed automatics and to the T93 eight-speed default valve; an impedance of about 200 kilohm, seen for 0.3 s of 0.5 s, sets a Type A fault in one trip. On the T87a eight-speed controllers an open default valve circuit is filed as P281D instead.",["Open coil in solenoid H","Terminal pushed back or loose in the connector","Broken wire in the internal or external transmission harness"],["MIL on after one trip","No converter clutch lockup, higher engine speed at cruise","Limited-slip differential disabled (Corvette dual-clutch)"],3,3,["P281D","P281E","P2819","P2812","P2817"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ H — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P281C:["Pressure Control Solenoid H Control Circuit Range/Performance","P281C is meant for a circuit of solenoid H that is electrically intact but does not behave plausibly, for example when the measured current fails to follow the commanded value. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 only demands functional monitoring of output circuits.",["Coil resistance of valve H outside specification","Corroded or loose contacts raising circuit resistance","Unstable supply voltage to the solenoid driver"],["MIL or transmission warning on","Shift quality varies from drive to drive","Possible substitute program"],3,3,["P281B","P281D","P281E","P2819","P2813"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ H — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P281D:["Pressure Control Solenoid H Control Circuit Low","P281D signals that the control line of solenoid H is shorted to ground. In GM's 2016 eight-speed table H is the on/off default valve; the low flag must persist for 0.3 s within 0.5 s and one trip lights the MIL.",["Control wire of solenoid H shorted to ground","Open default valve circuit reported as low (GM T87a eight-speed)","Coil insulation failure inside solenoid H"],["MIL on after a single trip","Transmission in default gear or fixed pressure mode","Converter lockup or differential lock unavailable"],3,3,["P281E","P281B","P2819","P2814","P2818"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ H — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P281E:["Pressure Control Solenoid H Control Circuit High","P281E sets when the line to solenoid H carries supply voltage where the module expects the load to pull it down. GM's 2020 tables cover the converter clutch valve on nine- and ten-speed automatics and the default valve on the eight-speed with the same timing as the low code: 0.3 s within 0.5 s, Type A, one trip.",["Control wire of solenoid H shorted to a voltage source","Moisture in the transmission connector bridging pins","Short between solenoid H and a neighbouring output"],["MIL on, possibly right after starting","Converter clutch or differential lock function lost","Firm shifts in a substitute program"],3,3,["P281D","P281B","P2819","P2815","P2818"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ H — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P281F:["Pressure Control Solenoid J","P281F is the umbrella code for pressure control solenoid J; usually a failure-type byte narrows it down, or the module stores one of the specific codes P2820 to P2827 instead. Which valve carries the letter J is up to each manufacturer.",["Valve J sticking due to abrasion particles in the fluid","Fault inside the mechatronic unit or valve body","Coil or connector fault at valve J","Low or aged transmission fluid"],["Harsh or delayed gear changes","Transmission warning message or MIL","Limited gears or emergency mode"],4,3,["P2820","P2821","P2822","P2828","P2816"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ J"],P2820:["Pressure Control Solenoid J Performance/Stuck Off","P2820 says valve J, though electrically sound, fails to deliver its hydraulic effect when commanded. On GM ten-speed automatics J is the default disable valve; if it sticks off, the box drops into its hydraulic limp gear (2nd or 7th) while another gear is requested. GM's 2020 tables detect this through gear ratio and clutch slip (50 rpm) and log Type A after 0.25 s.",["Casting debris or dirt blocking valve J or its passages","Restricted orifice in a spacer plate","Outdated control logic that misjudges the valve (Toyota CVT)","Internal transmission damage requiring a replacement unit"],["Transmission suddenly holds 2nd or 7th gear","Binding or jerky drive when the wrong clutches engage","Vehicle will not leave Park on dual-clutch models","MIL on"],4,3,["P2821","P281F","P2824","P2817","P2829"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ J — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2821:["Pressure Control Solenoid J Stuck On","P2821 is the mirror image of P2820: valve J keeps acting after the module has released it. GM bulletin PIP5557 (revisions up to C) concerns 2018 Cruze, Equinox, Malibu and Traverse with nine-speed automatics (RPO M3D, M3E, M3H, M3U, M3V) that stay in second gear and will not pass about 30 mph.",["Blocked orifice in the valve body spacer plate","Valve J or its spool stuck in the applied position","TCM software requiring the update released with the repair","Park lock piston or latching valve not draining (dual-clutch)"],["Stuck in second gear, no upshift","Top speed limited to about 50 km/h","Park lock does not engage as expected","MIL on"],4,3,["P2820","P281F","P2826","P2818","P282A"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ J — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2822:["Pressure Control Solenoid J Electrical","P2822 gathers electrical faults of solenoid J without saying whether the circuit is open or shorted; a failure-type byte adds that detail. Mercedes-Benz uses the code on two gearboxes, and in both J is pressure regulating valve 9.",["Short to positive in the valve J circuit","Signal timing when leaving transport mode on new vehicles (Mercedes 9G-Tronic)","Open or shorted coil of valve J","Corrosion or loose pins at the transmission connector"],["Transmission warning or MIL","Emergency mode with fixed gear","Code present on a new car without driveability complaint"],4,3,["P281F","P2824","P2826","P2827","P282B"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ J"],P2823:["Pressure Control Solenoid J Intermittent","P2823 is reserved for a fault at valve J that appears and disappears, either in its wiring or in its hydraulic action. No manufacturer publishes a description of this code. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 obliges makers to monitor transmission output devices for circuit and functional faults, yet leaves it to them whether to split off intermittent codes.",["Loose or spread pin at the transmission connector","Harness rubbing through under vibration","Coil that drops out only when hot","Valve J sticking now and then due to contaminated fluid"],["Occasional rough or unexpected shift","Warning that comes and goes","Sometimes delayed park lock response"],3,3,["P2822","P2824","P2826","P2827","P282C"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ J — תקלה לסירוגין"],P2824:["Pressure Control Solenoid J Control Circuit/Open","P2824 reports an open in the control line of solenoid J. GM's 2016 table for T87 eight-speed controllers uses J for the on/off boost valve of clutch 2 and flags the code in one trip once the fault persists 0.3 s within a half-second sample.",["Broken wire between TCM and valve J","Terminal pushed back or not latched in the connector","Open coil in solenoid J","Faulty output driver in the TCM"],["Hydraulic limp gear or no shifting","Park lock cannot be operated (dual-clutch models)","MIL on after one or two trips"],3,3,["P2826","P2827","P2822","P2820","P282D"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ J — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2825:["Pressure Control Solenoid J Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2825 would flag a J control circuit that is intact but behaves implausibly, for example a current that does not track the duty cycle the module commands. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, and CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 only requires functional checks of output circuits in general terms.",["Coil resistance out of specification when hot","High contact resistance at terminals","Sluggish valve J changing the electrical load"],["Shift quality varies","MIL or transmission warning"],3,3,["P2824","P2826","P2827","P2822","P282E"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ J — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2826:["Pressure Control Solenoid J Control Circuit Low","P2826 indicates that the line to solenoid J is pulled to ground. GM's 2020 tables name three uses for J: the clutch select valve of the nine-speed, the default disable valve of the ten-speed and the boost valve of the eight-speed. About 0.5 ohm to ground for 0.3 of 0.5 s gives a Type A fault, and T87a eight-speed controllers also log P2826 when the J circuit is open, so a broken wire can hide behind it.",["Control wire shorted to ground through chafed insulation","Coil of valve J shorted to its housing","Open J circuit reported as low on GM T87a controllers"],["Limp gear or loss of boost pressure","Park lock fault message (dual-clutch models)","MIL on"],3,3,["P2827","P2824","P2822","P281D","P282F"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ J — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2827:["Pressure Control Solenoid J Control Circuit High","P2827 sets when the J control line shows supply voltage although the load ought to pull it low. In GM's 2020 tables it covers the nine-speed clutch valve, the ten-speed default disable valve and the eight-speed boost valve, using the same 0.3-of-0.5 s window and Type A rating as the low code.",["Control wire shorted to a supply line","Short to a neighbouring solenoid output","Moisture in the transmission connector","Shorted coil turns lowering the load"],["Limp gear or blocked park lock function","Code returns right after a restart","MIL on"],3,3,["P2826","P2824","P2822","P281E","P2830"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ J — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2828:["Pressure Control Solenoid K","P2828 serves as the catch-all code for solenoid K and is normally refined by a failure-type byte or replaced by one of P2829 to P2830. Mercedes-Benz is the maker found to name it directly: on the 8G-DCT dual-clutch gearbox of model series 118, 177 and 247, P282800 denotes a malfunction of pressure regulating valve 10 and P282B00 an electrical fault of the same valve.",["Valve K sticking because of contaminated fluid","Fault in the mechatronic unit carrying valve K","Coil fault at valve K"],["Rough shifting or missing gears","Transmission warning or MIL","Emergency mode"],4,3,["P2829","P282A","P282B","P281F","P2816"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ K"],P2829:["Pressure Control Solenoid K Performance/Stuck Off","P2829 means valve K remains hydraulically inactive although it is commanded on. In GM's 2023 Corvette dual-clutch transmission K is the selector pilot valve, which steers the selector spool of the shift-rod hydraulics. The check runs inside a synchronizer integrity routine that starts after a gear or component fault: the TCM orders small rod movements and measures them.",["Selector pilot valve stuck in the off position","Abrasion particles in the transmission fluid","Selector spool itself stuck (same symptom, different part)"],["Some gears unavailable","Hesitation or failed gear preselection","MIL on"],4,3,["P282A","P2828","P282D","P27D9","P2820"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ K — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P282A:["Pressure Control Solenoid K Stuck On","P282A reports the reverse of P2829: K holds the selector mechanism in its pressurized state after being switched off. GM's 2023 Corvette dual-clutch software uses the same synchronizer integrity routine, this time with a test case whose selector target is hydraulic off.",["Selector pilot valve stuck in the applied position","Worn valve bore causing internal leakage","Contaminated fluid jamming the valve"],["Gears locked out or limp mode","Clunk or unexpected rod movement during shifts","MIL on"],4,3,["P2829","P2828","P2830","P27DA","P2821"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ K — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P282B:["Pressure Control Solenoid K Electrical","P282B covers electrical faults at solenoid K when the module does not break them down into open, low or high. Mercedes-Benz uses P282B00 on the 8G-DCT (transmission 724.1) for an electrical fault of pressure regulating valve 10; its 2025 information LI27.00-P-077141 includes the code among those the IPR guided routine analyses before parts are replaced, while P282800 stands for a functional fault of that valve.",["Broken coil winding in valve K","Damaged internal conductor in the mechatronic unit","Corrosion at the transmission plug"],["Rough clutch engagement","Transmission warning or MIL","Emergency mode"],4,3,["P2828","P282D","P282F","P2830","P2822"],"חשמלי סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ K"],P282C:["Pressure Control Solenoid K Intermittent","P282C is intended for an intermittent problem at solenoid K. No manufacturer publishes a description; CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 requires monitoring of transmission actuators without prescribing a separate code for sporadic faults.",["Weak pin tension or unlatched connector","Heat-related dropout of the coil or internal lead","Harness chafing under vibration"],["Occasional failed gear preselection","Warning that disappears after restart"],3,3,["P282B","P282D","P282F","P2830","P2823"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ K — תקלה לסירוגין"],P282D:["Pressure Control Solenoid K Control Circuit/Open","P282D marks an open control circuit of solenoid K. GM's 2023 Corvette dual-clutch software applies it to the selector pilot valve. With the low-side output off, a connected coil would pull the sense pin up to battery voltage; the driver instead attempts to keep the pin near ground using a very small current, and if the voltage settles between roughly 1.7 and 3 V the load is considered missing.",["Broken wire to the selector pilot valve","Terminal pushed back in the connector","Open coil in solenoid K"],["Gears on one shaft unavailable","MIL on immediately","Limp mode"],3,3,["P282F","P2830","P282B","P27DD","P2824"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ K — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P282E:["Pressure Control Solenoid K Control Circuit Range/Performance","P282E is meant for a solenoid K control circuit whose behaviour strays from what the TCM expects although there is no clean open or short. No manufacturer documents it publicly, and CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 states the monitoring duty only in general form.",["Coil resistance rising with temperature","Poor ground or supply to the driver stage","Weak output stage in the TCM"],["Uneven gear preselection","MIL or transmission warning"],3,3,["P282D","P282F","P2830","P282B","P2825"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ K — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P282F:["Pressure Control Solenoid K Control Circuit Low","P282F reports a ground fault on the control line of solenoid K. On the 2023 Corvette, GM checks the selector pilot valve while its low-side output is switched on; the TCM compares the voltage at the sense pin with a lower limit of about 1.7 V, and a reading below it points to a ground short. After 100 ms the module stores a Type A code, so the MIL lights during the same trip.",["Control wire to valve K shorted to ground","Damaged insulation inside the transmission harness","Coil of valve K shorted to ground internally"],["Gears on one clutch shaft blocked","MIL on in the same trip","Limp mode"],3,3,["P2830","P282D","P282B","P27DF","P2826"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ K — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2830:["Pressure Control Solenoid K Control Circuit High","P2830 is set when the K control line carries voltage where the switched-on low-side driver should pull it down. GM applies it to the selector pilot valve of the 2023 Corvette dual-clutch box with a limit that climbs as supply voltage increases, from about 0.7 V below 11.5 V to 1.1 V above 15.5 V, confirmed after 100 ms.",["Control wire shorted to a supply line","Short to an adjacent solenoid output","Moisture in the connector"],["Gear preselection fails, limp mode","Code back immediately after restart","MIL on"],3,3,["P282F","P282D","P282B","P27E0","P2827"],"סולנואיד בקרת לחץ‏ K — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2831:["Shift Fork A Position Circuit","P2831 is the general circuit code for the position signal of shift fork A in automated manual and dual-clutch gearboxes. How makers fill it varies widely. Mercedes-Benz uses P283100 for an electrical fault of the shift fork A position sensor in the 8G-DCT (transmission 724.1) and lists it among the codes of its guided repair tool.",["Shift fork A position sensor electrically defective","Fault in the module's motor current controller (Ford DPS6)","Poor contact at the sensor or module connector"],["Transmission warning, gear display may flash","Odd gears unavailable or limp-home mode","Delayed engagement or no drive when starting off"],4,3,["P2832","P2833","P2834","P2835","P2836"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2832:["Shift Fork A Position Circuit Range/Performance","P2832 means the fork A position reading is electrically valid but disagrees with what the gearbox is doing. GM's 2023 table for the Corvette dual-clutch box runs this as a consistency check on rod 1: when clutch shaft and output speeds prove a gear is engaged with over 600 N applied, yet the sensor sits more than 1100 µm away from the learned engaged position, a Type A fault follows a confirmation time;",["Sensor magnet or mounting shifted on the shift rod","Learned fork positions no longer valid after repair or wear","Shift rod, fork or drum binding mechanically"],["Gear on the odd shaft not engaged or dropped","Clunks or long pauses during shifts","Limp-home mode with warning lamp"],4,3,["P2831","P2833","P2834","P2835","P2837"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2833:["Shift Fork A Position Circuit Low","P2833 reports a fork A position signal stuck at the low end. On the Corvette dual-clutch gearbox the rod 1 sensor sends a pulse-width signal; GM's 2023 table sets the code when no pulses arrive and the pin stays under 2.0 V, or when the duty cycle drops below 8 %, each confirmed for 150 ms, with the 5 V sensor supply in range and rated Type A.",["Signal wire of the fork A sensor shorted to ground","Sensor output stage failed low","Open signal line letting the input float low"],["Warning lamp and limp-home mode","Gears of one shaft locked out","Car may only pull away in a fallback gear"],4,3,["P2834","P2831","P2835","P2832","P2838"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2834:["Shift Fork A Position Circuit High","P2834 is the high-side counterpart: the fork A position input sits at the upper limit. In GM's 2023 Corvette table the rod 1 sensor is flagged when pulses stop and the pin voltage stays above 3.5 V, or when the duty cycle climbs over 92 %; after 150 ms a Type A fault is stored, but only while the sensor supply lies between 4.5 and 5.5 V and the battery between 8.75 and 18 V.",["Signal wire shorted to the 5 V sensor supply or battery voltage","Sensor output transistor no longer pulling low","Lost sensor ground"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Shifts on the affected shaft blocked","Reduced driveability in limp-home mode"],4,3,["P2833","P2831","P2835","P2832","P2839"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2835:["Shift Fork A Position Circuit Intermittent","P2835 covers a fork A position signal that is present but unsteady. GM's 2023 Corvette dual-clutch table checks the carrier frequency of the rod 1 sensor and sets a Type A fault once it leaves the 1500 to 2500 Hz band for 150 ms; Ford's 2024 summary calls the same check on the TR9070 frequency out of range.",["Intermittent contact at the sensor or module connector","Interference or damaged shielding on the signal line","Faulty Hall sensor in the shift drum motor (Ford DPS6)"],["Occasional refused or late shift","Warning lamp that comes and goes","Hesitation or no drive when pulling away"],4,3,["P2831","P2833","P2834","P2832","P283A"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ A — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2836:["Shift Fork B Position Circuit","P2836 is the umbrella circuit code for the shift fork B position input. Mercedes-Benz stores P283600 when its 8G-DCT dual-clutch transmission (724.1) detects an electrical defect at the fork B sensor and includes it in the code set evaluated by its Intelligent Predictive Repair routine in XENTRY.",["Electrical defect in the fork B position sensor (Mercedes 8G-DCT)","Failed current-control chip for the second shift drum motor in the TCM (Ford DPS6)","Corroded or loose contacts between sensor and module"],["Transmission warning and stored code","Gears of fork B skipped or unavailable","Delayed engagement from Park or no drive (Ford DPS6)"],4,3,["P2837","P2838","P2839","P283A","P2831"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2837:["Shift Fork B Position Circuit Range/Performance","P2837 flags a fork B position reading that is electrically sound but contradicts the gearbox state. GM's Corvette summary from 2023 maps fork B to rod 2 on the odd-gear shaft. A Type A fault follows when the speed sensors confirm a gear under more than 600 N of shift force while the sensor sits over 1100 µm from the learned engaged point, and a second test catches a rod that hardly moves after a release command.",["Learned rod 2 positions no longer matching after repair or wear","Rod, fork or synchronizer binding so the gear does not engage or release cleanly","Sensor magnet or carrier loose on the rod","Blocked second shift drum motor (Ford DPS6)"],["Gear jumps out or is not engaged on fork B","Noticeable pause or clunk while the gearbox retries the shift","Warning lamp and limited gear selection"],4,3,["P2836","P2838","P2839","P283A","P284E","P2832"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2838:["Shift Fork B Position Circuit Low","P2838 is stored when the fork B position input reads at the bottom of its range. The Corvette's rod 2 sensor, fed by GM from the same 5 V reference A as rod 1, has to send a pulse-width signal; if pulses are missing while the pin is below 2.0 V, or the duty cycle drops under 8 %, the module waits 150 ms and logs a Type A fault.",["Fork B sensor signal wire chafed through to ground","Sensor output no longer producing pulses","Break in the signal or supply wire leaving the input low"],["Warning lamp with transmission in limp-home mode","Gears on rod 2 or fork B no longer selected","Rough or delayed shifts around the locked-out gears"],4,3,["P2839","P2836","P283A","P2837","P2833","P0642"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2839:["Shift Fork B Position Circuit High","P2839 covers the other end of the scale: the fork B input is pinned high. GM's 2023 Corvette table for rod 2 sets it when pulses stop and the pin carries more than 3.5 V, or once the duty cycle passes 92 %. The test runs all the time except during cranking, and only while system voltage lies between 8.75 and 18 V and reference A between 4.5 and 5.5 V; 150 ms of the condition produce a Type A code.",["Signal wire of the fork B sensor touching the 5 V or battery supply","Open sensor ground letting the output float high","Sensor output stage stuck in the high state"],["Warning lamp and fault message in the cluster","Fork B gears blocked, fewer gears available","Reduced acceleration in the substitute program"],4,3,["P2838","P2836","P283A","P2837","P2834","P0643"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P283A:["Shift Fork B Position Circuit Intermittent","P283A means the fork B signal is arriving, but not cleanly. For rod 2 of the Corvette dual-clutch gearbox GM measures the period of the sensor carrier and reacts once the equivalent frequency drops below 1500 Hz or rises above 2500 Hz for 150 ms, logging a Type A fault. Ford's 2024 summary files the matching frequency check of TR9070 rod sensor 2 under this number.",["Loose or spread terminal in the fork B sensor connector","Electrical noise coupling into the signal line through damaged shielding","Faulty Hall element in the second shift drum motor (Ford DPS6)"],["Sporadic warning lamp that clears after a restart","Occasional hesitation or refused shift","Intermittent engagement problems when pulling away (Ford DPS6)"],4,3,["P2836","P2838","P2839","P2837","P2835"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P283B:["Shift Fork C Position Circuit","P283B is the generic circuit code for the shift fork C position sensor. The only public manufacturer listing that uses it comes from Mercedes-Benz: on the 8G-DCT dual-clutch transmission (724.1) P283B00 stands for an electrical fault of the fork C sensor and belongs to the codes covered by its XENTRY repair routine for this gearbox.",["Fork C position sensor with an internal electrical fault","Poor contact or moisture at the sensor or TCM connector","Damaged sensor input in the transmission control module"],["Transmission warning in the instrument cluster","Gears handled by fork C no longer engaged","Emergency mode with reduced performance"],4,3,["P283C","P283D","P283E","P283F","P2836"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P283C:["Shift Fork C Position Circuit Range/Performance","P283C is the plausibility code for fork C, which GM's 2023 Corvette table assigns to rod 3 on the even-gear shaft. Besides the force and speed comparison during shifts (over 600 N, more than 1100 µm off the learned point, Type A), a static monitor runs here: with no shift force on the rod, the reading must stay inside tolerance bands around the learned neutral or engaged point.",["Rod 3 creeping out of position because of worn detent or fork","Position values not relearned after gearbox or sensor work","Synchronizer actuation on the even shaft not reaching target position"],["Even gears drop out or refuse to engage","Grinding or a knock during shifts on the even shaft","Warning lamp, gearbox limits gear choice"],4,3,["P283B","P283D","P283E","P283F","P2847","P2837"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P283D:["Shift Fork C Position Circuit Low","P283D reports the fork C input stuck low. In the Corvette dual-clutch gearbox GM feeds the rod 3 sensor from reference B rather than reference A, so its enable test watches that second 5 V rail and pauses while P0652 or P0653 are present. Within those limits the code sets after 150 ms if no pulses are seen and the pin stays below 2.0 V, or if the duty cycle falls under 8 %; it is classed Type A.",["Fork C signal line shorted to ground in the gearbox harness","Fork C sensor no longer switching its output","Damaged supply wire from reference B to the sensor"],["Limp-home mode with warning lamp","Gears of fork C unavailable","Possibly further fork D codes if the shared supply is affected"],4,3,["P283E","P283B","P283F","P283C","P2842","P0652"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P283E:["Shift Fork C Position Circuit High","P283E is the high-side fault of the fork C circuit. GM's 2023 summary checks the Corvette rod 3 sensor for two signs: no pulses at all with the pin above 3.5 V, and a duty cycle above 92 %. Either one, held for 150 ms with reference B in its 4.5 to 5.5 V window and the engine not cranking, stores a Type A code. Ford lists P283E for TR9070 rod sensor 3 as a pulse width beyond the upper limit, input stuck at one.",["Pinched harness with the fork C signal touching a feed wire","Water in the connector bridging signal and supply pins","Fork C sensor without ground connection"],["Warning lamp and gearbox fault message","Fork C gears locked out","Jerky driving in the substitute program"],4,3,["P283D","P283B","P283F","P283C","P2843","P0653"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P283F:["Shift Fork C Position Circuit Intermittent","P283F stands for an unstable fork C position signal rather than a hard short or open. The rod 3 sensor in GM's Corvette dual-clutch gearbox runs at a carrier between 1500 and 2500 Hz; if the measured period puts it outside that band for 150 ms, the module records a Type A fault, as long as reference B and battery voltage are valid. Ford's TR9070 summary assigns the frequency check of rod sensor 3 to this code.",["Fork C connector working loose under engine movement","Corroded terminal causing signal dropouts","Cracked insulation near hot components letting noise in"],["Occasional stutter or delay on even-gear shifts","Warning lamp appears only now and then"],4,3,["P283B","P283D","P283E","P283C","P283A"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ C — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2840:["Shift Fork D Position Circuit","P2840 is the overall circuit code for the shift fork D position input. Mercedes-Benz is the one maker that publicly documents it: in the 8G-DCT (transmission 724.1) of its compact models, P284000 marks an electrical fault of the fork D sensor, and the gearbox has a fifth fork E with its own codes from P2863 upward. The other two published dual-clutch strategies skip this code.",["Electrical failure of the fork D position sensor","Damaged wiring between fork D sensor and the TCM","Transmission control module input or software fault"],["Gears of fork D withheld, gearbox skips them","Transmission warning lamp","Reduced driving comfort in emergency mode"],4,3,["P2841","P2842","P2843","P2844","P283B"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ D — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2841:["Shift Fork D Position Circuit Range/Performance","P2841 indicates that fork D reports a believable voltage but an implausible position. GM's 2023 table runs the rod 4 consistency test in the Corvette only when neither the even-clutch speed signal nor the output speed signal has shown an electrical fault for at least 100 ms, so the comparison has trustworthy speeds behind it.",["Rod 4 or its synchronizer sticking so the fork lags behind the command","Outdated learned positions after a clutch or sensor replacement","Fork D sensor or magnet shifted in its mount"],["Hesitation or repeated attempts on even-gear shifts","Gear not held, slipping back to neutral","Warning lamp with reduced gear range"],4,3,["P2840","P2842","P2843","P2844","P2848","P283C"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ D — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2842:["Shift Fork D Position Circuit Low","P2842 sets when the fork D sensor signal collapses toward zero. GM's 2023 Corvette table expects a pulse train from the rod 4 sensor and flags the circuit if pulses vanish with less than 2.0 V present, or if the duty cycle is lower than 8 %, both held for 150 ms; the resulting fault is Type A. In Ford's TR9070 summary the matching rod sensor 4 entry covers a too-narrow pulse and an input frozen at zero.",["Fork D signal wire shorted to ground or housing","No 5 V feed reaching the sensor","Fork D sensor internally failed"],["Warning lamp, fork D gears blocked","Transmission in emergency program","Additional fork C code if the shared feed is at fault"],4,3,["P2843","P2840","P2844","P2841","P283D"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2843:["Shift Fork D Position Circuit High","P2843 means the fork D position line is sitting near supply level. GM's 2023 Corvette table raises it for rod 4 when there is no pulse activity and more than 3.5 V on the pin, or when the duty cycle is above 92 %; after a 150 ms confirmation a Type A code is set.",["Fork D signal wire in contact with a feed wire","Open ground circuit of the fork D sensor","Internal short in the sensor pulling its output high"],["Fault message and warning lamp","Some even gears no longer selected","Limp-home operation"],4,3,["P2842","P2840","P2844","P2841","P283E"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2844:["Shift Fork D Position Circuit Intermittent","P2844 points to a fork D signal whose timing wanders. GM's Corvette dual-clutch software derives the rod 4 sensor frequency from its period and expects 1500 to 2500 Hz; leaving that window for 150 ms stores a Type A fault, and the check is skipped while cranking or with reference B out of tolerance. Ford's 2024 summary books the frequency test of TR9070 rod sensor 4 under P2844.",["Chafed or loose harness section shared with the fork C sensor","Intermittent terminal contact at the fork D sensor","Sensor with an unstable output frequency"],["Sporadic hesitation on shifts","Warning lamp that may go out again"],4,3,["P2840","P2842","P2843","P2841","P283F"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ D — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2845:["Shift Fork A Position Sensor Incorrect Neutral Position Indicated","P2845 means the fork A sensor reports neutral although the gearbox state says a gear is engaged, or it reports an engaged position where neutral is expected. Public manufacturer documentation for P2845 is lacking, and CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 only asks that transmission inputs be checked for plausibility.",["Neutral position not learned or lost after repair or software update","Sensor magnet or target shifted on the rod","Worn fork or detent changing the neutral position"],["Gear display shows N while a gear is engaged, or the reverse","Shifts refused, transmission in limp-home mode","Warning lamp on"],3,3,["P2832","P2831","P2846","P2849","P284D"],""],P2846:["Shift Fork B Position Sensor Incorrect Neutral Position Indicated","P2846 flags a mismatch between the neutral reading of the fork B position sensor and the gear state the transmission module expects. Either the sensor claims fork B rests in neutral while the shaft speeds prove its gear carries load, or it reports an engaged fork where the module has commanded neutral. No manufacturer publicly documents P2846.",["Learned neutral position of fork B missing after repair or module replacement","Magnet or target on the fork B rod loosened or shifted","Worn detent letting fork B settle off its neutral point"],["Gears served by fork B refused or skipped","Transmission warning with reduced performance","Gear indicator disagrees with the actual gear"],3,3,["P2845","P2847","P2848","P2837","P2851"],""],P2847:["Shift Fork C Position Sensor Incorrect Neutral Position Indicated","With P2847 the module has decided that the neutral signal from the fork C sensor cannot be trusted. Before a dual-clutch or automated manual box preselects a gear on a shaft, it must know that the other forks on that shaft are out; a false neutral could let two ratios mesh at once, so the module normally locks the affected gears out.",["Fork C sensor or magnet repositioned during transmission work without relearn","Fork C bent, so neutral lies outside the learned band","Position sensor output drifting with temperature or age"],["Gears of fork C locked out, jumps between remaining ratios","Warning lamp and stored transmission code","Harsh or delayed shifts on the affected shaft"],3,3,["P2846","P2848","P2845","P283C","P2852"],""],P2848:["Shift Fork D Position Sensor Incorrect Neutral Position Indicated","P2848 is the neutral-plausibility code for the fourth fork. It sets when the fork D sensor signal and the logical state of that fork disagree about neutral, even though the signal itself is electrically sound. None of the published strategies uses the number: Mercedes-Benz lists four separate fork D sensor faults for its 8G-DCT (724.1), from P284000 to P284300, but not this one;",["Fork D positions not relearned after software update or repair","Sensor of fork D loose in its mount","Wear on fork pads or synchronizer sleeve shifting the rest position"],["Gears of fork D unavailable","Drive system warning, emergency program"],3,3,["P2847","P2846","P2845","P2841","P2852"],""],P2849:["Shift Fork A Stuck","P2849 says that fork A did not travel when the module ordered it to, so its gear could not be put in or taken out. The reading may be valid; the fork itself is not following the command. No manufacturer publishes a strategy for P2849, and the code relies on the CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 rule that transmission components be checked for proper function.",["Fork A actuator or its control valve not moving the rod","Shift rod of fork A seized in its bore or blocked by debris","Broken fork or damaged synchronizer sleeve jamming the shift"],["Gear of fork A will not engage or stays engaged","Limp-home mode with limited gears","Clunking or grinding during shift attempts"],4,3,["P284A","P284B","P284C","P2869","P2832"],"מזלג העברה‏ A — תקוע"],P284A:["Shift Fork B Stuck","P284A is stored when fork B stays put although the transmission module commanded a move, for instance from neutral toward an engaged gear or back. Published strategies avoid this code. Ford's 2024 summary for the TR9070 dual-clutch box diagnoses the same symptom per gear rather than per fork, with failure-to-engage codes such as P073F and failure-to-disengage codes such as P072B, while GM's Corvette software folds a…",["Fork B actuator, solenoid or hydraulic supply failing to apply force","Synchronizer of fork B gears jammed or damaged","Contaminated fluid restricting the fork B actuator"],["Gears of fork B missing or a gear stays engaged","Warning lamp and emergency mode","Rough starts or lack of drive in some gears"],4,3,["P2849","P284B","P284C","P073F","P072B"],"מזלג העברה‏ B — תקוע"],P284B:["Shift Fork C Stuck","P284B reports a third fork that refuses to travel. Two situations matter: stuck in neutral, which merely costs the gears of fork C, and stuck in an engaged gear, which is more serious because that shaft then turns with a fixed ratio and a second gear on the same shaft must never be selected. No published OBD strategy assigns P284B, so the code rests on what CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 demands for transmission parts.",["Selector or pilot valve not routing pressure to the fork C rod","Low or degraded transmission fluid","Fork C or its rod mechanically jammed"],["Car stays in one gear on one shaft or skips the fork C gears","Transmission warning lamp"],4,3,["P2849","P284A","P284C","P282A","P2829"],"מזלג העברה‏ C — תקוע"],P284C:["Shift Fork D Stuck","P284C applies when fork D, the fourth of the generic shift forks, fails to answer an actuation request. Whether the drive is hydraulic, as in most wet dual-clutch boxes, or electric, as in automated manuals with motor-driven drums, the module sees the request but no travel at the position sensor. No manufacturer documentation for P284C is public.",["Fork D actuator motor or hydraulic valve failed","Shift drum or rod binding at fork D","Module output stage not driving the fork D actuator"],["Gears of fork D unavailable or stuck engaged","Emergency program, reduced speed","Warning in the instrument cluster"],4,3,["P284B","P284A","P2849","P2869","P2840"],"מזלג העברה‏ D — תקוע"],P284D:["Shift Fork A Unrequested Movement","P284D means fork A has crept away from the position of the gear it is supposed to hold, without any shift being commanded. Several makers use it. Audi bulletin 2078846 covers 2025 A5 and Q5 models with the DL382 and DL552 dual-clutch boxes: the cluster reports a drive system fault with limited performance, and if guided fault finding finds no cause, the gear position distance sensors G487 to G490 are calibrated ten…",["Gear position sensors poorly calibrated (Audi DL382/DL552)","Transmission software needing an update","Leaking fork A actuator or weak detent letting the rod creep"],["Message about a drive system fault with limited performance","First or seventh gear cannot be selected (Audi report)","Gear may jump out under load"],3,3,["P284E","P284F","P2850","P286A","P2832"],""],P284E:["Shift Fork B Unrequested Movement","P284E reports that fork B drifted while no shift was asked for. GM's 2023 Corvette dual-clutch table describes the test on rod 2 in detail: with no actuating force applied, the measured position must stay inside wide limits around the learned point of the gear verified as engaged by clutch-shaft and output speed readings; leaving them for 500 ms is a fault.",["Synchronizer pressure valve for fork B leaking and pushing the rod","Weak detent or worn gear dog teeth on fork B gears","Outdated learned engaged positions"],["Gear on the odd shaft pops out or is re-engaged with a jolt","Warning lamp, possible limp-home mode"],3,3,["P284D","P284F","P2850","P2837","P286A"],""],P284F:["Shift Fork C Unrequested Movement","P284F covers drift of fork C away from its held gear. In GM's Corvette software this is rod 3, which sits on the shaft of the even clutch; the check compares the rod position with the learned point for the gear that the even clutch speed and the output speed confirm, and sets a Type A code once the wide limit is exceeded long enough or the drift correction keeps firing.",["Residual pressure on the fork C actuator from a leaking valve","Rod 3 sensor reading offset so the fork appears to move","Worn detent or synchronizer parts at fork C"],["Even-shaft gear disengages unexpectedly","Shift flare or jerk while cruising","Warning lamp with stored code"],3,3,["P2850","P284E","P284D","P277E","P283C"],""],P2850:["Shift Fork D Unrequested Movement","P2850 closes the drift series for the four main forks: fork D has shifted position although the module neither commanded a change nor applied force to it. GM uses the code for rod 4 of the Corvette dual-clutch unit, again as a Type A fault that runs continuously and hands over to the even-shaft synchronizer recovery.",["Leaking synchronizer or selector valve moving the fork D rod","Positions not relearned after module or sensor replacement","Weak detent or rounded dog teeth on fork D gears"],["Gear of fork D slips out under load","Gears of fork D blocked, emergency program"],3,3,["P284F","P284E","P284D","P277F","P2841"],""],P2851:["Shift Fork Position Sensor A/B Correlation","P2851 is meant for a plausibility comparison between the position sensors of forks A and B. Both readings may be in range on their own, yet together they describe an impossible state, such as both forks engaged at once, or they move in step in a way that points to a shared supply or ground fault. No maker publishes a strategy for this pair code.",["Shared supply or ground of the A and B sensors disturbed","One of the two sensors drifting while still in range","Corroded contacts at the internal transmission connector"],["Gears of forks A and B locked out","Warning lamp, limp-home mode"],3,3,["P2852","P2832","P2837","P2845","P2846"],"חיישן מצב מזלג העברה‏ A/B — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2852:["Shift Fork Position Sensor C/D Correlation","P2852 pairs the position sensors of forks C and D and sets when their readings do not fit together. In GM's numbering these are rods 3 and 4, both on the even shaft and fed from the second sensor reference; a reference fault there would shift both signals together.",["Reference voltage feeding the C and D sensors out of tolerance","Sensor C or D reporting a shifted value","Input circuit fault in the transmission module"],["Gears of forks C and D unavailable","Transmission fault message, reduced power"],3,3,["P2851","P283C","P2841","P2847","P2848"],"חיישן מצב מזלג העברה‏ C/D — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2853:["Clutch A Pressure Discharge Performance","P2853 is set when the pressure measured at clutch A falls short of what the control model predicts. GM's 2023 Corvette dual-clutch table applies it to clutch 1, the odd-gear clutch, as a Type A fault in two ways: the model expects more than 1 bar while the sensor shows under 0.5 bar for 5 s, or the measured value stays below the model by more than a calibrated margin for too long.",["Clutch A pressure control valve sticking or delivering too little","Leaking seal or piston ring in the clutch A circuit","Low fluid level or clogged filter reducing supply pressure"],["Weak or delayed launch, engine flares","Odd gears unavailable, limp-home mode","Warning lamp on"],4,3,["P2854","P2855","P2857","P0844","P0868"],"פריקת לחץ מצמד‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2854:["Clutch B Pressure Discharge Performance","P2854 is the even-side partner of P2853: the pressure sensor of clutch B reports less than the control model expects. In GM's Corvette software clutch 2 drives the even gears; the check uses the same logic as on clutch 1, with a modeled value above 1 bar facing a reading under 0.5 bar for 5 s, plus a second path that watches the absolute gap between model and sensor.",["Clutch B pressure control valve restricted by debris or wear","Seal leak in the clutch B feed or piston","Foamed or overheated fluid lowering effective pressure"],["Even gears skipped, car runs in odd gears only","Slipping or flare on shifts into even gears","Transmission warning"],4,3,["P2853","P2856","P2858","P0849","P0868"],"פריקת לחץ מצמד‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2855:["Clutch A Pressure Charge Performance","P2855 points the other way from P2853: clutch A carries more pressure than the model calls for. GM's Corvette table for clutch 1 uses three paths, all Type A. The measured pressure sits above the model by more than a set difference long enough to be confirmed; the absolute gap grows too large with the reading on the high side;",["Clutch A pressure control valve sticking toward high output","Excessive line pressure feeding the clutch circuit","Clutch adaptation values out of date after repair"],["Harsh engagement or jerky creep from standstill","Drag felt as if the brakes were applied","Limp-home mode with warning lamp"],4,3,["P2856","P2853","P2859","P0869","P0841"],"טעינת לחץ מצמד‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2856:["Clutch B Pressure Charge Performance","P2856 flags too much pressure at clutch B, the even-gear clutch in GM's and Ford's dual-clutch layouts. For the Corvette unit GM checks clutch 2 with the same high-side logic as clutch 1, including the hold-pressure case: an open clutch held at its standby pressure must not rise well above that point, because it would then pass torque while the other clutch is driving.",["Clutch B pressure control valve hanging in a high-pressure position","Safety shutdown valve for clutch B not venting","Clutch B pressure sensor reading high within its range"],["Shudder or binding during shifts","Even gears blocked, emergency program","Warning lamp"],4,3,["P2855","P2854","P285A","P0869","P0846"],"טעינת לחץ מצמד‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2857:["Clutch A Pressure Engagement Performance/Too Low","P2857 reports that clutch A did not build up enough holding force when the control unit asked it to engage, so the expected ratio or torque transfer never appeared. Mitsubishi documents it for the CVT with two-speed auxiliary gearbox fitted to Mirage and Mirage G4 models from 2014 to 2022: while that gearbox is shifted into its first ratio, a measured ratio of 2.232 or more for 2 s counts as a fault, provided the…",["Control valve (valve body) not delivering the commanded apply pressure to clutch A","Worn clutch A linings or leaking piston seals","Low, aerated or aged transmission fluid"],["Engine speed flares on take-off without matching acceleration","Hesitation or reduced power, transmission emergency mode","Warning lamp with stored transmission code"],4,3,["P2858","P2859","P2853","P2855","P286B","P2871"],""],P2858:["Clutch B Pressure Engagement Performance/Too Low","P2858 is the clutch B counterpart of P2857: the element that should close for the second stage never reaches the pressure needed to carry torque. In Mitsubishi's Mirage CVT the check runs while the auxiliary gearbox changes up to its second ratio; if the ratio still reads 2.232 or higher after at least 2 s, the TCM concludes the box is hanging in neutral between the stages.",["Control valve unable to raise clutch B pressure","Slip damage inside the transmission (belt, clutch B linings)","Fluid level or quality outside specification"],["Second stage or even gears engage late or not at all","Engine revs rise at cruising speed, acceleration lags","Reduced power with warning lamp"],4,3,["P2857","P285A","P2854","P2856","P2873","P2879"],""],P2859:["Clutch A Pressure Disengagement Performance/Too Low","P2859 concerns the release side of clutch A: during a ratio change the control unit sees that the pressure handover is not working as planned, so the old and new power paths overlap or the wrong ratio persists. Mitsubishi's Mirage CVT shows how this is tested.",["Outgoing clutch not venting in time, so both elements carry torque","Sticking pressure control solenoid or valve in the valve body","Clutch pressure switch reporting pressure that is not there"],["Harsh, doubled or tied-up shifts","Wrong gear stage held, engine speed too low or too high","Transmission warning and emergency program"],4,3,["P285A","P2857","P286C","P286F","P0876"],""],P285A:["Clutch B Pressure Disengagement Performance/Too Low","With P285A the module reports a release-side pressure fault involving clutch B. Mitsubishi's Mirage CVT evaluates it while the auxiliary gearbox is commanded into its second stage: a ratio that remains within 10 % of the first stage (1.639–2.003) for 0.5 s, or that drops to 0.500 or below or climbs to 1.500 or above for 0.2 s, sets the code.",["Defective control valve, especially when P0875 is stored at the same time","Leak in the clutch B circuit preventing a clean handover","Faulty clutch pressure switch or its wiring"],["Upper stage or even gears not available","Flare between shifts, then a hard engagement","Limp mode with warning lamp"],4,3,["P2859","P2858","P2874","P2877","P0875"],""],P285B:["Shift Fork A Actuator Circuit/Open","P285B covers the electrical drive of the actuator that moves fork A, for designs where an electric motor rather than oil pressure shifts the gears. The module sets it when the output stage sees no load, typically a broken winding, a cut lead or a connector that has backed out.",["Loose, corroded or backed-out connector at the fork A actuator motor","Broken lead between transmission module and actuator motor","Open phase winding inside the actuator motor","Failed motor output stage in the transmission module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp and transmission warning","First, third or fifth gear not available, car may only move in the even gears","Jerky starts or refusal to pull away"],3,3,["P285C","P285D","P285E","P285F","P2831","P2832","P2835"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P285C:["Shift Fork A Actuator Performance","P285C is the functional counterpart to the electrical fork A actuator codes. The circuit may be intact, yet the actuator does not achieve what it is asked to do: it moves too slowly, draws an unexpected current or leaves the fork short of its target. No manufacturer publishes a detection strategy for P285C.",["Worn or sluggish fork A actuator motor","Shift drum, rod or fork A binding mechanically","Worn reduction gearing between motor and drum","Low supply voltage to the module during shifts"],["Slow or harsh shifts into the gears of fork A","Wrench or transmission warning without engine lamp","Occasional gear skipping or neutral moments"],3,2,["P285B","P285D","P285E","P2860","P2832","P2849"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P285D:["Shift Fork A Actuator Circuit Low","P285D points to a fork A actuator line pulled toward ground: a chafed motor phase touching the case, water in the connector, or a short inside the motor. To protect its driver, the module normally shuts the output down at once. In Ford's 2012 OBD summary for the DPS6 gearbox this exact fault, a short to ground on the shift drum A motor, carries P285D; the MIL is requested, as Ford's 2014 code catalogue confirms.",["Actuator motor lead chafed through against the transmission case","Water or corrosion in the actuator connector","Internal short of a motor winding to its housing"],["Engine lamp on, odd gears locked out","Car starts in second gear or will not move off","Code returns immediately after clearing"],3,3,["P285B","P285E","P285C","P2861","P2831"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P285E:["Shift Fork A Actuator Circuit High","P285E is logged when a line of the fork A actuator carries supply voltage where the module expects it to be switched low. Usual explanations are a harness short to a battery-fed wire or a low-side transistor in the module that no longer turns on; with some driver designs, an unloaded output can also read high.",["Actuator lead shorted to a battery-fed wire in the harness","Low-side driver in the transmission module not switching","Bridged pins in the actuator or module connector"],["Engine lamp lit, gears 1, 3 and 5 unavailable","Gearbox stays in an even gear or neutral"],3,3,["P285B","P285D","P285C","P2862","P2831"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P285F:["Shift Fork B Actuator Circuit/Open","With P285F the module reports that the drive circuit of the fork B actuator is open: current cannot flow when the motor or valve is energised. In Ford's DPS6 dual-clutch box, the second shift drum is turned by its own three-phase motor and places the forks for reverse plus 2nd, 4th and 6th; an open motor circuit there is P285F and requests the MIL.",["Fork B actuator connector loose or with spread terminals","Open wire in the harness to the fork B actuator","Burnt or broken winding in the fork B motor"],["No reverse gear, even gears missing","Engine lamp and gearbox fault message","Car drives only in 1st, 3rd and 5th with large rpm steps"],3,3,["P2860","P2861","P2862","P285B","P2836","P2837","P283A"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2860:["Shift Fork B Actuator Performance","P2860 says the fork B actuator is electrically present but underperforms: travel takes too long, the target position is missed, or the effort needed to move it is out of line with what the module expects. No maker has published how it detects P2860.",["Stiff shift drum, rod or fork B","Fork B actuator motor with worn bearings or brushes","Debris or wear in the selector track"],["Delayed engagement of reverse or the even gears","Wrench lamp or gearbox message, engine lamp off","Clunk or shudder during upshifts to 2nd, 4th or 6th"],3,2,["P285F","P2861","P2862","P285C","P2837","P284A"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2861:["Shift Fork B Actuator Circuit Low","P2861 is set when a fork B actuator line reads near ground although the module has not switched it there, the classic signature of a short to ground. Ford's 2012 DPS6 summary assigns exactly this case on the motor of the drum for reverse and the even gears to P2861, and the 2014 Ford catalogue marks it as a MIL fault.",["Fork B motor lead rubbed through on a bracket or the case","Corrosion bridging a terminal to ground in the connector","Fork B motor winding shorted to its housing"],["Reverse not selectable","Engine lamp on, only odd gears in use"],3,3,["P285F","P2862","P2860","P285D","P2836"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2862:["Shift Fork B Actuator Circuit High","P2862 indicates that a fork B actuator line sits at or near battery voltage when it should be pulled low. In practice this is a short to a powered conductor or a module transistor that stays open. Ford documents P2862 in its 2012 OBD summary as the short-to-power check of the DPS6 motor that turns the drum for reverse and gears 2, 4 and 6; the 2014 catalogue lists the MIL for it.",["Fork B actuator wire shorted to a powered conductor","Module output transistor for fork B stuck","Insulation melted near the exhaust or a hot component"],["Engine lamp, no reverse or stuck in one even gear","Large rpm jumps because only odd gears are used"],3,3,["P285F","P2861","P2860","P285E","P2836"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2863:["Shift Fork E Position Circuit","P2863 is the general circuit code for the position sensor of a fifth shift fork, used where the module cannot or does not distinguish between low, high and erratic signals. Only transmissions with five forks need it, such as eight-speed dual-clutch units.",["Poor contact at the fork E sensor or module connector","Fork E position sensor failed internally","Sensor reference supply shared with other sensors disturbed"],["Gears on fork E blocked, drive continues in remaining gears","Drive system warning in the instrument cluster","Unusual shift sequence or skipped gears"],3,3,["P2864","P2865","P2866","P2867","P2840"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ E — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2864:["Shift Fork E Position Circuit Range/Performance","P2864 sets when the fork E position signal is electrically fine but contradicts what the shaft speeds show. GM's 2023 Corvette dual-clutch table uses it as the Type A consistency check of rod 5, which belongs to the even-gear clutch shaft. During an engagement with more than 600 N of rod force, the code matures if speeds prove the gear is in but the sensor stays over 1100 µm from the learned engaged point;",["Learned positions of rod 5 missing or outdated after repair or software update","Sensor magnet on the fork E rod shifted or loose","Synchronizer actuation valve for rod 5 sticking, so the rod barely moves","Implausible even-shaft or output speed signal misleading the check"],["Gears on fork E locked out, warning lamp on","Harsh or aborted shifts on the even shaft","Reduced performance mode"],3,3,["P2863","P2865","P2866","P2867","P2868","P2841","P27D5"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ E — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2865:["Shift Fork E Position Circuit Low","P2865 means the fork E position input is stuck low. On GM's 2023 Corvette, whose rod 5 sensor sends a pulse-width signal, the TCM runs two Type A checks under this number: no pulses at all while the pin rests below 2000 mV, or a duty cycle under 8 %, each confirmed after 150 ms. The test is suspended while cranking, outside 8.75 to 18 V battery voltage, or when the sensor reference supply leaves its band.",["Fork E sensor signal wire shorted to ground","Fork E sensor with internal short or failed output stage","Sensor supply missing because of an open feed"],["Warning lamp with fork E gears blocked","Fault returns at once after clearing"],3,3,["P2866","P2863","P2867","P2864","P2842"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2866:["Shift Fork E Position Circuit High","P2866 is the high-level fault of the fork E sensor input. GM's Corvette TCM, reading rod 5 as a pulse-width signal, stores it as Type A in two situations: the line delivers no pulses and stays above 3500 mV, or the duty cycle climbs past 92 %. Either must persist for 150 ms, and the check pauses during cranking or when battery or reference voltage lies outside its window.",["Fork E signal wire touching a supply voltage wire","Open ground of the fork E sensor letting the signal float high","Sensor electronics holding the output permanently high"],["Gears of fork E withheld, warning shown","Engine lamp after a short drive"],3,3,["P2865","P2863","P2867","P2864","P2843"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2867:["Shift Fork E Position Circuit Intermittent","P2867 reports that the fork E sensor signal is present but unsteady. GM's Corvette TCM times each cycle of the digital rod 5 signal and sets the code, Type A, when the frequency drops below 1500 Hz or rises above 2500 Hz for at least 150 ms, with the same voltage and cranking exclusions as the low and high tests. So the sensor keeps pulsing, just not at a rate the module accepts.",["Loose or fretted terminal in the fork E sensor circuit","Damaged shielding letting electrical noise into the signal","Sensor electronics failing intermittently when hot"],["Sporadic warning, sometimes without noticeable effect","Occasional lockout of fork E gears"],3,3,["P2863","P2865","P2866","P2864","P2844"],"מצב מזלג העברה‏ E — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2868:["Shift Fork E Position Sensor Incorrect Neutral Position Indicated","P2868 concerns the neutral information from the fork E sensor. The signal is electrically valid, but the module judges that the neutral it shows does not fit the real state of the fifth fork, either neutral claimed while a gear on that fork transmits drive, or a fork that seems engaged where neutral has been commanded. No manufacturer documents P2868 publicly.",["Learned neutral of fork E lost after module swap or repair","Magnet or target on the fork E rod displaced","Worn detent or bent fork moving the rest position"],["Gears served by fork E refused","Gear display does not match the gear actually engaged","Warning lamp with limp-home program"],3,3,["P2864","P2869","P2848","P2863"],""],P2869:["Shift Fork E Stuck","P2869 states that fork E does not follow its commands: a gear on that fork cannot be engaged or released, although the position input itself may be working. No manufacturer publishes a strategy for P2869; the basis is the CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 requirement to check transmission components for function. The only public method for a fifth rod comes from GM's 2023 Corvette table.",["Fork E rod seized in its bore or blocked by debris","Actuator or hydraulic valve of fork E not moving the rod","Synchronizer or sleeve of fork E jammed or broken"],["One gear stays engaged or cannot be selected","Transmission emergency mode, warning lamp","Grinding or clunking from the gearbox"],4,3,["P2864","P286A","P2868","P284C","P27D5"],"מזלג העברה‏ E — תקוע"],P286A:["Shift Fork E Unrequested Movement","P286A flags fork E creeping out of the position that belongs to its current gear, although no shift was requested and no force is being applied. GM uses the code in the 2023 Corvette dual-clutch TCM as the Type A drift fault of rod 5: as long as even clutch speed and output speed confirm the gear the module believes is engaged, the measured rod position must stay inside wide tolerance limits around that gear, and…",["Weak detent spring or worn detent notch on the fork E rod","Leaking synchronizer actuation valve pushing the rod","Position reference of rod 5 lost after repair"],["Gear on fork E jumps out or shudders under load","Unexpected reshift or brief loss of drive","Warning lamp and stored transmission code"],3,3,["P2869","P2864","P2850","P2868"],""],P286B:["Clutch A Pressure Engagement Too High","P286B means the pressure applied to clutch A during engagement exceeded the level the control unit had planned. A clutch pressed too hard closes abruptly, which shows up as a jolt, a harsh launch or a shunt through the driveline. No manufacturer documents P286B publicly; the basis is CARB 13 CCR 1968.2, which asks for functional monitoring of automatic transmission controls.",["Clutch A pressure control valve sticking towards high output","Clutch adaptation values missing or wrong after repair or software update","Clutch pressure sensor reading higher than actual"],["Harsh launch or jolt when clutch A closes","Clunk through the driveline during shifts","Warning lamp, possibly limp mode"],4,3,["P2873","P286C","P2857","P2855","P286E"],"שילוב לחץ מצמד‏ A — ערך גבוה מדי"],P286C:["Clutch A Pressure Disengagement Too High","P286C sets when clutch A still holds too much pressure while it is supposed to open. The residual force keeps the clutch dragging, so in a dual-clutch or planetary layout two power paths can briefly work against each other; the result is shudder, a braking feel during shifts or creeping with neutral selected. No manufacturer publishes a strategy for this exact code.",["Valve or exhaust passage for clutch A not venting fully","Debris or clutch material in the valve body","Pressure sensor showing residual pressure that is not real"],["Shudder or binding during shifts","Vehicle creeps or feels braked in neutral","Clutch overheating warning possible"],4,3,["P2874","P286B","P2859","P2872","P2855"],"ניתוק לחץ מצמד‏ A — ערך גבוה מדי"],P286D:["Clutch A Engagement Time Performance/Too Slow","P286D sets when clutch A takes longer to engage than the control unit allows. Volvo uses it in the inverter module (IEM) of the electric rear axle drive on its T8 plug-in hybrids: the rear e-motor is coupled to the wheels through a clutch, and when coupling is too slow, electric rear drive and all-wheel drive drop out and the MIL may light.",["Outdated control module calibration (Volvo IEM software)","Slow clutch fill from low, aerated fluid or a restricted feed","Internal fault of the clutch or drive unit"],["Electric rear drive or all-wheel drive unavailable","Delayed engagement with a pause in drive","MIL or hybrid warning"],3,3,["P2875","P286E","P286F","P2871","P2857"],""],P286E:["Clutch A Engagement Time Too Fast","P286E is the opposite of P286D: clutch A reaches its engaged state sooner than the control unit expects. An overly quick engagement usually means the fill phase is being skipped, because the piston was already partly applied, the pressure control overshoots or adaptation values are too aggressive; the driver feels a bang on take-off or during shifts. No manufacturer documents P286E in a public source.",["Clutch adaptation values too aggressive or not matched to new parts","Pressure control overshooting due to a sticking solenoid","Clutch piston not fully retracted before the next apply"],["Bang or jerk when clutch A engages","Harsh take-off from standstill"],3,3,["P286D","P2876","P286B","P2872","P2870"],""],P286F:["Clutch A Disengagement Time Performance/Too Slow","P286F tells that clutch A needs too long to release. Torque then keeps flowing after the control unit has ordered the clutch open, which disturbs shifts and can make the vehicle creep or stall the engine at a stop. Ford lists the code as an MIL item in its 2014 diagnostic code catalogue. In Ford's DPS6, clutch A serves first, third and fifth gear and a spring pushes it open when its electric motor is switched off.",["Control module software needing an update (Ford PCM/TCM, Volvo IEM)","Release mechanism or return spring of clutch A sticking","Clutch wear shifting the release point beyond the learned value"],["Shudder or clunk on shifts out of odd gears","Creeping or engine stalling when stopping","MIL on, reduced function"],3,3,["P2877","P2870","P286D","P2872","P07A3"],""],P2870:["Clutch A Disengagement Time Too Fast","P2870 flags clutch A opening faster than the control unit intended. During a shift the outgoing clutch has to pass torque smoothly to the incoming one; if it lets go too early, engine speed flares and the shift feels like a slip followed by a thump. No manufacturer publicly documents P2870.",["Leaking clutch A piston seal letting pressure drop too fast","Pressure control valve venting faster than commanded","Adaptation values not suited to the current clutch condition","Low fluid level"],["Engine flare during shifts, then a thump","Firmer substitute shift program"],4,3,["P2878","P286F","P286E","P2859","P2853"],""],P2871:["Clutch A Performance/Stuck Disengaged","P2871 means clutch A does not close, or slips so much that it behaves as if open. Mitsubishi documents this for the clutch in the front transaxle of the 2023 Outlander PHEV, which links the engine to the wheels in parallel mode: once parallel mode has been active for 2 s, the PHEV-ECU counts how often the speeds before and after the clutch differ by 75 rpm or more for 2 s, and after eight such events the code sets…",["Worn clutch A that slips under load","Low transaxle fluid or external leak","Valve body, oil pump, pressure regulator or relief valve not supplying pressure","Control unit fault or outdated software"],["Engine cannot drive the wheels directly, only series or electric drive","Engine speed rises without extra thrust","MIL on"],4,3,["P2872","P2879","P286D","P2857","P07A2"],""],P2872:["Clutch A Stuck Engaged","P2872 is set when clutch A stays closed although it should be open. Mitsubishi's 2023 Outlander PHEV uses it for the engine clutch in the front transaxle: in EV mode, or in series mode where an open clutch would leave a large speed gap, the front motor turns at 750 rpm or more, yet input and output of the clutch differ by 8 rpm or less for 3.5 s. Both the hybrid warning and the MIL come on.",["Clutch A plates seized or welded together","Foreign material holding the proportional valve in the apply position","Control unit commanding or reading clutch state incorrectly"],["Engine turns with the wheels in EV mode, unusual noise or drag","Engine stalls when the vehicle stops","Hybrid system warning and MIL"],4,3,["P2871","P287A","P286C","P286E","P07A3"],"מצמד‏ A — תקוע במצב משולב"],P2873:["Clutch B Pressure Engagement Too High","P2873 is set when clutch B is applied with more pressure than planned while it engages. In dual-clutch designs clutch B usually carries the even gears and reverse, as in Ford's DPS6 and GM's Corvette unit, so the fault tends to surface as jerky shifts into second, fourth or reverse and a hard bite when manoeuvring. Manufacturer documentation for P2873 is not public.",["Clutch B pressure control solenoid sticking high","System (line) pressure above specification","Drifted or reset adaptation values for clutch B","Clutch B pressure sensor over-reading"],["Jerky shifts into even gears or reverse","Hard bite when manoeuvring","Warning lamp, limp mode possible"],4,3,["P286B","P2874","P2858","P2856","P2876"],"שילוב לחץ מצמד‏ B — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2874:["Clutch B Pressure Disengagement Too High","P2874 indicates that clutch B keeps excess pressure while it is being released or should already be open. Clutch B then goes on carrying torque alongside the engaged path, which can be felt as binding, vibration during upshifts from even gears or a car that pulls while in neutral; an overheated clutch is a typical consequence. No manufacturer publishes P2874-specific criteria.",["Clutch B valve not venting pressure on release","Contamination in the valve body from clutch wear","Seized shutdown valve or clutch B actuator"],["Binding or vibration on upshifts from even gears","Car pulls in neutral","Clutch temperature warning"],4,3,["P286C","P2873","P285A","P287A","P2856"],"ניתוק לחץ מצמד‏ B — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2875:["Clutch B Engagement Time Performance/Too Slow","P2875 tells that clutch B takes too long to grip once the control unit has asked for it. Slow filling leaves a gap in drive during shifts into the gears served by clutch B, with a flare of engine speed before the clutch finally holds. No manufacturer explains P2875 in a public document; the requirement for functional monitoring comes from CARB 13 CCR 1968.2.",["Low or aerated fluid slowing the fill of clutch B","Partly blocked filter or valve passage","Worn seals leaking while the clutch fills","Electric clutch actuator running slowly"],["Delayed shifts into even gears with engine flare","Noticeable pause in drive during shifts","Warning lamp"],3,3,["P286D","P2876","P2877","P2858","P2879"],""],P2876:["Clutch B Engagement Time Too Fast","P2876 flags clutch B closing faster than its programmed fill and apply profile allows. Instead of a smooth handover the clutch grabs abruptly, which is often noticed as a knock when selecting reverse or when a dual-clutch box shifts into an even gear. No public manufacturer document describes P2876.",["Adaptation values not relearned after clutch or mechatronic work","Clutch B solenoid overshooting its target pressure","Software calibration fault in the control unit"],["Knock when engaging reverse or even gears","Abrupt, harsh shifts"],3,3,["P286E","P2875","P2873","P287A","P2878"],""],P2877:["Clutch B Disengagement Time Performance/Too Slow","P2877 means clutch B releases too slowly after the command to open. While it lingers, the outgoing clutch fights the incoming one, so shifts out of even gears and reverse feel heavy, the car may shudder or the engine can be pulled down at a stop. Ford includes P2877 as an MIL code in its 2014 diagnostic code list.",["Clutch B actuator or return spring not opening the clutch quickly","Clutch B wear or glazing changing the release behaviour","Restricted vent path on wet-clutch systems"],["Heavy or shuddering shifts out of even gears and reverse","Engine pulled down or stalling at a stop","MIL on"],3,3,["P286F","P2878","P2875","P285A","P07A5"],""],P2878:["Clutch B Disengagement Time Too Fast","P2878 reports that clutch B lets go sooner or more abruptly than the release ramp held in the control unit. During a powershift the outgoing clutch has to keep carrying torque until the incoming one has taken over; if clutch B drops out early, the engine flares for a moment and the next gear arrives with a jolt, mostly on shifts away from reverse and the even gears.",["Clutch B adaptation values no longer matching the linings","Actuator position count lost or misread by the hall sensors","On wet systems a clutch B valve venting pressure too quickly","Low fluid level or aerated fluid"],["Brief engine flare followed by a jolt when shifting","Harsh shifts out of even gears or reverse","Warning lamp, firmer substitute shift program"],3,3,["P2877","P2876","P2870","P2879","P287A"],""],P2879:["Clutch B Performance/Stuck Disengaged","P2879 is set when clutch B does not reach the torque it is asked for, or stays open altogether, so a large speed difference remains across it. No manufacturer publishes a test written for P2879.",["Worn or glazed clutch B slipping under load","Insufficient apply pressure from valve body, pump or regulator","Clutch B actuator motor or its drive failed","Wiring fault or control unit not commanding the clutch"],["Reverse or even gears missing","Engine speed rises without thrust","MIL and limp mode"],4,3,["P2871","P2875","P2878","P287A","P07A4"],""],P287A:["Clutch B Stuck Engaged","P287A means clutch B stays closed, or keeps transmitting torque, at a moment when it should be open. Ford lists P287A as an MIL code in its 2014 code catalogue. In the DPS6 gearbox Ford describes for 2012, clutch B carries reverse together with 2nd, 4th and 6th and is pushed open by a return spring once its electric motor backs off; the older summary books that motor case as P07A5.",["Clutch B actuator or return spring not opening the clutch","Clutch B plates seized or welded after overheating","On wet systems a valve held in the apply position by debris","Control unit or wiring commanding apply continuously"],["Shudder or binding, strong pull in neutral","Engine stalls when the car stops","MIL on, gears locked out"],4,3,["P2872","P2874","P2879","P2878","P07A5"],"מצמד‏ B — תקוע במצב משולב"],P287B:["Shift Fork A Calibration Not Learned","P287B says that the control unit has no valid learned reference positions for shift fork A and therefore cannot place it accurately in neutral or in its gears. On electrically shifted dual-clutch boxes such as Ford's DPS6, drum A moves the forks for 1st, 3rd and 5th;",["TCM replaced or reprogrammed without running the fork learn","Learn routine aborted by low voltage or other fault codes","Fork A position or drum fault preventing a valid learn","Worn fork, drum groove or detent"],["Odd gears engage late, roughly or not at all","MIL or transmission warning","Learn procedure with scan tool does not complete"],2,3,["P288D","P287C","P2831","P2832","P285B"],"כיול מזלג העברה‏ A — לא בוצע לימוד"],P287C:["Transmission Adaptive Values Not Learned","P287C means the transmission controller finds its trim or adaptation data missing, invalid or unfinished. GM's 2023 Corvette dual-clutch TCM runs the check at initialisation, covering end-of-line and online values such as clutch preload, kiss point, fill volume, rod and parking lock positions, and learn routines left incomplete; the code is Type C, without MIL.",["Replacement TCM installed without trim or learn data","Initial start-up or learn routine not completed","Stored data rejected after a software update","Memory fault inside the control unit"],["Rough or inconsistent shifts after TCM work","Learn or teach-in procedure refused","Transmission warning, often without MIL"],2,2,["P287B","P288D","P0700","P0613"],""],P287D:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump Motor Torque Out Of Range","P287D means the motor of the electric auxiliary transmission pump produces a torque outside its expected band, as estimated by the pump controller from phase current and speed. Too little torque hints at a pump that runs dry or draws air; too much hints at a dragging rotor, cold thick fluid or a blocked passage. No manufacturer documents P287D publicly; the duty to monitor the pump stems from CARB 13 CCR 1968.2.",["Low fluid or air drawn into the auxiliary pump","Dragging pump rotor or blocked suction or delivery path","Worn pump motor or faulty integrated controller","Control software needing an update"],["Start-stop or electric drive no longer available","Harsh engagement after engine restart","MIL on"],3,3,["P2797","P0C2A","P0C28","P0C27","P2796"],"מומנט מנוע משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר — מחוץ לטווח"],P287E:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Circuit/Open","In a parallel hybrid, the engine disconnect clutch (often called K0) sits between the combustion engine and the electric motor and is opened for electric driving. P287E reports that the control module sees no plausible current path through the actuator that operates this clutch, typically a pressure control solenoid in the transmission valve body or an electric actuator.",["Loose, corroded or water-damaged connector at the transmission or actuator","Broken wire in the actuator feed or return line","Open coil in the clutch pressure solenoid or actuator","Failed output stage in the transmission or hybrid control module"],["Malfunction or transmission warning in the instrument cluster","Engine does not start or cannot drive the wheels","Reduced power or limp-home operation"],3,3,["P287F","P2880","P2881","P288C","P2884"],"מפעיל מצמד ניתוק מנוע — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P287F:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Circuit Range/Performance","P287F concerns the actuator of the clutch that couples the engine to the electric motor of a parallel hybrid. The circuit is not broken; instead, the electrical feedback (current, voltage or duty cycle) does not match what the control module expects for its command, or the clutch reacts to the command differently than the model predicts.",["Clutch solenoid or actuator with drifting resistance or sticking spool","Low, aged or contaminated transmission fluid","Lost clutch adaptation values or outdated control software","High contact resistance at connector pins"],["Jerky or delayed engine engagement when switching from electric to hybrid mode","Transmission warning, sometimes only intermittently","Limited hybrid functions or limp-home operation"],3,3,["P287E","P2880","P2881","P2885"],"מפעיל מצמד ניתוק מנוע — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2880:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Circuit Low","P2880 is stored when the signal in the actuator circuit of the engine disconnect clutch stays below its permitted window. In practice this usually means a short to ground on the control side, or a feed that has lost supply voltage, so that the solenoid or actuator is either energised permanently or not at all, depending on which side is affected. The control module normally switches the output off to protect itself.",["Chafed control wire shorted to ground or housing","Missing supply voltage (fuse, relay, feed wire)","Internal short in the clutch solenoid coil","Faulty output stage in the control module"],["Hybrid or transmission warning lamp","Engine cannot be coupled, only electric driving available","Limp-home mode after the output is switched off"],3,3,["P287E","P2881","P288C"],"מפעיל מצמד ניתוק מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2881:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Circuit High","P2881 is the counterpart to P2880: the monitored signal in the circuit of the disconnect clutch actuator is above the upper limit. A control line touching battery voltage is the textbook case; an open return line or a missing ground at a low-side driver can produce the same reading, because the module then sees full voltage where it expects a pulled-down level. The clutch can no longer be commanded precisely.",["Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Open return line or missing ground on the actuator","Moisture bridging pins in the transmission connector","Faulty voltage sensing in the control module"],["Warning lamp with hybrid system message","Harsh or missing engine engagement","Limited driving mode"],3,3,["P287E","P2880","P288C"],"מפעיל מצמד ניתוק מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2882:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Excessive Slippage","P2882 means the clutch between combustion engine and electric motor slips more than allowed while it is supposed to be closed: the speed on the engine side and the speed on the motor side drift apart. Audi documents this code (P288200, symptom 20954) for the Q5 e quattro of 2020–2024 and the A7 e quattro of 2021–2022; the driver sees a gearbox fault message, and the code is stored in the engine control module.",["Transmission or electric drive software with faulty slip evaluation","Low transmission fluid level reducing clutch pressure","Clutch touch point not or wrongly adapted","Worn clutch plates or leaking hydraulic seal"],["Gearbox malfunction message in the cluster","Engine revs flare while torque on the wheels lags behind","Hybrid mode limited, more electric-only operation"],4,3,["P2883","P2884","P2885","P2871"],""],P2883:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Temperature Too High","P2883 protects the disconnect clutch from overheating. Most systems do not measure the friction plates directly; the control module models their temperature from slip speed, transmitted torque and fluid temperature, and sets the code when the estimate passes its limit. Long creeping, repeated engine starts under load, towing on steep grades or a clutch that slips for other reasons push the value up.",["Heavy load such as towing, creeping or stop-and-go on grades","Clutch slipping due to low pressure or wear","Restricted transmission fluid cooling or low fluid level","Temperature model in the control software too conservative"],["Warning to let the transmission cool down","Reduced power or restricted starting off","Smell of hot fluid after heavy use"],2,2,["P2882","P2885","P288C"],"טמפרטורת מצמד ניתוק מנוע — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2884:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Stuck Open","P2884 reports that the disconnect clutch stays open although the control module has asked it to close, so the running engine cannot pass torque to the transmission. Audi documented the code (P288400, held in the gearbox module J217) on the 2016–2017 A3 e-tron: a gearbox warning and limp-home mode, traced to a mechanically defective pressure valve of clutch 0;",["Faulty clutch pressure regulating valve in the mechatronic unit","Insufficient hydraulic pressure (fluid level, pump, leak)","Control software needing an update","Mechanical damage in the clutch pack or piston"],["Gearbox warning or wrench indicator","Engine runs but does not drive the vehicle","Limp-home or electric-only driving"],4,3,["P2885","P2886","P2882","P287E"],"מצמד ניתוק מנוע — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2885:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Engagement Fault","P2885 is the more general engagement code: the clutch does close, but the process does not run as planned – it takes too long, synchronisation of engine and motor speed fails, or torque arrives with a jolt. It does not claim that the clutch is permanently open or closed; those cases have P2884 and P2886.",["Outdated software in hybrid, transmission or engine control module","Weak hydraulic supply, e.g. auxiliary pump or low fluid","Clutch fill and touch point adaptation out of range","Faulty speed signal on engine or motor side"],["Jolt or hesitation when the engine is coupled in","MIL or wrench indicator","Hybrid mode restricted"],4,3,["P2884","P2886","P2882","P0810"],""],P2886:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Stuck Closed","P2886 is the opposite failure to P2884: the control module commands the disconnect clutch to open, yet engine and electric motor keep turning together. The engine is then dragged along during electric driving, which costs range and can stall it when the vehicle stops.",["Clutch control valve stuck in the apply position","Residual pressure from a blocked drain or faulty pump control","Overheated, welded clutch plates","Control software misjudging the clutch state"],["Engine turns during electric driving or stalls when stopping","Reduced electric range","Warning lamp and restricted hybrid mode"],4,3,["P2884","P2885","P2872"],"מצמד ניתוק מנוע — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2887:["Park Lock/Pawl Actuator Circuit","P2887 is the general circuit code for the actuator that engages and releases the park lock in park-by-wire transmissions. It covers faults that are not specifically open, low or high, and some manufacturers use it as a base code that carries a failure-type byte.",["Control software misjudging the actuator circuit","Loose, corroded or damaged actuator connector or harness","Park lock actuator or hold solenoid sticking or failed"],["Transmission service message or warning lamp","P cannot be selected or released reliably"],4,3,["P2888","P2889","P288A","P288B","P07E4","P07E6"],""],P2888:["Park Lock/Pawl Actuator Circuit/Open","P2888 flags an open circuit in the park lock actuator path: the output stage switches on but finds no load. Ford's 2024-25 OBD summary maps it, alongside P2887_13, for the 8F24, 8F35/8F40 and 8F57 front-drive automatics, and in the TR9070 dual-clutch gearbox as an open load on the parking lock hold solenoid, where it can also be reported as P2887_01.",["Broken wire or backed-out terminal at the actuator connector","Open coil in the park lock actuator or hold solenoid","Output stage in the control unit not switching"],["Vehicle stays in P or will not accept a gear","Shift system warning"],3,3,["P2887","P2889","P288A","P288B","P2824"],""],P2889:["Park Lock/Pawl Actuator Circuit Low","P2889 reports that the park lock actuator circuit sits lower than it should, as a rule because the line touches ground. Ford's 2024-25 summary pairs it with P2887_11, a short to ground, on the 8F24, 8F35/8F40 and 8F57 automatics; for the TR9070 dual-clutch unit it is called a shorted switch on the parking lock hold solenoid, meaning the switching side of the stage is pulled to ground.",["Harness chafed through and shorted to ground","Moisture or corrosion in the actuator connector","Actuator coil shorted to its housing"],["Park lock function blocked, warning shown","Difficulty selecting or leaving P"],3,3,["P2887","P2888","P288A","P288B","P2826"],""],P288A:["Park Lock/Pawl Actuator Circuit High","P288A is set when the park lock actuator circuit reads higher than allowed, typically because it has contact with battery voltage or the load itself is shorted. Ford's 2024-25 summary books it as P2887_12, short to power, on Ford's three transverse 8-speed automatics (8F24, 8F35/8F40, 8F57);",["Control line shorted to a battery-voltage feed","Shorted turns in the actuator or hold solenoid coil","Faulty earlier harness repair"],["Shift system warning, park lock function switched off","Car stays in its last position, P or drive range"],3,3,["P2887","P2888","P2889","P288B","P2827"],""],P288B:["Park Lock/Pawl Actuator Circuit Performance","P288B means the park lock actuator is electrically intact but does not do what it is told, for example the lock fails to move in time. Ford's 2024-25 summary calls it functionally stuck off on its front-drive 8-speeds and mechanically stuck off on the TR9070 dual-clutch box.",["Control software needing an update (Ford, Nissan, Audi, FCA)","Sluggish or sticking park lock actuator or pawl mechanism","Low supply voltage or poor connection under load"],["P cannot be selected or needs several attempts to leave","Unexpected shift to P during start-stop","Warning lamp or MIL"],2,3,["P2887","P2888","P2889","P288A","P07E4","P07B5"],""],P288C:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P288C does not look at the clutch itself but at the electronic switch inside the control module that powers its actuator. Modern driver chips measure their own current and junction temperature; if either exceeds the limit, they shut down and report this condition.",["Actuator coil or motor drawing excessive current","Partial short in the actuator wiring","Control module overheating from heat or poor cooling","Defective driver chip in the control module"],["Clutch actuator switched off, engine cannot be coupled","Warning lamp, often after long or hot drives","Limp-home operation"],3,3,["P287E","P2880","P2881","P2883"],"מפעיל מצמד ניתוק מנוע — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה"],P288D:["Shift Fork B Calibration Not Learned","P288D is the fork B counterpart of P287B: the stored learn values that tell the control unit where fork B or its drum sits in each gear are missing or rejected. No manufacturer documents P288D publicly, and Ford's 2014 catalogue still knew only one fork calibration code, P287B, which suggests the split into A and B came later.",["Fork learn not carried out after TCM or mechatronic work","Drum B position or motor fault aborting the learn","Worn or bent fork B, worn drum groove"],["Reverse or even gears hesitant or unavailable","Transmission warning, possibly MIL"],2,3,["P287B","P287C","P2836","P2837","P285F"],"כיול מזלג העברה‏ B — לא בוצע לימוד"],P288E:["Shift Fork A Actuator Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P288E is a self-protection code of the output stage that powers the actuator of shift fork A. The driver reports a current above its limit or an excessive chip temperature, and the module throttles or switches off that actuator. No manufacturer documents P288E publicly.",["Shorted winding or lead in the fork A actuator circuit","Binding drum or fork stalling the actuator under full current","High transmission temperature adding heat to the driver","Defective driver stage in the control unit"],["Odd gears do not engage, car may start in 2nd","Transmission warning and limp mode"],4,3,["P288F","P285B","P285D","P285E","P2831","P288C"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ A — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה"],P288F:["Shift Fork B Actuator Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P288F tells that the driver for the shift fork B actuator has crossed its current or temperature limit, after which the TCM curbs or stops the actuator to save the electronics. Public manufacturer criteria for P288F are not available.",["Short in the fork B actuator motor or its lead","Seized drum B or fork worn into its groove","Excessive fluid or ambient temperature","Driver stage in the TCM failing"],["Reverse not available, even gears skipped","Warning lamp and limp mode"],4,3,["P288E","P285F","P2861","P2862","P2836","P288C"],"מפעיל מזלג העברה‏ B — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה"],P2890:["Cylinder 1 Ion Current Sense Circuit","Some engines use the spark plug as a combustion sensor: between sparks a measuring voltage is applied, and the hot, ionised gas lets a small current flow whose shape reveals misfire and knock. P2890 is the basic circuit fault for this measurement on cylinder 1 – the module receives no usable ion signal from that cylinder at all.",["Ignition coil of cylinder 1 with failed ion measuring stage","Open ion signal wire or connector between coil 1 and the processing module","Faulty ion processing module or engine control module input"],["MIL with reduced knock and misfire monitoring on cylinder 1","Longer cranking if cylinder identification is affected","Retarded ignition and less power as a precaution"],2,3,["P2891","P2892","P2893","P2894","P0301","P0325"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 1 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P2891:["Cylinder 1 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","Here the ion signal of cylinder 1 is present but implausible: its level or waveform does not fit engine speed and load, or it differs clearly from the other cylinders. Fouled or worn spark plugs are a frequent reason, since soot or oil deposits form a leakage path that distorts the small measuring current; a cracked insulator or water in the plug well has a similar effect.",["Sooted, oil-fouled or worn spark plug in cylinder 1","Moisture or oil in the plug well of cylinder 1","Ion measuring stage of coil 1 drifting","Real combustion fault in cylinder 1 (mixture, compression)"],["MIL, sometimes together with misfire codes","Rough idle or hesitation","Reduced power due to cautious knock control"],1,1,["P2890","P2892","P2893","P2895","P0301"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 1 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P2892:["Cylinder 1 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P2892 says the ion measurement of cylinder 1 delivers a signal that stays below the expected range. Electrically this points to a signal line shorted to ground or a measuring stage that no longer builds up its bias voltage; Saab, for example, applies around 120 V across the plug gap between sparks to obtain the current. A heavily fouled plug can also drag the level down by bleeding off the measuring voltage.",["Ion signal wire of cylinder 1 shorted to ground","Coil 1 no longer generates its measuring voltage","Spark plug of cylinder 1 with leakage path through deposits"],["MIL and stored fault for cylinder 1","Noticeably less power from retarded ignition","Possibly unreported misfires on cylinder 1"],2,3,["P2890","P2891","P2893","P2896"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 1 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P2893:["Cylinder 1 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","With P2893 the ion signal from cylinder 1 sits above its plausible ceiling. A signal line touching a supply voltage is the most direct explanation; crosstalk from the ignition primary circuit or a defective evaluation stage that saturates can show the same picture.",["Ion signal wire of cylinder 1 shorted to a voltage source","Internal fault in coil 1 coupling ignition voltage into the signal","Saturated input in the ion processing module"],["MIL with cylinder 1 ion fault","Reduced power and possibly higher fuel consumption","Knock may go unnoticed on cylinder 1"],2,3,["P2890","P2891","P2892","P2897"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 1 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P2894:["Cylinder 2 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P2894 covers a general fault in the ion current circuit of cylinder 2: the processing electronics get no evaluable signal from this plug. Which physical position cylinder 2 occupies depends on the maker's numbering. On Saab's Trionic four-cylinder, cylinders 2 and 3 are fired together by waste spark during start-up, and only the ion signals tell the engine management which of the two actually burned;",["Ignition coil of cylinder 2 with dead ion measurement","Interrupted ion signal path from coil 2","Defective cylinder 2 input in the processing module"],["MIL with a stored cylinder 2 ion fault","Hard or longer starting in some cases","Cautious ignition timing and slightly less power"],2,3,["P2895","P2896","P2897","P2890","P0302","P0325"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 2 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P2895:["Cylinder 2 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P2895 is set when cylinder 2 delivers an ion signal that is electrically intact but does not behave plausibly – for example, it shows almost no combustion peak at normal load, or it scatters strongly from cycle to cycle compared with the neighbouring cylinders.",["Worn or fouled spark plug in cylinder 2","Combustion fault in cylinder 2 (injector, valve, compression)","Coil 2 measuring stage drifting with temperature"],["MIL, sometimes with misfire code P0302","Uneven running felt mainly at idle","Increased fuel consumption"],1,1,["P2894","P2896","P2897","P2891","P0302"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 2 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P2896:["Cylinder 2 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P2896 reports a cylinder 2 ion signal that remains under its lower limit. A ground short on the line from coil 2, a cracked plug insulator that drains the measuring voltage to the cylinder head, or a coil whose bias generator has failed can all produce a near-zero reading.",["Chafed ion signal wire of cylinder 2 touching ground","Cracked spark plug insulator in cylinder 2","Measuring voltage generator in coil 2 failed"],["MIL with ion fault on cylinder 2","Engine runs on a safe ignition map with less power","Misfire on cylinder 2 may not be detected"],2,3,["P2894","P2895","P2897","P2892"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 2 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P2897:["Cylinder 2 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P2897 applies when the ion current reading of cylinder 2 is stuck above the range the module accepts. Typical electrical reasons are a signal line that has contacted a supply or ignition feed, a damaged coil 2 that leaks primary voltage into its measuring output, or a missing ground at the coil that shifts the reference.",["Ion signal wire of cylinder 2 in contact with a voltage source","Coil 2 leaking primary voltage into the measuring output","Poor ground connection at coil 2"],["MIL and stored cylinder 2 ion fault","Less power due to retarded timing on cylinder 2","Knock protection for cylinder 2 limited"],2,3,["P2894","P2895","P2896","P2893"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 2 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P2898:["Cylinder 3 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P2898 marks a basic circuit failure in the ion current measurement of cylinder 3: the engine computer receives nothing it can evaluate from that spark plug. With ion sensing, the plug doubles as a probe, because a bias voltage across the gap drives a small current through the burning, conductive gas.",["Ignition coil of cylinder 3 whose ion measuring stage has failed","Loose or corroded connector at coil 3 or broken ion signal wire","Faulty cylinder 3 input in the ion processing module or engine module"],["MIL with ion fault stored for cylinder 3","Starting may take longer while cylinder identification is uncertain","Engine runs with cautious ignition timing and somewhat less power"],2,3,["P2899","P289A","P289B","P2894","P289C","P0303"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 3 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P2899:["Cylinder 3 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","With P2899 an ion signal from cylinder 3 does arrive, yet it fails the plausibility check: its amplitude is too weak for the current load, it fluctuates without reason, or it no longer matches the pattern of the remaining cylinders.",["Spark plug of cylinder 3 with deposits or excessive gap wear","Weak combustion in cylinder 3 (lean injector, low compression)","Damaged plug boot or moisture at the coil 3 connection"],["MIL, possibly together with P0303","Slight roughness at idle or under light load","Knock control retards timing more than usual"],1,1,["P2898","P289A","P289B","P2895","P0303"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 3 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P289A:["Cylinder 3 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P289A applies when the ion reading of cylinder 3 stays below the lower plausibility limit. Usually the signal path is pulled to ground somewhere, or the coil no longer supplies the measuring voltage of roughly 80 V that Saab's T7 cassette keeps across each gap between sparks. A cracked insulator or heavy carbon tracking on the plug can drain that voltage as well.",["Ion signal wire of cylinder 3 chafed through to ground","Carbon tracking or cracked insulator on the cylinder 3 plug","Coil 3 no longer builds up its measuring voltage"],["MIL with low ion signal on cylinder 3","Misfire codes or no misfire detection for cylinder 3","Less power because timing is pulled back as a precaution"],2,3,["P2898","P2899","P289B","P2896","P289E"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 3 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P289B:["Cylinder 3 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P289B signals that the ion channel of cylinder 3 sits permanently above its upper limit. A conductor touching battery voltage, a coil that couples ignition energy into its measuring output, or a lost ground reference are the usual electrical reasons.",["Ion signal wire of cylinder 3 shorted to battery or supply voltage","Coil 3 coupling ignition energy into its measuring output","Missing ground reference at coil 3 or the processing module"],["MIL with high ion signal fault on cylinder 3","Knock on cylinder 3 may go undetected, so timing is retarded","Reduced pulling power"],2,3,["P2898","P2899","P289A","P2897","P289F"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 3 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P289C:["Cylinder 4 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P289C stands for a general circuit fault in the ion measurement of cylinder 4, meaning no usable signal reaches the evaluation electronics from that plug. Cylinder 4 has a special role in Saab's Trionic four-cylinders: without a camshaft sensor, the engine fires cylinders 1 and 4 at the same time during start-up and decides from the ion response which of them is on the compression stroke.",["Ion measuring stage in the coil of cylinder 4 failed","Open circuit between coil 4 and the processing module","Cylinder 4 input of the processing module defective"],["MIL with ion fault stored for cylinder 4","Extended cranking because cylinder 1 and 4 cannot be told apart reliably","Conservative ignition timing with reduced power"],2,3,["P289D","P289E","P289F","P2890","P2898","P0304"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 4 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P289D:["Cylinder 4 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P289D is a rationality fault: cylinder 4 supplies an ion trace that is electrically present but not credible, for instance a combustion peak far smaller than the others at equal load, or erratic changes between cycles. Low-pass filtering of this trace gives the combustion information, band-pass filtering the knock content, so a distorted signal degrades both functions for cylinder 4.",["Worn or fouled spark plug in cylinder 4","Oil in the plug well of cylinder 4 from a leaking cover gasket","Mixture or compression problem in cylinder 4"],["MIL, sometimes accompanied by P0304","Noticeable vibration at idle","Fuel consumption rises slightly"],1,1,["P289C","P289E","P289F","P2899","P0304"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 4 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P289E:["Cylinder 4 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P289E means the ion signal of cylinder 4 remains below the range the module expects. A ground fault on the line from coil 4, a plug whose insulator conducts the bias voltage away, or a coil that has stopped generating that voltage are the main suspects. In Saab's T7 four-cylinder cassette, cylinders 3 and 4 share one detector that pulses engine module pin 6;",["Ion signal line of cylinder 4 shorted to ground","Spark plug insulator of cylinder 4 leaking the bias voltage","Bias voltage generation inside coil 4 failed"],["MIL with low ion signal on cylinder 4","Possible start delay or misfire codes","Power reduced by safety timing on cylinder 4"],2,3,["P289C","P289D","P289F","P289A","P2892"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 4 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P289F:["Cylinder 4 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P289F is set when the ion measurement of cylinder 4 is held above its plausible maximum. Electrically, look for a signal conductor in contact with a supply feed, an internally leaking coil 4, or a poor ground that lifts the reference level. On Saab's T7 V6, cylinder 4 is part of bank 2 with cylinders 2 and 6;",["Ion signal conductor of cylinder 4 touching a supply feed","Internal leakage in coil 4 raising the measuring output","Poor ground lifting the reference of the cylinder 4 channel"],["MIL with high ion signal on cylinder 4","Reduced performance from retarded ignition","Knock protection on cylinder 4 weakened"],2,3,["P289C","P289D","P289E","P289B","P2893"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 4 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P28A0:["Cylinder 5 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P28A0 reports that the ion current circuit of cylinder 5 delivers no evaluable signal. A cylinder 5 exists only on engines with five or more cylinders, which narrows the field considerably. The V6 of the Saab 9-5 with Trionic T7 is a documented ion-sensing example: cylinder 5 sits in bank 1 with 1 and 3, is triggered from engine module pin 31, and is fired together with cylinder 2 until synchronisation.",["Coil of cylinder 5 with failed ion measuring circuit","Connector or wire fault between coil 5 and the evaluation electronics","Evaluation input for cylinder 5 defective"],["MIL with ion fault stored for cylinder 5","Misfire monitoring of cylinder 5 restricted","Retarded timing and slightly reduced power"],2,3,["P28A1","P28A2","P28A3","P28A4","P0305"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 5 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P28A1:["Cylinder 5 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P28A1 flags a cylinder 5 ion signal that is electrically intact but implausible in size or shape compared with load, speed and the other cylinders. Ion current rises with chamber pressure and temperature, so a lean or poorly compressing cylinder 5 produces a weak trace exactly like a fouled plug does.",["Fouled or eroded spark plug in cylinder 5","Lean mixture in cylinder 5 from a clogged injector or intake leak","Low compression in cylinder 5"],["MIL, possibly with misfire code P0305","Uneven running under load","Higher fuel consumption"],1,1,["P28A0","P28A2","P28A3","P28A5","P0305"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 5 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P28A2:["Cylinder 5 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P28A2 is stored when the cylinder 5 ion reading stays under its lower threshold. The measurement relies on a constant bias across the plug gap between sparks – about 80 V on Saab's T7 discharge modules – and anything that drains it to ground pulls the reading down: a chafed signal conductor, a cracked plug insulator, or a coil whose bias supply has failed.",["Signal conductor of cylinder 5 chafed against ground","Cracked insulator on the cylinder 5 spark plug","Bias supply of coil 5 failed"],["MIL with low ion signal on cylinder 5","Misfire codes for cylinder 5 may appear","Safety ignition map reduces power"],2,3,["P28A0","P28A1","P28A3","P28A6","P0305"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 5 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P28A3:["Cylinder 5 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P28A3 indicates a cylinder 5 ion signal locked above its permitted ceiling. Contact between the signal path and a voltage source, a coil 5 that injects ignition energy into its output, or a disturbed ground reference can cause it.",["Signal path of cylinder 5 in contact with a voltage source","Coil 5 feeding ignition energy into its measuring output","Disturbed ground reference of the evaluation circuit"],["MIL with high ion signal on cylinder 5","Ignition retarded on cylinder 5, less power","Knock events may not be recognised"],2,3,["P28A0","P28A1","P28A2","P28A7"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 5 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P28A4:["Cylinder 6 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P28A4 is the general circuit code for the ion measurement of cylinder 6: the electronics get no usable signal from that plug. Only engines with six or more cylinders are affected, and among them ion sensing is rare. The V6 of Saab's 9-5 with Trionic T7 used it; there cylinder 6 is in bank 2 with 2 and 4, is triggered from engine module pin 32, and shares its start spark with cylinder 3.",["Ion measuring part of the cylinder 6 coil defective","Open ion signal circuit of cylinder 6 in the harness or connector","Processing input for cylinder 6 failed"],["MIL with ion fault stored for cylinder 6","Reduced misfire and knock monitoring on cylinder 6","Moderate power loss from cautious timing"],2,3,["P28A5","P28A6","P28A7","P28A0","P0306"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 6 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P28A5:["Cylinder 6 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P28A5 points to a cylinder 6 ion signal that exists but makes no sense for the operating point: too little combustion response, a trace that jumps between cycles, or one that departs from the remaining cylinders. Since ionisation follows the actual burn, a misfiring or lean cylinder 6 can trigger it as readily as a worn plug or a wet plug well.",["Spark plug of cylinder 6 worn or sooted","Water or oil in the plug well of cylinder 6","Poor combustion in cylinder 6 (injector, valve, compression)"],["MIL, often together with P0306","Rough running at idle or light throttle","Hesitation under acceleration"],1,1,["P28A4","P28A6","P28A7","P28A1","P0306"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 6 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P28A6:["Cylinder 6 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P28A6 describes an ion reading from cylinder 6 that never leaves the bottom of its range. Between sparks the system keeps a small voltage across the plug, and the hot gas of a normal combustion lets a measurable current pass; if that voltage leaks to ground through a damaged conductor, a cracked ceramic or carbon deposits, or the coil stops supplying it, the reading collapses.",["Damaged ion conductor of cylinder 6 leaking to ground","Cracked ceramic or heavy deposits on the cylinder 6 plug","Coil 6 no longer supplies the measuring voltage"],["MIL with low ion signal on cylinder 6","Misfires on cylinder 6 possibly unrecorded","Engine noticeably weaker on safe timing"],2,3,["P28A4","P28A5","P28A7","P28A2","P0306"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 6 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P28A7:["Cylinder 6 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P28A7 is logged when the ion signal of cylinder 6 is held above the upper limit the module accepts. A conductor in contact with battery voltage, crosstalk from the primary side of coil 6, or an evaluation stage driven into saturation are the typical electrical explanations.",["Ion conductor of cylinder 6 touching battery voltage","Crosstalk from the primary side of coil 6","Evaluation stage for cylinder 6 saturated"],["MIL with high ion signal on cylinder 6","Less power because of late ignition on cylinder 6","Knock on cylinder 6 may not be detected"],2,3,["P28A4","P28A5","P28A6","P28A3"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 6 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P28A8:["Cylinder 7 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P28A8 covers a basic circuit fault in the ion current measurement of cylinder 7, so the module obtains no evaluable signal from that plug. A cylinder 7 only exists on engines with eight or more cylinders, and Saab, the best-known user of ion sensing, applied it to four-cylinder and V6 engines; no maker publicly describes an eight-cylinder version. No manufacturer publicly documents P28A8.",["Coil of cylinder 7 with defective ion measuring function","Broken wire or loose connector in the cylinder 7 ion circuit","Cylinder 7 input of the evaluation electronics faulty"],["MIL with ion fault stored for cylinder 7","Misfire and knock monitoring of cylinder 7 unavailable","Some power loss from protective timing"],2,3,["P28A9","P28AA","P28AB","P28A4","P0307"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 7 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P28A9:["Cylinder 7 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P28A9 means cylinder 7 returns an ion signal that is electrically sound but not believable for the current speed and load, or that stands out against the other cylinders of an eight-or-more-cylinder engine. Because the current through the plug gap grows with combustion pressure and temperature, a lean or misfiring cylinder 7 produces this picture as readily as a fouled plug or moisture in the well.",["Fouled or worn spark plug in cylinder 7","Lean mixture or misfire in cylinder 7","Moisture in the plug well of cylinder 7"],["MIL, possibly together with P0307","Uneven idle","Knock control retards timing more often"],1,1,["P28A8","P28AA","P28AB","P28A5","P0307"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 7 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P28AA:["Cylinder 7 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P28AA reports that the ion current reading from cylinder 7 has dropped below the floor the engine computer accepts. Ion sensing places a measuring voltage on the spark plug between firings; Saab's Trionic T8 coils generate about 120 V for this themselves.",["Carbon track inside the cylinder 7 plug boot","Ion signal lead of cylinder 7 rubbed through to ground","Split ceramic insulator on the cylinder 7 plug","Measuring-voltage stage in coil 7 no longer working"],["MIL lit with a low ion reading stored for cylinder 7","Misfire code P0307 may appear although the engine runs smoothly","Reduced power from protective ignition timing"],2,3,["P28A8","P28A9","P28AB","P28AE","P0307"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 7 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P28AB:["Cylinder 7 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P28AB is set when the cylinder 7 ion signal sits above the highest value a healthy measuring circuit can deliver. Typical triggers are a signal lead touching a supply wire, moisture bridging the coil connector, or a coil whose ignition pulse bleeds into its measuring output. A constant high reading is treacherous for diagnosis because it can look like permanent combustion and so mask real misfire.",["Ion signal lead of cylinder 7 touching a supply wire","Moisture bridging contacts in the coil 7 connector","Coil 7 leaking its ignition pulse into the measuring output"],["MIL lit with a high ion reading stored for cylinder 7","Genuine misfire on cylinder 7 may go unreported","Timing pulled back on cylinder 7, slightly less power"],2,3,["P28A8","P28A9","P28AA","P28AF","P0307"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 7 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P28AC:["Cylinder 8 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P28AC flags a general electrical fault in the ion current path of cylinder 8, typically an open connection, so no usable signal reaches the evaluation electronics. On a V8 this is the highest-numbered cylinder, on V10 and V12 engines a middle one; which bank it sits on depends on the maker's numbering.",["Loose or corroded connector in the cylinder 8 ion line","Measuring stage of coil 8 failed","Broken conductor between coil 8 and the evaluation module","Cylinder 8 input of the evaluation module defective"],["MIL with a circuit fault stored for cylinder 8","No misfire or knock assessment for cylinder 8","Engine may run with conservative timing and lower power"],2,3,["P28AD","P28AE","P28AF","P28A8","P28B0","P0308"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 8 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P28AD:["Cylinder 8 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P28AD means the cylinder 8 ion signal is electrically intact but does not fit what the computer expects for the operating point, or it deviates clearly from the other cylinders. CARB treats such rationality checks as part of the monitoring of input components next to tests for wiring faults and for values outside the valid band.",["Worn electrodes or wrong gap on the cylinder 8 plug","Partly blocked injector on cylinder 8","Oil deposits on the cylinder 8 plug","Low compression in cylinder 8"],["MIL, often together with P0308","Rough running under load","Knock control intervenes more often on cylinder 8"],1,1,["P28AC","P28AE","P28AF","P28A9","P28B1","P0308"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 8 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P28AE:["Cylinder 8 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P28AE stands for an ion reading from cylinder 8 that stays too low or near zero. Either the measuring voltage never reaches the plug, because the coil's bias stage or its supply has failed, or it drains away to ground through a damaged signal wire, a wet plug well or a tracked boot.",["Water or oil in the cylinder 8 plug well","Damaged cylinder 8 signal wire shorted to ground","Bias stage of coil 8 not producing measuring voltage"],["MIL lit with a low ion reading for cylinder 8","Knock protection of cylinder 8 lost, timing retarded","Possible misfire report for cylinder 8"],2,3,["P28AC","P28AD","P28AF","P28AA","P28C1","P0308"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 8 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P28AF:["Cylinder 8 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P28AF is logged when cylinder 8 delivers an ion signal pinned at or above the upper limit. Possible reasons include the signal conductor shorted to battery voltage or to another live circuit in the harness, internal leakage inside coil 8 that lets the high-voltage side couple into the measuring line, or a lost reference ground at the evaluation input.",["Cylinder 8 signal conductor shorted to battery voltage","Internal leakage in coil 8 coupling into the measuring line","Lost reference ground at the evaluation input"],["MIL lit with a high ion reading for cylinder 8","Misfire on cylinder 8 may stay undetected","Safety timing reduces power somewhat"],2,3,["P28AC","P28AD","P28AE","P28AB","P0308"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 8 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P28B0:["Cylinder 9 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P28B0 marks an electrical circuit fault, usually an interruption, in the ion current measurement of cylinder 9. A ninth cylinder appears only on engines with ten or more cylinders, such as V10, V12 or W12 designs. Ion sensing as a production technique is publicly associated with Saab and Mecel, who brought it into series cars with the Trionic systems on four- and six-cylinder engines;",["Coil 9 connector not latched or with spread terminals","Ion output of coil 9 without function","Interrupted ion line of cylinder 9 in the harness"],["MIL with ion circuit fault for cylinder 9","Misfire and knock evaluation of cylinder 9 suspended","Slight loss of power from retarded timing"],2,3,["P28B1","P28B2","P28B3","P28AC","P28B4","P0309"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 9 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P28B1:["Cylinder 9 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P28B1 indicates that cylinder 9 produces an ion signal of believable electrical level whose shape or strength does not match engine speed, load or the neighbouring cylinders. Since the reading reflects combustion pressure and temperature, the root cause is often mechanical or mixture-related: a worn or oil-fouled plug, a leaking valve, a weak injector on cylinder 9, or condensation in the plug well.",["Worn or oil-fouled spark plug in cylinder 9","Weak spray from the cylinder 9 injector","Leaking valve on cylinder 9","Condensation in the cylinder 9 plug well"],["MIL, possibly with misfire code P0309","Noticeably uneven running at idle","Higher fuel consumption"],1,1,["P28B0","P28B2","P28B3","P28AD","P28B5","P0309"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 9 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P28B2:["Cylinder 9 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P28B2 is stored when the ion current measured at cylinder 9 remains under its lower plausibility limit. In an ion-sensing ignition each coil both fires the plug and supplies the measuring voltage, so a coil 9 with a weak bias stage, a cracked plug insulator or a signal wire grounded in the harness all reduce the current reaching the evaluator.",["Cylinder 9 signal wire grounded in the harness","Cracked insulator on the cylinder 9 plug","Coil 9 with weak bias stage"],["MIL with low ion reading on cylinder 9","P0309 often stored at the same time","Reduced power under load"],2,3,["P28B0","P28B1","P28B3","P28AE","P28B6","P0309"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 9 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P28B3:["Cylinder 9 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P28B3 shows that the cylinder 9 ion signal is held above the range a working circuit produces. Shorts from the sense line to a powered conductor, a coil 9 leaking high-voltage energy into its measuring output, or water in the connector can push it there. The fault matters for emissions monitoring, because a signal that always reports strong combustion would let real misfire on cylinder 9 go unnoticed.",["Cylinder 9 sense line shorted to a powered conductor","Coil 9 leaking high-voltage energy into its measuring output","Water in the coil 9 connector"],["MIL with high ion reading on cylinder 9","Real misfire on cylinder 9 can go unnoticed","Timing on cylinder 9 retarded as a precaution"],2,3,["P28B0","P28B1","P28B2","P28AF","P28B7","P0309"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 9 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P28B4:["Cylinder 10 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P28B4 is the basic circuit code for the ion current measurement of cylinder 10; typically the line from coil 10 to the evaluation module is interrupted or the coil's measuring stage is dead. Ten cylinders mean a V10 at minimum, where this is the last cylinder in the numbering, or a V12 or W12, where it is not.",["Open line between coil 10 and the evaluation module","Measuring stage of coil 10 dead","Corroded terminals at the coil 10 connector"],["MIL with ion circuit fault for cylinder 10","Cylinder 10 excluded from misfire and knock evaluation","Possible power reduction through protective timing"],2,3,["P28B5","P28B6","P28B7","P28B0","P28B8","P0310"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 10 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P28B5:["Cylinder 10 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P28B5 reports an ion signal from cylinder 10 that is electrically valid yet implausible: its amplitude or timing after the spark does not fit the load point or departs from the remaining cylinders. Because ionisation depends on how hot and dense the burning charge is, causes include an eroded electrode gap, oil-wetted plugs, mixture errors on cylinder 10 or a compression loss.",["Eroded electrode gap on the cylinder 10 plug","Oil-wetted plug in cylinder 10","Mixture error on cylinder 10","Compression loss in cylinder 10"],["MIL, sometimes together with P0310","Erratic ignition timing on cylinder 10","Hesitation when accelerating"],1,1,["P28B4","P28B6","P28B7","P28B1","P0310"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 10 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P28B6:["Cylinder 10 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P28B6 is set when the cylinder 10 ion reading is persistently too low. The measuring bias that should sit across the gap between sparks is missing or being drained: a coil 10 whose bias generator has failed, conductive deposits bridging the plug insulator, a wet boot, or a sense wire with insulation damage touching ground. Saab's T7 applied 80 V for this purpose, the later T8 about 120 V;",["Conductive deposits bridging the cylinder 10 plug insulator","Cylinder 10 sense wire with damaged insulation touching ground","Bias generator of coil 10 failed","Wet plug boot on cylinder 10"],["MIL with low ion reading on cylinder 10","P0310 may be stored as well","Cautious ignition timing, less pulling power"],2,3,["P28B4","P28B5","P28B7","P28B2","P0310"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 10 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P28B7:["Cylinder 10 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P28B7 means the ion signal of cylinder 10 is stuck above its valid window. The usual suspects are a sense lead shorted to a supply or to a neighbouring ignition circuit, breakdown inside coil 10 that lets spark energy into the measuring path, and a poor ground at the evaluation side that shifts the reference upward.",["Cylinder 10 sense lead shorted to a supply or adjacent ignition circuit","Internal breakdown in coil 10","Poor ground at the evaluation side"],["MIL with high ion reading on cylinder 10","Timing on cylinder 10 retarded for safety","Misfire on cylinder 10 may be masked"],2,3,["P28B4","P28B5","P28B6","P28B3","P28C2","P0310"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 10 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P28B8:["Cylinder 11 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P28B8 is the general circuit code for ion sensing on cylinder 11: the evaluation electronics receive nothing usable from that cylinder, most often because the line from coil 11 is broken or its connector has lost contact. Eleven cylinders only occur on V12 and W12 engines, and none of them with ion sensing is publicly described; no manufacturer documents P28B8.",["Loose, corroded or pushed-back pin in the cylinder 11 coil connector","Broken ion signal wire between coil 11 and the evaluation module","Measuring stage inside coil 11 failed","Cylinder 11 input of the evaluation module damaged"],["MIL on with a circuit fault stored for cylinder 11","Misfire and knock detection for cylinder 11 no longer available","Cautious ignition timing with slightly reduced power"],2,3,["P28B9","P28BA","P28BB","P28BC","P28B4","P0361","P0311"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 11 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P28B9:["Cylinder 11 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P28B9 stands for an ion signal from cylinder 11 whose voltage stays inside the valid band but whose behaviour makes no sense: too weak or too strong for the current speed and load, or out of line with the other eleven cylinders. Such rationality tests belong to the input-component monitoring CARB demands.",["Worn or oil-fouled spark plug on cylinder 11","Cylinder 11 injector delivering too little or spraying poorly","Low compression on cylinder 11 (valve or ring leakage)","Water or oil standing in the plug well of cylinder 11"],["MIL on after the fault is confirmed on a second trip","Slightly rough running, sometimes with misfire code P0311","Unsteady ignition timing on cylinder 11"],1,1,["P28B8","P28BA","P28BB","P28BD","P28B5","P0311"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 11 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P28BA:["Cylinder 11 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P28BA means the cylinder 11 ion reading has fallen below its lower limit. Between sparks a bias voltage sits across the electrodes – 80 V on Saab's T7 – and burning gas lets a current flow that pulls this voltage down in proportion to pressure and temperature.",["Ion signal wire of cylinder 11 chafed and touching ground","Conductive deposits on the cylinder 11 plug insulator","Moisture or a carbon track in the cylinder 11 plug boot","Bias voltage generation in coil 11 failed"],["MIL on with a low ion signal stored for cylinder 11","Misfire code P0311 possible although the engine runs smoothly","Power slightly reduced by conservative timing"],2,3,["P28B8","P28B9","P28BB","P28BE","P28B6","P0311"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 11 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P28BB:["Cylinder 11 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P28BB is stored when the cylinder 11 ion signal remains above the highest value the measuring circuit can legitimately produce. Common reasons are a sense wire shorted to battery voltage or to another ignition circuit, an internal breakdown in coil 11 that couples spark energy into the measuring output, and a missing ground at the evaluator that lifts the whole reference.",["Ion signal wire of cylinder 11 shorted to battery voltage or another ignition circuit","Internal breakdown in coil 11 feeding spark energy into the signal","Poor ground of the evaluation module shifting the reference"],["Stored code for a high ion signal on cylinder 11, lamp behaviour depends on the maker","Real misfire on cylinder 11 may go undetected","Retarded timing on cylinder 11"],2,3,["P28B8","P28B9","P28BA","P28BF","P28C2","P0311"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 11 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P28BC:["Cylinder 12 Ion Current Sense Circuit","P28BC covers a wiring-level failure in the ion measuring path of cylinder 12 that keeps a valid signal from arriving, typically an open wire or a connector without contact. Cylinder 12 is the last one on a V12 or W12; no such engine with ion sensing is publicly known, and no manufacturer documents P28BC.",["Open ion signal wire or connector at coil 12","Ignition trigger for cylinder 12 not reaching the detection module","Measuring stage of coil 12 dead","Cylinder 12 channel of the evaluation module faulty"],["MIL on with a circuit fault stored for cylinder 12","No combustion feedback from cylinder 12","Engine may run with reduced ignition advance"],2,3,["P28BD","P28BE","P28BF","P28B8","P0362","P0312"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 12 — תקלה במעגל החישה"],P28BD:["Cylinder 12 Ion Current Sense Circuit Range/Performance","P28BD reports that cylinder 12 delivers an ion signal of acceptable voltage whose content is not credible – its strength, timing or shape after the spark does not match the operating point or the rest of the engine.",["Eroded or oil-wetted spark plug on cylinder 12","Mixture error on cylinder 12 (injector, intake leak at that port)","Carbon build-up in the cylinder 12 combustion chamber","Reduced compression on cylinder 12"],["MIL on after the fault repeats on a later trip","Occasional roughness, sometimes with P0312","Knock control on cylinder 12 reacts erratically"],1,1,["P28BC","P28BE","P28BF","P28B9","P0312"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 12 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל החישה"],P28BE:["Cylinder 12 Ion Current Sense Circuit Low","P28BE is set when the ion reading of cylinder 12 stays below its minimum. On Saab's Trionic T8 each coil generates its own measuring voltage of about 120 V and keeps it applied to the plug; the module then reads how much current the ionised gas lets through.",["Water or oil in the cylinder 12 plug well draining the measuring voltage","Cracked plug insulator on cylinder 12","Sense lead of cylinder 12 grounded against a bracket or the engine","Coil 12 no longer builds up its measuring voltage"],["MIL on with a low ion signal stored for cylinder 12","Misfire code P0312 without noticeable roughness","Fault often appears after washing the engine or in wet weather"],2,3,["P28BC","P28BD","P28BF","P28BA","P0312"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 12 — אות נמוך במעגל החישה"],P28BF:["Cylinder 12 Ion Current Sense Circuit High","P28BF signals that the cylinder 12 ion input sits above its permitted window. A sense wire touching a powered conductor, moisture bridging pins in the coil 12 connector or spark energy escaping inside the coil can all push it there.",["Sense wire of cylinder 12 touching a powered conductor","Moisture bridging pins in the coil 12 connector","Internal flashover in coil 12 reaching the measuring path"],["Stored high ion signal code for cylinder 12, MIL depending on the maker","Noticeably less power from heavy timing retard","Higher fuel consumption from protective enrichment"],2,3,["P28BC","P28BD","P28BE","P28BB","P28C2","P0312"],"זרם יונים צילינדר‏ 12 — אות גבוה במעגל החישה"],P28C0:["Ion Sense Module Supply Voltage Circuit","P28C0 points to a fault in the power feed of the module that conditions ion signals – typically an open fuse, relay contact or wire, so the module is not powered at all. On Saab's Trionic T8 that module receives battery voltage via the main relay and its ground from a body point, and on the older T7 the ignition cassette took the same route.",["Blown fuse in the ion sense module feed","Main relay not switching through or burnt contact","Open supply wire or loose ground point of the module","Internal fault in the module's power stage"],["Engine cranks but does not start, or cuts out while driving","Ion-based misfire and knock detection lost on all cylinders","Warning lamp behaviour depends on the manufacturer"],2,3,["P28C1","P28C2","P0685","P0560"],""],P28C1:["Ion Sense Module Supply Voltage Low","P28C1 means the ion sense module is powered, but its supply sits below the level it needs to work reliably. That matters because such modules turn 12 V into far higher voltages: Saab's T7 cassette converted battery voltage to 400 V DC stored in a capacitor and also kept 80 V across each plug for measuring.",["Weak or deeply discharged battery","Voltage drop across a corroded main relay contact or connector","High-resistance ground point of the module","Alternator charging too little"],["Hard starting, especially when cold or with a weak battery","Misfire codes on several cylinders at once","Stored supply-voltage code, often together with system voltage codes"],1,3,["P28C0","P28C2","P0562","P0560"],""],P28C2:["Ion Sense Module Supply Voltage High","P28C2 is stored when the voltage feeding the ion sense module exceeds its upper limit. Since the module derives its measuring and, in cassette designs, its ignition voltages from this feed, an excessive input can raise the bias across the plugs, push signals toward the top of their range and stress the converter inside.",["Alternator voltage regulator letting the system voltage rise too high","Jump start or charger with excessive voltage (e.g. 24 V)","Poor module ground distorting the voltage reading","Faulty voltage measurement inside the module"],["Stored overvoltage code, often together with P0563","Flickering or unusually bright lamps, battery gassing","Erratic misfire or knock reports on several cylinders"],2,3,["P28C0","P28C1","P0563","P0560"],""],P28C3:["EVAP System High Load Purge Line B Performance","Under boost the intake manifold is above ambient pressure, so turbo engines add a high-load purge path: compressed air drives an ejector (venturi) that draws canister vapour into the compressor inlet, with check valves keeping boost out of the tank side.",["Check valve in high-load line B sticking, leaking or fitted the wrong way round","Line B to the compressor inlet pulled off, cracked or kinked","Ejector nozzle blocked by debris or oil residue","Leak in the boost-side hose that drives the ejector"],["MIL on, usually without any change in driving behaviour","EVAP readiness not completed","Occasional fuel smell after long full-load driving"],2,1,["P04F0","P04F1","P04AF","P0496","P0497"],""],P28C4:["Clutch A Motor Phase U-V-W Circuit Low","P28C4 means the transmission controller finds the voltage too low on a phase lead (U, V or W) of the electric motor that operates clutch A. This layout belongs to wet dual-clutch gearboxes without a valve block, such as the Getrag/Magna 7DCT300 and its hybrid derivative 7HDT300: a brushless motor per clutch spins a gerotor pump that feeds oil directly to the clutch piston.",["Phase wire to the clutch A motor chafed through and touching ground","Winding inside the clutch A motor shorted to the housing","Defective output transistor for the motor phases in the transmission controller"],["Transmission warning lamp, often together with the MIL","Odd or even gears locked out, depending on which shaft clutch A serves","Jerky or delayed pull-away"],3,3,["P28C5","P28C6","P28C7","P28D1","P28D2"],"פאזת מנוע מצמד‏ A U-V-W — אות נמוך במעגל"],P28C5:["Clutch A Motor Phase U-V-W Circuit High","With P28C5 the controller finds one or more phases of the clutch A motor sitting higher than the switching pattern allows, as if a lead were tied to battery voltage. The motor in question is the brushless drive of an on-demand pump actuator: Getrag introduced this concept with the 7DCT300, where one motor per clutch turns a gerotor pump and the pump pressure itself closes the clutch.",["Motor phase lead shorted to a supply line in the harness","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins at the actuator connector","High-side switch in the controller that no longer turns off"],["Warning lamp for the transmission and stored DTC","Half of the gear set unavailable, vehicle continues with reduced choice","Clutch A may not open or close on command"],3,3,["P28C4","P28C6","P28C7","P28D3"],"פאזת מנוע מצמד‏ A U-V-W — אות גבוה במעגל"],P28C6:["Clutch A Motor Phase U-V-W Circuit/Open","P28C6 is the general circuit code for the three-phase supply of the clutch A motor and is set above all when a phase carries no current although the controller drives it, i.e. an open line. A brushless motor needs all three windings to produce torque; with one missing it stalls or runs roughly, and the gerotor pump behind it can no longer build the oil pressure that engages clutch A.",["Terminal pushed back or loose in the clutch A motor connector","Cracked solder joint or winding connection inside the actuator","Phase wire broken at a bend or bracket"],["Clutch A does not engage, affected gears unavailable","Transmission warning and possibly MIL","Fault may come and go with vibration or temperature"],3,3,["P28C4","P28C5","P28C7","P28D4"],"פאזת מנוע מצמד‏ A U-V-W — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P28C7:["Clutch A Motor Phase U-V-W Performance","P28C7 flags that the clutch A motor's phases are electrically intact but the motor does not respond as expected, e.g. currents and rotation do not match the commanded drive. Stellantis documents it in bulletin 21-040-26 (May 2026) for European 2022-2025 Jeep Renegade and Compass with the 1.5 MHEV engine and the 7HDT300 hybrid dual-clutch gearbox: together with P2787 it points to the actuator cylinder of the odd-gear…",["Debris from the transmission jamming the pump in the clutch A actuator (Stellantis 7HDT300)","Worn or sluggish clutch A actuator motor","Increased resistance in a phase connection causing unbalanced currents"],["MIL and transmission warning lamp on","Odd gears unavailable on the 7HDT300","Often stored together with clutch A temperature code P2787"],3,3,["P28C4","P28C5","P28C6","P28C8","P2787","P28D5"],"פאזת מנוע מצמד‏ A U-V-W — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P28C8:["Clutch A Pump Motor Performance","P28C8 concerns the motor-and-pump unit of clutch A as a whole: the controller sees that the delivered result, typically the clutch pressure reported by the sensor or the motor effort needed to reach it, does not fit the command. In on-demand designs the gerotor pump is connected straight to the clutch cylinder, so pressure follows pump speed directly;",["Clutch A pump obstructed by abrasion particles","Internal leakage at the clutch A piston or pressure line seals","Worn gerotor set reducing delivery","Low transmission fluid level so the pump draws air"],["Slipping or delayed engagement of clutch A","Transmission warning, gears on clutch A may be locked out","Audible whine from the actuator under load"],3,3,["P28C7","P28C9","P28CA","P2855","P2857","P28D7"],"מנוע משאבת מצמד‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P28C9:["Clutch A Motor Overspeed","P28C9 is stored when the clutch A motor turns faster than the controller considers plausible for the pressure it is asked to hold. Because the pump in such actuators delivers oil straight into the closed clutch circuit, the motor should slow down once pressure is reached; if it keeps racing, the oil is escaping or the pump is not loaded.",["Oil escaping from the clutch A pressure circuit, e.g. worn piston seal","Pump drawing air because of low fluid level or clogged suction filter","Broken drive between motor shaft and gerotor rotor","Faulty motor position signal reporting too high a speed"],["Clutch A slips or fails to transmit full torque","Transmission warning and restricted gear choice"],3,3,["P28CA","P28C8","P28CB","P28CC","P28D8"],"מנוע מצמד‏ A — מהירות יתר"],P28CA:["Clutch A Motor Underspeed","P28CA means the clutch A motor stays below the speed the controller commands, so the pump cannot deliver oil fast enough to build or modulate clutch pressure. Mechanical drag is the usual culprit: particles wedged in the gerotor, a seized bearing, or very thick oil in deep cold. Stellantis reports debris blocking an actuator pump on the 7HDT300 (bulletin 21-040-26), though it lists P28C7 rather than this code.",["Particles jamming the gerotor pump of clutch A","Stiff or seized motor/pump bearing","Low supply voltage to the actuator or poor ground"],["Clutch A engages late or with a jolt","Transmission warning, especially after cold start","Affected gears may be withheld"],3,3,["P28C9","P28C8","P28D1","P28CC","P28D9"],"מנוע מצמד‏ A — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P28CB:["Clutch A Motor Position Sensor Circuit/Open","A brushless motor can only be commutated correctly if the electronics know where the rotor stands; P28CB reports that the signal from the sensor tracking the clutch A motor's rotor position is missing or electrically unusable, mostly through an open line. Without it the controller cannot switch the U-V-W phases in the right order or count motor revolutions, so the pump of clutch A is shut down.",["Open signal, supply or ground wire of the clutch A motor position sensor","Corroded or loose pin at the actuator connector","Failed position sensor inside the actuator"],["Clutch A disabled, gears on that shaft unavailable","Transmission warning lamp","Possibly also motor speed codes stored"],3,3,["P28CC","P28C9","P28CA","P28DA"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מצמד‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P28CC:["Clutch A Motor Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P28CC is the plausibility counterpart to P28CB: the position signal of the clutch A motor arrives, but its values or their sequence make no sense, for example jumps between rotor angles, a missing step in the pattern, or a speed that contradicts the phase currents. CARB expects rationality checks of this kind for input components where feasible.",["Partly broken wire or loose contact causing signal dropouts","Electrical interference on the position signal through a damaged shield","Loose sensor, shifted magnet or contaminated sensor target"],["Clutch A engages roughly or intermittently","Transmission warning, sometimes only while driving","Gear changes on one shaft delayed or withheld"],3,3,["P28CB","P28C9","P28CA","P28DB"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מצמד‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P28CD:["Clutch A Pressure Sensor Circuit/Open","P28CD concerns the pressure sensor that tells the transmission controller how much oil pressure acts on clutch A. In pump-actuated wet DCTs there is no proportional valve to set pressure; instead Getrag places a pressure sensor downstream of the clutch pumps and closes the control loop over motor speed.",["Open signal, 5-volt supply or ground wire of the clutch A pressure sensor","Sensor connector not fully latched or pin pushed out","Internal open in the pressure sensor"],["Clutch A shut off, half of the gears unavailable","Transmission warning lamp and stored code"],3,3,["P28CE","P28CF","P28D0","P28DC"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד‏ A — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P28CE:["Clutch A Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P28CE is logged when the clutch A pressure sensor output drops below the lowest voltage a working sensor can produce. Ratiometric pressure sensors are usually designed so that even zero pressure gives a small offset voltage; a reading underneath that band therefore means an electrical fault, not low pressure.",["Pressure sensor signal wire shorted to ground","5-volt reference pulled down by another sensor on the same supply","Internally shorted clutch A pressure sensor"],["Clutch A disabled with transmission warning","Other sensor codes may be stored at the same time","Reduced choice of gears"],3,3,["P28CD","P28CF","P28D0","P28DD"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P28CF:["Clutch A Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P28CF means the voltage from the clutch A pressure sensor climbs above the band a plausible measurement can reach, usually close to the reference or battery voltage. An open ground line is a frequent trigger, because many sensor circuits then float up to the supply level; a signal wire touching the 5-volt or 12-volt feed, or a sensor with a broken internal element, has the same effect.",["Open ground wire of the clutch A pressure sensor","Signal wire shorted to the 5-volt reference or battery voltage","Pressure sensor failed with output stuck high"],["Transmission warning, clutch A taken out of service","Pull-away or shifts only on the other clutch"],3,3,["P28CD","P28CE","P28D0","P28DE"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P28D0:["Clutch A Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P28D0 is the rationality fault of the clutch A pressure sensor: its voltage lies inside the valid window, but the indicated pressure does not match what the system should be producing. In a pump actuator the controller can cross-check this well, because pressure in the clutch circuit rises with pump motor speed and current; an EVS32 paper describes how directly the gerotor flow translates into clutch pressure.",["Clutch A pressure sensor drifting or sticking","Real pressure deviation from leakage or weak pump, misread as a sensor fault","Contact resistance in the signal path shifting the reading"],["Harsh or slipping engagement of clutch A","Transmission warning, possibly after some time driving","Gears on clutch A may be withheld"],3,3,["P28CD","P28CE","P28CF","P28C8","P2857","P28DF"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P28D1:["Clutch A Motor Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P28D1 is set when the power stage that drives the clutch A motor exceeds its current limit or its internal temperature limit. This output stage, usually part of the transmission controller or the actuator electronics, protects itself by shutting down or derating, after which clutch A can no longer be operated normally.",["Clutch A motor or pump hard to turn, e.g. jammed by particles","Long periods of high clutch pressure demand in stop-and-go or on gradients","Shorted motor winding drawing excess current"],["Transmission warning after heavy use, may clear after cooling down","Clutch A temporarily disabled","Possibly stored together with clutch temperature code P2787"],3,3,["P28C4","P28C7","P28CA","P2787","P28D6"],"מנוע מצמד‏ A — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר"],P28D2:["Clutch B Motor Phase U-V-W Circuit Low","P28D2 reports that on the U, V or W lead feeding the electric drive of clutch B a voltage below its expected level is measured, pointing to a short towards ground. Such motor-driven clutches are found in wet dual-clutch units of the Getrag/Magna pump-actuator family; the 7DCT300 went into series in 2015 with the Renault Espace, and the hybrid 7HDT300 uses the same principle.",["Insulation of a clutch B motor phase rubbed through against ground","Water or corrosion in the clutch B actuator plug pulling a phase low","Failed low-side transistor of the clutch B motor driver"],["Transmission warning light, MIL possible","Gears on the clutch B shaft unavailable (even gears on the 7HDT300)","Harsh or hesitant gear changes"],3,3,["P28D3","P28D4","P28D5","P28D6","P28C4"],"פאזת מנוע מצמד‏ B U-V-W — אות נמוך במעגל"],P28D3:["Clutch B Motor Phase U-V-W Circuit High","P28D3 is the high-voltage fault on the phase wiring of the clutch B motor: a lead reads above what the inverter pattern should produce, typically because it contacts a positive feed or the upper switch cannot turn off.",["Clutch B motor phase touching a neighbouring positive feed in the harness","Corroded pins bridging at the clutch B motor connector","Upper output switch for the clutch B motor stays conducting"],["Warning lamp and stored fault code","Vehicle drives on with only one clutch, gear choice reduced","Possible jerk when the controller drops clutch B"],3,3,["P28D2","P28D4","P28D5","P28C5"],"פאזת מנוע מצמד‏ B U-V-W — אות גבוה במעגל"],P28D4:["Clutch B Motor Phase U-V-W Circuit/Open","P28D4 covers the circuit of the three motor phases for clutch B in general and is mainly logged when the controller energises a phase and no current returns, meaning the path is broken. Getrag chose brushless ferrite motors without rare earths for this pump-actuator generation and reused them from the 6DCT250;",["Loose or spread crimp terminal on a clutch B motor phase","Phase wire fractured close to the clutch B actuator","Internal winding joint in the clutch B motor cracked by thermal cycling"],["Clutch B cannot be closed, its gears are blocked","Fault may appear only on rough roads or when hot","Transmission warning, MIL depending on make"],3,3,["P28D2","P28D3","P28D5","P28C6"],"פאזת מנוע מצמד‏ B U-V-W — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P28D5:["Clutch B Motor Phase U-V-W Performance","P28D5 means the clutch B motor wiring passes the electrical checks, yet the motor's behaviour, its phase currents and resulting rotation, does not follow what the controller demands. It is one of the few codes in this group with a public manufacturer reference: Stellantis bulletin 21-040-26 (May 2026), valid for Jeep Renegade and Compass of model years 2022-2025 sold in Europe with the 1.5 MHEV and the 7HDT300…",["Particles from the gearbox jamming a pump in the even-gear actuator (Stellantis 7HDT300)","Clutch B actuator motor running stiff or weak","Raised contact resistance on one phase causing uneven currents"],["MIL on, transmission warning shown","Even gears not available on the 7HDT300","Often logged together with clutch B temperature code P27F3"],3,3,["P28D2","P28D3","P28D4","P28D7","P27F3","P28C7"],"פאזת מנוע מצמד‏ B U-V-W — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P28D6:["Clutch B Motor Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P28D6 tells that the electronic switch stage powering the clutch B motor has hit its overcurrent or overtemperature protection. Normally these pump actuators draw very little; Getrag quotes roughly 31 W (NEDC) and 33 W (WLTC) for the complete 7DCT300 actuation, so a stage running into its limits indicates the motor is working against unusual resistance or a fault in the stage itself.",["Clutch B pump seized by particles, motor stalls and draws excess current","Turn-to-turn short in the clutch B motor winding","Prolonged high pressure demand with hot clutch, e.g. stop-and-go or towing","Defective output stage or poor heat transfer in the controller"],["Clutch B shut down temporarily, may recover after cooling","Transmission warning and restricted gears","May appear together with P27F3 or P28D5"],3,3,["P28D2","P28D5","P28D9","P27F3","P28D1"],"מנוע מצמד‏ B — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר"],P28D7:["Clutch B Pump Motor Performance","P28D7 judges motor and pump of clutch B as one unit: the oil pressure seen by the sensor, or the speed and current the motor needs for it, does not match the target. Getrag's hydraulic plan for the 7DCT300 has both clutch pumps drawing through a common suction filter, with a pressure sensor downstream of both pumps providing feedback.",["Clogged common suction filter, especially if P28C8 is stored too","Leaking seals in the clutch B pressure circuit","Worn or contaminated gerotor set of the clutch B pump","Transmission fluid level too low"],["Clutch B slips or engages late","Transmission warning, gears on clutch B possibly locked out","Unusual humming from the actuator area"],3,3,["P28D5","P28D8","P28D9","P28DF","P2858","P285A","P28C8"],"מנוע משאבת מצמד‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P28D8:["Clutch B Motor Overspeed","P28D8 sets when the clutch B motor spins faster than the controller expects for the commanded pressure. A gerotor works by positive displacement, the EVS32 model uses one with a seven-tooth outer rotor, so in a sealed clutch circuit its speed should fall once pressure is built; a motor that keeps accelerating means oil is escaping or the pump has lost its load.",["Worn piston or rotary feedthrough seal letting oil escape from the clutch B circuit","Aerated oil due to low level, pump runs without load","Sheared drive between clutch B motor shaft and inner rotor","Rotor position sensor reporting an excessive speed"],["Clutch B does not hold full torque, flaring on shifts","Transmission warning and limited gears"],3,3,["P28D9","P28D7","P28DA","P28DB","P28C9"],"מנוע מצמד‏ B — מהירות יתר"],P28D9:["Clutch B Motor Underspeed","P28D9 indicates that the clutch B motor cannot reach the speed it is commanded to, leaving the pump short of flow to raise or adjust clutch pressure. Getrag states that its pump actuators control pressure consistently down to low temperatures, so a motor that persistently lags points to extra drag rather than normal cold behaviour: particles caught in the gerotor, a tight bearing, or oil of the wrong grade.",["Particles caught in the clutch B gerotor pump","Tight or damaged bearing in the clutch B motor or pump","Incorrect transmission fluid with too high viscosity","Low supply voltage or poor ground at the actuator"],["Delayed or jerky engagement of clutch B","Fault more likely after standing in the cold","Clutch B gears may be withheld"],3,3,["P28D8","P28D7","P28D6","P28DB","P28CA"],"מנוע מצמד‏ B — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P28DA:["Clutch B Motor Position Sensor Circuit/Open","P28DA concerns the electrical circuit of the sensor that reports the rotor angle of the clutch B motor, and is chiefly stored when that signal disappears because a line is open. Electronic commutation of a brushless motor relies on this angle to energise U, V and W in the right order; it also lets the controller count revolutions and compare pump speed with the pressure sensor.",["Open supply, ground or signal line of the clutch B motor position sensor","Pin pushed out or bent at the clutch B actuator connector","Failed sensing element inside the clutch B actuator"],["Clutch B out of service, half of the gears missing","Transmission warning lamp on","Motor speed codes for clutch B may be stored as follow-up faults"],3,3,["P28DB","P28D8","P28D9","P28CB"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מצמד‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P28DB:["Clutch B Motor Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P28DB flags a rotor position signal for the clutch B motor that is electrically present but fails the plausibility tests: angle steps arrive in a wrong order, a transition is skipped, or the derived speed disagrees with the phase currents and the measured clutch pressure. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 calls for such rationality monitoring of input signals where it is technically feasible, beyond pure circuit checks.",["Electrical interference through a damaged screen on the sensor lead","Partly broken strand in the clutch B position sensor wiring","Sensor or target magnet shifted, or metallic debris on the target"],["Clutch B engages roughly or drops out intermittently","Transmission warning, sometimes only after several trips","Motor speed codes for clutch B stored alongside"],3,3,["P28DA","P28D8","P28D9","P28CC"],"חיישן מצב מנוע מצמד‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P28DC:["Clutch B Pressure Sensor Circuit/Open","P28DC concerns the sensor that reports the hydraulic pressure acting on clutch B of a dual-clutch or hybrid transmission. The code points to a broken connection: the module receives no usable signal at all, as happens when a signal, supply or ground wire is open or the connector has come off. No manufacturer documents P28DC publicly.",["Connector at the sensor or transmission plug loose, unplugged or with a pushed-back pin","Signal, supply or ground wire of the sensor broken","Pressure sensor internally open","Sensor input in the transmission control module faulty"],["Transmission warning or check engine light on","Gears served by clutch B blocked, transmission in emergency mode","Jerky launch or harsh shifts"],3,3,["P28DD","P28DE","P28DF","P28CD","P28DA"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד‏ B — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P28DD:["Clutch B Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","Set when the voltage from the clutch B pressure sensor falls below the lowest value the part can produce in normal service. Usually the signal line has a short to ground, the sensor supply is missing or the sensor has failed internally. Because the reading lies outside the valid band, the module treats it as an electrical fault rather than as low pressure. No manufacturer documents P28DD publicly.",["Sensor signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Sensor supply voltage missing or pulled down by another shorted sensor on the same supply","Pressure sensor electronics failed"],["Transmission warning or check engine light on","Transmission in emergency mode, some gears unavailable","Harsh or delayed engagement"],3,3,["P28DC","P28DE","P28DF","P28CE"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P28DE:["Clutch B Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P28DE means the clutch B pressure sensor delivers a voltage above anything a working sensor would show, even at full clutch pressure. Typical causes are a signal line touching a supply or battery feed, a broken sensor ground, or a signal line open at the sensor end where the input uses a pull-up resistor. No manufacturer documents P28DE publicly.",["Signal wire shorted to the sensor supply or to battery voltage","Sensor ground open or high resistance at the connector","Pressure sensor failed with output stuck high"],["Transmission warning or check engine light on","Emergency mode with limited gears","Slipping or weak pull when clutch B is in use"],3,3,["P28DC","P28DD","P28DF","P28CF"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P28DF:["Clutch B Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","Here the clutch B pressure signal is electrically valid, yet it does not fit the situation. Examples are a reading that stays well above zero while the clutch is released, a value that does not rise when the actuator builds pressure, or a mismatch between commanded and measured pressure that persists. No manufacturer documents P28DF publicly.",["Pressure sensor drifting or with offset at zero pressure","Actual clutch pressure wrong because of leaking seals, a weak actuator pump or low fluid","Corroded or loose contacts distorting the signal","Control software needs an update or new adaptation"],["Transmission warning or check engine light on","Shudder, slip or jerky engagement on clutch B","Emergency mode after a few drives"],3,3,["P28DC","P28DD","P28DE","P28D0","P28D7"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P28E0:["Shift Motor Phase U-V-W Circuit Low","The shift motor is the three-phase electric motor of an electronic range actuator: in shift-by-wire systems it turns the detent plate and selector shaft between P, R, N and D. A Denso patent describes such a motor whose driver energises the U, V and W phases in turn, with a motor relay in the supply; Hyundai Kefico sells its SBW actuator with a brushless motor.",["Phase lead to the actuator chafed and shorted to ground","Motor winding shorted to the actuator housing (moisture, insulation damage)","Output stage in the shift control unit faulty"],["Shift system warning in the cluster","Selected range cannot be changed, vehicle may stay in Park","Engine may not start because Park or Neutral is not confirmed"],3,3,["P28E1","P28E2","P28E3","P28E4"],"פאזת מנוע העברת הילוכים‏ U-V-W — אות נמוך במעגל"],P28E1:["Shift Motor Phase U-V-W Circuit High","P28E1 is the opposite of P28E0: on any of the three shift motor phases the controller sees a voltage that is higher than the switching state allows, for example while the low-side switch should pull it down. Likely reasons are a phase lead touching a battery-powered wire, a winding with an internal short to a live part, or a high-side switch in the driver that no longer turns off.",["Phase lead shorted to a battery-voltage wire in the harness","High-side switch in the shift control unit stuck on","Water or corrosion bridging pins in the actuator connector"],["Shift system warning in the cluster","No response to the gear selector","Vehicle may remain in Park"],3,3,["P28E0","P28E2","P28E3","P28E4"],"פאזת מנוע העברת הילוכים‏ U-V-W — אות גבוה במעגל"],P28E2:["Shift Motor Phase U-V-W Circuit/Open","P28E2 reports that no current can flow in at least one shift motor phase, usually a broken lead, a loose terminal or an open winding. Hyundai documents it in bulletin 22-AT-001H with failure type 14 (P28E214), an open UVW motor circuit, for the push-button shift-by-wire of the 2020-on Palisade and Sonata, the 2021-on Santa Fe and Santa Fe Hybrid and the 2022-on Tucson and Tucson Hybrid.",["Actuator harness chafed open, on the Santa Fe at the battery tray (Hyundai 22-AT-001H)","Loose or damaged pin in the SBW actuator connector","Open winding inside the SBW actuator"],["Shifter system malfunction message in the cluster","Cannot shift into or out of gear or out of Park","Wrong gear display or no start"],2,3,["P28E0","P28E1","P28E3","P28E5"],"פאזת מנוע העברת הילוכים‏ U-V-W — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P28E3:["Shift Motor Phase U-V-W Performance","P28E3 covers the phase circuits of the shift motor when none of them is clearly open or shorted, yet they do not behave as expected: one phase draws noticeably more or less current than the others, or the current pattern does not match the commutation step. Such an imbalance comes from a phase with raised resistance, a partly shorted winding or a weak switch in the driver, and it shows up as uneven torque.",["Corroded or loose contact raising the resistance of one phase","Partly shorted turns in a motor winding","Degraded switch in the motor driver"],["Shift system warning in the cluster","Slow or noisy range changes","Occasional refusal to change range"],3,3,["P28E0","P28E1","P28E2","P28E5"],"פאזת מנוע העברת הילוכים‏ U-V-W — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P28E4:["Shift Motor Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P28E4 says the output stage that powers the shift motor has reached its current or temperature limit and has protected itself. A blocked actuator is the classic trigger: if the detent plate, the park pawl linkage or the gear train inside the actuator binds, the motor stalls and current climbs. Shorts between phases, or many range changes in a row in hot conditions, can also heat the driver.",["Detent mechanism, park pawl linkage or actuator gearing binding","Short between two motor phases","Driver overheated after repeated range changes or high ambient heat"],["Shift system warning in the cluster","Range change stops halfway or is refused","Problem may disappear after the system cools down"],3,3,["P28E0","P28E1","P28E3","P28E5"],"מנוע העברת הילוכים — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר"],P28E5:["Shift Motor Performance","P28E5 judges the shift motor by its result: it is driven, but the actuator does not get to the commanded range as expected. Hyundai lists it in bulletin 22-AT-001H for the shift-by-wire Palisade, Santa Fe, Sonata and Tucson (including hybrids) with two failure types: P28E577, commanded position not reached, and P28E592, SBW motor performance.",["SBW actuator worn internally or mechanism stiff","Shift control unit or its harness not delivering motor current","Low 12 V supply during the shift","Shift control software needing an update"],["Shifter system malfunction message in the cluster","Range not engaged or engaged with delay","Wrong gear display"],3,3,["P28E3","P28E4","P28E6","P28EA","P07E6"],"מנוע העברת הילוכים — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P28E6:["Shift Motor Overspeed","P28E6 is set when the shift motor turns faster than its control allows. In a position-controlled actuator this is visible from the rotor feedback: the encoder count changes quicker than the commanded movement can explain.",["Broken gear or coupling inside the actuator, motor spins without load","Faulty rotor position or encoder signal","Control software error in the shift control unit"],["Shift system warning in the cluster","Wrong range engaged or range change aborted","Clicking or whirring from the actuator"],3,3,["P28E5","P28E3","P28EA"],"מנוע העברת הילוכים — מהירות יתר"],P28E7:["Shift Motor Position Sensor Circuit/Open","The shift motor position sensor tells the controller where the selector shaft of a shift-by-wire actuator stands. In a Denso patent it is a contactless magnetic sensor on the detent plate with two independent units, so two signals reach the ECU; Hyundai notes in bulletin 22-AT-001H that the readings of its two position sensors should add up to roughly 100 percent.",["Position sensor connector loose, corroded or unplugged","Signal, supply or ground wire of the sensor broken","Position sensor failed internally"],["Shift system warning in the cluster","Gear display missing or wrong","Vehicle refuses to shift or does not start"],2,3,["P28E8","P28E9","P28EA","P0705"],"חיישן מצב מנוע העברת הילוכים — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P28E8:["Shift Motor Position Sensor Circuit High","P28E8 means the shift motor position sensor reports a value above its permitted range. Kia documents it on the 2024-25 EV9: service action SA594 (bulletin ELE362, January 2025) covers cars built from 25 September 2023 to 4 September 2024 that may not leave Park while P28E812 is stored, which Kia attributes to an output shaft sensor reading above what it should be.",["Shift control unit software on the 2024-25 Kia EV9 (service action SA594)","Sensor signal shorted to supply or battery voltage","Open or high-resistance sensor ground","Position sensor failed with output stuck high"],["Vehicle cannot be shifted out of Park","Shift system warning in the cluster"],2,3,["P28E7","P28E9","P28EA"],"חיישן מצב מנוע העברת הילוכים — אות גבוה במעגל"],P28E9:["Shift Motor Position Sensor Circuit Low","P28E9 is stored when the signal of the shift motor position sensor sits below its valid band. Typical causes are a signal line shorted to ground, a sensor supply that has collapsed, for instance because another sensor on the same feed is shorted, or a failed sensor. No manufacturer documents P28E9 publicly; Kia documents the high counterpart P28E8 on the EV9.",["Sensor signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor supply missing or pulled down","Position sensor failed with output stuck low"],["Shift system warning in the cluster","Range changes blocked or gear display wrong","Engine or drive system may not start"],2,3,["P28E7","P28E8","P28EA"],"חיישן מצב מנוע העברת הילוכים — אות נמוך במעגל"],P28EA:["Shift Motor Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P28EA covers a position signal that is electrically valid but implausible: the two channels disagree, the value does not move although the motor runs, or the actuator ends up away from the expected detent. Hyundai uses the code in bulletin 22-AT-001H for its shift-by-wire models with two failure types, P28EA71, SBW actuator stuck, and P28EA77, commanded position not reached.",["SBW actuator stuck or not reaching the commanded position","Position sensor channels drifting apart (sum no longer near 100 percent)","Intermittent contact in the sensor or actuator harness"],["Shifter system malfunction message in the cluster","Cannot shift out of Park or into the requested range","Gear display does not match the selected range"],3,3,["P28E7","P28E8","P28E9","P28E5","P28EC"],"חיישן מצב מנוע העברת הילוכים — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P28EB:["Shift Motor Position Not Learned","A shift-by-wire actuator has to learn which motor positions match P, R, N and D before it can work precisely. A Hyundai Autron patent does this from motor current: while the actuator travels between P and D, the load changes each time the detent spring passes one of the four notches of the detent plate, so R and N are found first and P and D derived by offset.",["Learning routine not run after replacing the control unit or actuator","Learned values cleared by a software update or memory loss","Learning aborted by low battery voltage or an active fault"],["Shift system warning in the cluster","Imprecise or refused range changes until learning is done"],2,2,["P28EC","P28EA","P28E5"],"מצב מנוע העברת הילוכים — לא בוצע לימוד"],P28EC:["Shift Motor Position Sensor Exceeded Learning Limit","Unlike P28EB, learning did take place here, but the result lies outside the window the controller accepts. The learned sensor values for the end stop or for the P, R, N and D detents differ too far from the nominal ones, or the measured play is too large.",["Actuator or sensor mounted out of position after a repair","Worn or damaged detent plate, detent spring or linkage","Wrong or mismatched actuator or sensor fitted"],["Shift system warning in the cluster","Learning routine fails repeatedly","Range changes imprecise or blocked"],3,3,["P28EB","P28EA","P28E7"],""],P28ED:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Overspeed","Pump B is a second electrically driven transmission fluid pump that works independently of the engine, for example to hold pressure during start-stop or electric driving, or to feed clutch cooling. P28ED says its motor runs faster than commanded or faster than its permitted maximum.",["Low fluid level or air drawn in, so the pump runs without load","Blocked suction filter or inlet","Faulty speed feedback or control in the pump controller"],["Transmission warning or check engine light on","Start-stop or electric driving disabled","Whining from the pump area"],2,1,["P28EE","P277C","P27A3","P276D"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — מהירות יתר"],P28EE:["Electric/Auxiliary Transmission Fluid Pump B Underspeed","P28EE is the reverse of P28ED: electric transmission fluid pump B does not reach the speed its controller asks for. The motor is fed, but something holds it back, such as very cold and thick fluid, a binding or worn pump, debris in the gears or a low supply voltage. When the speed falls to zero the matching code is the stall P277C rather than this one. No manufacturer documents P28EE publicly.",["Pump binding, worn or contaminated with debris","Very cold, aged or wrong transmission fluid","Low supply voltage or high resistance in the pump feed"],["Transmission warning or check engine light on","Engine keeps running at stops, electric driving limited","Delayed engagement after an automatic engine restart"],2,1,["P28ED","P277C","P27A3","P276D"],"משאבת שמן תיבה חשמלי/עזר‏ B — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P28EF:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Performance/Stuck Off","In a P2 hybrid a clutch placed between combustion engine and e-machine lets the car drive electrically with the engine at rest and couples the engine back in when it is needed. P28EF says the device that applies this clutch is not doing its job: it is commanded to act, but the expected pressure or clutch response stays absent, so the actuator behaves as if switched off. No manufacturer documents P28EF publicly.",["Pressure regulating valve of the disconnect clutch sticking or mechanically faulty","Contaminated or low transmission fluid, so the actuator cannot build pressure","Electric or mechanical oil pump delivers too little pressure to the clutch circuit","Control software or learned clutch values out of date"],["Engine does not start or does not engage while driving in hybrid mode","Gearbox or hybrid system warning in the cluster","Reduced power or electric-only limp mode"],4,3,["P28F0","P28F6","P2884","P2885","P287E","P2D8D"],"מפעיל מצמד ניתוק מנוע — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P28F0:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Stuck On","P28F0 is the opposite of P28EF: the actuator of the engine disconnect clutch keeps applying the clutch although the controller wants it released. The engine then stays tied to e-machine and wheels, so electric-only driving and engine stop at standstill are no longer possible. No manufacturer documents P28F0 publicly.",["Clutch pressure valve stuck in the applied position, for example by debris","Valve or actuator driver permanently energised by a short in wiring or module","Clutch plates overheated and dragging so the actuator cannot release them"],["Engine stalls or shudders when the car comes to a stop","No electric-only driving, engine runs all the time","Hybrid system warning and restricted engine restarts"],4,3,["P28EF","P28F6","P2886","P2882","P2D8D"],"מפעיל מצמד ניתוק מנוע — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P28F1:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit","A hydraulically applied disconnect clutch often has its own pressure sensor so the controller knows how firmly the clutch is held. Ford fits one to the 10R80 modular hybrid transmission of the 2021 Explorer, Aviator and F-150 hybrids; a Ford bulletin covers fluid seeping out at this sensor because its fasteners worked loose, fixed by retightening them.",["Sensor connector loose, corroded or with a pushed-back terminal","Signal, reference or ground wire of the sensor broken","Pressure sensor electronics failed, possibly after fluid ingress at a leaking seal","Sensor input of the transmission or hybrid control module faulty"],["Hybrid or transmission warning light","Engine stays off or engages harshly when it should join in","Possible fluid wetness around the sensor"],3,3,["P28F2","P28F3","P28F4","P28F5","P2884"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד ניתוק מנוע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P28F2:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","Here the wiring is intact and the voltage lies inside the valid band, yet the reading does not fit the situation. A Hyundai and Kia patent describes one such test: when the car is parked, the electric oil pump for the engine clutch is off, a soak time has passed and the vehicle stands still, no pressure can exist, so a sensor output above a set reference counts as a fault.",["Pressure sensor zero point drifted or wrongly learned","Real residual pressure from a sticking valve, so the sensor is not at fault","High resistance in sensor ground or signal line shifting the reading"],["Clutch slips or engages abruptly when the engine is coupled in","Hybrid or transmission warning light","Shudder during engine start while driving electrically"],3,3,["P28F1","P28F3","P28F4","P28F5","P2882"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד ניתוק מנוע — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P28F3:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P28F3 is stored when the voltage of the disconnect clutch pressure sensor drops below the smallest value a healthy part can output, a level that stands for an electrical fault, not for an open clutch. The usual suspects are a signal wire chafed against ground, a sensor reference supply that is missing or dragged down by another shorted sensor on the same feed, or a failed sensor.",["Signal wire shorted to ground through chafed insulation","Sensor reference supply missing or pulled low by another shorted sensor","Pressure sensor failed with output stuck low"],["Hybrid or transmission warning light","Engine coupling blocked, car runs electrically or in limp mode","Harsh engagement if the clutch is still used"],3,3,["P28F1","P28F2","P28F4","P28F5"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד ניתוק מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל"],P28F4:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit High","With P28F4 the disconnect clutch pressure sensor sends a voltage above anything it could produce even at full clutch pressure. Typical reasons are a signal line touching the reference or battery supply, an open sensor ground, or on inputs with a pull-up resistor a signal wire that is broken at the sensor. No manufacturer publishes a threshold for P28F4.",["Signal wire shorted to sensor reference or battery voltage","Sensor ground open or corroded at the connector","Pressure sensor failed with output stuck high"],["Hybrid or transmission warning light","Clutch slips when the engine is meant to drive","Electric-only operation or reduced power"],3,3,["P28F1","P28F2","P28F3","P28F5"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד ניתוק מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל"],P28F5:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P28F5 covers a pressure signal from the engine disconnect clutch that jumps, drops out briefly or changes faster than the hydraulics physically allow. Each sample may sit inside the valid band, but the pattern points to a loose contact, a wire that breaks under vibration or heat, or an unstable sensor. No manufacturer documents P28F5 publicly.",["Loose or corroded terminal in the sensor or transmission connector","Harness wire breaking intermittently under vibration or heat","Sensor loose on its mounting or internally unstable"],["Hybrid warning that comes and goes","Occasional jerk when the engine is coupled in","Fluid seepage at the sensor in some cases"],3,3,["P28F1","P28F2","P28F3","P28F4"],"חיישן לחץ מצמד ניתוק מנוע — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P28F6:["Engine Disconnect Clutch Actuator Circuit Intermittent","P28F6 points at the electrical side of the disconnect clutch actuator rather than at its mechanics: the drive circuit to the valve or motor that applies the clutch loses or regains its normal state for short moments, typically spotted as current or feedback that flickers between plausible and implausible.",["Loose, spread or corroded terminal in the actuator circuit","Harness chafing intermittently against the transmission or body","Transmission fluid wicking into the connector","Actuator coil or motor winding with an intermittent break"],["Sporadic hybrid or transmission warning","Engine occasionally fails to couple in or drops out","Jerks or brief power loss in hybrid mode"],3,3,["P287E","P287F","P2880","P2881","P28EF","P28F0"],"מפעיל מצמד ניתוק מנוע — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P28F7:["Exhaust Pressure Too High Bank 1","P28F7 reports that the pressure in the exhaust of bank 1 is higher than the engine model allows. GM documents it in its 2025 diesel ECM tables (25OBDG04B): the monitor looks at the low-pressure EGR differential pressure and fails above 80 kPa while torque demand exceeds a speed-dependent minimum (around 520 Nm at low engine speed, falling to 20 Nm at high speed), counting 480 failures in 600 samples;",["Exhaust throttle valve stuck closed or its shaft linkage broken","Exhaust restricted downstream, for example by a heavily loaded particulate filter or damaged pipe","Chafed engine harness disturbing valve control (GM 21-NA-149)","Pressure sensor reading too high without a separate sensor code"],["Check engine light on","Reduced engine power","Higher fuel consumption and more frequent filter regenerations"],2,3,["P28F8","P28F9","P048A","P0476","P2383","P2463"],"לחץ פליטה — ערך גבוה מדי (בנק 1)"],P28F8:["Exhaust Pressure Too High Bank 2","P28F8 is the bank 2 twin of P28F7 and only appears on engines whose two cylinder banks have separately measured exhaust paths, such as V engines with one turbocharger or flap per bank. It means the exhaust pressure on that side exceeds the modelled value. No manufacturer documents P28F8 publicly;",["Exhaust flap or throttle on bank 2 stuck closed","Restriction downstream on bank 2, for example a blocked catalyst or filter section","Variable turbine of the bank 2 turbocharger stuck in a closed position"],["Check engine light on","Loss of power, possibly with uneven running between banks","Increased fuel consumption"],2,3,["P28F7","P28FA","P04A5","P047A","P2465"],"לחץ פליטה — ערך גבוה מדי (בנק 2)"],P28F9:["Exhaust Pressure Too Low Bank 1","P28F9 flags exhaust pressure on bank 1 that stays below what the engine should produce at the current load. Too little pressure ahead of the turbine means the gas is escaping or not being held back: a leak at the manifold, gasket or turbine inlet, an exhaust flap jammed open, or a variable turbine stuck wide open. No manufacturer documents P28F9 publicly.",["Exhaust leak at manifold, gasket or turbine inlet on bank 1","Variable turbine geometry stuck in the open position","Exhaust throttle or pressure flap jammed open","Leaking or cracked sensing tube to the exhaust pressure sensor"],["Check engine light on","Weak boost and sluggish acceleration","Ticking or hissing exhaust noise near the manifold"],2,3,["P28FA","P28F7","P047F","P0299","P0471","P0474"],"לחץ פליטה — ערך נמוך מדי (בנק 1)"],P28FA:["Exhaust Pressure Too Low Bank 2","P28FA is the bank 2 version of P28F9: the exhaust on the second cylinder bank carries less pressure than the load calls for. It presupposes an engine with a separate pressure reading per bank, such as a V engine with one turbocharger on each side. No manufacturer documents P28FA publicly.",["Cracked manifold or leaking gasket on bank 2","Bank 2 turbocharger vanes or wastegate stuck open","Exhaust pressure flap of bank 2 jammed open"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power and slow boost build-up","Exhaust noise or soot traces on bank 2"],2,3,["P28F9","P28F8","P04A4","P0299","P047B"],"לחץ פליטה — ערך נמוך מדי (בנק 2)"],P2A00:["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Sensor 1","Sensor 1 on bank 1 is the oxygen sensor ahead of the catalytic converter that the engine control module relies on for mixture feedback. P2A00 is a plausibility fault: a signal is present but does not behave the way fuel control expects.",["Sensor aged or poisoned (oil ash, silicone, coolant), signal too weak or sluggish","Leak in intake manifold or exhaust ahead of the sensor distorts the oxygen reading","High resistance or corrosion in signal, reference or heater wiring","Fuel delivery or injector fault the sensor correctly reports but fuel control cannot correct"],["Check engine light on","Engine runs in open loop, fuel consumption rises","Uneven idle or hesitation","Failed emissions inspection"],2,1,["P0130","P0133","P2195","P2196","P2A01","P2A03","P2A06"],"חיישן חמצן — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2A01:["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Sensor 2","Sensor 2 on bank 1 sits behind the catalytic converter and mainly serves to judge how well the converter stores oxygen. Ford uses P2A01 for a signal that is out of range on the low side: on petrol engines with certain Continental control modules from 2011, and still in its 2020–2023 summary, a reading under −0.2 V lasting 10 s sets the code, usually because signal and return wires are swapped or the sensor is worn.",["Downstream sensor worn or contaminated","Engine oil or moisture in the sensor connector (Mazda CX-9 connector C-34)","Signal and return wires swapped, e.g. after a sensor replacement","On diesels, oxygen output of the second NOx sensor drifting"],["Check engine light on","Catalyst or aftertreatment monitor stays incomplete","Usually no noticeable change in driving behaviour"],1,1,["P0136","P0137","P2270","P2271","P2A00","P2A04","P2A07"],"חיישן חמצן — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2A02:["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1 Sensor 3","Sensor 3 on bank 1 follows a second converter or, on diesels, a further aftertreatment stage. GM is the only maker found that documents P2A02: in its 2025 diesel tables the oxygen value of the third NOx sensor is held against that of sensor 2 while the engine runs at full load, and a gap of more than 6 % in either direction in 120 of 240 samples sets a two-trip Type B fault.",["Oxygen output of the third NOx or oxygen sensor drifting with age","Exhaust leak between sensor 2 and sensor 3 lets outside air in","Sensor coated with soot, ash or urea deposits"],["Check engine light on","Aftertreatment monitor does not complete","No noticeable effect on driving in most cases"],2,1,["P0142","P0145","P2274","P2A01","P2A05","P2A08"],"חיישן חמצן — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2A03:["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 2 Sensor 1","Bank 2 is the cylinder bank that does not contain cylinder 1, so P2A03 only occurs on V or flat engines; sensor 1 is the oxygen sensor ahead of that bank's converter used for fuel control. The fault is the bank-2 counterpart of P2A00: the sensor delivers a signal, yet fuel control cannot close the loop with it or keep it closed.",["Bank 2 front sensor aged or poisoned, too slow to reach closed loop","Sensor heater weak or wiring with high resistance, sensor stays too cold","Exhaust leak at the bank 2 manifold ahead of the sensor","Real mixture problem on bank 2 (injector, vacuum leak) the sensor reports correctly"],["Check engine light on","Higher fuel consumption","Rough idle or exhaust odour","Failed emissions inspection"],2,1,["P0150","P0153","P2197","P2198","P2A00","P2A04","P2A09"],"חיישן חמצן — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2A04:["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 2 Sensor 2","Sensor 2 on bank 2 is the oxygen sensor behind that bank's catalytic converter, used for converter monitoring and fine mixture trim. Ford documents P2A04 together with P2A01 for certain Continental control modules on petrol engines from 2011, and again in its 2020–2023 summary: a rear-sensor voltage that stays below −0.2 V over 10 s sets the code – a value an intact switching sensor should not produce, normally…",["Oil in the sensor connector from a leaking oil pressure switch (Mazda CX-9)","Downstream sensor on bank 2 worn","Signal and return wires swapped or sensors of both banks plugged in crosswise"],["Check engine light on","Often stored together with a stuck-lean code for the same sensor","Catalyst monitor of bank 2 not ready"],1,1,["P0156","P0157","P2272","P2273","P2A01","P2A03","P2A10"],"חיישן חמצן — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2A05:["O2 Sensor Circuit Range/Performance Bank 2 Sensor 3","P2A05 refers to the third oxygen sensor on bank 2, mounted behind a further converter or aftertreatment stage of a V or flat engine. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. The nearest documented case is its bank-1 counterpart: GM's 2025 diesel tables compare the oxygen value of sensor 3 with that of sensor 2 at full load and set P2A02 when the gap exceeds 6 % in 120 of 240 samples.",["Third sensor on bank 2 drifting or slow with age","Exhaust leak in the pipe between sensor 2 and sensor 3","Damaged or heat-affected wiring under the vehicle"],["Check engine light on","Readiness for the catalyst or aftertreatment monitor missing","Usually no change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P0162","P0165","P2276","P2A02","P2A04","P2A11"],"חיישן חמצן — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2, חיישן 3)"],P2A06:["O2 Sensor Negative Voltage Bank 1 Sensor 1","P2A06 means the switching oxygen sensor ahead of the converter on bank 1 is delivering a voltage below zero. A zirconia sensor generates its voltage from the oxygen difference between exhaust gas and reference air, normally about 0.1–0.9 V; a negative value means the exhaust side looks richer in oxygen than the reference side, or the polarity at the module is reversed. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Cracked ceramic element, for instance after water shock or impact","Signal and signal-return wires swapped at connector or after a repair","Reference air path of the sensor contaminated by oil, sealant or water"],["Check engine light on","Mixture control falls back to open loop, consumption rises","Possible rough idle or poor emissions result"],1,1,["P0130","P0131","P2A00","P2A07","P2A08","P2A09"],"מתח שלילי חיישן חמצן (בנק 1, חיישן 1)"],P2A07:["O2 Sensor Negative Voltage Bank 1 Sensor 2","Sensor 2 on bank 1 is the switching oxygen sensor behind the converter; P2A07 says its output has dropped below zero volts. Because the voltage comes from the oxygen difference across the zirconia element, a negative value points to reversed signal and return wires, a contaminated reference air path or a cracked element. No manufacturer documents P2A07 publicly.",["Signal and return wires swapped, e.g. after fitting a universal sensor","Cracked sensing element","Sensor degraded or reference air contaminated"],["Check engine light on","Catalyst monitor of bank 1 not ready","Usually no noticeable change while driving"],1,1,["P0136","P0137","P2A01","P2A06","P2A08","P2A10"],"מתח שלילי חיישן חמצן (בנק 1, חיישן 2)"],P2A08:["O2 Sensor Negative Voltage Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2A08 is the negative-voltage fault of the third oxygen sensor on bank 1, which sits behind a second converter or another aftertreatment stage. Such a sensor is normally a zirconia switching type whose output should stay above zero;",["Signal return shorted to another circuit or leads swapped","Cracked sensing element of sensor 3","Fault in the module's sensor input stage"],["Check engine light on","Converter monitor readiness missing","Normal driving behaviour in most cases"],2,1,["P0142","P0143","P2A02","P2A06","P2A07","P2A11"],"מתח שלילי חיישן חמצן (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2A09:["O2 Sensor Negative Voltage Bank 2 Sensor 1","P2A09 concerns the pre-converter oxygen sensor on bank 2, so it only arises on two-bank engines that use switching sensors ahead of the converters. The module reads a voltage below zero from it. Since a zirconia cell's output depends on the oxygen difference between exhaust and reference air, a negative value means swapped wires, a reference air path fouled by fluids or sealant, or a crack in the element;",["Cracked element in the bank 2 front sensor","Signal wires swapped or bank 1 and bank 2 connectors interchanged","Reference air path contaminated by oil, water or sealant"],["Check engine light on","Higher fuel consumption due to open-loop operation of bank 2","Possible rough idle"],2,1,["P0150","P0151","P2A03","P2A06","P2A10","P2A11"],"מתח שלילי חיישן חמצן (בנק 2, חיישן 1)"],P2A0A:["Manifold Absolute Pressure Sensor B Circuit","Engines with two intake manifold pressure sensors call the second one sensor B; in GM's tables for the Corvette's LT6 V8 it measures the manifold pressure of bank 2, next to the bank-1 sensor that uses the familiar P0105–P0109 codes. P2A0A is the general circuit fault of sensor B, meant for cases where the module sees a circuit problem without sorting it into low, high or intermittent.",["Loose connector, corroded terminal or damaged wire at sensor B","MAP sensor B failed internally","5 V reference shared with other sensors pulled down"],["Check engine light on","Uneven running or hesitation","Possible reduced power"],1,3,["P2A0B","P2A0C","P2A0D","P2A0E","P0105"],"חיישן לחץ סעפת (MAP)‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A0B:["Manifold Absolute Pressure Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2A0B means the MAP B signal stays inside its electrical range but does not fit the operating state. GM documents it for the Corvette's LT6 V8, where sensor B reads the bank-2 manifold pressure, with several checks: before the engine turns, the raw reading has to agree with ambient pressure within a few kPa, otherwise one trip and 5 s are enough;",["Air leak in the bank 2 intake behind the throttle","Sensor port blocked by deposits or frozen condensate","Sensor B drifting so that its reading no longer matches ambient or model"],["Check engine light on","Hesitation or uneven idle","Mixture or load faults on bank 2"],2,1,["P2A0A","P2A0C","P2A0D","P2A0E","P0106"],"חיישן לחץ סעפת (MAP)‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2A0C:["Manifold Absolute Pressure Sensor B Circuit Low","P2A0C reports that the MAP B signal voltage is too low. Manifold pressure sensors are usually three-wire parts fed from a 5 V reference; a signal close to zero means a broken reference or signal wire, a ground short or a dead sensor, because even deep vacuum would not pull a healthy sensor down that far.",["5 V reference or signal wire open","Signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor B failed internally"],["Check engine light on","Sluggish response or rough running","Possible reduced engine power"],1,3,["P2A0A","P2A0B","P2A0D","P2A0E","P0107"],"חיישן לחץ סעפת (MAP)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A0D:["Manifold Absolute Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","P2A0D is the high-voltage counterpart: the MAP B signal sits close to the reference voltage. Typical reasons are an open ground wire, a signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage, or a sensor that has failed internally. For the Corvette's LT6 V8, GM sets P2A0D when the bank-2 manifold pressure sensor reads above 4.5 V for 1.5 s, after a single trip;",["Sensor ground wire open or connector not seated","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage","Sensor B failed internally"],["Check engine light on","Rough running or hesitation","Possible limited power"],1,3,["P2A0A","P2A0B","P2A0C","P2A0E","P0108"],"חיישן לחץ סעפת (MAP)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A0E:["Manifold Absolute Pressure Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2A0E flags a MAP B signal that jumps or drops out for short moments instead of failing for good. No manufacturer documents P2A0E publicly; GM's LT6 tables, the only public description of a sensor B, cover just its low, high and plausibility faults.",["Loose or widened terminal in the sensor B connector","Harness chafing on engine parts, intermittent short or open","Moisture or corrosion in the connector"],["Intermittent stumble or hesitation","Fault comes and goes, warning light depending on manufacturer"],2,0,["P2A0A","P2A0B","P2A0C","P2A0D","P0109"],"חיישן לחץ סעפת (MAP)‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A0F:["Fuel Supply Heater Performance","A fuel supply heater warms the fuel on its way to the engine. On diesels it sits at the filter so that paraffin wax cannot block it in frost; on flex-fuel engines running on high ethanol blends heated fuel eases cold starts, as a Kia patent with a heated ethanol path to a separate cold-start injector shows.",["Heating element burnt out or with too high resistance","Heater relay, fuse or supply wiring not delivering full voltage","Fuel temperature sensor reports wrongly, so the heating effect seems absent"],["Hard starting in cold weather","Rough running or power loss in severe frost","Fault code stored, warning light depending on manufacturer"],2,0,["P2687","P2688","P2689","P0181"],"גוף חימום אספקת דלק — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A10:["O2 Sensor Negative Voltage Bank 2 Sensor 2","The downstream oxygen sensor of bank 2, behind that bank's converter, is reporting a negative voltage. Bank 2 only exists on V and flat engines. A healthy switching sensor swings between roughly 0.1 and 0.9 V; readings below zero come from swapped signal and return wires, for instance after splicing in a universal sensor, from a fouled reference air path or from a cracked ceramic.",["Signal and return wires swapped, e.g. on a spliced universal sensor","Cracked ceramic of the bank 2 downstream sensor","Reference air path fouled"],["Check engine light on","Catalyst monitor of bank 2 not ready","No change in driving behaviour"],1,1,["P0156","P0157","P2A04","P2A07","P2A09","P2A11"],"מתח שלילי חיישן חמצן (בנק 2, חיישן 2)"],P2A11:["O2 Sensor Negative Voltage Bank 2 Sensor 3","P2A11 is assigned to bank 2's third oxygen sensor, located after a second converter or additional aftertreatment of a two-bank engine, and says its signal has gone negative. For an intact, properly connected zirconia sensor that is not a normal state; likely explanations are reversed leads, a short within the harness or a cracked sensing element.",["Leads swapped or harness short near the exhaust","Cracked sensing element of sensor 3","Fault in the module's sensor input"],["Check engine light on","Dependent catalyst or aftertreatment monitor incomplete"],2,1,["P0162","P0163","P2A05","P2A08","P2A09","P2A10"],"מתח שלילי חיישן חמצן (בנק 2, חיישן 3)"],P2A12:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control C (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","The injection pump fuel metering codes cover electrically controlled actuators that decide how much fuel a diesel pump delivers – on distributor pumps the quantity solenoid, on common rail usually the inlet metering unit on the high-pressure pump, which a Bosch patent describes together with its flushing line. Actuators A and B have their own code groups (P0251 ff., P0256 ff.);",["Open circuit or poor contact in the actuator C wiring or connector","Metering actuator C coil failed or valve sticking","Dirt or water in the fuel jamming the metering valve"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power or limp mode","Hard starting or stalling"],3,3,["P2A13","P2A14","P2A15","P0251","P0256"],""],P2A13:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control C Range/Performance (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A13 flags metering element C of a diesel injection system as implausible: its circuit is electrically intact, yet the quantity or pressure it is supposed to produce does not follow the engine control module's command. The letter C stands for a third element – a further metering valve, a cam-driven pump plunger or a unit injector with its own solenoid. No manufacturer publishes P2A13.",["Fault in the high-pressure system (leak, relief valve, low-pressure supply) that the element cannot compensate","Worn or sticking metering element C (valve, plunger or cam lobe)","Outdated engine control software or calibration"],["Check engine light on","Lack of power, especially under load","Engine power derated by the control module"],3,3,["P2A12","P2A14","P2A15","P2A17","P0257"],""],P2A14:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control C Low (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A14 reports that the signal in the drive circuit of fuel metering element C has fallen below its expected window. In practice the control module sees too little voltage or current on that output, as happens when the line touches ground or, depending on the driver design, an open wire. C denotes a third metering element besides A and B, found only on pumps or engines with several separately driven elements.",["Control wire of element C chafed through and shorted to ground","Broken wire or corroded, loose connector pin in the element C circuit","Coil of metering element C open or shorted to its housing","Faulty output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power or limp mode","Rough running or misfire-like shaking"],2,3,["P2A12","P2A13","P2A15","P2A18","P0253"],""],P2A15:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control C High (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","With P2A15 the engine control module finds the circuit of metering element C reading too high: voltage where the driver expects a pulled-down line, or a current beyond the limit. Causes are a chafed wire touching battery voltage, a short between windings inside the actuator, or a failing output stage.",["Shorted turns in the coil of metering element C drawing excess current","Control wire of element C shorted to battery voltage","Output stage in the engine control module no longer switching correctly"],["Check engine light on","Strongly limited power and accelerator response","Engine may stall or refuse to start"],2,3,["P2A12","P2A13","P2A14","P2A19","P0259"],""],P2A16:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control D (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A16 is the umbrella code for fuel metering element D, used when the control module registers a malfunction of that element without assigning it to the more specific plausibility, low or high codes (P2A17–P2A19). The D series only makes sense on systems with at least four individually controlled metering elements, such as engines whose camshaft drives several pumping units.",["Wiring or connector fault in the circuit of element D","Metering element D (valve, pumping unit or injector solenoid) defective","Engine control module fault or software error"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power","Hard starting or uneven running"],3,3,["P2A17","P2A18","P2A19","P2A12","P2A1A"],""],P2A17:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control D Range/Performance (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A17 means fuel metering element D is not delivering what the control module commands, although its circuit shows no electrical fault. Volvo and Mack document the code for their 11 and 13 litre engines (including Mack MP7/MP8) built to the US17 emissions level, together with P0257 and P2A1F.",["Injector lobe turned on the assembled camshaft (Volvo/Mack US17)","Rail pressure problem such as an internal leak or poor low-pressure supply","Worn pumping injector or rocker of element D","Outdated diagnostic software leading to wrong test results"],["Check engine light on","Lack of power","Further rail pressure codes stored at the same time"],4,3,["P2A16","P2A18","P2A19","P0257","P2A1F","P0087"],""],P2A18:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control D Low (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A18 indicates a low reading in the control circuit of metering element D: the module detects that the output stays near ground or carries too little current. Typical triggers are a short to ground in the harness, a corroded connector pin or, with low-side drivers, an interrupted lead.",["Harness of element D shorted to ground","Corroded or spread connector pin at element D","Interrupted lead on the switched side of element D","Defective driver in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Limited power or limp mode","Fault may come and go with vibration or moisture"],2,3,["P2A16","P2A17","P2A19","P2A14","P0258"],""],P2A19:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control D High (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A19 is stored when the circuit of metering element D reads high – for instance a control line shorted to battery voltage, an actuator coil with shorted turns pulling excessive current, or a driver that no longer switches off. The fault is electrical; whether the element would still meter correctly cannot be judged until the circuit is repaired.",["Control line of element D shorted to battery voltage","Actuator coil of element D with shorted turns","Output stage in the control module stuck switched on"],["Warning lamp on immediately","Severe power reduction","Possible stalling or no start"],2,3,["P2A16","P2A17","P2A18","P2A15","P0254"],""],P2A1A:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control E (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A1A covers fuel metering element E in general: the engine control module has seen a malfunction of that element but files it under none of the more specific codes for plausibility (P2A1B) or low and high signal (P2A1C, P2A1D). A fifth separately driven element is rare; it presupposes engines that meter fuel per cylinder or per pumping unit.",["Wiring or connector fault at metering element E","Metering element E or its solenoid defective","Control module fault"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power","Uneven idle"],3,3,["P2A1B","P2A1C","P2A1D","P2A16","P2A1E"],""],P2A1B:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control E Range/Performance (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A1B reports that metering element E works electrically but its result is off: the pressure build-up or quantity attributed to it deviates from what was commanded, or its correction values sit at the limit. How a control module rates this is not published; rail pressure and fuel correction are the obvious inputs. No manufacturer documents P2A1B.",["Worn cam lobe, plunger or valve of metering element E","Insufficient low-pressure supply or clogged filter","Leak in the high-pressure circuit"],["Check engine light on","Lack of power under load","Longer cranking before start"],3,3,["P2A1A","P2A1C","P2A1D","P2A17","P2A1F"],""],P2A1C:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control E Low (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A1C is set when the drive circuit of the fifth metering element, E, reads below its permitted range. On solenoid-operated pump valves and unit injectors, a wire grounded against the engine block, water in a connector or a broken lead on the ground-switched side are typical.",["Wire of element E rubbing on the engine block and grounded","Moisture or corrosion in the connector of element E","Broken lead on the ground-switched side"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power or limp mode","Rough running"],2,3,["P2A1A","P2A1B","P2A1D","P2A18","P2A20"],""],P2A1D:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control E High (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A1D tells that metering element E's circuit sits above its plausible range. Faults that cause it include a lead rubbing through onto a powered wire, moisture bridging pins, an actuator winding shorted internally so that current climbs, or a defective output stage in the control unit. Element E only exists where five or more metering elements are driven individually. No manufacturer publishes P2A1D.",["Internal winding short in metering element E","Lead of element E chafed onto a powered wire or pins bridged by moisture","Defective output stage in the control unit"],["Check engine light on","Marked power limitation","Engine may cut out"],2,3,["P2A1A","P2A1B","P2A1C","P2A19","P2A21"],""],P2A1E:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control F (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A1E is the general fault of the sixth fuel metering element, F – the last letter of this code family. The control module stores it for a failure of that element that it cannot pin down as a plausibility (P2A1F), low (P2A20) or high (P2A21) fault. Six individually metered elements would fit, for example, a six-cylinder engine with one pumping unit or unit injector per cylinder.",["Wiring or connector fault in the circuit of element F","Pumping unit, valve or injector solenoid of element F defective","Engine control module fault"],["Check engine light on","Derated power","Uneven running"],3,3,["P2A1F","P2A20","P2A21","P2A1A","P2A16"],""],P2A1F:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control F Range/Performance (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A1F says that metering element F does not reach its target although its wiring checks out. Volvo and Mack document it for their US17-generation 11 and 13 litre engines, alongside P0257 and P2A17. On these engines three pumping injectors, driven through rockers by double cam lobes, deliver fuel into the rail at up to roughly 35,000 psi.",["Injector lobe spun on the assembled camshaft (Volvo/Mack US17)","Low-pressure supply too weak or a leak in the rail system","Worn pumping injector of element F","Outdated workshop software misleading the guided test"],["Check engine light on","Lack of power","Rail pressure codes stored alongside"],4,3,["P2A1E","P2A20","P2A21","P0257","P2A17","P0087"],""],P2A20:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control F Low (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A20 is the low-signal fault of metering element F: the module measures a voltage or current on that drive line that is lower than the switching state allows. Shorts to ground, broken conductors on low-side switched circuits and connectors pushed out of their housing are the usual suspects. Element F is the sixth individually controlled metering element, so the code only concerns engines with six such units.",["Drive line of element F shorted to ground","Terminal pushed out of the connector housing or broken conductor","Open coil in metering element F"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power","Rough idle"],2,3,["P2A1E","P2A1F","P2A21","P2A1C","P0253"],""],P2A21:["Injection Pump Fuel Metering Control F High (Cam/Rotor/Injector)","P2A21 marks a high reading in the circuit of the sixth metering element, F. The control module sees battery potential on the line or a current exceeding the driver limit – for instance when the harness rubs through onto a supply wire or the actuator coil is partly short-circuited. A driver stage that protects itself may then switch the output off, so the element can no longer meter at all.",["Partly short-circuited coil of metering element F","Harness of element F chafed onto a supply wire","Damaged output stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Severely limited power and throttle response","Possible stalling"],2,3,["P2A1E","P2A1F","P2A20","P2A1D","P0259"],""],P2A22:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit/Open","P2A22 covers the drive circuit of shutoff valve B, the electric lock on a further gas cylinder of a multi-tank CNG or LPG installation, when the module finds no current path at all. A broken lead, a loose plug or a burnt-out coil are the usual findings. No manufacturer documents P2A22 publicly; the upfitter TransEco lumps an open line into its Low code P2A24 instead.",["Broken lead or disconnected plug at the valve on tank B","Burnt-out solenoid coil of valve B","Corroded terminals in the valve connector"],["Check engine light","Noticeably shorter range on gas","Gas left in one cylinder after the others are empty"],3,1,["P2A23","P2A24","P2A25","P2A26","P224C"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A23:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2A23 is stored when valve B is switched on electrically, but the gas system does not react as if that cylinder had opened. Software can only judge this from pressure: after the command, the reading downstream of the tank should rise, and a tank B pressure sensor, where fitted, should fall while gas is being used. No manufacturer publishes P2A23 or its thresholds.",["Armature of valve B jammed closed, e.g. by debris","Manual valve on tank B left closed","Tank or line pressure sensor reporting the response wrongly"],["Check engine light","Tank B stays full while the others empty","Reduced range on gas"],3,1,["P2A22","P2A24","P2A25","P2A42","P224D"],"מעגל בקרת שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2A24:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit Low","P2A24 means the alternative fuel module sees the control line of shutoff valve B sitting too low. TransEco Energy, which converts trucks to CNG, assigns it in the fault table of its AFCM v1.4 to a lead shorted to ground or open, lights the MIL on dedicated and bi-fuel systems alike and does not force a fallback.",["Control wire of valve B chafed through to ground at a tank bracket","Open lead, which the TransEco module reports under this code","Shorted turns in the coil of valve B"],["Check engine light","Gas from tank B unavailable, range reduced"],3,1,["P2A22","P2A23","P2A25","P2A28","P224E"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A25:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve B Control Circuit High","P2A25 reports a voltage on the control circuit of tank valve B that is higher than the module expects, mostly because the wire touches a battery feed. TransEco Energy's fault table names a short to power as the cause, turns on the MIL and lets the gas system carry on.",["Control wire of valve B touching a battery feed","Output stage for valve B in the module stuck on","Wiring mistake during conversion or repair"],["Check engine light","Tank B may stay open with the engine off"],3,1,["P2A22","P2A23","P2A24","P2A29","P224F"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A26:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve C Control Circuit/Open","P2A26 is the open-circuit code for shutoff valve C, the solenoid on yet another gas cylinder. The module drives the coil and finds that no current flows, so the coil, its plug or the lead to it is interrupted. No manufacturer documents P2A26 publicly.",["Interrupted lead or unplugged connector at valve C","Open coil in valve C","Faulty driver for valve C in the control module"],["Check engine light","Gas in cylinder C cannot be used"],3,1,["P2A27","P2A28","P2A29","P2A22","P2A2A","P2A2E"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A27:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve C Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2A27 points to valve C: electrically commanded, yet apparently still shut. With several cylinders on one manifold, a single tank that stays isolated rarely stops the engine; the others keep supplying gas, and the fault appears as shorter range or a cylinder that never empties.",["Sticking or contaminated armature in valve C","Hand valve on cylinder C closed","Coil voltage too low because of a poor feed or ground"],["Check engine light","Cylinder C never empties","Shorter range on gas"],3,1,["P2A26","P2A28","P2A29","P2A47","P2A23"],"מעגל בקרת שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2A28:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve C Control Circuit Low","P2A28 tells that the control line of shutoff valve C reads too low. In TransEco Energy's AFCM table the cause is a lead to ground or an interruption; the MIL lights in both dedicated and bi-fuel conversions, and the vehicle continues without a forced change of fuel. Another number, P2A18, appears there alongside. Ford's Boss 302S list of 2014 carries P2A28 too.",["Insulation of the valve C wire worn through at a clamp","Interrupted lead, reported here by some modules","Coil of valve C shorted internally"],["Check engine light","Cylinder C not used or not shut off correctly"],3,1,["P2A26","P2A27","P2A29","P2A24","P2A2C"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A29:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve C Control Circuit High","P2A29 sets when the drive circuit of shutoff valve C sits at a high level, as with a wire touching battery voltage or a driver stage inside the module that will not switch off. TransEco's table for its AFCM v1.4 gives a short to power as the cause, with the MIL on and gas operation maintained. Ford names P2A29 in its Boss 302S code list.",["Valve C control wire in contact with battery voltage","Driver stage for valve C will not switch off","Valve C wired to a permanent feed after a conversion"],["Check engine light","Cylinder C not sealed when the engine is off"],3,1,["P2A26","P2A27","P2A28","P2A25","P2A2D"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A2A:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve D Control Circuit/Open","P2A2A marks an interrupted control circuit at shutoff valve D, which only exists on installations with four or more gas cylinders, mostly commercial trucks, vans and buses. When the module energizes the coil and measures no current, it stores this code. No manufacturer documents P2A2A publicly.",["Break in the branch of the harness leading to valve D","Coil of valve D open","Common supply via relay or inertia switch interrupted (several valve codes at once)"],["Check engine light","Reduced usable gas quantity"],3,1,["P2A2B","P2A2C","P2A2D","P2A26","P2A2E"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ D — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A2B:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve D Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2A2B is the functional fault of valve D: the module has commanded it open, but the pressure picture suggests that cylinder D is not contributing gas. Bus builder New Flyer gives figures for the scale involved: its tanks hold between 1,375 and 24,800 kPa, while the regulated side should read 648 to 827 kPa once the engine runs.",["Valve D mechanically stuck shut","Weak coil that no longer pulls the armature","Hand valve on tank D closed after service"],["Check engine light","Tank D stays at full pressure","Reduced range on gas"],4,1,["P2A2A","P2A2C","P2A2D","P2A27","P2A2F"],"מעגל בקרת שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ D — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2A2C:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve D Control Circuit Low","P2A2C records too low a level on the control wire of shutoff valve D. TransEco Energy treats it in its AFCM v1.4 fault list as a short to ground or open circuit and switches on the MIL while letting gas operation continue; P2A1C is printed beside it as an alternative number. Ford's Boss 302S list from 2014 contains P2A2C too.",["Valve D wire grounded at a chafe point on the cylinder rack","Salt corrosion in the valve D connector","Shorted coil in valve D"],["Check engine light","Gas from tank D not available"],3,1,["P2A2A","P2A2B","P2A2D","P2A28","P2A30"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A2D:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve D Control Circuit High","P2A2D reports excessive voltage on the control circuit of shutoff valve D. The AFCM fault list from TransEco Energy names a short to power, lights the MIL and keeps the gas system in service; P2A1D stands next to it. Ford's 2014 Boss 302S list includes P2A2D without the MIL marker. A wire pinched against a supply cable, a module output that stays on or an error while wiring a conversion kit are the likely findings.",["Valve D lead pinched against a supply cable","Module output for valve D stays on","Error while wiring a conversion kit"],["Check engine light","Tank D possibly open with the engine off"],3,1,["P2A2A","P2A2B","P2A2C","P2A29","P2A31"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A2E:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve E Control Circuit/Open","P2A2E is the open-circuit fault for shutoff valve E, the last letter of this series, so it only applies to systems with at least five gas cylinders, such as transit buses or heavy trucks. The module notices that the coil draws no current when commanded. No manufacturer documents P2A2E publicly, and TransEco's AFCM table lists valve E only with its Low and High codes.",["Valve E connector not plugged in after tank work","Open coil of valve E","Broken wire in the harness branch to tank E"],["Check engine light","Gas in cylinder E remains unused"],3,1,["P2A2F","P2A30","P2A31","P2A2A","P2A22"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ E — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A2F:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve E Control Circuit Performance/Stuck Off","P2A2F signals that valve E was energized but the system did not see the expected gas flow from that cylinder. No manufacturer publishes this code or its test conditions; CARB only requires output components to be checked for a proper reaction to commands. New Flyer's bulletin explains that its tank solenoids switch on while the starter spins the engine to about 400 rpm.",["Voltage drop during cranking, coil cannot lift the armature","Contaminated or sticking valve E","Manual valve on cylinder E closed"],["Check engine light","Cylinder E does not empty","Fault appears mainly after cold or weak-battery starts"],3,1,["P2A2E","P2A30","P2A31","P2A2B","P224D"],"מעגל בקרת שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ E — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2A30:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve E Control Circuit Low","P2A30 sets when the control circuit of shutoff valve E reads low. TransEco Energy's AFCM v1.4 table names a short to ground or an open lead as the reason and keeps both dedicated and bi-fuel vehicles running, MIL on; P2A20 is listed beside it. Ford's Boss 302S code list contains P2A30 as well. A low reading on valve E alone points to the branch of the harness serving that cylinder.",["Control lead of valve E touching ground","Shared ground or connector near the module (several low codes together)","Shorted coil in valve E"],["Check engine light","Gas from tank E not usable"],3,1,["P2A2E","P2A2F","P2A31","P2A2C","P2A24"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ E — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A31:["Alternative Fuel Tank Shutoff Valve E Control Circuit High","P2A31 closes the shutoff valve series with the high fault on valve E: the module measures voltage on the control wire where none should be. TransEco names a short to power and lights the MIL while the gas system continues; it prints P2A21 beside the code. Ford's Boss 302S list includes P2A31 without a MIL marker.",["Valve E wire shorted to a voltage source","Driver for valve E in the module stuck on","Valve E fed from a wrong circuit after an upfit"],["Check engine light","Cylinder E not locked when it should be"],3,1,["P2A2E","P2A2F","P2A30","P2A2D","P2A32"],"שסתום ניתוק מיכל דלק חלופי‏ E — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A32:["AFCM Power Relay Control Circuit/Open","Gas installations that carry a separate control unit for the gas side, the AFCM, may feed that unit through a relay whose coil is switched by a driver stage. P2A32 means this coil circuit shows no current path: the driver output sees an open line, a missing plug or a burnt coil. Ford's 2003 bi-fuel CNG pickups show how such a module manages relays itself;",["Broken control wire or unplugged relay socket","Relay coil burnt out","Blown fuse in the coil feed of the relay","Output driver in the controlling module faulty"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Gas mode cannot be selected, vehicle stays on petrol","Dedicated gas engine: no start"],2,3,["P2A33","P2A34","P2A35","P0685","U0108"],""],P2A33:["AFCM Power Relay Control Circuit Low","P2A33 concerns the control line that grounds the coil of the relay supplying the gas control module. Low means this line already sits near zero volts while the driver is switched off. A chafed wire touching the body is the classic finding; a coil with shorted windings can give the same picture.",["Control wire chafed through and touching ground","Shorted turns in the relay coil","Moisture in the relay socket bridging to ground"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Battery flat after the vehicle has been parked","Gas module stays active after ignition off"],2,1,["P2A32","P2A34","P2A36","P0686","U0108"],""],P2A34:["AFCM Power Relay Control Circuit High","With P2A34 the coil control line of the gas module power relay stays at high voltage even when the driver tries to pull it to ground. Either the wire has contact with a battery-fed circuit, or the coil draws so much current that the driver shuts itself off for protection. In both cases the relay does not close.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-fed circuit","Relay coil with too low resistance overloading the driver","Wrong relay type fitted after a repair"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Gas operation unavailable, bi-fuel vehicle runs on petrol only","Dedicated gas engine: cranks but does not start"],2,3,["P2A32","P2A33","P2A37","P0687","U0108"],""],P2A35:["AFCM Power Relay Sense Circuit","Besides driving the relay coil, a control module can read back the voltage behind the relay contacts to confirm that power actually arrives. P2A35 is the general fault of this feedback line for the relay that supplies the gas control module, without a statement about too low or too high. Typical are an open sense wire, a corroded pin or a blown fuse between contact and sense point.",["Sense wire open or pin backed out","Blown fuse between relay contact and sense point","Corroded terminals in relay socket or module plug"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Often no drivability change","Occasional fallback to petrol if the supply really drops"],2,1,["P2A36","P2A37","P2A32","P0688","U0108"],""],P2A36:["AFCM Power Relay Sense Circuit Low","P2A36 is set when the relay feeding the gas control module has been commanded on, yet the voltage read back after its contacts stays too low. Burnt or pitted contacts, a high-resistance joint, a grounded sense wire or a blown fuse in the switched path all lead there, as does a weak battery during cranking.",["Worn or burnt relay contacts","Blown fuse in the switched supply","Sense wire shorted to ground","Weak battery or poor main ground"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Gas mode drops out, bi-fuel vehicle switches to petrol","Communication fault with the gas module stored as well"],2,3,["P2A35","P2A37","P2A33","P0689","P0562"],""],P2A37:["AFCM Power Relay Sense Circuit High","Here the read-back line of the gas module supply relay carries voltage at a moment when it should not: the relay is commanded off, yet power is still present behind its contacts. A welded contact pair is the main suspect, followed by a sense wire touching another live circuit.",["Relay contacts welded closed","Sense wire shorted to another live circuit","Miswired retrofit gas installation feeding voltage back"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Battery drained after standing","Relay clicks are missing at ignition off"],2,1,["P2A35","P2A36","P2A34","P0690"],""],P2A38:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit/Open Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2A38 reports that the lead carrying positive current control for bank 1's third oxygen sensor has no continuity. That sensor sits behind a second converter or a later aftertreatment stage, and the code only makes sense where this position carries a wide-band probe: through this lead (pin APE/IP on a Bosch LSU 4.9) the controller drives between about −2 and +2.25 mA into the pump cell.",["Broken pump-current wire or pushed-back pin in the sensor plug","Sensor plug loose or not latched after exhaust work","Internal break in the pump cell of the probe"],["Check engine light","Sensor 3 value frozen near lambda 1 in live data","Downstream emission monitors not completed"],2,1,["P2A39","P2A3A","P2A3B","P22AB","P2237","P0142"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2A39:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2A39 is set when the pump-current lead feeding the rearmost wide-band probe on bank 1 (sensor 3) is pulled below its permitted window, typically because the wire rubs through to chassis ground near the hot rear exhaust section. At ignition-on Saab's 2010 9-5 shows roughly 2.8 V on the pump-current pins of its front probe, so a reading near zero points to a ground short. No manufacturer publishes P2A39 itself;",["Pump-current wire chafed through to body or exhaust bracket","Internal short in the probe after thermal shock or water ingress","Faulty sensor interface in the engine control module"],["Check engine light after repeated detection","Sensor 3 reading implausible or missing in live data"],2,1,["P2A38","P2A3A","P2A3C","P22AC","P0143"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2A3A:["O2 Sensor Positive Current Control Circuit High Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2A3A means the voltage on the pump-current (positive control) lead of probe number three, bank 1, sits above its expected level. The usual culprit is contact with a supply: the heater feed runs in the same harness and connector, and moisture or heat damage at the plug can bridge the two. An offset pump current would falsify the lambda value, so the controller stops trusting it.",["Pump-current wire touching the heater feed in harness or plug","Water or corrosion in the sensor connector under the car","Internal short between heater and pump cell of the probe"],["Check engine light after repeated detection","Sensor 3 reports an implausibly lean value"],2,1,["P2A38","P2A39","P2A3D","P22AD","P0144"],"זרם חיובי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2A3B:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit/Open Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2A3B points to a break in the negative current control line of wide-band sensor 3 on bank 1, the common return of pump and Nernst cell. Bosch calls it virtual ground (IPN/VM, pin 2 on the LSU 4.9), NTK names it COM; the controller holds it at a bias of about 2.5 V, as Saab's 2010 9-5 shows at the plug, so current can flow both ways. No manufacturer documents P2A3B publicly.",["Broken virtual-ground wire or loose pin in the sensor plug","Corroded terminals in the connector near the rear exhaust","Internal break of the common electrode inside the probe"],["Check engine light","Sensor 3 signal stuck around its mid voltage in live data","Catalyst or aftertreatment monitor not completed"],2,1,["P2A3C","P2A3D","P2A38","P22B2","P2251","P0142"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2A3C:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Low Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2A3C is stored when the virtual-ground return belonging to the third probe of bank 1 falls below its intended bias. Because this line normally floats around 2.5 V rather than at chassis potential, a chafed wire touching the body or an exhaust bracket drags it down and leaves the pump cell little room to reverse its current, so rich mixtures can hardly be measured. No manufacturer publishes P2A3C;",["Virtual-ground wire chafed through to chassis ground","Internal short from the common electrode to the sensor housing","Bias stage in the engine control module faulty"],["Check engine light after repeated detection","Downstream emission monitors stay incomplete"],2,1,["P2A3B","P2A3D","P2A39","P22B3","P0143"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2A3D:["O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit High Bank 1 Sensor 3","P2A3D flags the return line (virtual ground) of bank 1's sensor-3 wide-band probe as too high. Pulling this mid-level bias up to battery voltage usually takes a short to the heater supply, which shares the sensor plug, or water that has crept into a connector under the car. With its reference shifted, the controller can no longer centre the Nernst cell and rejects the lambda value.",["Virtual-ground wire shorted to the heater supply in harness or plug","Moisture bridging terminals in the sensor connector","Heater-to-electrode short inside a cracked probe"],["Check engine light after repeated detection","Sensor 3 lambda value rejected or shown as invalid"],2,1,["P2A3B","P2A3C","P2A3A","P22B4","P0144"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1, חיישן 3)"],P2A3E:["Alternative Fuel Delivery Error","P2A3E is the alternative fuel version of P0148: the system cannot supply the gas or propane quantity the engine asks for. Ford had already defined its own code P1048 with this wording, listed with a lamp in the 2014 Boss 302S OBD table.",["Gas or propane filter heavily restricted","Tank solenoid, rail solenoid or manual valve not fully open","Excess-flow valve on the tank tripped","Weak propane pump or pressure regulator not holding pressure","Tank pressure too low because the tank is nearly empty"],["Hesitation or stalling on gas","Automatic switch to petrol","Lean fuel trim codes stored as well","Warning lamp depending on manufacturer"],3,3,["P0148","P2A3F","P01A8","P2A23","P01A4"],""],P2A3F:["Excessive Time to Enter Alternative Fuel Control","On a bi-fuel or gas-start vehicle the control unit only changes over to gas once preconditions are met, for example warm coolant, enough pressure in the rail and a selected gas mode. P2A3F means this changeover did not happen within the calibrated time.",["Coolant warms up too slowly (thermostat stuck open, temperature sensor wrong)","Tank pressure too low for the switch-over","Regulator or vaporizer not heated enough by engine coolant","Tank or rail solenoid opening late or not at all"],["Vehicle keeps running on petrol much longer than usual","Gas indicator stays off or flashes","Check engine light, depending on calibration"],2,1,["P2A3E","P0125","P01A8","P019F"],""],P2A40:["Alternative Fuel System - Injector Leakage to Rail Detected","P2A40 reports that fuel is passing through an injector into a rail where it does not belong. The term fits dual-fuel direct injection, where one injector carries both diesel and gas: Caterpillar's patent US9422899B2 explains that the diesel is kept at a pressure equal to or a little above the gas to seal the gas needle, so liquid seeping into the nozzle space on the gas side is expected, and a check valve plus a…",["Worn internal seal or needle guide in a dual-fuel injector","Check valve between injector and gas rail leaking","Pressure difference between liquid and gas rail out of tolerance","Rail pressure sensor drifting and simulating a leak"],["Check engine light","Reduced power or operation on a single fuel","Rough running or smoke after a cold start"],4,3,["P2A3E","P01A4","P01A8","P0093","P22D9"],""],P2A41:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Pressure Sensor Circuit","Some multi-tank CNG installations give a second cylinder, tank B, its own pressure transducer, so the module knows the remaining gas per tank and can check that the tank valve responds. P2A41 is the general electrical fault of that sensor, set when the circuit is faulty without a clear verdict of low or high.",["Plug at the tank B sensor loose, corroded or harness damaged","Tank B pressure sensor faulty","5 V reference or sensor ground disturbed"],["Check engine light","Gas gauge wrong or showing empty","Tank B possibly no longer used"],3,1,["P2A42","P2A43","P2A44","P2A45","P019E"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A42:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Pressure Sensor Range/Performance","Unlike its electrical siblings, P2A42 deals with a tank B pressure reading that is electrically valid but makes no sense. Examples: the value does not fall while gas is drawn from tank B, it stays frozen after refuelling, or it differs clearly from the pressure of the other cylinders after a long stop, when all tanks connected to one fill line should settle at about the same level.",["Tank B pressure sensor drifting or stuck","Tank B solenoid stuck closed or manual valve shut","Contact resistance in the sensor connector shifting the signal"],["Check engine light","Gas gauge implausible after refuelling or driving","Reduced range on gas"],3,1,["P2A41","P2A43","P2A44","P2A23","P019F"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A43:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P2A43 is stored when the signal of the tank B pressure sensor drops below its lower electrical limit, a level that no real tank pressure produces. The usual reasons are a signal wire grounded against the frame, a missing 5 V reference or an internal short in the sensor.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","5 V reference open or pulled down by another sensor","Internal short in the tank B sensor"],["Check engine light","Gauge drops to empty for tank B","Less usable gas range"],3,1,["P2A41","P2A44","P2A42","P01A0"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A44:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Pressure Sensor Circuit High","The counterpart to P2A43: the voltage on the tank B pressure sensor signal sits above its valid range. TransEco, for the tank A sensor of its gas conversions, names an open sensor or a short to power as the cause of the High code, which matches the usual pull-up layout of such inputs where a broken signal or ground wire drives the reading upward.",["Sensor ground or signal wire open","Signal wire shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Tank B sensor faulty internally"],["Check engine light","Gauge stuck at full for tank B","Stumbling when tank B actually runs empty"],3,1,["P2A41","P2A43","P2A45","P01A1"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A45:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2A45 completes the tank B pressure group with the case that the other codes miss: the signal is mostly fine but jumps or drops out for moments, faster than any real gas pressure could change. Typical culprits are a plug that loses contact on rough roads, a wire rubbed through along the frame rail or a sensor with a cracked solder joint. Because the fault comes and goes, a single clean reading proves nothing.",["Tank B sensor plug with loose or corroded contacts","Harness chafed along frame or gas line","Intermittent internal fault in the sensor"],["Check engine light that comes and goes","Gas gauge flickering or jumping","Occasional unexpected switch to petrol on bi-fuel vehicles"],3,1,["P2A41","P2A42","P2A43","P2A44","P01A2","P2A4A"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A46:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Pressure Sensor Circuit","Larger CNG installations, for instance on trucks or buses, may carry three or more cylinders. Where a third one, tank C, has its own pressure transducer, P2A46 reports a general electrical fault in that sensor's circuit, stored when the module finds the signal unusable but cannot classify it as too low or too high.",["Wiring or plug at the tank C sensor damaged, loose or wet","Tank C pressure sensor faulty","Shared 5 V supply or sensor ground disturbed"],["Check engine light","Remaining gas shown wrongly","Tank C may be left unused"],3,1,["P2A47","P2A48","P2A49","P2A4A","P2A41","P019E"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A47:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Pressure Sensor Range/Performance","P2A47 is not about broken wires: the tank C sensor delivers a voltage inside its window, yet the pressure it reports cannot be true. Plausible tests are a value that stays flat while the engine draws gas from tank C, one that does not rise during filling, or a clear gap to tanks A and B after a long rest, since cylinders on a common fill manifold settle to similar pressure.",["Tank C sensor drifted or frozen at one value","Tank C solenoid not opening or manual valve closed","Corroded contacts shifting the signal"],["Check engine light","Gas level shown does not match refuelling or consumption","Shorter driving range on gas"],3,1,["P2A46","P2A48","P2A49","P2A27","P2A42","P019F"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A48:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","With P2A48 the voltage from the tank C pressure sensor has fallen beneath the lowest value a working sensor ever outputs, even with the cylinder empty. In such three-wire circuits a low reading points to the signal line touching ground, a dead 5 V supply or a short inside the transducer.",["Signal wire of the tank C sensor touching ground","5 V reference open or shorted by another sensor on the same line","Internal short in the tank C transducer"],["Check engine light","Tank C reported empty despite being filled","Less gas range than expected"],3,1,["P2A46","P2A49","P2A47","P2A43","P01A0"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A49:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P2A49 is the mirror image of P2A48: the tank C pressure signal sits above the band a healthy sensor uses, so the module rejects it. In TransEco's AFCM table the tank A equivalent traces back to a sensor with an open circuit or a short to the supply. An open ground is a classic trigger too, because the input is then pulled toward its supply rail. The practical danger is a cylinder that seems full when it is not;",["Ground or signal wire of the tank C sensor interrupted","Signal shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Tank C sensor open internally"],["Check engine light","Gauge for tank C stays at full","Hesitation once tank C really runs low"],3,1,["P2A46","P2A48","P2A4A","P2A44","P01A1"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A4A:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Unlike P2A48 or P2A49, which describe a signal stuck out of range, P2A4A covers a tank C pressure value that flickers: brief spikes, gaps or steps that no gas cylinder could produce, since pressure in a large tank changes only slowly.",["Connector pins at the tank C sensor with weak contact","Water ingress at a connector seal","Harness clip loose, cable rubbing"],["Check engine light appearing occasionally","Gas gauge jumps while driving","No noticeable effect between dropouts"],3,1,["P2A46","P2A47","P2A48","P2A49","P2A45","P01A2"],"חיישן לחץ מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A4B:["Alternative Fuel Temperature Sensor Circuit","Gaseous fuel changes density with temperature, so gas systems measure it to meter the right mass; Ford's 2003 bi-fuel CNG trucks, for example, use a thermistor at the rail for that density calculation and only switch to gas once both temperature and pressure allow it.",["Plug or wiring of the gas temperature sensor faulty","Temperature sensor element defective","Input stage or data link of the gas module disturbed"],["Check engine light","Bi-fuel vehicle stays on petrol or switches back","Rougher running on gas"],2,3,["P2A4C","P2A4D","P2A4E","P2A4F","P01B4","P01AA","P0180"],"חיישן טמפרטורת דלק חלופי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A4C:["Alternative Fuel Temperature Sensor Range/Performance","Here the gas temperature reading is electrically valid but implausible. A typical check compares it with other temperatures after a long cold soak, when gas, intake air and coolant should agree within a few degrees; another looks for the cooling that expansion in the regulator causes under heavy gas flow. A sensor that sticks at one value or lags far behind fails such tests.",["Sensor drifted, slow or stuck at one value","Sensor seated loosely or with poor thermal contact","Contact resistance in the connector"],["Check engine light after a drive cycle","Fuel trim off while running on gas","Often no noticeable driving issue"],2,1,["P2A4B","P2A4D","P2A4E","P2A4F","P01B5","P0181"],"חיישן טמפרטורת דלק חלופי — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A4D:["Alternative Fuel Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","P2A4D means the voltage of the gas temperature sensor is below its valid limit. Gas temperature sensors are normally NTC thermistors whose resistance drops as they warm up, so a low voltage would correspond to extremely hot gas; in practice it nearly always means the signal wire is grounded or the sensor is shorted inside.",["Signal wire of the gas temperature sensor shorted to ground","Thermistor shorted internally","Moisture bridging the connector pins"],["Check engine light","Gas mode refused, bi-fuel vehicle runs on petrol","Live data shows an implausibly hot gas temperature"],2,3,["P2A4B","P2A4E","P2A4C","P01B6","P0182"],"חיישן טמפרטורת דלק חלופי — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A4E:["Alternative Fuel Temperature Sensor Circuit High","The counterpart to P2A4D: the gas temperature signal rises above its upper limit. With the usual NTC thermistor fed through a pull-up resistor, that equals an absurdly cold reading, and the most frequent reason is an open circuit, either a broken wire, a loose terminal or a sensor that has gone open inside. A short to a voltage source has the same effect.",["Broken wire or loose terminal in the sensor circuit","Thermistor open internally","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source"],["Check engine light","Live data shows gas temperature at its coldest limit","Bi-fuel vehicle falls back to petrol"],2,3,["P2A4B","P2A4D","P2A4F","P01B7","P0183"],"חיישן טמפרטורת דלק חלופי — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A4F:["Alternative Fuel Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Temperature changes slowly, so a gas temperature reading that leaps by tens of degrees within moments is not physics but wiring. P2A4F is set for such spikes and dropouts of the gas temperature signal, while P2A4D and P2A4E cover signals that stay out of range.",["Fretting corrosion or loose terminal at the sensor plug","Wire broken inside its insulation near the regulator","Sensor element with intermittent contact"],["Check engine light that comes and goes","Short switches to petrol on bi-fuel vehicles","Jumping gas temperature in live data"],2,3,["P2A4B","P2A4C","P2A4D","P2A4E","P01B8","P0184"],"חיישן טמפרטורת דלק חלופי — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A50:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer A Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit","A vaporizer, often called reducer or converter on LPG systems, turns liquid gas into vapour with heat taken from the engine coolant. The sensor in P2A50 sits on the outlet side of vaporizer A and tells the control unit whether that unit is warm enough. Patent US7073489B2 explains why this matters: with too little heat the liquid does not fully evaporate and can block the regulator jet.",["Plug or wiring of the vaporizer A outlet sensor faulty","Outlet temperature sensor of vaporizer A defective","Input stage of the gas control module disturbed"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Vehicle stays on petrol or switches back from gas","Gas mode indicator flashes or stays off"],2,3,["P2A51","P2A52","P2A53","P2A54","P2A55","P2A5A","P2A8B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A51:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer A Outlet Temperature Sensor Range/Performance","P2A51 does not point to a broken wire: the outlet temperature of vaporizer A is electrically valid but does not fit the operating state. Typical tests compare it with coolant and ambient after a long stop, expect it to climb as the engine warms up, and expect a dip when heavy gas flow draws heat out of the unit. A value that freezes, drifts or lags badly fails such checks.",["Sensor drifts or sticks at one value","Sensor badly seated or mounted at an unsuitable point","Vaporizer A really too cold (low coolant, air in the circuit, stuck thermostat)"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Late or no switch-over to gas after a cold start","Uneven running or hesitation on gas"],2,1,["P2A50","P2A52","P2A53","P2A54","P2A56","P2A8B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A52:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer A Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","Temperature sensors of this type are usually thermistors whose resistance falls as they get warmer, the same principle Ford describes for the fuel rail sensor of its 2003 bi-fuel CNG trucks. A signal under the lower limit would therefore mean an impossibly hot vaporizer A; in practice the signal line touches ground or the sensor is shorted inside. AC STAG lists this case as a reducer temperature sensor short.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor shorted internally","Moisture or coolant in the connector"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Gas mode blocked, vehicle runs on petrol","Live data shows an implausibly hot vaporizer"],2,3,["P2A50","P2A51","P2A53","P2A54","P2A57"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A53:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer A Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit High","P2A53 is the opposite case: the voltage of the vaporizer A outlet sensor sits near the supply reference, which a thermistor input reads as extreme cold. A broken wire, an unplugged or corroded connector, an open sensor element or a short to a voltage source all produce this. AC STAG names the open variant a missing reducer temperature sensor.",["Wire broken or connector unplugged","Sensor element open inside","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","No switch-over to gas, bi-fuel vehicle stays on petrol","Live data shows a vaporizer far below freezing"],2,3,["P2A50","P2A51","P2A52","P2A54","P2A58"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A54:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer A Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","A vaporizer full of coolant has a lot of thermal mass, so its outlet temperature can only change gradually. P2A54 is set when the vaporizer A signal jumps, drops out briefly or flickers in a way no real temperature could; the fault may be gone by the time a technician looks. Loose or corroded pins, a wire chafing on a hot hose and engine vibration are the usual reasons.",["Loose or corroded connector pins","Wire chafing on a hose or bracket","Sensor with an internal loose contact"],["Intermittent check engine light, depending on calibration","Occasional switching back to petrol","Jumping vaporizer temperature in live data"],2,3,["P2A50","P2A51","P2A52","P2A53","P2A59"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ A — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A55:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer B Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit","A second vaporizer appears where one heat exchanger cannot supply enough gas, for instance on large or heavy-duty engines. On LNG trucks the job is harder still: Westport's patent CA2862664C starts from liquid near −160 °C, heats it with engine coolant and places a gas temperature sensor downstream of the exchanger to choose how the coolant flows.",["Plug or harness of the vaporizer B sensor damaged","Vaporizer B outlet sensor failed","Fault in the sensor input of the control module"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Reduced power or gas mode limited","Fall-back to the second fuel on dual-fuel engines"],2,3,["P2A56","P2A57","P2A58","P2A59","P2A50","P2A5A","P2A8C"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A56:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer B Outlet Temperature Sensor Range/Performance","With two vaporizers fed by the same coolant, their outlet temperatures should behave alike, which gives the module a natural cross-check. P2A56 means the vaporizer B reading is electrically fine but out of line with that expectation, with the engine state or with its own history.",["Vaporizer B sensor reads off or sluggishly","Vaporizer B gets too little coolant (air lock, kinked or blocked hose)","Sensor seated loosely in its port"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Power drop under high load on gas","Clear temperature gap between vaporizer A and B in live data"],2,1,["P2A55","P2A57","P2A58","P2A59","P2A51","P2A8C"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A57:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer B Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","P2A57 sets when the outlet sensor on vaporizer B pulls its signal below the lowest valid voltage. On a thermistor that loses resistance with heat, as in the Ford CNG rail sensor, this would mean extreme heat, so the realistic causes are a signal lead grounded against the chassis and an internally shorted sensor. Long harness runs, common when the gas parts sit far from the controller, add chafing points.",["Signal lead of the B sensor grounded","Vaporizer B sensor shorted internally","Insulation worn through on a long harness run"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Gas operation limited or switched off","Vaporizer B shown far hotter than vaporizer A"],2,3,["P2A55","P2A56","P2A58","P2A59","P2A52"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A58:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer B Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit High","Here the signal of the vaporizer B outlet sensor rests at or near the reference voltage, so the module would see a deep-frozen unit. Typical reasons are an open wire, a plug that has backed out, a sensor element that has failed open or a short to a supply line.",["Open wire or plug of the B sensor backed out","Vaporizer B sensor element open","Signal lead touching a supply line"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Gas delivery reduced or fall-back fuel used","Vaporizer B shown at an impossibly low temperature"],2,3,["P2A55","P2A56","P2A57","P2A59","P2A53"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A59:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer B Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","On heavy vehicles the gas hardware sees constant shaking, and long harness runs to the vaporizers add connectors that can loosen. P2A59 records that the vaporizer B outlet signal changed faster or more erratically than real temperature can, or kept dropping out for short moments. Such faults tend to come and go with road surface, engine speed or coolant heat.",["Connector of the B sensor loose or corroded","Harness damaged by vibration or strain","Intermittent contact inside the sensor"],["Check engine light comes and goes, depending on calibration","Sporadic switching to petrol","Flickering gas indicator"],2,3,["P2A55","P2A56","P2A57","P2A58","P2A54"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A5A:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer C Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit","Vaporizer C is the third unit in a gas system that splits the conversion of liquid fuel over several heat exchangers, a layout that only makes sense for engines with very high gas demand. Each unit needs its own outlet sensor because a vaporizer that cannot keep up shows it first by a falling outlet temperature;",["Connector or wiring of the vaporizer C sensor faulty","Vaporizer C outlet sensor broken","Control module input for sensor C faulty"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Gas operation limited, less power at high load","Vehicle falls back to the other fuel"],2,3,["P2A5B","P2A5C","P2A5D","P2A5E","P2A50","P2A55","P2A8D"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A5B:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer C Outlet Temperature Sensor Range/Performance","With three outlet sensors in one system, a plausibility check can use a majority: if A and B agree and C stands apart, vaporizer C or its sensor is the odd one out. P2A5B means the C value is electrically valid but fails such a comparison or does not follow warm-up and load as it should.",["Sensor C stuck, drifting or slow","Vaporizer C genuinely too cold from lack of coolant or fouling","Sensor without good thermal contact"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Power loss at full load on gas","Vaporizer C differs clearly from A and B in live data"],2,1,["P2A5A","P2A5C","P2A5D","P2A5E","P2A51","P2A56","P2A8D"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A5C:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer C Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","P2A5C stands for a vaporizer C outlet signal below the valid range. Since such inputs are normally NTC thermistors, the module would read an implausibly hot unit; a signal lead touching ground or a sensor shorted internally is far more likely. Coolant that has seeped into the connector can also create a path to ground.",["Signal lead of sensor C shorted to ground","Coolant or water in the connector","Sensor C shorted inside"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Gas operation blocked or limited","Vaporizer C shown far too hot"],2,3,["P2A5A","P2A5B","P2A5D","P2A5E","P2A57"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A5D:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer C Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit High","P2A5D says the vaporizer C sensor signal is stuck high, near the reference voltage, which reads as extreme cold. An interrupted wire, a disconnected or corroded plug, an open sensor or a short to battery voltage are the candidates. Gas controllers that use vaporizer temperature as a release condition, as AC STAG does before switching to gas, will hold off gas mode when they see such a value.",["Wire to sensor C interrupted or plug disconnected","Sensor C open inside","Signal lead shorted to battery voltage"],["Check engine light, depending on calibration","Gas mode held back or output reduced","Vaporizer C shown at extreme cold"],2,3,["P2A5A","P2A5B","P2A5C","P2A5E","P2A58"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A5E:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer C Outlet Temperature Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2A5E marks an unsteady vaporizer C signal: brief dropouts, spikes or a jagged trace that a coolant-heated part cannot really produce. The fault often clears itself and returns, so it matters what conditions trigger it. Gas controllers such as AC STAG store a frozen frame of the moment an error occurs; logging the three outlet temperatures side by side during a test drive shows quickly whether only C misbehaves.",["Connector of sensor C without firm grip","Contact pin pushed back in the housing","Cable rubbing on a bracket"],["Check engine light now and then, depending on calibration","Gas operation drops out occasionally","Spiky vaporizer C trace in recorded data"],2,3,["P2A5A","P2A5B","P2A5C","P2A5D","P2A59"],"חיישן טמפרטורת יציאת מאדה דלק חלופי‏ C — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A5F:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Level Sensor Circuit","How the content of a second gas tank is measured depends on the fuel. CNG has no liquid surface, so the level is worked out from pressure, often corrected by tank temperature; GM's 2015 Impala Bi-Fuel shows full near 3,600 psi and empty near 400 psi. LPG, being liquid, allows a float whose magnet passes its position through the tank wall to a Hall element, as in Rochester's R3D dials.",["Plug or wiring of the tank B sender faulty","Tank B level sender or Hall module defective","Reading module or data link to the engine module disturbed"],["Check engine light","Gauge ignores the content of tank B","Range estimate on gas too low"],2,1,["P2A60","P2A61","P2A62","P2A63","P2A64","P01AF","P2065"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A60:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Level Sensor Range/Performance","P2A60 flags a tank B level that is electrically valid but does not behave like a real fuel quantity: it fails to drop while gas is used from tank B, does not climb after filling, or swings wildly although the tank is at rest. Roush documents the stuck logic for its propane primary sender as P25B0, set when the value stays put over a considerable distance.",["Float arm in tank B bent or jammed (LPG)","Pressure or temperature input behind the calculated level drifting (CNG)","Contact resistance shifting the sender signal"],["Check engine light after several trips","Gas gauge does not move as fuel is used","Unexpected running out of gas"],2,1,["P2A5F","P2A61","P2A62","P2A63","P2A65","P01B0","P2066"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A61:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Level Sensor Circuit Low","P2A61 is stored when the tank B level signal falls below the smallest voltage the sender produces even with the tank empty. Roush's manual for its dual-tank propane trucks names a sender wire shorted to ground or a damaged sender as causes of the low case and adds that the second-tank code P2067 leaves only the primary tank on the gauge.",["Sender signal wire of tank B shorted to ground","Tank B sender damaged","Supply voltage of a Hall-type sender missing"],["Check engine light","Tank B shown empty or left out of the gauge","Shorter displayed gas range"],2,1,["P2A5F","P2A62","P2A60","P2A66","P01B1","P2067"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A62:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Level Sensor Circuit High","P2A62 is set when the tank B level signal climbs above the highest voltage a working sender delivers at full. For its dual-tank propane trucks Roush blames the high case on a disconnected sender or a wire shorted to more than 5 V, and with the second-tank code P2068 the gauge again falls back to the primary tank only. A broken ground at the sender gives the same picture on most pull-up inputs.",["Tank B sender unplugged or wire open","Sender ground interrupted","Signal wire shorted to a voltage above 5 V"],["Check engine light","Gauge shows only the primary tank","Content of tank B unknown to the driver"],2,1,["P2A5F","P2A61","P2A63","P2A67","P01B2","P2068"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A63:["Alternative Fuel Tank B Level Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","Fuel slosh makes any level reading wobble a little, and modules filter that out. P2A63 goes further: the tank B level signal drops out or jumps in steps no filter can explain, then returns to normal. Contacts at the sender are the main suspect, since the tank sits low on the chassis and is exposed to spray and road salt;",["Corroded contacts at the tank B sender from road spray","Cable pinched by a tank strap","Worn wiper track or loose Hall module in the sender"],["Gas gauge for tank B jumps or briefly drops","Check engine light from time to time","Range display unsteady"],2,1,["P2A5F","P2A60","P2A61","P2A62","P2A68","P01B3","P2069"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A64:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Level Sensor Circuit","A third gas tank, C, may have its own level input, either a real float sender in an LPG vessel or, on CNG, a value the module derives from that tank's pressure, the way Ford's 2003 bi-fuel trucks turned tank pressure into a gauge reading. P2A64 reports that the tank C level circuit is faulty without saying whether the signal is too low or too high; P2A66 and P2A67 make that distinction.",["Long harness run to tank C damaged or plug loose","Tank C sender defective","Fault in the tank C pressure input the level is derived from (CNG)"],["Check engine light","Gauge or range leaves out tank C","Otherwise normal driving"],2,1,["P2A65","P2A66","P2A67","P2A68","P2A5F","P2A46","P01AF"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A65:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Level Sensor Range/Performance","For tank C this code reports a level that stays within the valid voltage window yet contradicts what happens to the tank. Examples are a reading that remains unchanged over many kilometres although tank C supplies the engine, no rise after a fill, or a level that disagrees with the pressure in a CNG cylinder. With LPG a float that sticks or a sender fitted at the wrong angle are likely;",["Float in tank C sticking or sender mounted at a wrong angle (LPG)","Pressure or temperature input of tank C drifting (CNG)","Contact resistance shifting the level signal"],["Check engine light after several trips","Level for tank C frozen or illogical","Range estimate unreliable"],2,1,["P2A64","P2A66","P2A67","P2A68","P2A60","P2A47","P01B0"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A66:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Level Sensor Circuit Low","P2A66 says the tank C level signal is below its lower electrical bound. With voltage-output senders that typically comes from a signal wire grounded somewhere along its route, a sender shorted inside, or a missing supply to a ratiometric Hall module such as those Rochester builds for LPG vessels, which needs a few volts to produce any output.",["Tank C sender signal wire grounded","No supply voltage at a Hall-type sender","Tank C sender shorted internally"],["Check engine light","Tank C displayed as empty","Refuelling earlier than needed"],2,1,["P2A64","P2A67","P2A65","P2A61","P01B1"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A67:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Level Sensor Circuit High","P2A67 is the high-side partner of P2A66: the tank C level voltage lies above anything a correctly working sender outputs at full. An unplugged connector, a broken signal or ground wire and a short to a supply voltage all push the input there. Roush names such faults for the high case of its propane senders and notes for the second-tank code P2068 that only the primary tank is then shown;",["Tank C sender plug loose or knocked off","Signal or ground wire broken","Signal shorted to a supply voltage"],["Check engine light","Tank C missing from the gauge","Driver unsure about remaining gas"],2,1,["P2A64","P2A66","P2A68","P2A62","P01B2"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A68:["Alternative Fuel Tank C Level Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","The last code of this block covers a tank C level signal that flickers: it is valid most of the time but suffers short gaps or jumps unrelated to fuel movement. On vehicles with three tanks the wiring to tank C is often the longest and has the most joints, each a chance for a loose crimp or green corrosion; frame flex can open a fractured conductor for an instant.",["Loose crimp or corroded joint in the long tank C harness","Conductor fractured, opening under frame flex","Unsteady tank C pressure input behind a calculated level (CNG)"],["Tank C level jumps on the display","Check engine light now and then","Range display unsteady"],2,1,["P2A64","P2A65","P2A66","P2A67","P2A63","P2A4A","P01B3"],"חיישן מפלס מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A69:["Alternative Fuel Rail Pressure Regulator Inlet Pressure Sensor Circuit","On a gaseous-fuel engine, the rail pressure regulator takes gas straight from the storage cylinders and steps it down for the injector rail. P2A69 covers the transducer on the high-pressure side of that regulator, set when its circuit is faulty without a clear low or high verdict. GM's 2015 Impala bi-fuel mounts a three-wire sensor on top of the regulator that reads cylinder pressure as high as 3,600 psi;",["Connector or harness at the regulator damaged by heat, vibration or corrosion","Inlet pressure transducer on the regulator faulty","5 V reference or sensor ground disturbed","Engine or alternative fuel control module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Gas mode not available, bi-fuel vehicle stays on petrol","Gas gauge implausible or showing empty"],2,3,["P2A6A","P2A6B","P2A6C","P2A6D","P2A6E","P2A6F","P01A0"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת וסת לחץ מסילת דלק חלופית — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A6A:["Alternative Fuel Rail Pressure Regulator Inlet Pressure Sensor Range/Performance","P2A6A flags a regulator inlet pressure reading that is electrically valid but implausible. Upstream of the regulator the value should fall slowly as gas is burned, jump after refuelling and, with the engine at rest, roughly equal cylinder pressure. A reading that stays frozen, climbs while driving, or sits below the regulated rail pressure although the engine runs normally points to a drifting transducer.",["Inlet pressure transducer drifted or contaminated by oil carried in the gas","Manual or solenoid tank valve closed, so the reading does not change","Contact resistance in connector shifts the signal"],["Check engine light on","Gas gauge does not match the actual fill level","Unexpected switch to petrol or gas mode refused"],2,3,["P2A69","P2A6B","P2A6C","P2A6D","P2A6E","P2A6F","P01A4"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת וסת לחץ מסילת דלק חלופית — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A6B:["Alternative Fuel Rail Pressure Regulator Inlet Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P2A6B is stored when the signal voltage of the regulator inlet pressure sensor drops below its valid band. With a typical three-wire transducer (5 V feed, signal, ground) that means a signal lead shorted to ground, a lost 5 V reference or a failed sensor element. A low voltage would read as an almost empty cylinder, so a bi-fuel vehicle may refuse gas mode or show an empty gauge with a full tank;",["Signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","5 V reference open or pulled down by another sensor on the same feed","Inlet pressure transducer internally shorted"],["Check engine light on","Gas gauge shows empty although the tank is full","Gas mode refused, bi-fuel vehicle runs on petrol"],2,3,["P2A69","P2A6A","P2A6C","P2A6D","P01A0"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת וסת לחץ מסילת דלק חלופית — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A6C:["Alternative Fuel Rail Pressure Regulator Inlet Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P2A6C means the regulator inlet pressure signal sits above its plausible voltage ceiling. Typical causes are a signal wire touching a 5 V or battery-voltage circuit, an open sensor ground, an open signal line that the module pulls up internally (depending on its design), or an internal transducer fault.",["Sensor ground open or connector terminal pushed out","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Inlet pressure transducer internally faulty"],["Check engine light on","Gas gauge stuck at full regardless of consumption","Gas mode blocked, bi-fuel vehicle switches to petrol"],2,3,["P2A69","P2A6A","P2A6B","P2A6D","P2A6F","P01A1"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת וסת לחץ מסילת דלק חלופית — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A6D:["Alternative Fuel Rail Pressure Regulator Inlet Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2A6D is the dropout code of the regulator inlet pressure sensor: the signal jumps or briefly vanishes, but not long enough for a steady low or high verdict. The regulator normally lives in the engine bay, next to the right-hand strut mount on GM's 2015 Impala bi-fuel, and Blackstone requires warm engine coolant to circulate through its SAN209 unit so that it does not ice up.",["Loose or widened terminal in the sensor connector","Condensation or corrosion in the plug near the coolant-heated regulator","Harness rubbing on hoses or brackets with intermittent contact"],["Check engine light on, sometimes clearing again","Gas gauge flickers or jumps","Sporadic switch from gas to petrol while driving"],2,3,["P2A69","P2A6A","P2A6B","P2A6C","P01A2"],"חיישן לחץ כניסת וסת לחץ מסילת דלק חלופית — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A6E:["Alternative Fuel Rail Pressure Regulator Inlet Pressure Too Low","P2A6E is not a wiring fault: the inlet pressure sensor works, but the gas reaching the regulator is too weak for it to hold rail pressure. A regulator can only reduce pressure, so once the supply approaches its outlet setpoint, rail pressure sinks with it. ITT's CNG regulator patent addresses exactly this low-supply phase with a bypass that opens below a set inlet pressure.",["Gas cylinder nearly empty","Tank solenoid or manual shut-off valve not fully open","High-pressure filter clogged or line restricted","Inlet pressure sensor reading too low within its range"],["Check engine light on","Loss of power or stumbling in gas mode, especially at high load","Automatic switch to petrol or engine stalls on dedicated gas engines"],3,3,["P2A6F","P2A69","P2A6A","P01A8","P240E"],"לחץ כניסת וסת לחץ מסילת דלק חלופית — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2A6F:["Alternative Fuel Rail Pressure Regulator Inlet Pressure Too High","P2A6F reports a regulator inlet pressure above the calibrated maximum. Only cylinder pressure is present upstream of the regulator, so a genuinely high value usually comes from the tank side, such as overfilling at a dispenser without temperature compensation or a cold-filled cylinder that later warms up strongly; a transducer reading high but still in range is the other option.",["Inlet pressure sensor reading too high within its range","Cylinder overfilled or strongly warmed after a cold fill","Sensor or calibration not matching the installed cylinder pressure rating"],["Check engine light on","Gas mode blocked as a precaution","Often appears right after refuelling"],3,3,["P2A6E","P2A69","P2A6A","P2A6C","P01A9"],"לחץ כניסת וסת לחץ מסילת דלק חלופית — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2A70:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Fuel Pump Select Valve Control Circuit","Some heavy-duty LNG systems do not drive the cryogenic tank pump directly but through hydraulics: an engine- or motor-driven hydraulic pump supplies oil to a reciprocating hydraulic drive on each tank pump. Westport's patent US8726785B2 shows two LNG vessels whose pumps sit inside the tanks, plus a selector valve that the controller switches to decide which pump receives hydraulic flow.",["Damaged harness or connector at the select valve on the frame","Select valve solenoid coil faulty","Output stage in the controlling module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Fuel drawn from one LNG tank only, range reduced","Loss of gas supply, dual-fuel engine falls back to diesel-only or derates"],3,3,["P2A71","P2A72","P2A73","P2A74","P2A75"],"שסתום בחירת משאבת דלק הידראולית דלק חלופי — תקלה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A71:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Fuel Pump Select Valve Control Range/Performance","P2A71 concerns the function of the hydraulic fuel pump select valve rather than its wiring: the circuit is intact, but the system does not respond as expected after a switch command. In Westport's design the controller links the hydraulic pressure it measures to whichever pump the selector valve should be feeding;",["Valve spool sticking due to contaminated hydraulic oil","Worn valve leaking internally, flow reaches both pumps","Solenoid force too low, for example from low supply voltage"],["Check engine light on","Tank changeover does not happen or happens late","Uneven LNG levels between tanks"],4,3,["P2A70","P2A72","P2A73","P2A74","P2A76"],"בקרת שסתום בחירת משאבת דלק הידראולית דלק חלופי — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A72:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Fuel Pump Select Valve Control Circuit Low","P2A72 is set when the control circuit of the hydraulic fuel pump select valve reads lower than expected for the commanded state. On a low-side driver this typically means the control wire is shorted to ground, so the valve coil may stay energised; on a high-side driver a short to ground or a shorted coil pulls the output down and may trip its protection.",["Control wire chafed on the frame and shorted to ground","Select valve coil with shorted turns","Water in the connector bridging to ground"],["Check engine light on","Select valve stays switched, one tank pump runs permanently","Gas supply interrupted when the active tank runs empty"],3,3,["P2A70","P2A71","P2A73","P2A74"],"שסתום בחירת משאבת דלק הידראולית דלק חלופי — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A73:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Fuel Pump Select Valve Control Circuit High","P2A73 signals that the select valve control circuit sits at a higher voltage than the commanded state allows. Typical faults are an open coil or broken wire on a low-side driven valve, which leaves the line at supply voltage, or a short to battery voltage that the output cannot pull down. The valve then stays in its spring-return position, so hydraulic flow keeps going to one tank pump whatever the command.",["Valve coil or control wire open","Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Corroded connector pins with very high resistance"],["Check engine light on","Second LNG tank not used, range clearly shorter","Gas supply stops although fuel remains"],3,3,["P2A70","P2A71","P2A72","P2A74"],"שסתום בחירת משאבת דלק הידראולית דלק חלופי — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A74:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Fuel Pump Select Valve Control Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2A74 covers brief, recurring faults in the select valve control circuit that clear before a firm low or high verdict. On LNG trucks the valve usually sits near the tank-mounted pump and hydraulic lines, where frame flex, road spray and very cold surfaces around the cryogenic tank stress connectors and insulation. A valve that drops out for a moment can cut hydraulic flow to the working pump mid-stroke;",["Loose terminal in the select valve connector","Moisture or ice in the connector near the cryogenic tank","Harness chafed along the frame rail with intermittent contact"],["Check engine light on, may go out again","Brief hesitation or pressure dips in gas mode","Irregular tank changeover"],3,3,["P2A70","P2A71","P2A72","P2A73"],"שסתום בחירת משאבת דלק הידראולית דלק חלופי — אות לא יציב במעגל הבקרה"],P2A75:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit","In a hydraulically driven LNG pump system the controller watches the oil pressure delivered by the hydraulic pump. Westport's patent US8726785B2 places this sensor in the supply line between the hydraulic pump outlet and the hydraulic drive, using it for three jobs: reversing the drive at each stroke end, spotting an empty tank when peak pressure stays low, and flagging leaks or other abnormal conditions.",["Connector or harness at the hydraulic pressure sensor damaged","Hydraulic pump pressure sensor faulty","Sensor supply or ground disturbed"],["Check engine light on","LNG pump stops or strokes irregularly, gas pressure drops","Dual-fuel engine runs on diesel only or with reduced power"],3,3,["P2A76","P2A77","P2A78","P2A79","P2A7A","P2A70"],"חיישן לחץ משאבה הידראולית דלק חלופי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A76:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pump Pressure Sensor Range/Performance","P2A76 is set when the hydraulic pump pressure reading looks electrically sound yet makes no sense for the operating state. Westport's patent explains why a fixed expectation is not enough: pressure rises with hydraulic pump speed, which follows engine speed when the pump is engine-driven, and with the LNG pressure the cryogenic pump works against.",["Hydraulic pressure sensor drifted","Low hydraulic oil level or external leak","Worn hydraulic pump or drive seals"],["Check engine light on","Uneven LNG pressure or slow pressure build-up","Empty-tank warning although LNG remains"],4,3,["P2A75","P2A77","P2A78","P2A79","P2A7B","P2A71"],"חיישן לחץ משאבה הידראולית דלק חלופי — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A77:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P2A77 is set when the signal from the hydraulic pump pressure sensor drops below the range a working sensor can deliver, typically because the signal wire or the 5 V reference is shorted to ground or the reference feed is open.",["Signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","5 V reference open or pulled to ground","Pressure sensor failed internally"],["Warning lamp with false empty-tank indication","Unexpected switching between LNG tanks","Gas supply stopped or reduced engine power"],3,3,["P2A75","P2A76","P2A78","P2A79","P2A7C"],"חיישן לחץ משאבה הידראולית דלק חלופי — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A78:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P2A78 indicates that the hydraulic pump pressure sensor reports a voltage above its plausible maximum, as happens when the signal line touches the reference or battery voltage or the sensor ground is open. A false high reading is critical for the pump cycle, because rising oil pressure is the usual cue that a stroke has ended: Caterpillar's patent US9228574B2 names this as the conventional way to reverse the drive.",["Sensor ground open or corroded at the connector","Signal wire shorted to reference or battery voltage","Pressure sensor failed with output at full scale"],["Warning lamp and very short or no pump strokes","Falling gas pressure and loss of power","Engine switches to reduced power or stops on gas"],3,3,["P2A75","P2A76","P2A77","P2A79","P2A7D"],"חיישן לחץ משאבה הידראולית דלק חלופי — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A79:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pump Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2A79 records a hydraulic pump pressure signal that jumps or drops out for short moments without staying low or high long enough for P2A77 or P2A78. In a reciprocating LNG pump the controller reads this sensor continuously to find each stroke end, so a single spike can be mistaken for the end of travel and a brief dropout for a missing pressure peak.",["Loose or fractured crimp terminal in the sensor circuit","Moisture or ice in the sensor plug","Harness damaged by vibration at the hydraulic unit"],["Uneven fuel pressure or surging power on gas","Sporadic warning lamp that clears again","Occasional false empty-tank message"],3,3,["P2A75","P2A77","P2A78","P2A7E","P2A70"],"חיישן לחץ משאבה הידראולית דלק חלופי — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A7A:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pressure Sensor Circuit","P2A7A is the general circuit fault of the alternative fuel hydraulic pressure sensor, a measuring point that the code list keeps apart from the hydraulic pump pressure sensor of P2A75. Where it sits is not defined publicly, and no manufacturer documents the split.",["Damaged connector or harness at the hydraulic sensor","Hydraulic pressure sensor faulty","Fault in a sensor reference or ground shared with other sensors"],["Warning lamp on","Reduced LNG delivery or power limitation"],3,3,["P2A7B","P2A7C","P2A7D","P2A7E","P2A75"],"חיישן לחץ הידראולי דלק חלופי — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2A7B:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pressure Sensor Range/Performance","P2A7B covers a hydraulic pressure signal that is electrically valid but does not fit the operating state. Plausibility can be judged because pressures in the hydraulic drive of an LNG pump follow a known pattern: during a stroke the working side carries load pressure, while the return side stays close to reservoir level until the valve reverses.",["Sensor drift or offset","Sensor port blocked by contaminated oil","Restricted return line or filter raising return pressure"],["Warning lamp after several drive cycles","Irregular pump strokes or reduced power on gas"],4,3,["P2A7A","P2A7C","P2A7D","P2A7E","P2A76"],"חיישן לחץ הידראולי דלק חלופי — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A7C:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pressure Sensor Circuit Low","P2A7C is set when the hydraulic pressure sensor signal falls below its valid band, most often from a signal wire grounded against the chassis, an open 5 V reference or a sensor with an internal short. If this sensor watches the return side, as in one of Caterpillar's layouts, a dead-low reading would hardly stand out at first, since return pressure is low anyway;",["Signal wire grounded against chassis or hydraulic lines","Open 5 V reference to the sensor","Sensor shorted internally"],["Warning lamp on","Pump stops or delivers less LNG","Additional sensor codes if the reference is shared"],3,3,["P2A7A","P2A7B","P2A7D","P2A7E","P2A77"],"חיישן לחץ הידראולי דלק חלופי — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2A7D:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pressure Sensor Circuit High","P2A7D means the hydraulic pressure sensor reads above its upper limit, typically because the signal line is touches the reference or battery supply, or its ground connection is broken. Unlike P2A7C, this fault is obvious at once: a full-scale reading while the pump is idle or retracting contradicts every other input.",["Sensor ground open or high resistance","Signal line shorted to reference or battery voltage","Sensor output stuck at maximum"],["Warning lamp on","Erratic or stopped pump strokes","Reduced power on gas"],3,3,["P2A7A","P2A7B","P2A7C","P2A7E","P2A78"],"חיישן לחץ הידראולי דלק חלופי — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2A7E:["Alternative Fuel Hydraulic Pressure Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2A7E flags a hydraulic pressure sensor signal that breaks up or spikes briefly, then recovers before the low or high checks of P2A7C and P2A7D mature. Pressure in a pump drive pulses with every stroke anyway, so the controller has to tell genuine pressure swings from electrical noise; what it treats as erratic is a change faster than the hydraulics can produce, or a signal vanishing between strokes.",["Loose terminal in the sensor connector","Wiring rubbing on hydraulic hoses","Condensation or ice near the cryogenic tank"],["Warning lamp that comes and goes","Uneven pump cycling or brief power dips"],3,3,["P2A7A","P2A7B","P2A7C","P2A7D","P2A79"],"חיישן לחץ הידראולי דלק חלופי — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2A7F:["Alternative Fuel Pump A Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit/Open","Hydraulically driven LNG pumps use solenoid valves to admit high-pressure oil to the drive side for the compression stroke and to vent it again for refilling. Caterpillar's patent US10060421B2 gives each of its six pumping elements, other counts being possible, a solenoid pilot that moves a spool between fill and drain positions; the controller sets timing and length of every stroke this way.",["Open wire or loose connector at valve A","Solenoid coil of valve A burnt open","Output stage in the control module faulty"],["Warning lamp on","Reduced LNG delivery and lower power","Gas pressure drops under load"],3,3,["P2A80","P2A81","P2A82","P2A83","P2A87"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A80:["Alternative Fuel Pump A Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2A80 concerns the compression stroke valve of pump A when its circuit is intact but the outcome of a command does not match. In the patented multi-element design, the time the solenoid holds the spool in the fill position sets the stroke, and a shorter command yields a partial stroke; the controller therefore expects a defined gain in gas pressure or hydraulic load per activation.",["Spool of valve A sticking or slow","Contaminated or varnished hydraulic oil","Weak return spring in the valve"],["Warning lamp after several drive cycles","Uneven gas pressure and slight power loss"],4,3,["P2A7F","P2A81","P2A82","P2A84","P2A88"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2A81:["Alternative Fuel Pump A Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit Low","P2A81 is stored when the control circuit of pump A's compression stroke valve sits lower than the commanded state allows. With a low-side driver this mostly points to the control wire touching ground, which can energise the solenoid permanently; with a high-side driver a coil with shorted turns or a grounded feed pulls the output down until its protection trips.",["Control wire of valve A shorted to ground","Shorted turns in the solenoid coil","Water in the valve connector"],["Warning lamp on","Pump A stops delivering, power drops at high load"],3,3,["P2A7F","P2A80","P2A82","P2A85","P2A89"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A82:["Alternative Fuel Pump A Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit High","P2A82 shows the drive line to pump A's compression stroke valve at a higher level than the commanded state permits, most likely because the coil winding or its wire is broken where the valve is switched to ground, or because the line touches battery voltage and the output stage loses control of it.",["Open coil or broken wire at valve A","Control wire shorted to battery voltage","Corroded valve connector"],["Warning lamp on","Falling gas pressure and power loss","Engine may stall on gas with a single pump element"],3,3,["P2A7F","P2A80","P2A81","P2A86","P2A8A"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A83:["Alternative Fuel Pump B Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit/Open","P2A83 reports an open or otherwise faulty control circuit at the compression stroke valve of alternative fuel pump B. Whether a second pump exists depends on the layout: in Westport's patent US8726785B2, two LNG vessels each carry their own hydraulically driven pump, while Caterpillar's multi-element pump splits one unit into several separately switched elements.",["Open wire or loose connector at valve B","Solenoid coil of valve B open","Output stage for valve B faulty"],["Warning lamp on","LNG in one tank cannot be used","Reduced power under high load"],3,3,["P2A84","P2A85","P2A86","P2A7F","P2A87"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A84:["Alternative Fuel Pump B Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2A84 is set when pump B's compression stroke valve is electrically sound yet the pump does not respond as commanded. A controller that drives several pumps or elements in turn can compare them: in Caterpillar's multi-element patent, flow results from how often the elements are fired and how long each waits, so an element adding less pressure per command than its neighbours stands out.",["Spool of valve B slow or leaking internally","Contaminated hydraulic oil","Worn plunger seals on the cryogenic side of pump B"],["Warning lamp after several drive cycles","Lower delivery from one tank or element"],4,3,["P2A83","P2A85","P2A86","P2A80","P2A88"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2A85:["Alternative Fuel Pump B Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit Low","P2A85 means the drive output for pump B's compression stroke valve reads too low for its commanded state. Typical are a control wire chafed through to the frame, which can keep the solenoid energised even when the controller wants it off, or a coil with shorted windings that draws excessive current. A valve stuck in the fill position leaves pump B's plunger parked at full extension;",["Control wire of valve B chafed through to the frame","Coil of valve B with shorted windings","Output stage for valve B shorted"],["Warning lamp on","Pump B delivers nothing, reduced power or range"],3,3,["P2A83","P2A84","P2A86","P2A81","P2A89"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A86:["Alternative Fuel Pump B Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit High","P2A86 is stored when pump B's compression stroke valve circuit shows a higher voltage than its state allows, pointing to an interrupted coil, a broken return wire where the valve is switched on the ground side, or a short to the supply. The valve then rests in its drain position: drive oil bypasses pump B and its plunger stays retracted.",["Open coil or broken wire at valve B","Control wire shorted to supply voltage","Corroded terminals in the valve B plug"],["Warning lamp on","One LNG tank is no longer emptied","Shorter range on gas"],3,3,["P2A83","P2A84","P2A85","P2A82","P2A8A"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A87:["Alternative Fuel Pump C Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit/Open","P2A87 covers the control circuit of the compression stroke valve on alternative fuel pump C, reporting an open or otherwise unusable circuit. A third pump valve only exists on systems with at least three separately switched pumping units.",["Open wire or loose connector at valve C","Solenoid coil of valve C open","Output stage for valve C faulty"],["Warning lamp on","Uneven gas pressure, slight power loss at high load"],3,3,["P2A88","P2A89","P2A8A","P2A7F","P2A83"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A88:["Alternative Fuel Pump C Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2A88 reports that the compression stroke valve of pump C works electrically but its effect does not match the command. In a sequenced multi-element pump, each activation should add a similar amount of pressure to the gas accumulator or rail; an element that keeps falling short, or whose share fluctuates, stands out against its neighbours.",["Deposits making the spool of valve C open late","Partly blocked oil passage to element C","Worn cryogenic seals on element C"],["Warning lamp after several drive cycles","Little noticeable change in driving"],4,3,["P2A87","P2A89","P2A8A","P2A80","P2A84"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2A89:["Alternative Fuel Pump C Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit Low","P2A89 is set when the drive circuit of pump C's compression stroke valve reads low for the commanded state. Most often the control wire has found a path to ground, so the solenoid may stay on, or the coil has shorted turns and pushes the output stage into current limiting. A valve stuck in fill keeps pressurised oil behind element C; that element stops cycling, and the others have to carry its share.",["Control wire of valve C shorted to ground","Shorted turns in the coil of valve C"],["Warning lamp on","Reduced power at high load"],3,3,["P2A87","P2A88","P2A8A","P2A81","P2A85"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A8A:["Alternative Fuel Pump C Compression Stroke Valve Control Circuit High","P2A8A indicates that pump C's compression stroke valve circuit sits higher than the commanded state allows, from an open coil, a broken wire or a short to the supply rail. The solenoid cannot shift the spool, which stays in the drain position, and element C never starts a compression stroke. Unlike the low fault P2A89, nothing stays pressurised;",["Open coil or broken wire at valve C","Fault in the supply or ground shared by the pump valves","Control wire shorted to the supply rail"],["Warning lamp on","Uneven gas pressure at high load"],3,3,["P2A87","P2A88","P2A89","P2A82","P2A86"],"שסתום מהלך דחיסת משאבת דלק חלופית‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A8B:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer A Performance","P2A8B means vaporizer A is not doing its job well enough, rather than reporting a wiring fault. On LPG engines this unit, also called reducer or converter, draws engine coolant heat to turn liquid gas into vapour at a steady pressure. Patent US7073489B2 explains the risk: evaporation chills the converter, the chill grows with gas flow, and an underheated unit can ice up until its regulator jet blocks.",["Too little coolant reaching vaporizer A (air lock, kinked hose, thermostat stuck open)","Worn diaphragm or seat in the pressure stage of vaporizer A","Oily residues from the gas clogging the vaporizer chambers","Outlet temperature sensor reading wrong but still within range"],["Check engine or gas warning lamp on","System stays on petrol longer after a cold start or falls back to petrol under load","Hesitation, rough running or stalling after coasting on gas","Frost or condensation on the vaporizer body"],3,3,["P2A8C","P2A8D","P2A50","P2A51"],"מאדה דלק חלופי‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A8C:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer B Performance","P2A8C flags vaporizer B as underperforming: the gas leaving it is colder, or less completely vaporized, than the module expects for the current flow. With LNG the temperature gap is extreme, and Westport's patent CA2862664C describes the typical failure. At a cold start, at idle or under light load coolant crawls through the exchanger and can freeze inside it;",["Coolant partly frozen inside vaporizer B after cold start or long idling","Valve that switches between parallel and counter flow stuck","Low coolant level or too little antifreeze in the mixture","Deposits reducing heat transfer in vaporizer B"],["Malfunction lamp on","Reduced power or gas mode blocked, especially when cold","Ice on the vaporizer or gas lines behind it"],4,3,["P2A8B","P2A8D","P2A55","P2A56"],"מאדה דלק חלופי‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A8D:["Alternative Fuel Vaporizer C Performance","P2A8D concerns a third vaporizer, found where large engines or several fuel branches need more heat exchange than one or two units provide. The code means unit C turns too little liquid into usable gas, or delivers it too cold, while its outlet sensor works. Where A and B run under the same conditions, the module can single out C by comparison, and that is the likely logic, though no maker publishes it.",["Coolant branch to vaporizer C restricted or unbalanced against A and B","Fouled heat exchange passages in vaporizer C","Pressure stage of vaporizer C sticking or leaking internally","Outlet sensor of C drifting so that the comparison fails"],["Warning lamp on, often with little noticeable change in driving","Loss of power at high load when all vaporizers are needed","One vaporizer housing noticeably colder than the others"],4,3,["P2A8B","P2A8C","P2A5A","P2A5B"],"מאדה דלק חלופי‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A8E:["Alternative Fuel Pump A Performance","P2A8E reports that alternative fuel pump A no longer delivers what it should, a mechanical or hydraulic fault rather than an electrical one. Such pumps move liquid fuel, typically LNG out of a cryogenic tank.",["Worn dynamic piston seals in pump A","Leaking inlet or outlet check valve of pump A","Hydraulic drive of pump A delivering too little force or speed","Impurities in the fuel passing the filter and damaging the pump"],["Malfunction lamp on","Power loss at high load, gas pressure sagging","Pump runs noticeably longer to refill the accumulator","Engine switched to reduced output or diesel-only operation"],4,3,["P2A8F","P2A90","P2A7F","P2A80"],"משאבת דלק חלופית‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A8F:["Alternative Fuel Pump B Performance","P2A8F applies to a second alternative fuel pump whose output has fallen short of expectations. Layouts with two pumps usually give each LNG vessel its own pump, a redundancy Westport's documents mention explicitly. In US20080302111A1, a selector valve decides which pump delivers, and once the controller judges one pump degraded it can switch to the other.",["Worn seals reducing the delivery of pump B","Tank served by pump B almost empty, mimicking a weak pump","Broken drive shaft or coupling between hydraulic drive and pump B"],["Malfunction lamp on","Usable range shorter, fuel left in one tank","System changes to the other tank earlier than usual"],4,3,["P2A8E","P2A90","P2A83","P2A84"],"משאבת דלק חלופית‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A90:["Alternative Fuel Pump C Performance","P2A90 marks pump C of the alternative fuel system as delivering too little. A third pump may belong to a further tank or, in Caterpillar's design US10060421B2, be one of several pumping elements driven in sequence.",["Vapour at the inlet of pump C after warm soak, causing cavitation","Worn seals or valves in pump C","Clogged inlet strainer or filter ahead of pump C"],["Warning lamp on","Weak pull or hesitation shortly after a long stop","Gas pressure recovers slowly after heavy acceleration"],4,3,["P2A8E","P2A8F","P2A87","P2A88"],"משאבת דלק חלופית‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A91:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve A Control Circuit/Open","A tank select valve decides which storage vessel feeds the fuel system. That sets it apart from a tank shutoff valve (P224C, P2A22 and onward), which simply opens or isolates one cylinder, and from the hydraulic fuel pump select valve (P2A70 and onward), which routes drive oil to a pump.",["Loose connector or broken wire to select valve A","Burnt-out solenoid coil of valve A","Faulty output stage in the alternative fuel module"],["Malfunction lamp on","Only one tank is used, range noticeably shorter","Fuel gauge shows content left although the engine runs short of gas"],3,3,["P2A92","P2A93","P2A94","P2A95","P2A99","P224C","P2A70"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A92:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve A Control Performance","P2A92 is the functional check for tank select valve A: the wiring tests pass, yet the fuel system does not behave as if the commanded vessel were connected. Software can judge this only through pressures.",["Select valve A sticking from dirt, ice or wear","Valve A leaking across its seat so both vessels are drawn","Tank pressure sensor giving a misleading reading"],["Malfunction lamp on","Tanks empty unevenly or in the wrong order","Short gas supply although one vessel still holds fuel"],4,3,["P2A91","P2A93","P2A94","P2A96","P2A9A","P019E"],"בקרת שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2A93:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve A Control Circuit Low","P2A93 is stored when the module measures a voltage on the control line of tank select valve A that falls short of the level expected for the commanded state. With a low-side driver this usually means the line touches ground, which can energise the solenoid permanently and keep valve A in its switched position regardless of the command.",["Control wire of valve A chafed through to ground","Condensation or water in the connector of valve A","Shorted turns in the coil of valve A"],["Malfunction lamp on","Tank selection stuck, one vessel emptied completely","Fuse or output protection of the gas module trips"],3,3,["P2A91","P2A92","P2A94","P2A97","P2A9B"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A94:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve A Control Circuit High","P2A94 reports a control voltage at tank select valve A above what the module expects for the commanded state. On a valve switched to ground by the module, an open coil or broken lead leaves the line floating at supply voltage; alternatively a chafed wire contacts a battery feed that the output stage cannot pull down.",["Open coil or broken lead on a ground-switched valve A","Control wire of valve A touching a battery feed","Corroded pins with high resistance at valve A"],["Malfunction lamp on","No change to the next tank, gas runs out early","Engine switches to its other fuel or reduced power"],3,3,["P2A91","P2A92","P2A93","P2A98","P2A9C"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A95:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve B Control Circuit/Open","P2A95 says the module finds no proper current path through tank select valve B. Where a second select valve exists, it typically serves the next vessel or supply in line. Cespira's patent for a gas engine fed from two compressed-gas supplies shows how much depends on such valves: the controller connects each supply either to a compressor or to the regulator, and only by switching can it keep using a supply whose…",["Loose plug or broken wire to select valve B","Open solenoid coil of valve B","Output stage for valve B in the module defective"],["Malfunction lamp on","Content of one vessel cannot be used","Range well below the usual figure"],3,3,["P2A96","P2A97","P2A98","P2A91","P2A99","P2A22"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A96:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve B Control Circuit Performance","P2A96 is about tank select valve B working electrically but not doing what it is told. In an LNG layout like the one in Westport's US8726785B2, where one pump draws from either of two vessels through an insulated select valve, the module can verify the switch from the pump's behaviour: right after selecting a full vessel, the drive work per stroke should be normal, whereas a reading that stays low suggests the pump…",["Valve B held by ice or cold-hardened seals","Debris preventing valve B from shifting fully","Pump defect interpreted as a select valve problem"],["Malfunction lamp on","Gas supply drops right after a tank change","One vessel stays full while the other runs dry"],4,3,["P2A95","P2A97","P2A98","P2A92","P2A9A","P2A42"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2A97:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve B Control Circuit Low","P2A97 indicates that the drive line of tank select valve B reads too low. If the module feeds the valve from the positive side, a short to ground in the wire or a coil with shorted windings drags the output down, and the stage switches off to protect itself, so valve B falls back to its spring position. If the module switches the ground side instead, the same short can hold the valve energised all the time.",["Wire to valve B chafed against a tank strap or bracket","Shorted windings in the coil of valve B","Moisture bridging the pins of the valve B plug"],["Malfunction lamp on","Tank change does not happen or happens at the wrong time","Gas mode ends early with fuel still on board"],3,3,["P2A95","P2A96","P2A98","P2A93","P2A9B"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A98:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve B Control Circuit High","P2A98 appears when the voltage on the control circuit of tank select valve B stays higher than the module allows for the commanded state. A ground-switched valve with an interrupted winding or lead shows this pattern, as does a wire that has picked up battery voltage. The valve will then not move on command, and the system keeps drawing from whichever vessel the resting valve connects.",["Interrupted winding or lead at valve B","Control line of valve B in contact with battery voltage","Corrosion at the valve B connector raising resistance"],["Malfunction lamp on","Second vessel never used, gas runs out early","Gauge shows reserve while power drops"],3,3,["P2A95","P2A96","P2A97","P2A94","P2A9C"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A99:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve C Control Circuit/Open","P2A99 belongs to installations with at least three selectable vessels or supplies and reports an open or otherwise broken control circuit at select valve C. Published designs mostly show two vessels, such as Westport's LNG arrangement with one pump and a valve choosing the tank, or Cespira's pair of compressed-gas supplies; a third valve extends the same principle.",["Disconnected plug or broken lead at select valve C","Coil of valve C burnt out","Module output for valve C failed"],["Malfunction lamp on","Third vessel stays full or is never isolated","Total range reduced"],3,3,["P2A9A","P2A9B","P2A9C","P2A91","P2A95","P2A26"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2A9A:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve C Control Circuit Performance","With P2A9A, select valve C passes its electrical tests, but the effect of switching does not show up as expected. The likely evidence is pressure: once vessel C is selected, its own tank pressure sensor should begin to fall with consumption and the pressure ahead of the regulator should match that vessel's level.",["Valve C not shifting fully because of wear or contamination","Internal leakage letting vessel C feed in the wrong position","Faulty tank C pressure reading misleading the check"],["Malfunction lamp on","Tank C level hardly changes over a tank cycle","Fault appears mainly in cold weather"],4,3,["P2A99","P2A9B","P2A9C","P2A92","P2A96","P2A46","P2A47"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2A9B:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve C Control Circuit Low","P2A9B is logged when the control circuit of tank select valve C reads below the expected level. Common electrical findings are a lead grounded against the frame, a pinched wire under a tank strap or a coil with internal shorts. What follows depends on how the output is wired: a ground-side driver may now keep valve C switched permanently, while a supply-side driver shuts down and lets the valve drop back.",["Lead of valve C grounded against the frame or pinched under a tank strap","Internal short in the coil of valve C","Water in the plug of valve C"],["Malfunction lamp on","Third tank used constantly or not at all","Unexpected tank changes during the drive"],3,3,["P2A99","P2A9A","P2A9C","P2A93","P2A97"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2A9C:["Alternative Fuel Tank Select Valve C Control Circuit High","P2A9C reports a control voltage at select valve C above the level the commanded state permits. The usual reasons are an interrupted coil or wire on a valve the module switches to ground, which leaves supply voltage on the line, or a foreign voltage fed in from a damaged neighbouring wire. Valve C then ignores commands.",["Open coil or wire on ground-switched valve C","Foreign voltage from a damaged neighbouring wire","Corroded terminals at valve C"],["Malfunction lamp on","Third vessel never drawn, range reduced","Earlier change to the other fuel"],3,3,["P2A99","P2A9A","P2A9B","P2A94","P2A98"],"שסתום בחירת מיכל דלק חלופי‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2A9D:["Alternative Fuel High Pressure System Small Leak","P2A9D points to a slow loss of gas from the high-pressure side, from the cylinders up to the regulator, too small to notice while driving. A Toyota and Denso patent, US6467466B1, explains the catch: with the valves open, a modest pressure drop cannot be told apart from consumption.",["Seeping high-pressure fitting or loosened connection","Tank or shutoff valve not sealing fully when closed","Aged O-rings in the filter or regulator inlet","Drifting high-pressure sensor simulating a pressure loss"],["Malfunction or gas warning lamp on","Tank pressure noticeably lower after parking","Faint gas smell near the tanks or lines","Gas mode blocked at the next start on some systems"],4,3,["P240E","P240D","P0442","P01A0"],""],P2A9E:["Alternative Fuel Return Line Valve Control Circuit/Open","Liquid-phase propane and LPG systems pump more fuel to the rail than the injectors use; the surplus flows back to the tank and carries heat and vapor away with it. A return line valve opens or blocks that path. With P2A9E the drive circuit of this valve is open or broken in some other way, so the module can no longer switch it and the valve rests in its unpowered state.",["Corroded, wet or loose connector at the tank-mounted valve","Broken wire in the frame or tank harness","Open solenoid coil in the return valve","Blown fuse or faulty relay in the valve supply","Failed output stage in the fuel control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Hard or long cranking on a warm engine, as vapor is not flushed out of the rail","Switch to the base fuel or reduced power on bi-fuel or dedicated systems"],2,3,["P2A9F","P2AA0","P2AA1","P2AA2"],""],P2A9F:["Alternative Fuel Return Line Valve Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2A9F covers the grey zone between a clean open and a clean short: the control circuit of the return line valve is connected, but the current or voltage the output stage measures while driving it does not fit the command. Typical reasons are a coil whose resistance has drifted, a few shorted windings, or high contact resistance in a corroded connector that lets the coil pull in only weakly or late.",["Solenoid coil resistance out of range or partially shorted windings","High contact resistance from corrosion or water in the connector","Low supply voltage at the valve from a weak relay contact or ground","Output stage of the fuel control module measuring incorrectly"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Occasional hard starts after a hot soak","Fault comes and goes with temperature or moisture"],2,3,["P2A9E","P2AA0","P2AA1","P2AA2"],""],P2AA0:["Alternative Fuel Return Line Valve Control Circuit Low","P2AA0 means the module reads too low a voltage on the control line of the return line valve, which almost always points to a short to ground. What follows depends on which side the module switches. In the ROUSH CleanTech Gen 4 propane layout the valve has a fused battery feed and its ground wire runs to a relay module;",["Control wire chafed through and touching the frame or tank","Water in the valve connector bridging to ground","Internal short in the solenoid coil","Damaged output stage in the fuel control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Return valve stays open or the valve fuse blows, depending on the circuit layout","Irregular rail pressure or switch to the base fuel"],2,3,["P2A9E","P2A9F","P2AA1","P2AA2"],""],P2AA1:["Alternative Fuel Return Line Valve Control Circuit High","P2AA1 is the opposite electrical case to P2AA0: the valve drive wire sits at too high a voltage, usually because it touches a battery-fed wire. Where the module switches the ground side, as in the ROUSH CleanTech Gen 4 propane system with its relay-module ground, a line stuck at supply level leaves no voltage across the coil, so the valve cannot be energized at all and stays in its rest position.",["Control wire shorted to a battery-fed wire in the harness","Solenoid winding shorted to its supply terminal","Bent or bridged pins in the valve connector","Output stage in the fuel control module shorted internally"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Return valve cannot be switched and stays in its rest position","Poor hot starts or switch to the base fuel"],2,3,["P2A9E","P2A9F","P2AA0","P2AA2"],""],P2AA2:["Alternative Fuel Return Line Insufficient Flow","P2AA2 is a hydraulic fault, not an electrical one: too little liquid fuel comes back from the rail to the tank. The return keeps the fuel in the rail cool and liquid, so a weak return lets it warm up and boil.",["Return valve or return check valve sticking closed","Kinked, crushed or clogged return line or filter","In-tank pump delivering too little, leaving no surplus to return","Faulty pressure regulator in the return path"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Hard starting or stalling after a hot soak from vapor in the rail","Hesitation or lean running under load","Switch to the base fuel or reduced power"],3,3,["P2A9E","P2A9F","P2AA0","P2AA1","P2A8E"],""],P2AA3:["Cold Start EGR B Flow Insufficient Detected","P2AA3 belongs to the cold-start strategy (CSERS) newer diesels run in the first minutes after a long soak. CARB phases in from 2026 to 2028 that the OBD system must confirm, under defined monitoring conditions such as a soak of six hours or more, that the EGR valve and the EGR cooler bypass actually follow their cold-start setpoints by a clearly measurable amount, in the right direction and beyond normal start-up…",["EGR valve B sticking or slow from soot at low temperature","Faulty position sensor on EGR valve B misleading the control","Clogged EGR cooler or passage in loop B","Control software needing an update"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Usually no noticeable change in driving","Higher NOx in the warm-up phase, possible inspection failure"],2,1,["P2AA4","P04DD","P2D1C","P0401"],""],P2AA4:["Cold Start EGR B Flow Excessive Detected","P2AA4 is the mirror case of P2AA3: during the cold-start phase, EGR path B recirculates more exhaust than intended. Many calibrations deliberately keep EGR low in a cold engine, so a valve that leaks or hangs open is the classic cause. CARB's cold-start component checks require a response that is robustly detectable and in the commanded direction;",["EGR valve B leaking or stuck partly open from carbon","Position sensor offset making the valve open further than commanded","Intake or exhaust throttle fault raising the pressure difference across loop B"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Rough idle and smoke after a cold start","Stalling or hesitation while the engine is cold"],2,1,["P2AA3","P04DE","P2D1C","P0402","P045E"],""],P2AA5:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High Bank 1","P2AA5 comes from the H-bridge that drives the DC motor of the bank 1 EGR cooler bypass flap: the driver chip itself reports that it is getting too hot. GM's diesel summary tables carry this monitor from 2017 (17OBDG04) to 2025 (25OBDG04A) as a motor overtemperature check. The fault flag comes from the hardware layer when the bridge exceeds 170 °C;",["Bypass flap binding on soot or corrosion, motor working against resistance","Internal fault in the bypass actuator motor","Partial short between the motor wires","Overheating or faulty H-bridge in the engine control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on after two trips","Bypass flap no longer driven, so warm-up EGR cooling stays at its last state","Possible further EGR or cooler efficiency codes"],3,1,["P2AA6","P245A","P245C","P245D","P24A5"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2AA6:["EGR Cooler Bypass Control Circuit Driver Current/Temperature Too High Bank 2","P2AA6 is the bank 2 version of the bypass driver protection code. It only exists on engines with a separate EGR cooler and bypass actuator for the second cylinder bank, typically V engines whose banks each have their own exhaust manifold feeding EGR. The output stage for that actuator reports excessive current or junction heat and shuts itself off, which leaves the flap where it was.",["Bank 2 bypass flap binding on soot or corrosion","Internal fault in the bank 2 actuator motor","Partial short in the bank 2 actuator wiring","Faulty driver stage in the engine control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Bank 2 bypass flap stays in its last position","Possible NOx or EGR temperature codes for bank 2"],3,1,["P2AA5","P248E","P2490","P2491","P24A6"],"מעקף מצנן EGR — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר של מעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2AA7:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Circuit","Thermal management modules on modern engines use motor-driven rotary valves to split coolant between radiator, heater, oil or transmission cooler and engine block. A position sensor reports each valve's angle so the module can regulate it in closed loop. P2AA7 is the general circuit code for the sensor of valve B, used when the signal is unusable but cannot be classed as low (P2AA9) or high (P2AAA).",["Loose, corroded or coolant-wetted connector, or damaged sensor wiring","Lost 5 V supply or ground to the position sensor","Failed position sensor inside the valve module","Faulty sensor input in the engine control module"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Slow warm-up or reduced cabin heating","Fluctuating or elevated coolant temperature reading"],2,3,["P2AA8","P2AA9","P2AAA","P2AAB","P26A4","P23C3"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2AA8:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","With P2AA8 the position sensor of coolant valve B delivers an electrically valid signal, but its content is implausible: it sticks while the motor turns the valve, jumps by more than a real valve could move, or lies outside the end stops the module learned. A worn sensor track, a magnet that has shifted on the valve shaft or a slipping gear between motor and sensor are typical findings.",["Worn or contaminated position sensor in the valve module","Slipping gear or shifted magnet between valve shaft and sensor","Intermittent contact in the connector causing signal jumps","Learned end stops lost after a module or valve replacement"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Engine warms up slowly or runs hotter than usual","Heater output varies"],2,3,["P2AA7","P2AA9","P2AAA","P26B0","P26A5"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2AA9:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2AA9 is set once the position sensor on coolant valve B reports a value below its valid band, which nearly always means the signal wire or the sensor output is pulled toward ground. Rotary coolant valves in thermal management modules report their angle so the engine computer can steer coolant between radiator, heater and other loops. No manufacturer documents P2AA9 publicly.",["Sensor signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Position sensor electronics in the valve module failed (often only as complete valve unit)","Coolant or moisture in the sensor connector creating a leakage path to ground"],["Check engine light on","Engine warms up slowly or runs cooler than usual","Cabin heating or transmission warm-up weaker, depending on what valve B serves"],2,3,["P2AAA","P2AA7","P2AA8","P2AAB","P26A6","P23C4"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2AAA:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Circuit High","With P2AAA the position sensor of coolant valve B reports a value above anything a working sensor would deliver. Typical reasons are a signal line touching a supply wire, a damaged output stage inside the sensor or, depending on how the input is wired, an interrupted ground.",["Signal wire in contact with a supply or reference voltage wire","Sensor ground open at the connector or splice","Position sensor in the valve module defective"],["Check engine light on","Coolant temperature swings or stays off target","Possibly reduced engine power if the module protects against overheating"],2,3,["P2AA9","P2AA7","P2AA8","P2AAB","P26A7","P23C5"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2AAB:["Engine Coolant Bypass Valve B Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2AAB covers a position signal from coolant valve B that is valid most of the time but drops out, jumps or flickers for short moments. Such patterns usually come from a contact that opens under vibration or heat, a lead that rubs against hot engine parts, or interference on the digital sensor line.",["Widened or loose terminal in the valve connector","Harness rubbing on hot or moving engine parts","Electrical interference or poor ground on the sensor line"],["Check engine light that comes and goes","Occasional temperature swings without a steady pattern","Often no noticeable change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P2AA7","P2AA8","P2AA9","P2AAA","P26A8","P26B0"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף נוזל קירור מנוע‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2AAC:["Diesel Fuel Presence Sensor Circuit","P2AAC is the general circuit fault of a sensor meant to recognise diesel where only gasoline belongs, so the system can react to misfuelling before damage occurs. No manufacturer documents this sensor or the code publicly, and its exact design is not described in sources available.",["Corroded or loose connector at the sensor near the tank or fuel line","Damaged wiring along the underbody","Sensor electronics failed"],["Check engine light on","Misfuelling warning unavailable or shown without reason","Usually no change in how the engine runs"],2,1,["P2AAD","P2AAE","P2AAF"],""],P2AAD:["Diesel Fuel Presence Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2AAD means the diesel presence sensor delivers an electrically valid signal whose content does not make sense: it may report diesel although no refuelling has taken place, never change at all, or contradict other information the engine computer has about the fuel. No manufacturer documents this code or its test publicly.",["Sensing element coated with deposits or residues","Sensor characteristic drifted with age","Calibration of the plausibility check not suited to the fuel quality in use"],["Check engine light on","Unjustified misfuelling message, or a real misfuelling going unnoticed"],2,1,["P2AAC","P2AAE","P2AAF"],""],P2AAE:["Diesel Fuel Presence Sensor Circuit Low","P2AAE is stored when the diesel presence sensor signal falls below the lowest value the input accepts, which points to a short to ground on the signal line or a sensor whose output has collapsed. Whether a low reading would otherwise stand for diesel or for gasoline is not published, so the code says nothing about the fuel in the tank, only that the reading cannot be used. No manufacturer documents P2AAE publicly.",["Signal wire shorted to ground, often chafed on the underbody","Internal short in the sensor","Sensor supply or reference voltage missing"],["Check engine light on","Misfuelling protection inactive"],2,1,["P2AAF","P2AAC","P2AAD"],""],P2AAF:["Diesel Fuel Presence Sensor Circuit High","P2AAF reports the diesel presence sensor signal stuck above its upper limit. Common reasons are a signal wire touching a battery-fed line, an open ground or signal path that lets an internal pull-up drive the input high, or a sensor with a failed output stage. No manufacturer documents P2AAF publicly, and no public source states which signal level stands for diesel.",["Signal wire shorted to a voltage source","Open sensor ground or signal wire","Sensor output stage failed"],["Check engine light on","Misfuelling warning unreliable"],2,1,["P2AAE","P2AAC","P2AAD"],""],P2AB0:["Particulate Matter Sensor Processor Performance","P2AB0 concerns the electronics of the particulate matter sensor rather than its sensing element: the sensor control unit, which feeds the electrodes, measures their current and reports over CAN, finds an internal error in its own measuring path.",["Internal fault in the PM sensor control unit (sensor and control unit usually replaced as one part)","CAN wiring fault that older sensor versions also report as P2AB0","Unstable supply or ground at the sensor control unit"],["Check engine light on","Particulate filter monitoring cannot complete","Driving behaviour usually unchanged"],2,1,["P24AE","P24AF","U02A3","U0080","P24D1"],"מעבד חיישן חלקיקים — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2AB1:["Catalyst Heater Control Module Performance","P2AB1 reports that the control module of an electrically heated catalyst does not work as it should, for example because its self-test fails or the heating it delivers does not match the demand. Such heaters bring a catalyst to working temperature right after start or in low-load driving.",["Internal fault in the heater control module (power stage or self-test)","Module software fault, update may be available","Module overheated due to poor cooling or high ambient heat at its mounting"],["Check engine light on","Higher emissions after cold start; inspection may fail","Driving behaviour largely unchanged"],3,1,["P2AB2","P0429","P0439","P0423","P0433"],"מודול בקרת גוף חימום ממיר קטליטי — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2AB2:["Catalyst Heater Control Module Supply Voltage","P2AB2 points to the power feed of the catalyst heater control module: the voltage it measures at its own supply input lies outside the window in which it may switch the heater. That window matters because these heaters draw several kilowatts; Vitesco's demonstration vehicle used a 4 kW disc, fed in 48-volt mild hybrids from energy recovered while braking, as DieselNet reports.",["Blown fuse or faulty relay in the heater supply","Corroded or loose ground or high-current terminal","Weak 48-volt battery or faulty DC/DC converter in mild-hybrid systems"],["Check engine light on","Catalyst heating not available, higher emissions after cold start","Further voltage-related fault codes possible"],2,1,["P2AB1","P0429","P0439","P0562","P0563"],"מתח אספקה מודול בקרת גוף חימום ממיר קטליטי"],P2AB3:["Cold Start Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Open Bank 1","P2AB3 is part of the cold-start component checks that CARB phases in for 20, 50 and 100 percent of new vehicles in 2026, 2027 and 2028. Right after a start that follows a long standstill, charge motion, runner and swirl valves must follow the cold-start command clearly, toward the target and further than they would at a start without that strategy.",["Actuator or vacuum unit too weak to move the flaps when cold","Flap shaft stiff from carbon or oil deposits","Linkage detached or broken between actuator and shaft"],["Check engine light on","Rougher idle in the first minutes after a cold start","Higher cold-start emissions, otherwise often unnoticed"],2,1,["P2AB4","P2AB5","P2AB6","P2004","P2006"],"בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה התנעה קרה — תקוע במצב פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2AB4:["Cold Start Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Open Bank 2","P2AB4 is the bank 2 version of the open-stuck check during cold start, so it only appears on engines with a separate runner control for each cylinder bank, typically V or flat engines. The runner flaps of the second bank fail to leave their open position as long as the cold-start routine runs, so that bank burns its mixture with less charge motion than intended. No manufacturer documents P2AB4 publicly;",["Leaking vacuum line or diaphragm on the bank 2 actuator","Bank 2 flap shaft stiff from deposits","Electric actuator for bank 2 defective"],["Check engine light on","Uneven running between the banks shortly after a cold start","Higher cold-start emissions"],2,1,["P2AB3","P2AB6","P2AB5","P2005","P2007"],"בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה התנעה קרה — תקוע במצב פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2AB5:["Cold Start Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Closed Bank 1","P2AB5 is the opposite of P2AB3: during cold start the runner control on bank 1 remains in its closed position and does not follow a command to open. CARB requires, for 2026 to 2028 phase-in vehicles, that such valves react measurably and in the commanded direction while the cold-start conditions hold, meaning a soak of six hours or more and coolant close to ambient.",["Flaps stuck closed by deposits or condensate freezing at low temperature","Actuator motor or vacuum valve does not move the shaft","Broken return spring or worn shaft bushing"],["Check engine light on","Less power in the first minutes after a cold start","Higher cold-start emissions"],2,1,["P2AB6","P2AB3","P2AB4","P2006","P2004"],"בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה התנעה קרה — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 1)"],P2AB6:["Cold Start Intake Manifold Runner Control Stuck Closed Bank 2","P2AB6 reports the runner flaps of bank 2 held in the closed position during the cold-start phase, against a command to open them. Like its siblings it exists only on engines that control each bank's runners separately and only becomes testable after a soak of six hours or more at ambient temperatures from -6.7 °C upward, as defined in CARB's cold-start rules. No manufacturer documents P2AB6 publicly.",["Bank 2 flaps seized by deposits or ice","Bank 2 actuator or its control valve defective","Shared actuator supply or vacuum source weak (often with P2AB5)"],["Check engine light on","Slightly uneven running and reduced pull after a cold start","Higher cold-start emissions"],2,1,["P2AB5","P2AB4","P2AB3","P2007","P2005"],"בקרת מובילי סעפת יניקה התנעה קרה — תקוע במצב סגור (בנק 2)"],P2AB7:["Wastegate Position Sensor A Circuit","P2AB7 is the general circuit fault for the position sensor on wastegate A, found on engines whose wastegate is moved by an electric motor rather than a vacuum can. Turbo A is the first one in the exhaust flow on series layouts or the bank 1 unit on parallel layouts.",["Electric wastegate actuator failed, e-clip missing or actuator rod damaged (sensor sits in the actuator)","Chafed harness or loose connector near the hot turbocharger","PCM calibration that sets the code falsely (reflash available for some models)"],["Check engine light on","Noticeable lack of power, boost limited","Often stored together with P0299 or the stuck wastegate codes P25B3/P25B4"],2,3,["P2AB8","P2AB9","P2ABA","P2B81","U0644","P25B3","P25B4","P0299"],"חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2AB8:["Wastegate Position Sensor A Circuit Low","P2AB8 means the wastegate A position signal has fallen below its valid floor, which points to a short to ground, an open signal or reference wire, or a dead sensor. GM's 2019 tables for the 2.7L L3B read the sensor as a percentage of its reference and fail below 5 % in 30 of 38 samples taken every 100 ms; the 2025 tables use below 1 % in 10 of 12.",["Sensor harness pinched or chafed between turbocharger and intake hose (short to ground)","Open reference or signal wire, or pushed-out terminal in the actuator connector","Position sensor inside the electric actuator failed"],["Check engine light from the first trip","Reduced power because boost control is restricted","May appear together with P0245 when a shared harness section is damaged"],2,3,["P2AB7","P2AB9","P2ABB","P2B81","P0245","P0641"],"חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2AB9:["Wastegate Position Sensor A Circuit High","P2AB9 is logged when the wastegate A position signal climbs above its valid ceiling. Typical reasons are a signal wire shorted to the sensor supply or to battery voltage, an open ground return that lets the input float upward, or an internal sensor fault.",["Signal wire shorted to the sensor supply or battery voltage","Open sensor ground or corroded ground terminal","PCM calibration that sets the code falsely (Ford reflash for listed models)","Position sensor inside the electric actuator failed"],["Check engine light from the first trip","Lower power under load, boost held back","Powertrain fault (wrench) indicator on some Ford models"],2,3,["P2AB7","P2AB8","P2ABC","P2B81","P2B93","P0299"],"חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2ABA:["Wastegate Position Sensor B Circuit","P2ABA covers a general circuit fault of the position sensor on the wastegate of turbocharger B, so it can only occur on engines with two turbos and electric wastegates: on a parallel layout the turbo of bank 2, on a series layout the second one downstream. Ford uses it on twin-turbo EcoBoost V6 engines.",["PCM calibration that sets the code falsely (Ford reflash for listed models)","Damaged harness or connector at the bank 2 turbocharger","Electric wastegate actuator B with its built-in position sensor failed"],["Check engine light, on Ford also the powertrain (wrench) indicator","Reduced power, boost limited"],2,3,["P2ABB","P2ABC","P2AB7","P2B82","U0674","P25B5","P25B6"],"חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2ABB:["Wastegate Position Sensor B Circuit Low","P2ABB reports that the position signal of the turbocharger B wastegate is too low, as a short to ground, a broken signal or supply wire or a failed sensor would cause. Ford's 2020-23 gasoline summary applies the same window as for turbo A and sets the code below 0.50 V after 4 s.",["Sensor wire chafed to ground near the bank 2 turbocharger","Open reference supply or signal wire, loose connector","Position sensor in wastegate actuator B failed"],["Check engine light","Less power, especially when accelerating hard"],2,3,["P2ABA","P2ABC","P2AB8","P2B82","P0249","P0651"],"חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2ABC:["Wastegate Position Sensor B Circuit High","P2ABC is the high-voltage fault on the wastegate B position sensor: according to Ford's 2020-23 gasoline summary the input sits above 4.50 V for 4 s, a picture typical of a signal line shorted to the reference supply or an open sensor ground. On the 2.7L F-150 of model years 2021-22 Ford blames false P2ABC entries on calibration and fixes them by reprogramming the PCM (TSB 22-2357);",["PCM calibration that sets the code falsely (Ford reflash for listed models)","Open sensor ground or heat-damaged terminal at the actuator","Signal wire shorted to the reference supply or battery voltage"],["Check engine light, on Ford possibly the wrench indicator","Reduced power under load"],2,3,["P2ABA","P2ABB","P2AB9","P2B82","P2B94","P0250"],"חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2ABD:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate Actuator A Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P2ABD is raised by the output stage that powers the electric wastegate actuator of turbocharger A when it detects excessive current or overheating. Ford's 2020-23 gasoline summary groups it with P0243 in the wastegate A circuit check: the PCM's smart driver chip recognises a short to battery or ground and an open load on its own and reports within 0.4 s, and the stuck open/closed tests P25B3/P25B4 are only allowed…",["Wastegate flap or rod binding from soot, corrosion or heat so the motor stalls","Electric actuator motor shorted internally","Actuator supply wires chafed to ground or to each other","Driver stage in the PCM faulty"],["Check engine light on","Clearly reduced power because the wastegate is no longer driven","Stuck wastegate checks P25B3/P25B4 not run while the code is stored"],3,3,["P2ABE","P0243","P0244","P25B3","P25B4","P2AA5"],"מפעיל שסתום Wastegate של המגדש‏ A — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר"],P2ABE:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Wastegate Actuator B Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P2ABE is the turbo B counterpart of P2ABD: the output stage driving the second electric wastegate actuator signals overcurrent or thermal overload. It therefore applies only to twin-turbo engines with two electric actuators, such as Ford's EcoBoost V6. Ford's summary treats it together with P0247 as the B circuit check, with the fault detected inside the smart driver chip and a monitoring time of 0.4 s;",["Wastegate B rod or flap seized by corrosion or heat","Shorted winding in electric actuator B","Actuator harness pinched against the turbocharger"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power, uneven boost between the two banks"],3,3,["P2ABD","P0247","P0248","P25B5","P25B6"],"מפעיל שסתום Wastegate של המגדש‏ B — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר"],P2ABF:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit/Open Bank 1","P2ABF points to an open circuit in the reference voltage line of the intake air oxygen sensor on bank 1. This sensor is a wide-band element placed in the intake tract, usually before the intercooler, that measures how much oxygen the incoming charge still contains and therefore how much exhaust has been recirculated.",["Broken reference wire or pushed-back pin between sensor and ECM","Corroded or loose sensor connector in the damp intake area","Sensing cell of the intake oxygen sensor internally open"],["Check engine light on","EGR runs without sensor feedback or is reduced, higher NOx emissions"],2,1,["P2AC0","P2AC1","P2AC2","P2AC3","P2B88","P2AE3"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2AC0:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1","P2AC0 is set when the reference voltage circuit of the bank 1 intake air oxygen sensor is electrically present but behaves implausibly, for example drifting or not matching what the ECM expects for the current EGR and pressure state. Stellantis documents it explicitly for the 2.0L turbo four (sales code EC2) of the Alfa Romeo Giulia and Stelvio: TSB 18-067-22 REV. B for 2022 Giulia and TSB 18-041-23 REV.",["Engine software that detects the fault falsely (Stellantis reflash for Giulia/Stelvio 2.0L)","Intake oxygen sensor aged or contaminated by oil mist from crankcase ventilation","High resistance in the reference wire or connector"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable change in driveability"],1,1,["P2ABF","P2AC1","P2AC2","P2AC4","P2B89","P0401","P0402"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2AC1:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Low Bank 1","P2AC1 flags a reference voltage below the range the ECM accepts on the bank 1 intake oxygen sensor. This usually means the reference lead is shorted to ground or the sensing cell inside the sensor has broken down. Without a stable reference the ECM cannot operate the cell, so the oxygen reading used to work out the EGR rate becomes useless and recirculation is typically cut back or run open loop.",["Reference wire chafed through to ground","Sensing cell of the intake oxygen sensor broken down internally","Sensor interface in the ECM faulty"],["Check engine light on","EGR reduced or uncontrolled, possibly higher NOx and a failed emissions test"],2,1,["P2ABF","P2AC0","P2AC2","P2AC5","P2B89"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2AC2:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit High Bank 1","P2AC2 means the reference voltage at the intake oxygen sensor of bank 1 reads above its permitted range. A reference lead shorted to a supply wire or battery voltage in the harness, a lost ground on the sensor side or water in the connector are the usual triggers; a sensor with an internally damaged cell can produce the same picture.",["Reference wire shorted to a supply or battery voltage wire","Moisture or corrosion bridging pins in the sensor connector","Open ground on the sensor side"],["Check engine light on","EGR reduced, NOx emissions may rise"],2,1,["P2ABF","P2AC0","P2AC1","P2AC6","P2B8A"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2AC3:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit/Open Bank 2","P2AC3 is the open circuit fault in the reference voltage lead of the intake air oxygen sensor assigned to bank 2. A second intake sensor only exists where each cylinder bank has its own intake or EGR path, for example on V engines with two separate charge air routes; engines with a single sensor use the bank 1 code P2ABF. No manufacturer has published P2AC3 or a vehicle using it.",["Broken reference wire or loose terminal at the bank 2 sensor","Harness damaged by heat near the bank 2 turbocharger or exhaust","Sensing cell of the bank 2 intake oxygen sensor internally open"],["Check engine light on","EGR on bank 2 reduced or uncontrolled"],2,1,["P2AC4","P2AC5","P2AC6","P2ABF","P2AEC"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מעגל תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2AC4:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Range/Performance Bank 2","P2AC4 marks an implausible but electrically intact reference voltage on the second-bank intake oxygen sensor. It is the bank 2 twin of P2AC0, which Stellantis documents for the four-cylinder Alfa Romeo 2.0L; an inline four with one intake path has no bank 2, so P2AC4 would only appear on engines fitted with a second intake sensor. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Bank 2 intake oxygen sensor aged or contaminated by crankcase vapours","Calibration that judges the signal too strictly","High resistance in the reference wire or connector"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2AC3","P2AC5","P2AC6","P2AC0","P0401","P0402"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2AC5:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit Low Bank 2","P2AC5 reports that the bank 2 intake oxygen sensor sees a reference voltage below the permitted limit, typically a short to ground in the reference lead or a breakdown of the sensing cell. No manufacturer publishes this code, and engines with a separate intake oxygen sensor for bank 2 are rare.",["Reference wire of the bank 2 sensor shorted to ground","Sensing cell broken down internally","Shared sensor supply or ECM fault (if P2AC1 is present as well)"],["Check engine light on","Higher NOx, possibly a failed emissions test"],2,1,["P2AC3","P2AC4","P2AC6","P2AC1"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2AC6:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Reference Voltage Circuit High Bank 2","P2AC6 indicates an excessive reference voltage on the intake oxygen sensor serving bank 2, as happens when the reference wire touches a supply or battery feed, when the sensor ground is open or when moisture bridges the connector pins. Like the other bank 2 codes of this group, it is not documented by any manufacturer;",["Reference wire of the bank 2 sensor shorted to a supply or battery feed","Open sensor ground","Moisture bridging pins in the connector"],["Check engine light on","EGR on bank 2 reduced, NOx may rise"],2,1,["P2AC3","P2AC4","P2AC5","P2AC2"],"מתח ייחוס חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2AC7:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit","P2AC7 is the general circuit fault of the second coolant temperature sensor in the low-temperature loop that serves a water-cooled charge air cooler. Where two sensors exist, one usually sits at the cooler inlet and the other at its outlet, so the module can judge how much heat the cooler removes; in GM's 2025 diesel table, sensor A measures the water entering the cooler.",["Loose, corroded or coolant-contaminated sensor B connector","Chafed or broken wire between sensor B and the module","Internally defective temperature sensor B","Faulty sensor input or reference in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Implausible or missing value for sensor B in live data","Reduced boost or power on some engines"],1,3,["P2AC8","P2AC9","P2ACA","P2ACB","P00DE"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2AC8:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2AC8 sets when charge air cooler coolant temperature sensor B delivers an electrically valid value that makes no sense for the situation, for example after a long engine-off period when every temperature in the engine bay should have converged, or when it fails to change while the loop pump runs and the cooler heats up. No maker documents this exact check publicly;",["Low coolant level or air trapped in the low-temperature loop","Sensor B drifting out of its characteristic","Electric charge air cooler coolant pump weak or not running","Control module software needing an update"],["Check engine light on, often only after several drives","Sensor B reads clearly different from sensor A after a cold soak","Higher intake air temperature under load"],2,3,["P2AC7","P2AC9","P2ACA","P2ACB","P00DF"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2AC9:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","P2AC9 reports that the signal of charge air cooler coolant temperature sensor B has dropped below its permitted window. These sensors are NTC thermistors, so a low signal stands for an implausibly hot coolant and usually means the signal wire touches ground or the element is internally shorted.",["Signal wire of sensor B shorted to ground","Sensor B internally shorted","Coolant in the connector bridging the terminals"],["Check engine light on","Live data shows an extremely high coolant temperature for sensor B","Coolant pump of the loop runs constantly or boost is reduced"],1,3,["P2AC7","P2ACA","P2AC8","P2ACB","P00E0"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2ACA:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","P2ACA is the opposite end: the voltage from charge air cooler coolant temperature sensor B sits above anything a real temperature would produce. For a thermistor input this looks like extreme cold and is typical of an unplugged connector, a broken signal wire, a lost sensor ground or a short to a voltage source.",["Disconnected plug or broken signal wire of sensor B","Open ground or return line of the sensor","Sensor B element open internally","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source"],["Check engine light on","Live data shows an extremely low coolant temperature for sensor B","Reduced boost on some engines"],1,3,["P2AC7","P2AC9","P2AC8","P2ACB","P00E1"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2ACB:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Temperature Sensor B Intermittent/Erratic","P2ACB covers a sensor B signal that jumps or briefly drops out instead of following the slow temperature changes of a coolant loop. The title, without the word circuit, also includes erratic values while the wiring stays intact. No maker publishes the B-side check.",["Terminal with weak contact tension in the sensor B plug","Harness rubbing through intermittently under vibration","Coolant crept into the connector","Sensor B element with unstable output"],["Check engine light comes and goes","Sensor B value jumps in live data"],1,1,["P2AC7","P2AC8","P2AC9","P2ACA","P00E2"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ B — אות לא יציב"],P2ACC:["Reductant Temperature Sensor B Circuit","P2ACC is the general circuit code for a second reductant (DEF) temperature sensor outside the tank; the tank sensors have their own series (P205A ff. and P2ADA ff.). Sensor A, coded P2042 ff., is placed by Deutz in the SCR supply path (SPN 4337) and by Volvo and Mack in the DEF pump. Where a B sensor sits is left to the maker, and no manufacturer publicly documents P2ACC.",["Connector of sensor B corroded by DEF residue","Damaged wiring between sensor B and the controller","Defective reductant temperature sensor B"],["Check engine light and DEF/SCR warning","Countdown or speed limitation if the fault persists"],2,3,["P2ACD","P2ACE","P2ACF","P2AD0","P2042"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2ACD:["Reductant Temperature Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2ACD flags a reductant temperature sensor B reading that is electrically fine but disagrees with the other temperatures the SCR controller knows, typically checked after a cold soak, when DEF lines, tank and ambient should read about the same. No manufacturer publicly describes P2ACD.",["Controller software with an overly tight plausibility check","Sensor B drifting from its characteristic","Line heater warming the sensor area during the check"],["Check engine light after a cold start","SCR warning with no noticeable driving change"],2,1,["P2ACC","P2ACE","P2ACF","P2AD0","P2043"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2ACE:["Reductant Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","P2ACE means the signal of reductant temperature sensor B lies below its valid voltage band. With the NTC elements used for DEF temperature, a low voltage translates into an extremely hot reading, so a signal line rubbing through to ground, a crushed connector or DEF that has wicked into the plug and bridges the contacts are the usual suspects. No maker publishes a threshold for P2ACE.",["Signal wire of sensor B shorted to ground","DEF wicked into the connector bridging the terminals","Sensor B internally shorted"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","Implausibly high DEF temperature in live data","Frozen DEF lines in winter"],2,3,["P2ACC","P2ACF","P2ACD","P2AD0","P2044"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2ACF:["Reductant Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","P2ACF is set when reductant temperature sensor B reports a voltage above its valid band. For a thermistor that reads as deep cold, and it is what an open signal wire, a missing sensor ground, a disconnected plug or a short to supply voltage cause. No public document gives a limit for P2ACF; Deutz records the A-side equivalent as P2045-00, short to battery, and keeps the plain open circuit apart as P2042-13.",["Open signal wire or disconnected plug at sensor B","Missing sensor ground","Signal wire shorted to supply voltage"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","Implausibly low DEF temperature in live data","Delayed start of dosing after a cold start"],2,3,["P2ACC","P2ACE","P2ACD","P2AD0","P2045"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2AD0:["Reductant Temperature Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","P2AD0 stands for short interruptions or jumps in the signal of reductant temperature sensor B. The current title reads circuit intermittent only, without erratic. No manufacturer publishes this test. The closest documented logic is GM's tank sensor check P205E in its 2025 DEF controller, which counts a failure when the value moves more than 4 °C within a ten-sample window and needs three such failures out of nine;",["Moisture or DEF residue in the sensor B connector","Terminal loosened by vibration","Wire breaking intermittently inside the insulation"],["Check engine light that appears sporadically","Jumping DEF temperature in live data"],2,1,["P2ACC","P2ACD","P2ACE","P2ACF","P2046"],"חיישן טמפרטורת אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2AD1:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch C/G Voltage Correlation","P2AD1 compares the voltages of position signals C and G and sets when they stop describing the same position. What the letters mean depends on the layout; GM's 2023 table 23OBDG07 for an engine with two throttle bodies is the clearest public key: C is sensor 1 and G sensor 2 of the bank 2 throttle (P0227/P0228 and P212C/P212D), so C/G is the internal pair of that second throttle, the counterpart of the bank 1 pair…",["Raised contact resistance in the throttle connector","Worn or drifting sensor track in the second throttle body","Fault on the shared 5 V reference or sensor ground"],["Check engine light on","Reduced power or limited throttle response"],2,3,["P2AD2","P2AD3","P2135","P0228","P212C","P212D"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ C/G — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2AD2:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch B/G Voltage Correlation","P2AD2 sets when signals B and G no longer agree in voltage. On engines with one throttle body per bank this is a cross-bank comparison: with GM's 2023 letter scheme, B is the second track of the bank 1 throttle and G the second track of the bank 2 throttle.",["High resistance at the pins of the throttle actuator connectors","Drifting position track in one of the throttle bodies","Damaged wiring to one throttle actuator"],["Check engine light on","Possible loss of power","Further throttle codes such as P2135 or P2136 stored"],2,3,["P2AD1","P2AD3","P2135","P2136","P212B"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ B/G — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2AD3:["Throttle/Pedal Position Sensor/Switch A/G Voltage Correlation","P2AD3 compares tracks A and G. In GM's 2023 scheme A is the first sensor of the bank 1 throttle body and G the second sensor of the bank 2 unit, so the pair links both throttles of a V engine and can reveal that one plate is not where the other suggests.",["Raised contact resistance in the connectors of both throttle actuators","One throttle body with a faulty position sensor","Fault on a shared sensor supply or ground"],["Check engine light on","Possible loss of power or emergency throttle mode"],2,3,["P2AD1","P2AD2","P2135","P2136","P212B"],"מתח חיישן/מתג מצב מצערת/דוושה‏ A/G — חוסר התאמה בין האותות"],P2AD4:["Intermediate System Voltage Low","P2AD4 reports that the voltage of an intermediate system, a supply level between the 12 V network and a high-voltage traction battery, has fallen below its lower limit. In practice this describes 48 V networks of mild hybrids, which carry a belt or integrated starter-generator and loads such as electric compressors; German makers agreed on such a level in 2011, and Audi and Mercedes-Benz use it since 2018.",["Weak or deeply discharged 48 V battery","Starter-generator not charging the intermediate network","DC/DC converter drawing the network down","Loose or corroded high-current connection"],["Warning lamp or message about the electrical system","Start-stop and electric boost unavailable","Engine may not restart via the starter-generator"],3,3,["P2AD5","P0562","P0A94"],"מערכת ביניים — מתח נמוך"],P2AD5:["Intermediate System Voltage High","P2AD5 is the high counterpart: the intermediate voltage level, in current vehicles mostly a 48 V mild-hybrid network, rises above its permitted maximum. Overvoltage typically arises when the starter-generator regenerates harder than the battery can accept, for example with a full or cold 48 V battery, a battery that has disconnected itself internally, or a faulty regulator in the generator or DC/DC converter.",["Starter-generator regulating the voltage too high","48 V battery disconnected internally or unable to accept charge","Faulty DC/DC converter feeding back into the network"],["Warning message about the electrical system","Recuperation, electric boost and start-stop unavailable"],3,3,["P2AD4","P0563","P0A94"],"מערכת ביניים — מתח גבוה"],P2AD6:["Reductant Pump Motor Position Sensor Circuit","P2AD6 is the general circuit code of the position sensor in the motor of the reductant (DEF) pump. Modern supply pumps often use a brushless motor whose rotor position must be known for commutation and speed control; a Cummins Emission Solutions patent names a Hall-effect rotor position sensor as one option and back-EMF evaluation as the sensorless alternative. No manufacturer publishes a description of P2AD6.",["Position sensor or electronics inside the pump module defective","DEF residue or corrosion in the pump connector","Missing supply or ground for the pump electronics"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","DEF dosing stops; countdown to speed limitation"],2,3,["P2AD7","P2AD8","P2AD9","P208A"],"חיישן מצב מנוע משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue) — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2AD7:["Reductant Pump Motor Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2AD7 sets when the motor position signal of the reductant pump is electrically valid but does not fit what the pump should be doing, for instance a rotor position or derived speed that is out of step with the commanded drive pattern. No maker documents P2AD7 publicly.",["Pump stiff or partly frozen, crystallised DEF in the pump head","Position sensor inside the pump giving a shifted signal","Controller software needing an update"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","Pressure build-up of the DEF system fails, often after cold nights"],2,3,["P2AD6","P2AD8","P2AD9","P208B"],"חיישן מצב מנוע משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue) — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2AD8:["Reductant Pump Motor Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2AD8 reports a reductant pump motor position signal stuck below its valid range. For Hall-type sensors this mostly means the output is pulled to ground permanently: a signal wire shorted to ground, a sensor that has lost its supply, or an internal short in the pump electronics.",["Internal short in the pump electronics","Position signal shorted to ground","Sensor supply missing, e.g. blown fuse or open feed"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","DEF pump does not run, no dosing"],2,3,["P2AD6","P2AD9","P2AD7","P208C"],"חיישן מצב מנוע משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2AD9:["Reductant Pump Motor Position Sensor Circuit High","P2AD9 is the high-side fault: the pump motor position signal stays above its permitted range. An open signal line pulled up by the controller's internal resistor, a broken sensor ground or a short to the supply rail produce this picture. Without changing position information, speed control fails and the pressure build-up may be aborted;",["Open signal line or broken sensor ground","DEF residue corroding the pump connector","Signal shorted to the supply rail"],["Check engine light and SCR warning","No DEF pressure build-up, dosing stops"],2,3,["P2AD6","P2AD8","P2AD7","P208D"],"חיישן מצב מנוע משאבת אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2ADA:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2ADA checks whether the second DEF tank temperature reading is plausible. GM documents it twice. In its 2017–2018 diesel tables (and again in 25OBDG06C) it is the DEF quality sensor temperature offset: after more than 28,800 s off, the quality sensor's thermistor may differ from the average of the exhaust temperature sensors by no more than 35 °C; 40 of 50 samples failing set a Type A code.",["DEF quality sensor with drifting temperature element","Reference temperature sensors reading wrong","Chafed engine harness disturbing the signals","Controller software needing an update"],["Check engine light after a cold start","DEF or SCR warning message"],2,1,["P2ADB","P2ADC","P2ADD","P2ADE","P205B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2ADB:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","P2ADB flags a value from the second DEF tank temperature sensor that lies below the lowest temperature the sensor can physically report, so the controller treats it as a circuit fault and not as cold fluid. GM is the documented user.",["Defective thermistor in the DEF quality or tank sensor unit","Moisture or DEF crystals in the sensor connector","Damaged signal or supply wiring to the tank sensor"],["Check engine light right after the fault is detected","DEF or SCR system warning in the cluster","Countdown to reduced power or restart lock if left unrepaired"],2,3,["P2ADA","P2ADC","P2ADD","P2ADE","P205C"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2ADC:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","P2ADC is the upper limit check on the same sensor B: the reported DEF temperature is higher than the fluid in the tank could ever get. In GM's 2017 and 2018 diesel calibrations the quality sensor thermistor has to exceed 155 °C in 40 of 50 samples, with cranking finished and more than 11 V at the powertrain relay; the outcome is a Type A code.",["Internal fault in the quality sensor or smart tank sensor unit","Chafed engine harness disturbing the sensor circuit","Corroded or loose pins at the tank sensor connector"],["Check engine light on","DEF system message, often together with other harness-related codes","Possible inducement countdown toward reduced power"],2,3,["P2ADA","P2ADB","P2ADD","P2ADE","P205D"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2ADD:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2ADD judges how the sensor B signal moves over time instead of how high it is. Fluid in a tank warms and cools slowly, so sudden jumps suggest a loose contact or a failing element. GM's 2017 and 2018 diesel tables compare every raw thermistor sample with an envelope that starts at the last good value and widens toward the −55 °C and 155 °C limits as bad samples pile up; 40 failures in 50 samples give a Type A code.",["Loose or corroded contact at the tank sensor connector","Chafed harness with intermittent contact","Degrading thermistor in the quality or tank sensor unit"],["Check engine light that may return after clearing","Jumping DEF temperature in live data","DEF or SCR warning message"],2,3,["P2ADA","P2ADB","P2ADC","P2ADE","P205E"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2ADE:["Reductant Tank Temperature Sensor B Circuit","P2ADE is the general circuit code for reductant tank temperature sensor B, intended for systems that report a fault on this input without splitting it into low, high or erratic. No manufacturer documents P2ADE publicly.",["Open signal line or unplugged tank sensor connector","Failed tank sensor unit","Input fault in the SCR or engine control module"],["Check engine light on","DEF or SCR warning","Possible inducement countdown"],2,3,["P2ADA","P2ADB","P2ADC","P2ADD","P205A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מיכל אוריאה (AdBlue)‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2ADF:["Intake Air System Leak Bank 2","P2ADF means the engine control module has concluded that air reaches the cylinders of bank 2 without passing the air measurement. Audi documents the code for the 4.0 litre TFSI V8 in the A8, S8, SQ7, SQ8, RS Q8, RS 6 Avant and RS 7 from model years 2019 to 2023. Drivers notice the check engine or exhaust warning lamp and a whistle from the engine bay;",["Leaking full-load crankcase breather line on bank 2 (Audi 4.0 TFSI)","Split intake or boost hose on bank 2","Leaking intake manifold gasket on bank 2","Crankcase ventilation valve not sealing"],["Check engine or exhaust warning light on","Whistling noise from the engine bay","Rough idle or misfire codes"],2,1,["P2279","P0174","P2189","P0507"],"דליפת מערכת אוויר יניקה (בנק 2)"],P2AE0:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Open Bank 1","P2AE0 says the calibration (trim) wire of bank 1's intake O2 sensor has lost continuity. On a Bosch-type wide-band element this is pin 5 (RT/IA), which connects a resistor in the plug that Bosch uses to set the characteristic of each individual sensor; without it the ECM scales the oxygen signal wrongly. No manufacturer documents P2AE0 publicly, and no bulletin lists it.",["Trim lead (pin 5) broken in the harness","Trim contact pushed back or corroded in the sensor plug","Calibration resistor inside the sensor connector open"],["Check engine light on","EGR reduced or run without oxygen feedback","NOx emissions may rise"],2,1,["P2AE1","P2AE2","P2AE9","P2AE3","P2626"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מעגל פתוח (נתק) (בנק 1)"],P2AE1:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Low Bank 1","P2AE1 is stored when the voltage on the trim circuit of the bank 1 intake oxygen sensor falls below its window. With the ignition on, the 2010 Saab 9-5 expects roughly 2.8 V on terminal 5 of its wide-band probe, the trim connection; a value near zero suggests a lead rubbing on ground or a shorted resistor in the sensor plug.",["Trim lead chafed through to ground","Calibration resistor in the sensor plug shorted","Open trim lead on sensors whose interface reports it as low"],["Check engine light on","EGR cut back, possibly higher NOx"],2,1,["P2AE0","P2AE2","P2AEA","P2AE4","P2627"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2AE2:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit High Bank 1","P2AE2 means the voltage on the trim lead of the intake air O2 sensor for bank 1 is too high. In the six-wire harness of a wide-band probe this line runs next to the heater feed, so a pinched wire or moisture bridging the pins in the connector can drag it towards battery voltage. Ford's 2012 OBD summary books a trim lead shorted to battery as P2628 on NTK probes and under the general high code P0132 on Bosch probes;",["Trim lead touching the heater supply","Moisture bridging contacts in the sensor plug","Internal short in the sensor or its connector module"],["Check engine light on","EGR reduced, NOx may rise"],2,1,["P2AE0","P2AE1","P2AEB","P2AE5","P2628"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2AE3:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit Open Bank 1","P2AE3 reports a break in the pumping current lead of the bank 1 intake oxygen sensor, pin 1 of a Bosch LSU 4.9 (APE/IP). Through this wire the ECM drives current into the pump cell while the Nernst cell is kept on its set point; Ford's patent US9441564B2 explains that the size of that current reflects the oxygen share of the charge, from which the EGR dilution is calculated.",["Pump current lead (pin 1) broken","Sensor plug loose or not latched","Pump cell inside the sensor open"],["Check engine light on","EGR runs without sensor feedback or is switched off"],2,1,["P2AE4","P2AE5","P2AE6","P2AEC","P2AE0","P2237"],"זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מעגל פתוח (נתק) (בנק 1)"],P2AE4:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit Low Bank 1","P2AE4 flags too low a level in the pumping current circuit belonging to the bank 1 intake sensor, usually a pump lead chafed through to ground or an internal short in the pump cell. Saab's 2010 9-5 gives a useful reference for the same wire on its exhaust probe: about 2.8 V on terminal 1 at ignition-on with the sensor unplugged, and its low code P2238 sets when the signal stays under 1.7 V for 3 s on overrun.",["Pump current lead shorted to ground","Internal short in the pump cell","Sensor interface in the ECM faulty"],["Check engine light on","EGR reduced or switched off","Possibly higher NOx at an emissions test"],2,1,["P2AE3","P2AE5","P2AED","P2AE1","P2238"],"זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2AE5:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit High Bank 1","P2AE5 is the high-side fault of the pumping current lead on the bank 1 intake oxygen sensor. A short to the heater supply or another battery feed in the harness is the classic cause; because the intake sensor works in damp air close to where blow-by gas and EGR enter, water in the plug comes next.",["Pump current lead shorted to the heater or another supply","Water or condensate in the sensor plug","Sensor interface in the ECM damaged by the short"],["Check engine light on","EGR reduced, NOx may rise"],2,1,["P2AE3","P2AE4","P2AEE","P2AE2","P2239"],"זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2AE6:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Open Bank 1","P2AE6 points to an open negative current control line on the bank 1 intake air oxygen sensor. This is the shared return of pump and Nernst cell, which Bosch names virtual ground (IPN/VM, pin 2); Saab's 2010 9-5 shows about 2.5 V on it at ignition-on, a bias that lets the pump current change direction.",["Virtual-ground return lead (pin 2) broken","Corroded or loose return contact in the plug","Internal break of the common electrode in the sensor"],["Check engine light on","EGR runs without oxygen feedback"],2,1,["P2AE7","P2AE8","P2AE3","P2AEF","P2251"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מעגל הבקרה פתוח (נתק) (בנק 1)"],P2AE7:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Low Bank 1","P2AE7 is set when the virtual-ground return of the bank 1 intake oxygen sensor is pulled below its bias. In operation this lead sits roughly 2.5 V above chassis, as Saab's 2010 9-5 documents for its wide-band probe; a wire touching the engine block, a bracket or the intake pipe drags it towards zero.",["Return lead chafed against engine or bracket","Internal short of the common electrode to ground","Bias source in the ECM faulty"],["Check engine light on","EGR cut back, possibly higher NOx"],2,1,["P2AE6","P2AE8","P2AE4","P2AF0","P2252"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2AE8:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit High Bank 1","P2AE8 reports that, on bank 1's intake air oxygen sensor, the negative current control line sits above its intended level. For the bias on this return to climb towards battery voltage, something must feed it: most often the heater supply sharing the six-pin plug, sometimes condensate in a connector that collects moisture from the intake air.",["Return lead shorted to the heater supply","Condensate inside the sensor connector","Internal short between heater and cell"],["Check engine light on","EGR reduced, NOx may rise"],2,1,["P2AE6","P2AE7","P2AE5","P2AF1","P2253"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2AE9:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Open Bank 2","P2AE9 is the bank 2 version of the open trim circuit: the line from the ECM to the calibration resistor of the second intake air oxygen sensor has no continuity. A separate sensor for bank 2 only makes sense where each cylinder bank draws its charge or EGR through its own path; nobody has published a vehicle that uses P2AE9.",["Trim contact pushed back in the plug","Trim lead broken, often near the hot exhaust of bank 2","Calibration resistor in the sensor connector open"],["Check engine light on","EGR on bank 2 reduced or without feedback"],2,1,["P2AEA","P2AEB","P2AE0","P2AEC","P2629"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מעגל פתוח (נתק) (בנק 2)"],P2AEA:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit Low Bank 2","P2AEA reports a trim circuit voltage below the permitted range at the bank 2 intake O2 sensor. Likely culprits are a trim wire grounded where the harness passes the second turbocharger, or a damaged resistor inside the sensor connector. Ford's 2012 summary assigns the exhaust analog P2630 to NTK probes for an open or grounded RL lead, a reminder that a low reading need not mean a short.",["Trim lead grounded near the second turbocharger","Calibration resistor in the plug damaged","Fault in a ground or ECM path shared with bank 1"],["Check engine light on","Higher NOx, driveability usually unchanged"],2,1,["P2AE9","P2AEB","P2AE1","P2AED","P2630"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2AEB:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Trim Circuit High Bank 2","P2AEB indicates excessive voltage on the trim wire serving the second bank's intake O2 sensor. A short to the heater or another supply wire, or moisture bridging contacts in the plug, can lift the line; Saab's 2010 9-5 test procedure for the comparable exhaust probe expects roughly 2.8 V on its trim terminal at ignition-on, so a reading near battery voltage is a clear sign.",["Trim lead shorted to the heater or another supply","Moisture bridging contacts in the plug","Internal short in the sensor connector module"],["Check engine light on","EGR on bank 2 reduced, NOx may rise"],2,1,["P2AE9","P2AEA","P2AE2","P2AEE","P2631"],"תיקון זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2AEC:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit Open Bank 2","P2AEC means the pumping current wire of the second-bank intake oxygen sensor is interrupted. On a Bosch-style element the ECM uses this lead to push oxygen into or out of the measuring gap until the Nernst cell is balanced; the current needed is the oxygen signal.",["Pump current lead broken, often from heat near bank 2 exhaust","Sensor plug loose or not latched","Pump cell inside the sensor open"],["Check engine light on","EGR on bank 2 without feedback or switched off"],2,1,["P2AED","P2AEE","P2AEF","P2AE3","P2240"],"זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מעגל פתוח (נתק) (בנק 2)"],P2AED:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit Low Bank 2","P2AED stands for a pumping current circuit on the bank 2 intake oxygen sensor that reads below its limit. A pump lead grounded on the engine or a breakdown inside the pump cell are the usual reasons.",["Pump current lead grounded on the engine","Breakdown inside the pump cell","ECM sensor interface faulty (likely if bank 1 also reports)"],["Check engine light on","EGR on bank 2 limited, possibly higher NOx"],2,1,["P2AEC","P2AEE","P2AE4","P2AEA","P2241"],"זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2AEE:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Pumping Current Circuit High Bank 2","P2AEE marks the pumping current lead of the bank 2 intake air oxygen sensor as too high. Contact with the heater feed in the shared plug, chafing against a live wire or water that has entered the connector can raise it. On exhaust probes of bank 2, Ford records a battery short of the IP wire as P0152, and CARB obliges the ECM to detect such out-of-range inputs;",["Pump current lead touching the heater feed","Harness chafed against a live wire","Water inside the sensor connector"],["Check engine light on","EGR on bank 2 reduced, NOx may rise"],2,1,["P2AEC","P2AED","P2AE5","P2AEB","P2242"],"זרם שאיבת חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2AEF:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Open Bank 2","P2AEF indicates that the return line, or virtual ground, of the bank 2 intake oxygen sensor is open. Both cells of a wide-band element reference this lead, pin 2 (IPN/VM) on the Bosch LSU 4.9, which the ECM biases so current can flow both ways.",["Return lead (pin 2) broken","Return contact corroded or loose","Internal break of the common electrode"],["Check engine light on","Usually no noticeable change in driveability"],2,1,["P2AF0","P2AF1","P2AEC","P2AE6","P2254"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מעגל הבקרה פתוח (נתק) (בנק 2)"],P2AF0:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit Low Bank 2","P2AF0 is stored when the negative current control circuit of the bank 2 intake oxygen sensor falls below its window. Because the return is meant to sit at a bias of roughly 2.5 V, which Saab's 2010 9-5 lists as the test value on terminal 2 of its exhaust probe, any path to chassis ground pulls it down: insulation worn through at a clip, a crushed connector or an internal short in the sensor.",["Return lead worn through at a clip or bracket","Crushed or damaged sensor connector","Internal short of the sensor to ground"],["Check engine light on","EGR on bank 2 cut back, possibly higher NOx"],2,1,["P2AEF","P2AF1","P2AED","P2AE7","P2255"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2AF1:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Negative Current Control Circuit High Bank 2","P2AF1 is the high-side fault of the virtual-ground return on the bank 2 intake air oxygen sensor. Lifting this biased line towards supply voltage requires contact with a feed, most often the heater circuit in the same plug, or condensed water inside a connector. Once the return drifts up, the ECM can neither regulate the Nernst cell nor interpret the pump current, so the oxygen share of the bank 2 charge is lost.",["Return lead shorted to the heater circuit","Condensed water inside a connector","Bias source in the ECM faulty"],["Check engine light on","EGR on bank 2 reduced, NOx may rise"],2,1,["P2AEF","P2AF0","P2AE8","P2AEE","P2256"],"זרם שלילי חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2AF2:["Starter Relay C Control Circuit/Open","P2AF2 reports an open or otherwise faulty control line for a third starter relay. Such a relay appears where cranking is split across several switching stages, for instance on stop-start engines. No manufacturer documents P2AF2 publicly.",["Broken control wire or unplugged relay connector","Open relay coil","Blown fuse or missing supply to the relay coil","Faulty output driver in the control module"],["Stop-start function disabled","Occasional or permanent no-crank","Warning lamp depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P2AF3","P2AF4","P2AF5","P2AF6","P2AF7","P0615","P26E4"],"ממסר מתנע‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2AF3:["Starter Relay C Control Circuit Low","P2AF3 sets when the control line of starter relay C is pulled toward ground at a moment the module expects a different level. What that does to the relay depends on the driver type: with ground-side switching the short acts like a permanent on command, with supply-side switching the coil never gets current. No manufacturer publishes a set condition for P2AF3.",["Control wire chafed through to ground","Shorted relay coil","Faulty output driver in the control module"],["Stop-start inoperative","Relay energised all the time or not at all, depending on circuit design","Possible no-crank"],2,1,["P2AF2","P2AF4","P2AF5","P2AF8","P0616","P26E5"],"ממסר מתנע‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2AF4:["Starter Relay C Control Circuit High","P2AF4 points to a control wire of starter relay C that carries battery voltage when the module has switched its driver off, typically because it touches a 12 V feed or because the driver leaks. With supply-side switching that can keep the coil energised; with ground-side switching the module can no longer pull the relay in. No manufacturer publishes P2AF4.",["Control wire shorted to a 12 V circuit","Leaking or failed output driver","Water in the relay socket or power distribution box"],["Stop-start disabled","Relay may stay engaged with ignition off","Warning lamp depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P2AF2","P2AF3","P2AF5","P2AF9","P0617","P26E6"],"ממסר מתנע‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2AF5:["Starter Relay C Stuck On","P2AF5 means starter relay C remains in its energised state when it should have dropped out. Stellantis uses it as Starter Relay 3 Stuck On for the power control relay of its dual-battery stop-start system: Jeep Grand Cherokee 2021 to 2025, Wagoneer and Grand Wagoneer 2022 to 2025, RAM 1500 2025, and earlier Pacifica, Durango, Compass, Wrangler and Gladiator.",["Loose or corroded B+ connection at main or auxiliary battery","Depleted auxiliary battery causing a false fail","Open or poorly seated 150 A fuse or fuse array","Power control relay mechanically stuck"],["No crank or no start","Stop-start inoperative, service message for the system","Auxiliary battery not being charged"],1,1,["P2AF6","P2AF2","P2AFA","P00FD","P0562","P26F0"],"ממסר מתנע‏ C — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2AF6:["Starter Relay C Stuck Off","P2AF6 is the reverse fault on relay C: commanded to switch, the relay does not change state. Stellantis names it Starter Relay 3 Stuck Off, on some Wagoneers Dual Starter Relay Stuck. During an auto-start the PCM energises the relay to split the batteries;",["Power distribution centre connector not fully seated","PCM software needing an update","Depleted auxiliary battery causing a false fail","Power control relay not switching"],["Check engine light on","Stop-start disabled","Occasional failure to restart after an auto-stop"],1,1,["P2AF5","P2AF2","P2AFB","P00FD","P26F1"],"ממסר מתנע‏ C — תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2AF7:["Starter Relay D Control Circuit/Open","P2AF7 is the open-circuit or general fault on the control line of a fourth starter relay, relay D. Four separately monitored starter relays only make sense where there is more than one cranking path, for example a pinion relay, a second starter or a battery isolation stage on a stop-start engine. No manufacturer documents P2AF7 publicly, and the Stellantis bulletins that use relay C do not name a relay D.",["Broken control wire or corroded connector","Open coil in relay D","Blown fuse feeding the relay coil"],["Auto-stop not available","Intermittent no-crank","Stored code, lamp depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P2AF8","P2AF9","P2AFA","P2AFB","P2AF2","P0615"],"ממסר מתנע‏ D — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2AF8:["Starter Relay D Control Circuit Low","P2AF8 is logged when the control line of starter relay D shows a short to ground. Depending on whether the module switches the coil on its ground side or its supply side, the relay then either sits permanently energised or can no longer be operated.",["Spread or bent terminals in the power distribution centre connector","Control wire shorted to ground","Shorted relay coil"],["No start or no crank","Several unrelated electrical faults at the same time","Stop-start unavailable"],2,1,["P2AF7","P2AF9","P2AF3","P0616","P0627"],"ממסר מתנע‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2AF9:["Starter Relay D Control Circuit High","P2AF9 indicates that the control line of starter relay D sits at supply voltage although the driver is switched off, mostly a short to a 12 V circuit or a leaking driver stage. With ground-side switching the module can then no longer energise the coil, because both coil ends see battery voltage;",["Control wire chafed against a live circuit","Leaking output driver in the control module","Internal fault in relay D"],["Stop-start disabled","Starter may not engage, or in rare cases keep running","Stored code, lamp depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P2AF7","P2AF8","P2AFA","P2AF4","P0617"],"ממסר מתנע‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2AFA:["Starter Relay D Stuck On","P2AFA describes starter relay D staying engaged although the control module has commanded it to release; the module infers this from a feedback signal, a voltage or current that should have changed. No manufacturer documents P2AFA publicly. The closest published case is relay C at Stellantis, where Starter Relay 3 Stuck On (P2AF5) is detected from the voltage gap between main and auxiliary battery.",["Welded relay contacts","Control wire receiving voltage from another circuit","Output driver not switching off"],["Starter keeps turning or grinding after the engine starts","Stop-start disabled","Battery drain while parked"],2,1,["P2AFB","P2AF5","P2AF9","P26F0","P26F2"],"ממסר מתנע‏ D — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2AFB:["Starter Relay D Stuck Off","P2AFB is set when starter relay D ignores an on command: the module energises it, but the expected change of voltage or current in the switched circuit never appears. No manufacturer documents P2AFB publicly. Stellantis shows on relay C how such a check works.",["Burnt or corroded relay contacts","Low supply voltage or poor ground at the relay","Loose connector at the relay or distribution box"],["Engine does not crank on the affected path","Auto-stop permanently unavailable","Stored code, lamp depending on manufacturer"],2,1,["P2AFA","P2AF6","P2AF7","P26F1","P26F3"],"ממסר מתנע‏ D — תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2AFC:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 4 Circuit","P2AFC is the general circuit code for a fourth engine coolant temperature sensor. Engines with split cooling, electric pumps or separate head, block, radiator and heater circuits carry several such sensors, and how they are numbered is up to each maker. No manufacturer documents a set condition for P2AFC publicly;",["Open wire or loose connector at sensor 4","Failed NTC element in sensor 4","Faulty input stage in the engine control module"],["Check engine light on","Cooling fans running more than usual on substitute value","Thermal management in default mode"],1,1,["P2AFD","P2AFE","P2AFF","P2BB4","P2182","P01E3","P2B2B"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 4 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2AFD:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 4 Circuit Range/Performance","P2AFD flags a sensor 4 coolant reading that stays inside the electrical limits but makes no sense, for instance a value that disagrees with the engine's other temperature readings once everything has cooled down for hours, or that hardly moves while the engine warms up. CARB requires such rationality checks for coolant temperature inputs used by emission controls.",["Drifting sensor element","Corrosion adding resistance in the connector","Air pocket at the sensor after coolant service","Control software needing an update"],["Check engine light, often only after a cold start","Sensor 4 value clearly differing from the others in live data"],1,1,["P2AFC","P2AFE","P2AFF","P2BB4","P2183","P01E4","P2B2C"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 4 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2AFE:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 4 Circuit Low","Coolant sensors are NTC thermistors, so a signal from sensor 4 that is too low stands for an impossibly hot reading, usually a signal wire grounded or a shorted element. GM documents P2AFE for the 2.7 L turbo four (L3B) in its 2019 tables: the configurable temperature input system sets it when the resistance of the sensor 4 channel drops below about 41 Ω, corresponding to 150 °C, for 5 s within a 6 s window;",["Signal wire shorted to ground, for example by harness chafing","Internally shorted sensor","Faulty input in the engine control module"],["Check engine light after two trips","Cooling fans running at full speed","Implausibly high coolant temperature in live data"],1,1,["P2AFF","P2AFC","P2AFD","P2BB4","P2184","P01E5","P2B2D"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 4 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2AFF:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 4 Circuit High","P2AFF reports an excessive sensor 4 signal. For an NTC thermistor that means an implausibly cold reading, mostly from an open circuit, an unplugged connector or a line shorted to voltage. GM's 2019 tables for the 2.7 L L3B set P2AFF once the resistance rises above roughly 355 kΩ, equal to −60 °C, for 5 s in a 6 s window, with an engine run time above 10 s among the enabling conditions;",["Open signal wire or unplugged connector","Chafed engine harness","Sensor element open internally"],["Check engine light after two trips","Implausibly cold coolant temperature in live data","Thermal management running on a default value"],1,1,["P2AFE","P2AFC","P2AFD","P2BB4","P2185","P01E6","P2B2E"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 4 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2B00:["Cylinder 1 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B00 says the engine module could not confirm, with the engine past its cold-start phase, that injection pulses it commanded for cylinder 1 really happened. GM documents the check for its petrol direct-injection engines: the ECM digitises the voltage across both injector wires and looks for the small flux signature the armature leaves when it lifts.",["Engine harness chafed through to ground (GM L3B – above the camshaft carrier or near the left shock tower)","Armature or needle of the cylinder 1 injector sticking, so no opening signature appears","Outdated ECM calibration (GM service update for the 1.2 L LIH)","High contact resistance at the cylinder 1 injector connector"],["Check engine light after the second faulty trip","Rough running or misfire on cylinder 1 (P0301), sometimes no noticeable symptom","With a harness short, several unrelated codes at once and possibly a no-start"],2,1,["P2B08","P2B01","P2B96","P02EE","P0201","P0301"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B01:["Cylinder 2 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B01 is stored when the ECM keeps missing the opening signature of the cylinder 2 injector in normal running, i.e. it has no proof that fuel was delivered on that cylinder's commanded pulses. GM uses the code on direct-injection petrol engines. The 2019 table for the 2.7 L L3B judges 100 failures out of 380 samples; the 2025 tables reach a verdict sooner, after 50 to 100 samples.",["Engine harness shorted to ground at a chafe point (GM L3B bulletin series PIT5677)","Cylinder 2 injector opening sluggishly or not at all (deposits, worn armature)","Corroded or loose injector 2 connector distorting the feedback voltage"],["Warning lamp after two trips","Uneven idle, possibly misfire on cylinder 2","Together with many other codes and erratic behaviour when the harness is shorted"],2,1,["P2B09","P2B00","P2B02","P2B96","P02EF","P0202","P0302"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B02:["Cylinder 3 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B02 concerns cylinder 3: in warm operation the ECM did not see the voltage bump that marks the cylinder 3 injector actually opening, often enough to count pulses as not delivered. On GM's 1.2 L LIH three-cylinder, cylinder 3 is the last one, and the 2025 table for that family (cylinders 1–3 only) decides after 50 to 100 samples, Type B.",["ECM calibration with false detections (GM 1.2 L LIH, service update A202310450)","Cylinder 3 injector not lifting reliably","Damaged injector 3 wiring or connector"],["Check engine light, often without any driveability complaint","On a real injector fault rough running on cylinder 3 (P0303)"],2,1,["P2B0A","P2B01","P2B03","P2B96","P02F0","P0203","P0303"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 3 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B03:["Cylinder 4 Injection Pulse Performance","With P2B03 the engine module reports that cylinder 4 injection pulses went unconfirmed after warm-up: the coil voltage showed no proof of the armature moving. In GM's lists the code belongs to four-cylinder direct-injection engines – the three-cylinder tables end at P2B02 – and GM's 2025 four-cylinder table needs 50 to 100 samples for a Type B verdict with two trips.",["Harness chafed near the turbo actuator or elsewhere on the engine (GM 2.7 L)","Poor contact in the fuel rail injector connector","Cylinder 4 injector worn or sticking"],["Lamp on after the second faulty trip","Possibly misfire on cylinder 4 (P0304) or under load","Further injector codes of the same cylinder stored at the same time"],2,1,["P2B0B","P2B02","P2B04","P2B96","P02F1","P0204","P0304"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 4 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B04:["Cylinder 5 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B04 extends the warm-running missed-pulse check to cylinder 5, so it only matters on engines with five or more cylinders. No manufacturer documents P2B04 publicly as a monitor of its own. Among GM's 2025 V8 documents it turns up solely inside code lists attached to common calibration maps;",["Cylinder 5 injector sticking or opening too slowly","Chafed or high-resistance wiring to injector 5","Calibration error in the engine software"],["Engine warning lamp on","Rough running or misfire on cylinder 5 (P0305)"],2,1,["P2B0C","P2B03","P2B05","P2B96","P02F2","P0205","P0305"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 5 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B05:["Cylinder 6 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B05 marks missed injection pulses on cylinder 6 outside the cold-start window; on a six-cylinder engine this is the last cylinder in the order of numbers. No manufacturer documents P2B05 publicly as a stand-alone check. GM's 2025 V8 calibration (25OBDG06A/06B) lists it only in the support tables shared by the pulse family.",["Deposits or wear on the cylinder 6 injector hampering small pulses","Contact problem at the injector 6 plug","Injector driver or voltage sensing in the ECM faulty"],["Check engine light","Slight shaking at idle or low speed, misfire on cylinder 6 (P0306)"],2,1,["P2B0D","P2B04","P2B06","P2B96","P02F3","P0206","P0306"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 6 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B06:["Cylinder 7 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B06 is the warm-engine pulse check for cylinder 7 and so practically limited to V8 and larger engines. No manufacturer documents P2B06 publicly in its own entry. In GM's 2025 V8 tables the code appears only in the lists of a shared calibration: a pulse counts as missing when the measured opening magnitude stays below a fixed value of 75 across rail pressures from 0.4 to 24 MPa.",["Cylinder 7 injector with weak or missing armature lift","Wiring to injector 7 damaged by heat or chafing","Rail pressure outside the plausible range, distorting the opening signal"],["Engine light on after two trips","Misfire on cylinder 7 (P0307), rough idle"],2,1,["P2B0E","P2B05","P2B07","P2B96","P02F4","P0207","P0307"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 7 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B07:["Cylinder 8 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B07 closes the warm-running row at cylinder 8, and the engine-wide check counting missed pulses over all cylinders is P2B96. No manufacturer documents P2B07 publicly as a separate monitor; GM's 2025 V8 tables mention it only in the code lists of shared calibration tables, while their cylinder 8 warm faults run as P10B1/P10B2.",["Cylinder 8 injector not opening properly","Heat-damaged harness section at the rear of the engine","Loose or corroded injector 8 connector"],["Check engine light","Misfire on cylinder 8 (P0308), especially at idle"],2,1,["P2B0F","P2B06","P2B96","P02F5","P0208","P0308"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 8 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B08:["Cold Start Cylinder 1 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B08 is the cold-start version of the cylinder 1 pulse check. While the catalyst is being heated, many direct-injection engines split each injection into two or three small pulses, and CARB requires for 20/50/100 % of model years 2026/2027/2028 that missing split or multiple pulses be detected during the cold-start strategy.",["Cold-start software anomaly (GM 1.2 L LIH, fixed by ECM reprogramming)","Cylinder 1 injector sluggish when cold, missing the short split pulses","Contact fault in injector 1 wiring that shows mainly when cold"],["Warning lamp, often with the engine running normally once warm","Possibly slightly rough running in the first seconds after a cold start","Code returns only after a long standstill, not on warm restarts"],2,1,["P2B00","P2B09","P2B95","P050D","P0201","P0301"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B09:["Cold Start Cylinder 2 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B09 reports that while the catalyst is being warmed after a cold start the ECM missed the opening trace of injector 2 on too many commanded pulses. CARB defines the window: at least six hours engine-off, ambient at or above −6.7 °C and coolant no more than 15 °C warmer than ambient. GM already ran the test in 2019 on the 2.7 L L3B, setting it after 100 failures in 380 samples, Type B.",["Outdated ECM calibration (GM bulletin 20-NA-230)","Cylinder 2 injector not responding to the short cold-start pulses","Wiring or connector problem on injector 2"],["Check engine light after cold starts on two trips","Usually no driveability issue once the engine is warm"],1,1,["P2B01","P2B08","P2B0A","P2B95","P0202","P0302"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B0A:["Cold Start Cylinder 3 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B0A stands for missed cold-start pulses on cylinder 3. For the GM 1.2 L LIH with its three cylinders it is the highest cold-start cylinder code, since that engine's 2025 table stops at P2B0A.",["ECM software anomaly on the GM 1.2 L LIH (service update A202310450)","Cylinder 3 injector reacting too slowly when cold","Injector 3 connector with poor contact"],["Lamp on, code stored only after a cold start","Engine runs normally once warm"],1,1,["P2B02","P2B09","P2B0B","P2B95","P0203","P0303"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 3 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B0B:["Cold Start Cylinder 4 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B0B covers cylinder 4 during the cold-start strategy and in GM's tables belongs to four-cylinder and larger engines. GM's 2025 four-cylinder table sets the window via P2B95 differently from the three-cylinder: catalyst below 400 °C, 450–2,800 rpm, pedal up to 35 % and less than 100 s run time, so the test may continue while pulling away. The cylinder code itself is Type B after 50 to 100 samples.",["ECM calibration needing an update (GM bulletin 20-NA-230)","Harness damage or poor contact at the fuel rail connector (GM 2.7 L)","Cylinder 4 injector sluggish at low temperature"],["Warning lamp after cold starts","Possibly slightly uneven running during the first minute"],2,1,["P2B03","P2B0A","P2B0C","P2B95","P0204","P0304"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 4 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B0C:["Cold Start Cylinder 5 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B0C flags cylinder 5 when its injector fails to show an opening signature on the split pulses used to heat the catalyst after a cold start. Publicly it is documented only by GM, in the 2025 V8 table 25OBDG06A, which lists the cold-start codes for all eight cylinders (P2B08–P2B0F): Type B, decision after 50 to 100 samples.",["Cylinder 5 injector not lifting on the short cold-start pulses","Injector 5 wiring or connector with a contact fault","ECM calibration issue (check for software updates)"],["Check engine light after two cold-start trips","Usually unremarkable running once warm, maybe a short rough idle when cold"],2,1,["P2B04","P2B0B","P2B0D","P2B95","P0205","P0305"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 5 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B0D:["Cold Start Cylinder 6 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B0D belongs to the cold-start family and points at cylinder 6: while the engine was splitting injections to heat the catalyst, the ECM failed to register the armature-lift voltage signature on too many of that injector's pulses. GM publishes it in the 2025 V8 table 25OBDG06A as Type B with a verdict after 50 to 100 samples.",["Cylinder 6 injector opening sluggishly on short pulses when cold (deposits, worn armature)","Corroded connector or chafed wire at injector 6 distorting the feedback voltage","ECM calibration detecting the opening signature unreliably in the cold-start phase"],["Check engine light after two cold starts with the fault","Uneven idle in the first minute after a cold start, later normal"],2,1,["P2B05","P2B0C","P2B0E","P2B95","P0206","P0306"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 6 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B0E:["Cold Start Cylinder 7 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B0E is the cylinder 7 entry of the cold-start pulse check. On engines that fire two or three short injections per cycle while heating the catalyst, the ECM expects each of them to show an opening signature on the injector feedback voltage; for cylinder 7 too many did not.",["Cylinder 7 injector not lifting on the very short split pulses (deposits, armature wear)","Enable or command wire of injector 7 damaged, falsifying the measured voltage","ECM software with an overly strict opening-signature evaluation"],["Warning lamp after the second faulty cold start","Slight shaking right after a cold start, often nothing noticeable"],2,1,["P2B06","P2B0D","P2B0F","P2B95","P2B96","P0207","P0307"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 7 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B0F:["Cold Start Cylinder 8 Injection Pulse Performance","P2B0F closes the cold-start series with cylinder 8, so it only appears on eight-cylinder engines; publicly GM documents it, in table 25OBDG06A for its 2025 V8 family (Type B, two trips, 50 to 100 samples). The ECM reads the voltage across the injector enable and command wires and treats a pulse as undelivered when no opening magnitude shows up during catalyst heating.",["Needle or armature of the cylinder 8 injector sticking on cold short pulses","Loose or corroded connector at injector 8","Chafed injector harness on the bank carrying cylinder 8"],["Check engine light, frequently without driveability complaints","With a real injector fault, rough cold idle and possibly misfire on cylinder 8 (P0308)"],2,1,["P2B07","P2B0E","P2B95","P2B96","P0208","P0308"],"פולס הזרקת צילינדר התנעה קרה‏ 8 — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B10:["Cylinder 1 Injection Pulse Offset Not Learned","P2B10 means the engine control holds no valid learned offset for injector 1 – the correction of the opening time used for very small injection quantities has not been established. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Ford, the one maker with a published monitor for this group, lists only the exceeded-limit codes (P2B11 and siblings) for its Power Stroke diesels.",["Learn values cleared – after replacing injector 1 or the control unit, or after an adaption reset with a scan tool","Too few coasting phases with fuel cut-off for the learn to run","Injector 1 opening inconsistently, so no stable value is found"],["Warning lamp, otherwise often no noticeable effect","Possibly harder combustion noise at idle on cylinder 1"],2,1,["P2B11","P2B12","P02CC","P02CD","P0263","P0201"],"היסט פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 1 — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2B11:["Cylinder 1 Injection Pulse Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B11 says the learned small-quantity correction for injector 1 has drifted beyond what the engine control may apply. Ford documents the code for its 3.0 L and 6.7 L Power Stroke diesels under Zero Fuel Calibration: the PCM fires a tiny test injection, compares the energising time that produced a measurable effect with the target stored for that injector and sets the code when the result is at least 156 µs too short…",["Incorrectly learned injector values in the PCM (Ford TSB 18-2015, reset and reprogramming)","Injector 1 worn or coked so its opening behaviour has really shifted","Disturbed crankshaft speed signal falsifying the learn result"],["Check engine light","Diesel knock at idle, sometimes together with balance code P0263"],2,1,["P2B10","P2B13","P0263","P02CC","P02CD","P02EE"],""],P2B12:["Cylinder 2 Injection Pulse Offset Not Learned","P2B12 is stored when injector 2's pulse offset has not been learned, so the controller still relies on a default value for the smallest injections. The public record contains no manufacturer using this exact code; the explanation here follows from the title and from the neighbouring monitors.",["Driving profile without enough fuel cut-off phases (constant load, towing)","Adaption values reset after work on injector 2 or the fuel system","Crankshaft speed signal too noisy to detect the test injection"],["Warning lamp without a clear driveability complaint","Possibly louder combustion on cylinder 2 at low load"],2,1,["P2B13","P2B10","P2B14","P02CE","P02CF","P0266"],"היסט פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 2 — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2B13:["Cylinder 2 Injection Pulse Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B13 concerns injector 2 on Ford's Power Stroke diesels: its zero-fuel learn value has run past the permitted band. Ford's 2023 OBD summary shows when the learn runs: continuously, typically within about 30 s, with coolant of at least 50 °C, intake air between 0 and 75 °C, fuel of at least 10 °C, at least 10 V supply, almost no pedal (up to 2 %) and rail pressure within 50 bar of its target.",["Steering wheel oscillation disturbing the crank or cam signal (Ford SSM 48877)","Injector 2 with genuinely shifted opening time due to wear or deposits","Implausible learned values in the PCM"],["Check engine light","Often no running fault; with a worn injector, knocking or rough idle"],2,1,["P2B12","P2B11","P2B15","P0266","P02CE","P02CF","P0335"],""],P2B14:["Cylinder 3 Injection Pulse Offset Not Learned","P2B14 tells that no offset has yet been learned for injector 3. No carmaker publishes this code for a specific engine, and the GM and Ford tables checked do not contain it. A GM patent on fast learning of diesel injector corrections shows why such a learn can take long: corrections are kept per injector and per rail pressure level, so a six-cylinder with four pressure levels needs 24 learned cells, each filled only…",["Learn not yet completed for all rail pressure levels of injector 3","Injector 3 or control unit recently replaced without completing the learn","Rail pressure not holding steady enough during the test injection"],["Warning lamp, driving behaviour mostly unchanged","Slightly uneven idle in some cases"],2,1,["P2B15","P2B12","P2B16","P02D0","P02D1","P0269"],"היסט פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 3 — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2B15:["Cylinder 3 Injection Pulse Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B15 reports that the zero-fuel correction learned for injector 3 has reached Ford's limit. For its 3.0 L six-cylinder diesel Ford adds conditions so the test injection takes place in a defined overrun: engine speed between 890 and 2,400 rpm, a gear from fourth to tenth held without shifting, the torque converter locked and the fuel balance wheel learn already finished.",["Learned values unsuitable after fuel system repairs (Ford TSB 23-2076, software and adaption reset)","Injector 3 drifted mechanically (wear, coking, internal leakage)","Outdated PCM calibration"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Possibly knocking or rough running at idle"],2,1,["P2B14","P2B13","P2B17","P0269","P02F0","P02D0","P02D1"],""],P2B16:["Cylinder 4 Injection Pulse Offset Not Learned","P2B16 indicates a missing learned pulse offset for injector 4. Public manufacturer material does not tie it to any engine; Ford's published diesel monitor and its bulletins use only the exceeded-limit partner P2B17. Why the learn matters is set out in a Bosch patent: pilot injections are kept as small as possible, and if tolerances mean the injector does not open at all, combustion becomes noticeably louder.",["Injector 4 or PCM replaced, or adaptions reset, and the learn not yet completed","Learn conditions (warm engine, fuel cut-off) rarely reached","Injector 4 not opening on minimal pulses at all"],["Warning lamp","Louder combustion noise, especially at idle"],2,1,["P2B17","P2B14","P2B18","P02D2","P02D3","P0272"],"היסט פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 4 — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2B17:["Cylinder 4 Injection Pulse Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B17 is set when injector 4's learned pulse offset goes past the allowed band. For the 6.7 L engine in 2020–2022 F-Super Duty trucks Ford saw this after fuel system work: stored learned values no longer matched the new parts.",["Old learn values after fuel system work, cleared by a warm idle relearn (Ford SSM 50646/50816)","Injector 4 worn or leaking internally","Rail pressure deviating from target during the test injection"],["Check engine light shortly after a fuel system repair","Usually unchanged driving behaviour"],2,1,["P2B16","P2B15","P2B19","P0272","P02D2","P02D3","P0087"],""],P2B18:["Cylinder 5 Injection Pulse Offset Not Learned","P2B18 means injector 5 has no learned offset. No manufacturer documents this exact code. On petrol direct injection GM covers a related idea with codes of its own: in the 2025 V8 table the ECM adds up the opening magnitude and closing time compensation of each injector, both derived from the feedback voltage, and P10AB or P10AC set for cylinder 5 when that sum is below the minimum or above the maximum limit (Type B,…",["New injector 5 or control unit without a completed learn","Enabling conditions for the learn not met often enough","Faulty injector 5 wiring preventing a valid measurement"],["Warning lamp","Rarely noticeable; at most slightly uneven low-load running"],2,1,["P2B19","P2B16","P2B1A","P2B04","P02D4","P02D5","P0275"],"היסט פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 5 — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2B19:["Cylinder 5 Injection Pulse Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B19 flags injector 5: its learned zero-fuel offset exceeds the calibrated limit. Ford's diesel OBD summary groups the code with the other odd numbers from P2B11 to P2B1F under the Zero Fuel Calibration monitor, which it files under fuel system feedback control.",["Learned values skewed by driving above about 760 m (Ford SSM 53340)","Injector 5 with changed opening behaviour","PCM software without the later calibration fix"],["Check engine light after mountain or high-plateau driving","Possibly slightly rough idle"],2,1,["P2B18","P2B17","P2B1B","P0275","P02D4","P02D5"],""],P2B1A:["Cylinder 6 Injection Pulse Offset Not Learned","P2B1A reports that the pulse offset for injector 6 has not been learned. Public manufacturer sources do not name this code; on the 3.0 L V6 Power Stroke built by Ford, where cylinder 6 is the last one, Ford's summary lists only the exceeded-limit code P2B1B.",["Learn for injector 6 still pending after a reset or parts replacement","Mostly short trips with a cold engine, so the learn rarely starts","Injector 6 delivering so erratically that no value can be fixed"],["Warning lamp","Perhaps slightly harder combustion noise at idle"],2,1,["P2B1B","P2B18","P2B1C","P02D6","P02D7","P0278"],"היסט פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 6 — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2B1B:["Cylinder 6 Injection Pulse Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B1B concerns injector 6. On Ford's 3.0 L V6 Power Stroke it is the last cylinder the zero-fuel monitor checks, on the 6.7 L V8 the sixth of eight. The code means the energising time at which injector 6 starts to deliver has moved too far from its stored target, beyond the learn limit.",["PCM software learning wrong values at altitude (Ford TSB 25-2262)","Injector 6 drifted by wear or deposits","Adaptions not reset after an earlier repair"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Slightly rough idle, driveability otherwise normal"],2,1,["P2B1A","P2B19","P2B1D","P0278","P02D6","P02D7","P02F3"],""],P2B1C:["Cylinder 7 Injection Pulse Offset Not Learned","P2B1C says no learned offset exists for injector 7, which only applies to engines with at least seven cylinders, in practice V8s. No manufacturer publishes a monitor for this code. A GM patent on small-quantity adaption shows that a learn can also fail to finish because results do not settle: several test injections during fuel cut-off are compared, and an injector whose consecutive values scatter too much gets a…",["Test results for injector 7 scattering too much to be accepted","Learn restarted after injector or control unit replacement","Leak in the high-pressure system disturbing the test injection"],["Warning lamp","With an erratic injector, uneven idle or knocking on one cylinder"],2,1,["P2B1D","P2B1A","P2B1E","P02D8","P02D9","P0281"],"היסט פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 7 — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2B1D:["Cylinder 7 Injection Pulse Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B1D reports that the correction learned for injector 7 during Ford's zero-fuel calibration has gone beyond its limit; cylinder 7 exists only on the 6.7 L V8. Ford's TSB 25-2412 for 2023–2025 F-Super Duty trucks calls the warning lamp in many such cases incorrect: learned values skewed by operation above 762 m, sometimes with a slightly uneven idle.",["Calibration learning wrong values at altitude (Ford TSB 25-2412)","Injector 7 worn, often with balance code P0281 as well","Interference on the crank or cam speed signal"],["Check engine light, sometimes without a real fault","Slightly uneven idle"],2,1,["P2B1C","P2B1B","P2B1F","P0281","P02D8","P02D9","P02F4"],""],P2B1E:["Cylinder 8 Injection Pulse Offset Not Learned","P2B1E means injector 8 has not received a learned pulse offset. As the final cylinder in the group it belongs to V8 engines; Ford's 6.7 L V8 would be the obvious candidate, but Ford publishes only the exceeded-limit code P2B1F for it, so no manufacturer source for P2B1E exists.",["Learn values reset or injector 8 replaced, learn not finished","Few coasting phases with fuel cut-off in everyday use","Fault in the crank speed signal or the injector 8 wiring"],["Warning lamp","Mostly no noticeable change in running"],2,1,["P2B1F","P2B1C","P2B10","P02DA","P02DB","P0284"],"היסט פולס הזרקת צילינדר‏ 8 — לא בוצע לימוד"],P2B1F:["Cylinder 8 Injection Pulse Offset Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B1F is the last code of the series: the offset learned for injector 8 has crossed the learning limit. Ford uses it on the 6.7 L V8 Power Stroke. For 2023–2025 F-Super Duty trucks, special service message 53896 links these codes to driving above 762 m;",["Adaption skewed by high-altitude driving (Ford SSM 53896, reset with FDRS)","Injector 8 worn or coked","Outdated PCM calibration"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","Slightly rough idle in some cases, otherwise normal running"],2,1,["P2B1E","P2B1D","P2B11","P0284","P02DA","P02DB","P02F5"],""],P2B20:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit","Sensor B is a second temperature sensor in the coolant loop that serves the hybrid or EV power electronics, such as inverter, DC/DC converter or on-board charger; where it sits relative to sensor A is up to the vehicle maker. P2B20 is the undifferentiated circuit code: the controller finds the signal unusable without deciding between low and high. No manufacturer documents P2B20 publicly.",["Loose connector, corroded pins or broken wire in the sensor B circuit","Sensor B element open or shorted internally","Faulty input stage or reference supply in the controlling module"],["Hybrid or EV system warning and stored fault code","Reduced drive or charging power as a precaution","Electronics coolant pump running more often or at higher speed"],2,3,["P2B21","P2B22","P2B23","P2B24","P0CEE","P2D2A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2B21:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","Here sensor B delivers a voltage inside its electrical window, yet the temperature it reports does not fit the rest of the vehicle: it may stay flat while the electronics warm up, or disagree with other temperatures after the car has stood for hours. No manufacturer publishes the set condition of P2B21. NTN-SNR names it a deviation or malfunction of the sensor B signal.",["Sensor B element drifted out of its characteristic curve","Air pocket around the sensor after coolant service or a leak","Corroded or loose terminals adding resistance to the signal","Controller calibration that needs an update"],["Hybrid system warning, often only after a cold start","Cooling pump or fan behaviour that does not match conditions","Occasionally limited electric power"],2,1,["P2B20","P2B22","P2B23","P2B25","P0CEF","P2D2A"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2B22:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","P2B22 says the signal voltage of electronics coolant sensor B has fallen below its valid band. Since these sensors are NTC thermistors, a low voltage would mean an absurdly hot coolant, so the usual explanation is a signal wire touching ground, moisture bridging the connector or an internally shorted element. No manufacturer documents P2B22 publicly; NTN-SNR's catalogue calls it a too-small signal of sensor B.",["Sensor B signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Water or coolant in the sensor connector","Internally shorted sensor element"],["Warning lamp or hybrid system message","Electronics coolant pump and fans running at high output","Reduced electric drive or charging power"],2,3,["P2B23","P2B20","P2B21","P2B26","P0CF0"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2B23:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","With P2B23 the signal of electronics coolant sensor B climbs close to the reference voltage. For an NTC sensor that reads as extreme cold, which in practice nearly always points to an interruption: an unplugged or water-damaged connector, a broken signal or ground lead, an open element, or more rarely a short to a voltage source. No manufacturer documents P2B23 publicly;",["Open signal or ground wire, or connector not fully seated","Water intrusion and corroded pins in a connector of the sensor circuit","Sensor B element open","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source"],["Hybrid or EV system warning with MIL","Coolant temperature for sensor B shown at about −40 °C in live data","Power reduced as a precaution"],2,3,["P2B22","P2B20","P2B21","P2B27","P0CF1"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2B24:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit","Some electrified drivetrains measure the power electronics coolant at three points, for example ahead of the inverter, behind it and at the charger or DC/DC converter. P2B24 covers the third of these sensors, C, and reports a circuit fault the controller does not classify further. Which component sensor C watches is not standardised and varies by make. No manufacturer documents P2B24 publicly.",["Connector or wiring fault in the sensor C circuit","Failed sensor C element","Input stage of the evaluating module faulty"],["Stored fault code, possibly with a hybrid system message","Lower charging or drive power in hot conditions"],2,3,["P2B25","P2B26","P2B27","P2B20","P0CEE"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2B25:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P2B25 is the plausibility code for the third electronics coolant sensor. The signal is electrically sound, but its value cannot be right, for example because sensor C still reads cold while sensors A and B in the same loop have long warmed up, or because it jumps by an amount the coolant could not follow. No manufacturer publishes a set condition for P2B25.",["Sensor C reading drifted away from the true temperature","Air in the loop or a weak pump leaving sensor C without flow","Corrosion in the sensor C connector"],["Fault code set after a cold start or a long drive","Cooling system reacting inconsistently","Possible limitation of charging power"],2,1,["P2B24","P2B26","P2B27","P2B21","P0CEF"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2B26:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit Low","The voltage on the signal line of sensor C, the third coolant sensor in the power electronics loop, is lower than the controller accepts. Low means voltage here, not temperature: on an NTC sensor it corresponds to an implausibly hot value. A pinched or chafed lead touching the body, a short inside the sensor or coolant that has crept into the plug are the usual findings. No manufacturer documents P2B26 publicly;",["Sensor C signal lead pinched or chafed against ground","Coolant wicking into the sensor plug","Shorted sensor C element"],["Warning lamp or system message","Pump and radiator fan running hard even when cool","Reduced power in some situations"],2,3,["P2B27","P2B24","P2B25","P2B22","P0CF0"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2B27:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit High","P2B27 is logged when sensor C in the power electronics coolant loop sends a signal near the top of the reference, which the controller would have to read as deep frost. Far more often than real cold, the reason is a circuit that has opened: a connector that has backed out, a terminal pushed out of its cavity, a broken wire near a moving part or a failed element; shorting to the battery feed is rarer.",["Connector backed out, terminal pushed out or wire broken","Sensor C element open","Signal line shorted to battery voltage"],["Warning lamp and hybrid system message","Sensor C shown far below outside temperature in live data","Limited electric power"],2,3,["P2B26","P2B24","P2B25","P2B23","P0CF1"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת היברידי/חשמלי‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2B28:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Pump A Performance","P2B28 means battery coolant pump A is electrically reachable but does not perform as the battery controller expects. VW and Audi store P2B2800 in battery management J840: VW bulletin 93-21-02 (2021 ID.4) traces it to air left when pump V590 did not run during the fill-and-bleed routine, and Audi's 2068363 series (Q4 e-tron 2022–2024, message Electric drive fault) names dry running from residual air, prescribes two…",["Residual air in the battery coolant loop, often after service","Battery or hybrid controller software needing an update","Worn or failing battery coolant pump","Low coolant level from a leak"],["Electric drive fault message or MIL","Reduced drive or charging power","Short or missing engine auto-stops on mild hybrids"],2,3,["P2B29","P0CFF","P0C4A","P0C47","P0E3B"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B29:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Coolant Pump A Overspeed - Dry Run","A centrifugal pump that suddenly spins faster while drawing less current has lost its liquid: it is churning air. P2B29 reports exactly this for battery coolant pump A. Porsche describes the detection for the 2018 Panamera 4 E-Hybrid, where the pump watches its speed and current draw against the commanded speed and reports a dry run to the battery controller, but files it as P0C4A00 and notes it may take hundreds of…",["Air in the battery coolant loop after service or incomplete bleeding","Leak in a battery cooling line lowering the level","Battery controller software misjudging pump feedback (Ford 2020 hybrids)"],["MIL or hybrid system warning","Pump audibly gurgling or whining","Battery power or charging limited"],2,3,["P2B28","P0CFF","P0C4A","P0E3B","P2B2A"],""],P2B2A:["Hybrid/EV Electronics Coolant Pump A Overspeed - Dry Run","The pump in the low-temperature loop that cools power electronics and often the drive unit reports that it is turning too fast for its load, the sign of air instead of coolant. Mercedes documents P2B2A7A in the powertrain control unit of the 167 series (GLE/GLS) with M177 V8 and 48 V system before model year 2024: the 15 W pump beside the transmission switches to an emergency dry-run mode when the circuit holds air,…",["Air in the low-temperature circuit after filling or a leak","Damaged or leaking coolant hose (Audi e-tron)","Pumps of the wrong part number or position (Mercedes 167)"],["Coolant or drive system warning in the instrument cluster","Churning noise from the affected pump","Reduced drive power until the loop is bled"],2,2,["P2E46","P0CEA","P0CE9","P2C67","P2B29"],""],P2B2B:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 5 Circuit","Engines with split cooling, electric pumps or separate head, block, radiator and heater branches can carry five or more coolant sensors; the numbering is the maker's choice. P2B2B is the generic circuit code for number 5, meant for controllers that do not separate low from high. No manufacturer documents a set condition for P2B2B publicly.",["Loose connector or broken lead at sensor 5","Failed NTC element in sensor 5","Faulty sensor input in the engine control module"],["MIL with stored code","Cooling fans or thermal management running on default values"],1,1,["P2B2C","P2B2D","P2B2E","P2BB5","P2AFC","P2182"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 5 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2B2C:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 5 Circuit Range/Performance","P2B2C concerns a fifth coolant sensor whose signal is electrically valid but does not behave like coolant temperature: after a long cold soak it differs clearly from the other engine temperatures, it barely rises during warm-up although the engine heats normally, or it sits stuck at one value. CARB requires such rationality checks for coolant inputs that emission controls rely on.",["Sensor 5 element drifting or sluggish","No coolant flow in the sensor's branch (stuck valve, failed pump, air)","Corroded sensor connector","Engine software needing an update"],["MIL, often after a cold start","Heater or fan behaviour that does not match engine temperature"],1,1,["P2B2B","P2B2D","P2B2E","P2BB5","P2AFD","P2183"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 5 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2B2D:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 5 Circuit Low","A low signal from coolant sensor 5 means its NTC resistance has collapsed, which the engine computer would read as an impossibly hot engine; a grounded signal wire or a shorted element is the usual reason.",["Signal wire grounded, for example by a chafed harness","Shorted sensor 5 element","Engine control module input fault"],["MIL after two trips","Radiator fans running constantly at high speed","Other harness-related codes stored at the same time"],1,1,["P2B2E","P2B2B","P2B2C","P2BB5","P2AFE","P2184"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 5 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2B2E:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 5 Circuit High","P2B2E is stored when the fifth coolant sensor shows a resistance so high that only an open circuit, an unplugged connector or a line shorted to voltage can explain it; the NTC curve would put the coolant below −60 °C. GM sets it once the channel exceeds about 298 kΩ in the 2019 L3B tables or about 174 kΩ in the 2025 ECM tables, for 5 s within 6 s, after an engine run time above 10 s or with intake air above −20 °C;",["Open signal or ground wire, or unplugged connector","Chafed engine harness interrupting the circuit","Open sensor 5 element"],["MIL after two trips","Sensor 5 reads around −40 °C or lower in live data","Engine runs on a substitute temperature value"],1,1,["P2B2D","P2B2B","P2B2C","P2BB5","P2AFF","P2185"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 5 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2B2F:["Fan 1 Performance/Stuck Off","Unlike the circuit codes P0480, P0691 and P0692, P2B2F judges the result: radiator fan 1 is commanded on but does not deliver, up to not turning at all. Detection uses fan speed feedback from a PWM or LIN fan module, or the missing temperature drop when the fan should be cooling.",["Fan 1 motor worn or seized, or blades blocked by debris","Fan control module or relay not switching the motor","Engine software judging the fan wrongly (FCA 2.0 L)","Poor power feed or ground at the fan"],["MIL","Rising coolant temperature in slow traffic","Weak air conditioning at standstill"],2,3,["P2B30","P2B31","P0480","P0691","P0692","P0483","P0494"],"מאוורר‏ 1 — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2B30:["Fan 1 Stuck On","P2B30 states that radiator fan 1 does not follow the command to stop or to change speed, as judged from its speed feedback or module diagnosis. The classic electrical background is a welded relay contact or a fan module that keeps driving the motor.",["Road debris jamming the fan (Audi e-tron GT)","Fan relay contacts welded closed","Fan control module ignoring the off command"],["Fan keeps running after switch-off, draining the 12 V battery","Weak cabin heating or cooling on electric vehicles","Grinding noise from the front wheel area"],2,3,["P2B2F","P2B32","P0480","P0692","P0495"],"מאוורר‏ 1 — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2B31:["Fan 2 Performance/Stuck Off","P2B31 is the functional code for a second radiator fan: its circuits test fine (otherwise P0481, P0693 or P0694 would be set), yet the fan turns too slowly or not at all when commanded. Twin-fan cooling packs usually run fan 2 for high load or A/C demand, so a failure tends to show up only in heat or traffic. No manufacturer documents P2B31 publicly.",["Fan 2 motor worn, seized or jammed by debris","Fan module or relay for fan 2 not switching on","Weak supply or ground to fan 2"],["MIL or cooling warning","Temperature climbing at high load or with A/C on"],2,3,["P2B32","P2B2F","P0481","P0693","P0694","P2CB9"],"מאוורר‏ 2 — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי"],P2B32:["Fan 2 Stuck On","With P2B32 the controller finds that the second radiator fan keeps operating, or does not change state, against its command. On conventional cars this usually traces back to a relay stuck closed, a fan 2 control line shorted to its active level or a module that has lost control of the motor.",["Debris from the wheel housing jamming fan 2 (Audi e-tron GT)","Fan 2 relay stuck closed","Fan 2 control line shorted to its active level"],["Fan audible after the vehicle is switched off","Reduced heating, cooling or charging on electric vehicles","Flat 12 V battery after parking"],2,3,["P2B31","P2B30","P0481","P0694","P2CBA"],"מאוורר‏ 2 — תקוע במצב פעיל"],P2B33:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit/Open Bank 1","P2B33 concerns the second profile actuator on the intake camshaft (camshaft A) of bank 1. Such actuators are solenoids that extend a pin into a groove on a sliding cam sleeve and so move lobes of a different lift under the valves. GM uses the code on the 2.7-litre turbo four L3B (Silverado and Sierra 1500 from 2019), whose sliding cam system has four intake and two exhaust actuators; GM calls this one actuator 2.",["Connector at the actuator on the camshaft carrier loose, corroded or not latched after valve cover work","Solenoid winding of actuator B open","Control wire broken in the engine harness","Output stage in the engine control module faulty"],["MIL on after the first drive with the fault","No change of intake lift profile, less pull or higher fuel use depending on the stuck profile","Cylinder deactivation no longer engages"],2,3,["P2B34","P2B35","P2B36","P2B39","P001A","P2B4F"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2B34:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit Low Bank 1","On bank 1 the intake camshaft (A) carries a second shifting solenoid, actuator B, which GM's L3B 2.7-litre four labels actuator 2. P2B34 reports a short to ground on its control line: while the driver is switched on, the ECM measures 0.5 Ω or less from signal to ground and stores the fault after 4 failed out of 5 samples at more than 11 V, lighting the MIL at once (Type A).",["Engine harness chafed through on the camshaft carrier or near the left shock tower (GM PIT5677)","Shorted turns or short to housing in actuator B","Oil or moisture in the actuator connector creating a path to ground"],["MIL on, often together with other codes from the same harness section","Lift switching and cylinder deactivation unavailable","With a chafed harness also rough running, reduced power or blown fuses"],2,3,["P2B33","P2B35","P2B37","P2B3A","P001B","P2B53"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2B35:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit High Bank 1","P2B35 is the short-to-voltage counterpart for intake-side actuator B on bank 1, the second of the sleeve-shifting solenoids on camshaft A. In GM's L3B tables (2019 and again 2025) this test runs while the output is off: if the control line shows 0.5 Ω or less towards the controller supply, a short to power is assumed, and 4 hits in 5 samples set a Type A code with the warning lamp on in the same drive.",["Control wire chafed against a powered circuit in the engine harness","Internal short in actuator B","Output stage in the engine control module faulty"],["MIL on during the drive in which the fault appears","Intake lift profile no longer changes as commanded","Higher fuel use because cylinder deactivation is blocked"],2,3,["P2B33","P2B34","P2B38","P2B3B","P001C"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2B36:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit/Open Bank 2","P2B36 describes an open control circuit at the second profile actuator of the intake camshaft (camshaft A) on bank 2. A second bank exists only on V or boxer engines. No manufacturer documents this code publicly: the one known user of the series, GM's L3B, is an inline four and only sets the bank 1 code P2B33, where it treats 200 kΩ or more with the driver on as open.",["Actuator connector on bank 2 unplugged, loose or corroded","Open coil in actuator B","Broken control wire between engine module and bank 2"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 intake stays on one lift profile, possibly uneven running between the banks"],2,3,["P2B37","P2B38","P2B33","P2B3C","P001D","P2B50"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2B37:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit Low Bank 2","Code P2B37 stands for a control line shorted to ground at intake-side actuator B of bank 2, the second lobe-switching solenoid on camshaft A of the other cylinder bank. Publicly, no maker assigns it to a vehicle. The bank 1 analogue P2B34 is defined by GM for the L3B four-cylinder, which flags a ground short at 0.5 Ω or less while the output is on; a V engine would need a mirror-image test for its second bank.",["Harness to the bank 2 actuator chafed through on the cylinder head or a bracket","Oil or water in the actuator connector","Shorted winding in actuator B"],["Check engine light on","Lift switching inactive on bank 2, less power or more fuel use"],2,3,["P2B36","P2B38","P2B34","P2B3D","P001E"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2B38:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit High Bank 2","P2B38 marks a short to battery voltage in the control circuit of intake camshaft actuator B on bank 2. No published manufacturer documentation uses it; only the bank 1 version P2B35 is covered, by GM's L3B summary tables, which check with the output off and react to 0.5 Ω or less towards supply.",["Pinched or chafed control wire touching a powered circuit","Internal short in actuator B","Faulty output stage in the engine module"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 intake lift no longer changes, uneven power delivery"],2,3,["P2B36","P2B37","P2B35","P2B3E","P001F"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2B39:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit/Open Bank 1","Camshaft B is the exhaust camshaft, and actuator B is the second shifting solenoid on it. On GM's 2.7-litre L3B the exhaust side has only two such actuators, so this is the last of them; GM's tables call it exhaust camshaft profile actuator 2. P2B39 flags an open control circuit: with the output commanded on, the ECM reads an impedance of at least 200 kΩ to ground.",["Exhaust actuator connector loose or corroded on the camshaft carrier","Broken wire in the engine harness","Open solenoid coil in exhaust actuator B"],["MIL on in the first drive","Exhaust lift profile no longer switches, cylinder deactivation unavailable"],2,3,["P2B3A","P2B3B","P2B3C","P2B33","P002A","P2B51"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2B3A:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit Low Bank 1","P2B3A points to a short to ground in the control line of exhaust-side actuator B on bank 1, i.e. the second pin solenoid that slides the lobe sleeve along camshaft B. GM documents it for the L3B four-cylinder in its 2019 and 2025 OBD tables: driver on, a resistance to ground not above 0.5 Ω, 4 of 5 samples, supply over 11 V, Type A with immediate MIL.",["Engine harness rubbed through where it crosses the camshaft carrier","Shorted turns in exhaust actuator B","Oil wicking into the actuator connector"],["Check engine light on immediately","Exhaust profile and cylinder deactivation no longer switch","With harness damage often further codes and rough running"],2,3,["P2B39","P2B3B","P2B3D","P2B34","P002B"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2B3B:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit High Bank 1","For the second exhaust-camshaft profile actuator on bank 1 (camshaft B, actuator B), P2B3B means its control circuit is shorted to a voltage source. GM's L3B strategy checks this with the driver switched off: a resistance of no more than 0.5 Ω between the line and controller power counts as a fault, and four out of five such readings at a supply above 11 V store a Type A code, MIL on at once.",["Control wire chafed against a live wire in the engine harness","Internal short in exhaust actuator B","Engine module output stage faulty"],["Check engine light comes on during the drive","Exhaust lift stays in one profile, cylinder deactivation blocked"],2,3,["P2B39","P2B3A","P2B3E","P2B35","P002C"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2B3C:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit/Open Bank 2","This code reports an interrupted control circuit at actuator B on the exhaust camshaft (camshaft B) of bank 2. No vehicle manufacturer is known to use P2B3C in public documents. Its bank 1 twin P2B39 appears in GM's tables for the 2.7-litre L3B, an inline engine without a second bank, where an impedance of 200 kΩ or more with the output on counts as open.",["Connector of the bank 2 exhaust actuator unplugged or loose","Broken lead to the actuator","Open coil in exhaust actuator B"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust lift on bank 2 no longer switches"],2,3,["P2B3D","P2B3E","P2B39","P2B36","P002D","P2B52"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 2)"],P2B3D:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit Low Bank 2","P2B3D: the control wire of the second exhaust-side profile actuator on bank 2 (camshaft B, actuator B) has contact with ground. Publicly documented use by a manufacturer is not known. For comparison, GM's L3B diagnostics define the bank 1 code P2B3A as a ground short of at most 0.5 Ω with the driver on and four failed tests out of five.",["Wire chafed at a bracket or valve cover edge on bank 2","Shorted coil in exhaust actuator B","Oil or water in the connector"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 exhaust stays on one lift profile"],2,3,["P2B3C","P2B3E","P2B3A","P2B37","P002E"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2B3E:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Circuit High Bank 2","P2B3E is set when the control circuit of exhaust camshaft profile actuator B on bank 2 is shorted to supply voltage. No manufacturer documents the code publicly, so the details come from the analogue: GM's L3B tests the bank 1 counterpart P2B3B while the output is off and treats 0.5 Ω or less towards controller power as a short.",["Damaged insulation bringing the control wire against a powered line","Solenoid in exhaust actuator B shorted internally","Output stage in the engine module faulty"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust lift on bank 2 fixed, slightly higher consumption"],2,3,["P2B3C","P2B3D","P2B3B","P2B38","P002F"],"מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 2)"],P2B3F:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Bank 1","P2B3F is the general circuit code for position sensor B of the intake camshaft actuator (camshaft A) on bank 1, the side with cylinder 1; the NTN-SNR sensor guide also places it on the inlet side. Mercedes-Benz uses this code family on its M176/M177 V8 engines, where each CAMTRONIC lift actuator reports its own sensor signal and sensor B belongs to solenoid 2. No manufacturer documents P2B3F itself publicly.",["Connector at the actuator loose, corroded or wire broken","Position sensor in the actuator failed (actuator replacement)","Engine harness damaged by heat or chafing","Engine control module fault"],["Check engine light on","Lift switching or cylinder deactivation unavailable","Slightly higher consumption, sometimes less power"],2,3,["P2B40","P2B41","P2B42","P2B43","P2B47","P34AC","P03E5"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2B40:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Range/Performance Bank 1","With P2B40 the wiring of the intake-side sensor B (camshaft A, bank 1) is electrically fine, but its signal does not fit what the engine module commanded. Engines with switchable cam lift use such feedback to confirm that a pin really moved;",["Actuator pin sluggish or sticking (wear, oil sludge)","Engine control software outdated (Mercedes CAMTRONIC update)","Sensor signal disturbed by loose contact","Cam sleeve or shift groove damaged"],["Check engine light on","Valve-lift change held in a safe position","Uneven running when the system tries to switch"],3,3,["P2B3F","P2B41","P2B42","P2B44","P2B48","P34AD","P03E6"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2B41:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Low Bank 1","P2B41 reports a voltage below the permitted window from sensor B, which watches the intake actuator of bank 1. That usually points to a grounded signal line or a sensor that has failed internally. Mercedes describes the matching low fault on the exhaust side (P34BE, sensor of CAMTRONIC solenoid 1) literally as a short to ground, which shows how the family is meant; a public text on P2B41 itself is not known.",["Signal wire shorted to ground (chafed harness)","Sensor shorted internally","Sensor supply interrupted"],["Check engine light on","Cam lift switching disabled","Possibly further codes from sensors on the same supply"],2,3,["P2B3F","P2B40","P2B42","P2B45","P2B49","P34AE","P03E7"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2B42:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit High Bank 1","Here sensor B of the bank 1 intake actuator reports a value stuck above its upper limit. Typical reasons are an open sensor ground, a signal line touching 5 V or battery voltage, or a defective sensor. No manufacturer explains P2B42 publicly; the supplier list from NTN-SNR only names it as the inlet-side sensor B with a signal that is too high.",["Sensor ground open or connector corroded","Signal wire shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Sensor (actuator) faulty"],["Check engine light on","Intake lift change locked out","Usually no noticeable change in driving, sometimes reduced power"],2,3,["P2B3F","P2B40","P2B41","P2B46","P2B4A","P34AF","P03E8"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2B43:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Bank 2","P2B43 covers the wiring of sensor B at the bank 2 intake actuator, i.e. on the cylinder bank without cylinder 1, so it only appears on V or boxer engines. The engine module sees an open line or a signal it cannot accept at all. On Mercedes V8s with CAMTRONIC (M176/M177) the intake actuator of bank 2 is exactly where bulletin LI05.20-P-080192 places the sister fault P2B44;",["Harness near the bulkhead damaged by heat","Actuator connector loose or corroded","Sensor in the actuator failed"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder deactivation or lift change switched off","Possibly limp-home message of the valve-lift system"],2,3,["P2B3F","P2B44","P2B45","P2B46","P2B4B","P34B0"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P2B44:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Range/Performance Bank 2","P2B44 is the one code of this group with a public manufacturer use. Mercedes-Benz bulletin LI05.20-P-080192 (January 2026) lists P2B4400 on M176/M177 V8 engines – AMG 63 models, S 580, G 550, GLS 580 – and reads it as an implausible sensor signal from CAMTRONIC solenoid 2 on the intake side of bank 2.",["Engine control software needs the CAMTRONIC update (Mercedes)","Actuator of an older part number (Mercedes replaces it)","Harness heat-damaged near the windshield"],["Check engine light on","CAMTRONIC limp-home mode, cylinder deactivation off","Higher fuel consumption at part load"],4,3,["P2B40","P2B43","P2B45","P2B46","P2B4C","P34B1","P34C1","P2B50"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P2B45:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Low Bank 2","P2B45 means the bank 2 intake actuator's position sensor B delivers an unusually low voltage – on bank 2, which a V engine places opposite cylinder 1. A grounded signal wire is the classic cause; an internally shorted sensor or a missing supply gives the same picture.",["Signal wire grounded through chafing or heat damage","Sensor in the actuator shorted","Supply to the sensor missing"],["Check engine light on","Lift change on bank 2 stops working","Possibly limp-home message"],2,3,["P2B41","P2B43","P2B44","P2B46","P2B4D","P34B2","P34C2"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2B46:["A Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit High Bank 2","P2B46 flags a signal from position sensor B on the bank 2 intake camshaft actuator that is stuck too high. Most often the sensor has lost its ground, the signal line has contact with a supply line, or the sensor element itself has failed. There is no public manufacturer description of P2B46; NTN-SNR lists it simply as inlet sensor B, second bank, signal too high.",["Sensor ground interrupted","Signal line in contact with a supply line","Sensor element in the actuator failed"],["Check engine light on","Cam lift held in default position on bank 2","Slightly increased fuel consumption"],2,3,["P2B42","P2B43","P2B44","P2B45","P2B4E","P34B3"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2B47:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Bank 1","P2B47 moves the circuit fault to the exhaust side: it concerns position sensor B on the actuator of camshaft B, bank 1. NTN-SNR's supplier code list reads camshaft B as the outlet camshaft. Mercedes-Benz, in its CAMTRONIC bulletin for the M176/M177 V8, documents exhaust-side feedback faults only for sensor A of solenoid 1 (P34BD, P34BE);",["Connector unplugged or corroded, wire broken","Exhaust actuator sensor failed","Engine control module fault"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust cam lift change unavailable","Little change in driving behaviour"],2,3,["P2B3F","P2B48","P2B49","P2B4A","P2B4B","P34BC","P03F6"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2B48:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Range/Performance Bank 1","P2B48 is the plausibility code for sensor B at the bank 1 exhaust actuator (camshaft B): the circuit works, yet the reported position contradicts the command. Mercedes handles this fault type on its CAMTRONIC V8s for the exhaust sensor of solenoid 1 as P34BD and fixes it through software and newer actuators; P2B48 itself is not found in any public manufacturer source.",["Actuator pin sticking from deposits or wear","Outdated engine control software","Shift groove or cam sleeve damaged"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust lift switching held in one position","Possibly rough running during shift attempts"],3,3,["P2B40","P2B47","P2B49","P2B4A","P2B4C","P34BD","P03F7"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 1)"],P2B49:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Low Bank 1","With P2B49 the module reads too low a signal from position sensor B at the exhaust camshaft actuator of bank 1. A short between signal line and ground, a sensor with an internal short or a missing feed are the usual suspects. The nearest public manufacturer reference is P34BE on the Mercedes M176/M177: the sensor of exhaust solenoid 1 for CAMTRONIC, bank 1, described as shorted to ground.",["Signal line shorted to ground","Sensor shorted internally","Sensor feed missing"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust cam lift change switched off","Occasionally further sensor codes"],2,3,["P2B41","P2B47","P2B48","P2B4A","P2B4D","P34BE","P03F8"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2B4A:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit High Bank 1","P2B4A says the position sensor B signal of the bank 1 exhaust camshaft actuator is above its limit. An interrupted sensor ground, a short to a voltage source or a failed sensor are typical. No manufacturer describes P2B4A publicly, and the Mercedes CAMTRONIC bulletin does not include any high fault of this family.",["Sensor ground interrupted or connector corroded","Signal line shorted to a voltage source","Sensor failed"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust lift system kept in safe position","Usually unchanged driveability"],2,3,["P2B42","P2B47","P2B48","P2B49","P2B4E","P34BF","P03F9"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2B4B:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Bank 2","P2B4B is set when the circuit feeding the second position sensor (B) of the exhaust actuator on bank 2 is open or otherwise unusable. Bank 2 exists only on engines with two cylinder rows, such as the Mercedes M176/M177 V8, whose CAMTRONIC bulletin lists exhaust feedback faults on bank 2 for sensor A (P34C1, P34C2) but not for sensor B.",["Plug or wires at the actuator open","Heat damage to the harness above the bulkhead","Sensor in the exhaust actuator failed"],["Check engine light on","Cylinder deactivation or exhaust lift change unavailable","Somewhat higher consumption"],2,3,["P2B43","P2B47","P2B4C","P2B4D","P2B4E","P34C0"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 2)"],P2B4C:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Range/Performance Bank 2","P2B4C stands for an implausible but electrically valid signal from the B sensor watching the exhaust actuator of bank 2. It is the exhaust-side mirror of P2B44, which Mercedes-Benz documents on CAMTRONIC V8s (M176/M177) for intake solenoid 2 of bank 2; for P2B4C itself there is no public manufacturer text.",["Exhaust actuator pin sticking (deposits, wear)","Engine control software outdated","Intermittent contact in the sensor signal"],["Check engine light on","Lift system or cylinder deactivation in limp-home","Higher part-load consumption"],3,3,["P2B44","P2B48","P2B4B","P2B4D","P2B4E","P34C1"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים (בנק 2)"],P2B4D:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit Low Bank 2","A too-low signal from position sensor B at the bank 2 exhaust camshaft actuator sets P2B4D. In practice this is a signal wire touching ground, a shorted sensor, or a sensor that gets no supply. The closest documented case is P34C2 on Mercedes M176/M177 V8s, where solenoid 1 on the bank 2 exhaust side reports a sensor short to ground; P2B4D is not described by any manufacturer in public.",["Signal wire touching ground (heat or chafe damage)","Sensor in the actuator shorted","No supply to the sensor"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust lift change on bank 2 out of action","Possibly limp-home message of the lift system"],2,3,["P2B45","P2B49","P2B4B","P2B4C","P2B4E","P34C2"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2B4E:["B Camshaft Position Actuator Position Sensor B Circuit High Bank 2","P2B4E closes the group: the exhaust-side position sensor B of bank 2 sends a signal above its upper limit. Usually the sensor ground is open, the signal line is shorted to a supply, or the sensor is faulty. No manufacturer explains P2B4E publicly; the NTN-SNR code list only gives outlet sensor B, second bank, signal too high.",["Sensor ground open","Signal line shorted to a supply","Sensor faulty (actuator replacement)"],["Check engine light on","Bank 2 runs on the default cam profile","Slightly higher fuel use"],2,3,["P2B46","P2B4A","P2B4B","P2B4C","P2B4D","P34C3"],"חיישן מצב מפעיל מצב גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל (בנק 2)"],P2B4F:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Performance/Stuck Off Bank 1","P2B4F covers the second profile actuator (B) on the intake camshaft of bank 1, a solenoid whose pin engages a groove on a sliding cam sleeve to change valve lift. Despite the title wording, GM's L3B 2.7-litre four (19OBDG03D, again in 25OBDG03B) uses it for the reverse case: a Hall element reports three pin states (extending 55, extended 45, retracted 68), and if the signal falls below 55 although no shift was…",["Actuator B pin extends without a command (sticking solenoid, weak return spring)","Hall feedback of the actuator delivers wrong pin states","Shift groove on the cam sleeve worn so the pin is dragged out"],["MIL on in the first drive with the fault","Intake lift switching locked out, less pull or higher consumption","Cylinder deactivation no longer available"],2,3,["P2B53","P2B50","P2B51","P2B33","P003C"],"בקרת מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 1)"],P2B50:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Performance/Stuck Off Bank 2","Bank 2 of a V-engine has its own intake camshaft (A), and P2B50 reports that the second profile actuator on it does not do its job or stays in the off position. Mercedes-Benz documents the code for the M176 and M177 V8 with CAMTRONIC (for example AMG C63, GLC63 and S 580 models): in topic LI05.20-P-080192 of January 2026, solenoid 2 for the intake side of bank 2 is described as faulty or jammed off, with fault type…",["CAMTRONIC actuator of an older part number, superseded by Mercedes","Engine control software that needs the available update","Harness heat-damaged above the bulkhead near the windscreen","Actuator pin mechanically jammed in the retracted position"],["Check engine light on","CAMTRONIC lift switching inactive on bank 2, possibly limp-home mode of the system","Slightly uneven running or higher fuel use at part load"],2,3,["P2B4F","P2B54","P2B52","P2B36","P003E"],"בקרת מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 2)"],P2B51:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Performance/Stuck Off Bank 1","On the exhaust camshaft (B) of bank 1 the second sliding-cam solenoid is monitored by P2B51. GM applies it to the L3B 2.7-litre turbo four, whose exhaust side carries two such actuators. Its table entry mirrors the intake check: the ECM tracks the Hall feedback of the pin and treats a drop below the extending level of 55 without any shift request as an unintended firing.",["Exhaust actuator B pin releases without command, often heat-related sticking","Faulty Hall feedback in the actuator or its signal line","Sludge or debris at the actuator bore hindering the pin"],["MIL on immediately (Type A)","Exhaust lift profile no longer changes, turbo response may feel different","Cylinder deactivation disabled"],2,3,["P2B55","P2B4F","P2B52","P2B39","P005A"],"בקרת מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 1)"],P2B52:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Performance/Stuck Off Bank 2","P2B52 is the bank 2 version for actuator B on the exhaust camshaft (B): the second shifting solenoid either does not move its cam sleeve or remains in the off position. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly. NTN-SNR lists it in its camshaft sensor guide as actuator never active, and CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 (e)(13) requires valve control systems to be checked for failure to reach the commanded state.",["Actuator B of the bank 2 exhaust camshaft does not extend its pin","Poor contact at the actuator connector or heat-damaged harness","Engine control calibration that judges the shift too strictly"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust lift switching inactive on bank 2","Possibly slightly lower power in the upper speed range"],2,3,["P2B56","P2B51","P2B50","P2B3C","P005C"],"בקרת מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים או תקוע במצב כבוי (בנק 2)"],P2B53:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Stuck On Bank 1","P2B53 means actuator B of the bank 1 intake camshaft is caught in the engaged position. GM documents it for the L3B 2.7-litre four as pin stuck: after a shift the Hall feedback must climb back above the retracted level of 68; if extending (55) or extended (45) was seen but the pin never reports home before the engine cycle ends, the ECM logs a stuck-out pin.",["Actuator pin does not retract (sticking plunger, varnish, weak spring)","Engine harness chafed on the camshaft carrier (GM PIT5677 / 21-NA-149)","Hall feedback does not report the home position although the pin is back"],["MIL on in the first drive","Lift switching and cylinder deactivation locked out","With a damaged harness also other codes, rough running or blown fuses","Possible ticking from the valve cover if the pin rubs in the groove"],2,3,["P2B4F","P2B54","P2B55","P2B34","P003D"],"בקרת מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 1)"],P2B54:["A Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Stuck On Bank 2","With P2B54 actuator B, the second shifter on the bank 2 intake camshaft, is reported as stuck on, meaning its pin or valve stays engaged after the command to release. A public manufacturer description of this exact code was not found. GM's L3B tables show how the bank 1 twin, P2B53, is judged: the Hall feedback must return to the retracted level within the engine cycle, otherwise a stuck pin is assumed.",["Actuator B on the bank 2 intake camshaft stays engaged (sticking plunger)","Control line shorted so the solenoid remains energised","Position feedback of the actuator stuck at the engaged value"],["Check engine light on","Uneven running between the banks, especially at part load","Profile switching disabled by the engine control"],2,3,["P2B53","P2B50","P2B56","P2B37","P003F"],"בקרת מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ A‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 2)"],P2B55:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Stuck On Bank 1","P2B55 flags actuator B on the bank 1 exhaust camshaft as stuck on. Even GM, whose L3B four has a second exhaust actuator and uses P2B51 for it, lists no stuck-on code for that actuator in its 2019 and 2025 tables; no other maker documents P2B55 publicly either. The fault logic can be inferred from the intake twin P2B53: a pin that does not report back to its rest position after shifting.",["Pin of exhaust actuator B does not retract, often from heat and deposits","Solenoid stays powered because of a wiring or driver fault","Damaged shift groove holds the pin"],["Check engine light on","Changed turbo response or reduced power","Possible metallic noise from the camshaft area"],2,3,["P2B51","P2B53","P2B56","P2B3A","P005B"],"בקרת מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 1)"],P2B56:["B Camshaft Profile Actuator B Control Stuck On Bank 2","P2B56 completes the series: on bank 2 the second actuator of the exhaust camshaft remains engaged after it should have released. No manufacturer publishes a description of this exact code. NTN-SNR lists it as permanently active; CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 (e)(13) is the legal basis for monitoring such valve control functions.",["Solenoid of exhaust actuator B on bank 2 sticking in the engaged state","Aged or wrong engine oil slowing the pin","Worn shift groove on the exhaust cam sleeve"],["Check engine light on","Bank-to-bank imbalance felt as rough idle or part-load vibration","Lift switching locked by the engine control"],2,3,["P2B52","P2B55","P2B54","P2B3D","P005D"],"בקרת מפעיל פרופיל גל זיזים‏ B‏ B — תקוע במצב פעיל (בנק 2)"],P2B57:["Low Engine Oil Pressure - Camshaft Control Disabled","P2B57 is a status code rather than a circuit fault: the engine control has measured or calculated oil pressure too low for safe camshaft adjustment and has therefore switched the cam control off. Hydraulic cam phasers and oil-operated lift switching need a minimum pressure to hold position; below it the parts would rattle or drift. No manufacturer documents the code publicly;",["Oil level too low or oil of the wrong viscosity","Worn oil pump, faulty pump control or clogged pickup screen","Oil pressure sensor reading too low although pressure is fine","Worn bearings causing internal oil leakage at high temperature"],["Check engine light on, often together with an oil pressure warning","Camshaft adjustment inactive, weaker low-end torque and rough idle","Rattle from the cam phasers at start or when hot"],2,3,["P0520","P0521","P0524","P06DD","P0011"],""],P2B58:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Motor Current High","P2B58 reports that the electric motor driving the engine coolant flow control valve draws too much current. GM documents the check for its 3.0-litre inline-six Duramax diesel: in the 2025 table 25OBDG04B the driver stage flags a current above 5.5 A, and 80 failures in 100 samples taken every 12.5 ms set a Type B fault, so the MIL follows on the second trip.",["Rotary valve stiff or seized from deposits or debris in the housing","Valve motor with shorted turns","Chafed engine harness on GM LM2 (bulletin 21-NA-149)"],["MIL on after the second drive with the fault","Slow warm-up or weak cabin heat","Fans may run more often as a precaution"],3,1,["P2B59","P2B5A","P2B5B","P2B60"],"זרם מנוע שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — ערך גבוה"],P2B59:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Control Circuit/Open","P2B59 is the open-circuit check for the drive of the coolant flow control valve. In GM's 25OBDG04B (3.0 L Duramax) the driver reports a load resistance above 200 kΩ, meaning one of the motor wires is disconnected; 80 of 100 samples set a Type B fault.",["ECU judgement logic on Hyundai/Kia 2.5 Theta III (software update 26-EM-009H / ENG 264)","Valve connector unplugged, loose or with a pushed-out terminal","Motor wire broken in the harness or valve motor winding open"],["MIL on, often without any noticeable driveability change","Valve stays in its default position, slower warm-up possible"],2,1,["P2B5A","P2B5B","P2B58","P2B5C"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2B5A:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Control Circuit Low","P2B5A stands for a short to ground in the control wiring of the coolant flow control valve motor. GM's 2025 table for the 3.0-litre Duramax describes the detection: the driver sees more than 9 A flowing, which it interprets as one motor wire touching ground, and 80 out of 100 samples at 12.5 ms set a two-trip Type B fault once relay voltage exceeds 11 V.",["Motor wire chafed or pinched against ground","Coolant or water in the valve connector","Internal short to housing in the valve motor"],["MIL on after two drives","Engine temperature control fixed, slower warm-up or higher running temperature"],2,1,["P2B59","P2B5B","P2B58"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2B5B:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Control Circuit High","P2B5B covers a short to battery voltage on the motor leads of the coolant flow control valve. GM's diesel table 25OBDG04B evaluates it through the driver stage as well: a current above 9 A with a lead tied to supply counts as a failure, and the usual 80-of-100 rule with 12.5 ms sampling stores a Type B code.",["Motor lead chafed against a powered circuit (GM LM2, 21-NA-149)","Corroded or wet connector bridging to supply","Driver stage in the engine control module faulty"],["MIL on after two drives, possibly further codes from the same harness","Blown fuses or rough running if the harness is chafed","Weak heater output during warm-up"],2,1,["P2B59","P2B5A","P2B5C"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2B5C:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Supply Circuit Low","With P2B5C the supply voltage reaching the driver of the coolant flow control valve motor is too low. GM monitors this on the 3.0-litre Duramax (25OBDG04B): if the motor driver sees less than 6 V while the powertrain relay delivers more than 11 V, the difference points at the feed path, and a Type B fault follows after 80 hits in 100 samples.",["Blown or loose fuse, corroded relay contact in the valve feed","Supply wire damaged or chafed in the engine harness","High resistance at a ground or splice of the feed circuit"],["MIL on after two drives","Valve does not move, temperature control in fallback mode"],2,1,["P2B58","P2B59","P2B5B"],"אספקת שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2B5D:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Position Sensor Circuit","P2B5D is the general circuit code for the position sensor of the coolant flow control valve, the feedback that tells the engine computer how far the rotary valve has turned. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly. GM's 3.0-litre Duramax, whose valve reports its position digitally over a SENT link, covers the sensor through the low and high codes P2B5E and P2B5F and a separate communication check instead.",["Loose or corroded terminals at the valve connector","Signal, reference or ground wire of the sensor interrupted","Position sensor inside the valve faulty"],["Check engine light on","Coolant flow control in fallback, warm-up or heating behaviour changed"],2,1,["P2B5E","P2B5F","P2B60"],"חיישן מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2B5E:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2B5E reports a position sensor reading below its valid window. On GM's 3.0-litre Duramax the valve sends its angle as a raw SENT value in percent of 5 V; anything under 2 % counts as too low, and 80 failures in 100 samples at 6.25 ms set a Type B fault, provided there is no SENT communication fault and the relay supplies more than 11 V.",["5 V reference or signal wire interrupted or shorted to ground","Chafed engine harness on GM LM2 (21-NA-149)","Position sensor in the valve faulty"],["MIL on after two drives","Coolant flow no longer regulated, warm-up slower"],2,1,["P2B5D","P2B5F","P2B60"],"חיישן מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2B5F:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Position Sensor Circuit High","P2B5F is set when the valve position signal sits above the top of its window. The 2025 Duramax calibration (3.0 L, 25OBDG04B) treats a SENT raw value over 98 % of 5 V as implausibly high and stores a two-trip Type B code after 80 of 100 readings, sampled every 6.25 ms while the SENT link itself is healthy.",["Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage","Moisture or corrosion bridging contacts in the valve connector","Position sensor in the valve faulty"],["MIL on after two drives","Slow warm-up or weak cabin heat"],2,1,["P2B5D","P2B5E","P2B60"],"חיישן מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2B60:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Position Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2B60 checks whether the valve actually goes where it is told. On GM's 3.0 L Duramax the code sets when the gap between desired and measured position exceeds 12 % in 160 of 200 samples, only with a steady command, closed-loop control active and no coolant or outside temperature sensor fault (Type B).",["Engine control software (GM 20-NA-039 / 22-NA-082, Hyundai/Kia ITM logic)","Corroded terminals at the valve actuator connector (GM PIP5764)","Valve sluggish or not learned, needs a relearn after test","Valve does not follow commands although wiring is fine"],["MIL on after two drives","Engine temperature fluctuates or warms up slowly","Often no driveability complaint beyond the warning lamp"],2,1,["P2B5E","P2B5F","P2B61","P00B7"],"חיישן מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2B61:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Stuck Closed","P2B61 indicates that the coolant flow control valve stays closed although the engine computer asks it to open, so coolant cannot reach the radiator path as intended. Jaguar Land Rover uses it on the 2.0-litre Ingenium petrol four (2019–2020): in bulletin JLRTB02030NAS1, P2B61-73 appears with P26CB-72 when the movable shroud that diverts coolant in the electrically controlled pump stays put, and the PCM runs the fans…",["Valve or diversion shroud mechanically stuck closed (JLR variable coolant pump)","Engine control software that needs an update","Valve drive or its wiring no longer moves the valve"],["Radiator fans running constantly at high speed, loud noise from the engine bay","Rising engine temperature under load","Check engine light on"],3,3,["P2B60","P26CB","P00B7","P0126"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2B62:["Coolant Pump B Supply Voltage Circuit","P2B62 flags a supply voltage problem at coolant pump B, an electrically driven auxiliary pump with its own electronics. Ford's 2024 gasoline OBD summary files it as failure type 1C (supply voltage outside its permitted band) under base code P261A, in the check of pump B, which Ford defines as the high-temperature-loop auxiliary pump for component cooling #1.",["Pump fuse blown or supply relay not closing properly","Corroded or loose power or ground connection at the pump","Weak battery or charging system fault lowering supply voltage","Voltage detection inside the pump electronics faulty"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Auxiliary pump runs slowly or not at all","Rising temperature of the component cooled by pump B"],2,3,["P261A","P2B63","P2B64","P2B9D","P2B69"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ B — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2B63:["Coolant Pump B Stuck/Stalled","P2B63 means coolant pump B is powered and commanded but its rotor does not turn, or stays far below target speed. Brushless auxiliary pumps notice this themselves, for example from high current without rotation, and report it to the engine computer. Ford lists the code in its 2024 gasoline OBD summary as failure type 71 (actuator stuck) of pump B, base code P261A, checked continuously above 11 V battery voltage.",["Bearing seized or impeller jammed by debris or deposits","Electric motor or electronics inside the pump failed","Coolant frozen in the pump because antifreeze concentration is too low"],["Warning lamp with stored code","No audible pump run after the ignition is switched on","Overheating of the component served by pump B"],2,3,["P2B62","P2B65","P261B","P2B9C","P2B6A"],""],P2B64:["Coolant Pump B Control Module Overtemperature","P2B64 reports that the electronics built into coolant pump B have become too hot and the pump has protected itself, usually by derating or shutting down. In Ford's 2024 gasoline OBD summary it is failure type 98 (system over temperature) of the pump B check under P261A, monitored continuously.",["Coolant level low or air at the pump, so the electronics are not cooled","Sluggish impeller raises motor current and heat","Power stage inside the pump degraded","Damaged heat shield or high radiant heat at the mounting point"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Pump stops intermittently, often after long or hot drives","Reduced cooling of the served component"],2,3,["P2B62","P2B63","P2B65","P2B9E","P2B6B"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ B — חום יתר"],P2B65:["Coolant Pump B Overspeed/Air in System","When a coolant pump draws in air, its impeller loses load: speed climbs and current drops. P2B65 reports this for coolant pump B. Ford's 2024 gasoline OBD summary lists it as failure type B1 (overspeed/dry run) of pump B under P261A.",["Air left in the circuit after filling or repair","Coolant loss through a leak, level too low","Restricting check valve in the vent hose (Bentley W12, 975 122 447H)","Speed or current detection inside the pump faulty"],["Coolant or overheating warning in the instrument cluster","Falling coolant level in the expansion tank","Gurgling noise or fluctuating temperature display"],2,3,["P2B86","P2B63","P2B64","P2B6C","P261B"],""],P2B66:["Coolant Pump D Control Circuit/Open","P2B66 is the open-circuit code for the control line of coolant pump D, the pump a manufacturer labels D in its thermal management. The driver stage in the engine computer detects a broken wire, an unplugged connector or a pump input that no longer draws current. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly.",["Pump connector loose, corroded or unplugged","Control wire broken between engine computer and pump","Control input inside the pump open"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Pump D does not respond to commands","Higher temperature in the loop served by pump D"],2,3,["P2B67","P2B68","P2B69","P26F4","P2DF4"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ D — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2B67:["Coolant Pump D Control Circuit Low","P2B67 means the control line of coolant pump D sits too low, typically because it is shorted to ground or the driver stage sees excess current. No manufacturer publishes this code. Ford's comparable entries for pumps A and B (P2602, P261C) set when the smart driver in the engine computer reports an output fault, checked continuously above 11 V.",["Control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Moisture or corrosion in the pump connector","Control input inside the pump shorted"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Pump D runs constantly or not at all"],2,3,["P2B66","P2B68","P26F5","P2DF5","P261C"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ D — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2B68:["Coolant Pump D Control Circuit High","P2B68 flags a control line for coolant pump D that reads too high: it touches a voltage source or is pulled up while the driver should switch it. No manufacturer documents the code publicly. In Ford's 2024 summary the matching pump A and B codes (P2603, P261D) rest on the same principle, with the smart driver in the engine computer reporting an output circuit fault during a continuous check above 11 V.",["Control wire shorted to a battery or ignition feed","Moisture bridging pins in the connector","Fault in the pump electronics pulls the line up"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Pump D runs at a fixed speed or ignores commands"],2,3,["P2B66","P2B67","P26F6","P2DF6","P261D"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ D — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2B69:["Coolant Pump D Supply Voltage Circuit","P2B69 reports that coolant pump D does not receive a usable voltage on its power feed, as distinct from the control line covered by P2B66 to P2B68. No manufacturer documents this code publicly. Ford shows the same failure type for pump B as P2B62 (type 1C, supply outside its permitted band) and for pump A as P2B9D, each checked continuously above 11 V battery voltage.",["Fuse blown or supply relay contacts worn","High resistance at the pump ground or ground point","Weak battery or charging fault"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Pump D slow or inactive","Code returns mainly at low battery voltage or high electrical load"],2,3,["P2B66","P2B6A","P2B62","P26F7","P2DFA","P2B9D"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ D — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2B6A:["Coolant Pump D Stuck/Stalled","P2B6A reports that coolant pump D is blocked or stalled: supply and command are present, yet the rotor does not come up to speed. No manufacturer documents the code publicly. Ford uses the identical failure type 71 (actuator stuck) for pump B as P2B63 and for pump A as P2B9C, and GM's patent US20160047374A1 explains how deviations of measured current and speed from expected values expose a faulty electric coolant…",["Bearing seized or impeller jammed by debris or sludge","Motor winding or pump electronics failed","Coolant frozen because antifreeze concentration is too low"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Pump D silent although commanded","Overheating of the loop served by pump D"],2,3,["P2B69","P2B6B","P2B6C","P2B63","P26F8","P2DF9"],""],P2B6B:["Coolant Pump D Control Module Overtemperature","With P2B6B the integrated electronics of coolant pump D report excessive temperature, and the pump derates or switches itself off to survive. No manufacturer documents this code publicly; the equivalent for pump B is P2B64, which Ford lists as failure type 98 (system over temperature), and for pump A it is P2B9E.",["Too little coolant or air at the pump","Sluggish impeller overloads the motor","Power stage inside the pump degraded"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Pump D cuts out after longer operation and restarts after cooling"],2,3,["P2B6A","P2B6C","P2B64","P26F9","P2DFB","P2B9E"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ D — חום יתר"],P2B6C:["Coolant Pump D Overspeed/Air in System","P2B6C means coolant pump D is spinning faster than its command would explain, the signature of an impeller moving air instead of liquid. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly. For pump B, Bentley stores the counterpart P2B6500 on W12 models and traces it to a restricting vent hose, and Ford lists P2B65 as failure type B1 (overspeed/dry run).",["Circuit not fully bled after filling or repair","Coolant lost through a leak","Vent line or bleed valve restricted, air cannot escape"],["Coolant warning or rising temperature display","Gurgling from the cooling circuit","Coolant level drops in the expansion tank"],2,3,["P2B6A","P2B6B","P2B65","P26FA","P2DF7","P2B86"],""],P2B6D:["Engine Coolant Flow Control Valve Position Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2B6D covers a position signal from the engine coolant flow control valve that drops out or jumps for short moments, even though single readings may still lie inside the valid window. This exact code appears in no public manufacturer document. In GM's 3.0 L Duramax diesel the valve sends its angle digitally via SENT;",["Loose or widened terminal in the valve connector","Fretting corrosion on the signal or reference pins","Harness rubbing or flexing with engine movement","Position sensor inside the valve unstable"],["Warning lamp, code often stored as intermittent","Temperature display or warm-up behaviour fluctuates"],2,1,["P2B5D","P2B5E","P2B5F","P2B60","P2B61"],"חיישן מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת נוזל קירור מנוע — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2B6E:["Turbocharger/Supercharger A Temperature Sensor Circuit","P2B6E is the general circuit code for temperature sensor A on the turbocharger or supercharger. SAE J2012 names the sensor but leaves its measuring point open, so the manufacturer decides what it watches, and no manufacturer documents this exact code publicly.",["Corroded or heat-damaged sensor connector","Intermittent break in signal or ground wire","Temperature sensor A failed"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Implausible or jumping turbo temperature value in live data"],2,1,["P2B6F","P2B70","P2B71","P2B8F","P2EA6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2B6F:["Turbocharger/Supercharger A Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","P2B6F reports that the signal of turbocharger/supercharger temperature sensor A has fallen below its valid range. If the sensor is an NTC thermistor, whose resistance drops as it warms, a low voltage stands for a very high temperature, so the usual electrical causes are a signal wire shorted to ground or a sensor failed internally short.",["Signal wire shorted to ground, for example chafed near the exhaust","Sensor element shorted internally","Input circuit in the engine computer faulty"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Live data shows an extreme value even with the engine cold"],2,1,["P2B6E","P2B70","P2B71","P2B90","P2EC0"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2B70:["Turbocharger/Supercharger A Temperature Sensor Circuit High","P2B70 is set when sensor A on the turbocharger or supercharger delivers a signal above its valid range. For an NTC thermistor this corresponds to an implausibly cold reading, the classic result of an open signal or ground wire, an unplugged connector or a short to the 5 V reference; for a PTC-type element it would indicate extreme heat.",["Signal or ground wire open, connector unplugged","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or another voltage","Sensor element open internally"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Live data shows a fixed extreme value"],2,1,["P2B6E","P2B6F","P2B71","P2B91","P2EC1"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2B71:["Turbocharger/Supercharger A Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2B71 covers a reading from temperature sensor A on the turbocharger or supercharger that is electrically valid yet does not fit the operating state. Typical plausibility tests compare the value after a long engine-off soak with other temperature sensors, or check it against a model;",["Sensor element aged by heat and reading off","Contact resistance at the connector distorting the signal","Sensor loose or not fully seated in its bore"],["Warning lamp, often without noticeable driving change","Turbo temperature in live data differs clearly from other temperatures after a cold start","Boost may be trimmed back as a precaution"],2,1,["P2B6E","P2B6F","P2B70","P2B92","U0643"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2B72:["Coolant Heater A Control Circuit/Open","P2B72 says the command line to coolant heater A is open or has lost continuity. Keep it apart from the engine coolant heater family P01E8–P01EF: the other J2012 codes for this heater – internal module, supply voltage and over-temperature under P2DA4–P2DA7, lost communication under U069E – point to a unit with its own electronics, such as the electric coolant heater of hybrids and EVs.",["Command wire to the heater broken or connector not latched","Terminal pushed back or corroded in the heater connector","Input stage of the heater electronics open internally","Output stage in the commanding control module faulty"],["Little or no cabin heat, especially in electric driving","Engine starts more often in cold weather to provide heat (hybrids)","Warning or fault message, depending on the manufacturer"],2,0,["P2B73","P2B74","P2B75","P2B76","P01E8","U069E"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ A — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2B73:["Coolant Heater A Control Circuit Low","P2B73 is the low case on the command circuit of coolant heater A: the commanding module reads the line at or near ground when it expects a higher level. Usual reasons are a chafed wire touching body ground, coolant or water in a connector, or an input in the heater that pulls the line down.",["Command wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Coolant or water in the heater connector","Input of the heater electronics shorted internally","Commanding module cannot drive the line high"],["Coolant heater does not switch on, weak cabin heat","Engine runs more often in the cold (hybrids)","Fuse for the request circuit may blow repeatedly"],2,0,["P2B72","P2B74","P2B77","P01E9"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2B74:["Coolant Heater A Control Circuit High","P2B74 is the opposite of P2B73: the command circuit of coolant heater A sits at or near supply voltage while the module expects it low, or the output stage measures excess current and shuts down. A wire rubbed through onto a 12 V feed, a crushed harness next to the heater's own supply cable or a shorted input in the heater electronics are typical.",["Command wire shorted to a 12 V circuit","Harness crushed or melted near the heater supply cable","Heater electronics input shorted to its supply","Output stage of the commanding module faulty"],["Coolant heater off, or running without request","Higher 12 V or high-voltage battery drain when parked if the heater runs on","Weak cabin heat in cold weather"],2,0,["P2B72","P2B73","P2B78","P2DA4","P2DA6"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2B75:["Coolant Heater A Control Circuit Performance","P2B75 is set when the command circuit of coolant heater A tests electrically sound but the heater's response does not match the request – the coolant leaving it fails to warm, for instance, or reported power or current stays off target. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 (e)(15.2.2) asks for this kind of functional check on output components.",["Air trapped in the heater loop or low coolant level","Heating element weak or partly failed","Internal fault in the heater control electronics","Coolant pump or valve in the heater loop not circulating enough"],["Cabin warms slowly or only with the engine running","Heater core temperature in live data stays low despite full heat request","Electric range reduced in winter because the engine starts for heat"],3,0,["P2B72","P2B79","P2DA4","P2DA6","P01EB"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2B76:["Coolant Heater B Control Circuit/Open","P2B76 reports an open command circuit for coolant heater B. Where a vehicle has two separately requested heaters or heating stages – Hyundai and Kia patent US11378000B2 describes one housing with several sheath elements that a controller switches individually – B stands for the second channel. Which physical heater carries the letter is up to the manufacturer, and none documents P2B76 publicly.",["Request wire for heater B broken at a flex point","Terminal pushed out of the heater connector","Fuse feeding the request circuit blown","Heater B input open inside the heater electronics"],["Reduced heating power, cabin warms more slowly","Defrosting takes longer in cold weather","Fault entry often without other noticeable effects"],2,0,["P2B77","P2B78","P2B79","P2B72","P01EC"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2B77:["Coolant Heater B Control Circuit Low","P2B77 means the command circuit of coolant heater B reads low: the line is pulled toward ground although the module drives or expects a higher level. With a second heating stage this usually costs part of the heating power rather than all of it, because stage A can still run.",["Harness branch along the coolant hoses shorted to ground","Coolant seepage corroding the heater connector","Heater B input shorted inside the heater electronics"],["Heating power noticeably lower than usual","Cabin and windows take longer to warm up","Possible traces of coolant at the heater connector"],2,0,["P2B76","P2B78","P2B73","P01ED"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2B78:["Coolant Heater B Control Circuit High","P2B78 flags the command line of coolant heater B as too high: voltage is present where the commanding module expects a low level, or its driver reports overcurrent. A short to a 12 V circuit is the classic cause; with a low-side driver, a heater input that has failed short can produce it as well.",["Request wire for heater B shorted to a 12 V circuit","Heater B input failed short inside the heater","Damage in a harness section shared with heater A"],["Heater stage B off, or running although not requested","Unusual battery drain while parked","Lower heating power in winter"],2,0,["P2B76","P2B77","P2B74","P01EE"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2B79:["Coolant Heater B Control Circuit Performance","P2B79 says that coolant heater B is wired correctly but does not do what it is told: after a request the expected warming, current or status feedback fails to appear. In layouts with several stages, as in Hyundai and Kia patent US11378000B2, the controller switches the stages individually and shuts them down when outlet or housing surface temperature runs too high – a stage disabled by that protection can look like…",["Low coolant or trapped air, so protection shuts the stage down","Heating element of stage B weak or open","Internal fault in the heater electronics for stage B"],["Heating power lower than expected","Heater outlet temperature rises slowly in live data","Fault may only appear at low outside temperatures"],3,0,["P2B76","P2B75","P2DA6","P01EF"],"גוף חימום נוזל קירור‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2B7A:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch C Circuit","P2B7A is the general circuit fault of a third EVAP pressure sensor or switch, C, alongside A (P0450 range) and B (P24D5 range). Each maker assigns the letters itself. Audi V6 and V8 engines (bulletin 2069531, 2022–2025) call it tank ventilation pressure sensor 3, part GX49, and use P2B7A for its electrical fault; the bulletin adds that some control units logged this fault wrongly as P0450.",["Sensor of an early design (VW G400 with narrow orifice)","Pressure sensor C failed electrically","Open or short in reference, ground or signal wire","Control unit logs a wrong fault entry (Audi bulletin 2069531)"],["Check engine light on","EVAP readiness monitor stays incomplete","Usually no change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P2B7B","P2B7C","P2B7D","P2B7E","P0450","P24D5"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2B7B:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch C Circuit Range/Performance","P2B7B means sensor C delivers a signal that is electrically valid but implausible. Mercedes-AMG documents it as P2B7B26 on the GT63 S E Performance (2024–2026): the ME control unit sees the signal change too slowly, caused by interference on the line, and bulletin LI07.70-P-078293 cures it by twisting the sensor leads that run between the engine computer and the EVAP sensors.",["Interference on untwisted sensor wiring (Mercedes-AMG)","Sensor port or orifice too narrow or blocked","Fault entry assigned to the wrong sensor (Audi bulletin 2069531)","Pressure sensor C drifting or sluggish"],["Check engine light on, no driveability complaint","EVAP readiness monitor not completing","Code returns after clearing, often after a few drives"],2,1,["P2B7A","P2B7E","P24D6","P0451"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2B7C:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch C Circuit Low","P2B7C reports that the signal of EVAP pressure sensor C stays below its valid voltage window. The only public manufacturer reference is VW: on the 2025–2026 Jetta (engine DNKA) and Taos FWD (DYBA) the code points to fuel tank pressure sensor G400 with its NVLD switch, and bulletin 01-26-01 replaces the sensor assembly with the revised plug housing (part 5WA201700B) if the old version is fitted.",["5 V reference to the sensor missing or shorted","Signal wire shorted to ground","Early-version sensor assembly (VW Jetta/Taos)","Pressure sensor C failed internally"],["Check engine light on","EVAP leak tests not carried out, readiness incomplete","Other sensors on the same 5 V supply may report faults too"],2,1,["P2B7A","P2B7D","P24D7","P0452"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2B7D:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch C Circuit High","P2B7D is the high counterpart to P2B7C: the signal of EVAP pressure sensor C sits above its valid range. VW lists it in bulletin 01-26-01 for the 2025–2026 Jetta and Taos FWD, whose fuel tank pressure sensor G400 came with a plug-housing orifice that proved too small; the first step is to check which housing version is installed. Public limits for sensor C do not exist;",["Sensor ground wire open or high resistance","Signal wire shorted to 5 V reference or battery voltage","Early-version sensor assembly (VW Jetta/Taos)","Pressure sensor C failed internally"],["Check engine light on","EVAP readiness not set after clearing codes","Car usually drives normally"],2,1,["P2B7A","P2B7C","P24D8","P0453"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2B7E:["EVAP System Pressure Sensor/Switch C Circuit Intermittent","P2B7E covers a signal from EVAP pressure sensor C that drops out or jumps for brief moments instead of failing for good. No manufacturer documents P2B7E publicly; Audi and VW use only P2B7A and P2B7B, VW also P2B7C and P2B7D, for this sensor.",["Loose or corroded terminal at the sensor connector","Harness chafing near the tank or along the underbody","Electrical interference on the signal line","Pressure sensor C with an intermittent internal fault"],["Check engine light comes and goes","Pressure reading jumps in live data","Fault often appears only on rough roads or in wet weather"],2,1,["P2B7A","P2B7B","P24D9","P0454"],"חיישן/מתג לחץ מערכת אדי הדלק (EVAP)‏ C — תקלה לסירוגין במעגל"],P2B7F:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Control Module A Calibration Not Learned/Programmed","P2B7F applies where boost control A is handled by its own electronic module, typically a smart actuator on the charger, and that module reports missing or invalid calibration data. Honeywell patent US7689376B2 describes such a controller holding a multi-point calibration measured for its individual turbocharger, and Melett notes for REA-type actuators that this data is unique to each unit, so swapped or new parts…",["New or used module or charger fitted without programming or learn routine","Programming aborted, for example by low battery voltage","Module has lost its stored calibration (internal fault)"],["Warning lamp right after a repair on the turbo system","Reduced boost or emergency mode"],4,3,["P2B80","P0045","P003A","P2563"],""],P2B80:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Boost Control Module B Calibration Not Learned/Programmed","P2B80 is the counterpart of P2B7F for the second boost control module, which only exists where two chargers or two separately driven actuators each carry their own electronics. It is set when module B has no valid calibration or its learn step was never completed.",["Module B or its charger replaced without programming or learn routine","Modules or chargers fitted on the wrong side","Programming session aborted"],["Warning lamp after work on the second charger","Reduced power because boost on one side is limited"],4,3,["P2B7F","P003B","P2587"],""],P2B81:["Wastegate Position Sensor A Circuit Performance","P2B81 reports that electric wastegate A does not behave as commanded although its sensor signal is electrically fine. GM documents it for the 2.7L L3B (table 19OBDG03D): with the actuator in normal operation the fault counts if the position error exceeds 20 % for over 1 s, actuator current exceeds 1.0 A for over 1 s or duty cycle exceeds 40 % for over 1 s, and 25 of 30 samples must fail;",["Wastegate valve or linkage binding (GM PIP6007A, turbo replacement)","Electric wastegate actuator worn or drawing excessive current","Linkage clip missing or rod detached"],["MIL in the first trip","Boost too low or too high, flat or jerky acceleration","Reduced power mode possible"],3,3,["P2B82","P2B93","P2AB7","P2AB8","P2AB9","P0244","P2C9B","U0644"],"חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ A — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2B82:["Wastegate Position Sensor B Circuit Performance","P2B82 is the performance fault for the second electric wastegate, found only on engines with two turbochargers and position-controlled wastegates. No manufacturer documents this exact code publicly. By analogy with GM's checks for wastegate A (P2B81 in 19OBDG03D), the computer would flag lasting gaps between commanded and measured position, or a motor that needs abnormal current or duty cycle to hold its target.",["Wastegate valve B or linkage binding from heat and deposits","Actuator B worn, gear or motor weak","Loose linkage or retaining clip"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Uneven or reduced boost, weaker pull"],3,3,["P2B81","P2B94","P2ABA","P2ABB","P2ABC","P0248","P2C9C","U0674"],"חיישן מצב שסתום עקיפת טורבו (Wastegate)‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2B83:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump A Overspeed/Air In System","P2B83 concerns the electric pump that keeps coolant moving through a water-cooled charge air cooler. When the impeller runs in air instead of liquid, load vanishes and the motor spins up. GM documents this in its 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B: a reported pump speed of 8,500 rpm or more in 8 of 10 one-second samples sets the code, provided the pump is fitted and enabled, the engine is not cranking and relay voltage is…",["Air pocket in the charge air cooler loop after service or a leak","Low coolant level in the separate low-temperature loop","Impeller loose or broken on the pump shaft","Pump electronics reporting an implausible speed"],["Check engine light after two drives with the fault","Reduced power under load because the intake air gets hot","Falling level in the charge air cooler coolant reservoir"],2,3,["P2B84","P026E","P2BC1","P2CB1","P023A"],""],P2B84:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump A Underspeed","P2B84 reports that the electric charge air cooler pump is turning too slowly or not at all, judged by the speed its own electronics send back. GM lists the code next to P2B83 in the 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B as the low out-of-range case of the pump speed, with the limit printed as a reading below -115 rpm;",["Worn or seized pump bearing, or debris blocking the impeller","Water or corrosion in the pump connector","Low supply voltage or poor ground at the pump","Pump motor or its electronics worn out"],["Check engine light after the second faulty drive","Less power under heavy load or when towing","High charge air temperature shown in live data"],2,3,["P2B83","P026E","P2BC1","P2CB2","P2BC2"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ A — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2B85:["Engine Coolant Pump Underspeed","P2B85 applies to engines whose main water pump is electric: the pump turns clearly slower than commanded. On GM's 2.7-litre L3B (table 19OBDG03D) the filtered gap between commanded and reported speed must exceed a map value – 200 rpm at low commands, up to 800 rpm at 8,000 rpm – during 8 of 10 seconds, with 300–6,250 rpm requested and more than 11 V;",["Failed control board inside the electric water pump","Loose or poorly latched plug at the pump","Bearing wear or deposits slowing the impeller","Low supply voltage or high resistance in power or ground"],["Rising coolant temperature and overheating warnings","Reduced engine power to protect the engine","Check engine light, often on the first trip","Engine may be shut down if driving continues"],3,3,["P2BA2","P26CE","P26CB","P26CA","P26D3","P0217"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מנוע — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2B86:["Coolant Pump A Overspeed/Air in System","P2B86 says coolant pump A spins faster than it was told to – the typical sign of air at the impeller. In GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG03A, 25OBDG04B) the filtered gap between command and feedback must stay beyond a map limit, the pump running 200 to 348 rpm too fast depending on the 300–3,480 rpm request, over 8 s of a 10 s span at more than 11 V; Type B.",["Air trapped in the loop after a repair or incomplete bleeding","Coolant loss through a leak, low level in the reservoir","Foreign object such as a loose O-ring at the pump ports","Restricted bleed or vent hose keeping air in the system"],["Check engine light after the second faulty trip","Weak or fluctuating cabin heat","Coolant warning or gurgling noise in the heater area"],2,1,["P2B87","P2B65","P2B6C","P26FA","P2DF7","P2600"],""],P2B87:["Coolant Pump A Underspeed","With P2B87 the reported speed of coolant pump A stays below the commanded one. GM's 2025 tables (25OBDG03A, 25OBDG04B) compare filtered command and feedback against a calibrated limit while 300–3,480 rpm is requested and more than 11 V is present; 8 s in a 10 s window, Type B. Ford's 2024 gasoline summary lists it as the underspeed type of the cabin-heating auxiliary pump, checked continuously from 11 V.",["Outdated software in the module that commands the pump","Impeller slowed by debris or a foreign O-ring","Worn bearing or motor in the auxiliary pump","Low voltage or poor contact at the pump connector"],["Check engine light, often without any other complaint","Reduced cabin heat at idle or with the engine stopped"],2,1,["P2B86","P2B9C","P2B9F","P2BA0","P2601"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ A — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2B88:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Circuit Bank 1","P2B88 is the catch-all electrical code for the oxygen sensor that some turbocharged engines mount in the intake tract, behind compressor and charge air cooler, to judge how much exhaust the recirculation system is feeding back. Ford's patents describe this intake sensor as a heated wide-band element whose pumping current shrinks as recirculated gas dilutes the fresh charge.",["Corroded or loose sensor plug, often wetted by charge air cooler condensate","Open or chafed signal wire between sensor and engine module","Intake oxygen sensor element internally failed","Fault in the sensor input stage of the engine module"],["Check engine light on","EGR reduced or switched off, with slightly higher fuel use or knock-limited power","Often no noticeable change in driving behaviour"],2,1,["P2B89","P2B8A","P2B8B","P2ABF","P2AC0"],"חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — תקלה במעגל החשמלי (בנק 1)"],P2B89:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Circuit Low Voltage Bank 1","With P2B89 the bank 1 intake oxygen sensor signal sits below the lowest voltage the engine module accepts. Typical electrical reasons are a signal lead shorted to ground, a damaged element or a corroded plug near the charge air cooler, where condensate gathers.",["Engine software detecting falsely (Alfa Romeo Giulia 2.0 EC2, fixed by reflash)","Signal wire shorted to ground or pinched in the harness","Moisture or corrosion in the sensor connector","Sensor element cracked or contaminated"],["Check engine light on","EGR flow limited or disabled by the engine module","Other stored codes such as P2AC0 or P0402 on the same vehicle"],2,1,["P2B88","P2B8A","P2AC0","P2AC1","P0402"],"חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מתח נמוך במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2B8A:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Circuit High Voltage Bank 1","P2B8A is the mirror image of P2B89: the bank 1 intake oxygen sensor delivers a voltage above its valid window. On a wide-band element this usually comes from a signal wire touching a supply or the heater feed, from an open ground or reference return that lets the input float upward, or from water inside the connector.",["Signal wire shorted to a supply or to the heater feed","Open ground or reference return lead of the sensor","Water in the sensor connector","Internal sensor fault"],["Check engine light on","EGR switched off, possibly slightly higher fuel consumption","Intake oxygen reading on the scan tool above the fresh-air value"],2,1,["P2B88","P2B89","P2AC2","P2AE3"],"חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מתח גבוה במעגל (בנק 1)"],P2B8B:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Heater Control Circuit/Open Bank 1","P2B8B is about the heater of bank 1's intake oxygen sensor: the module switches the heater on but sees no current, the classic sign of a broken heater coil, an open feed or control lead, or a blown fuse in the heater supply. A wide-band sensor only measures once its ceramic is hot.",["Heater coil inside the sensor burnt through or cracked","Blown fuse or failed relay in the heater supply","Open heater feed or control wire, loose connector pin","Heater driver in the engine module failed"],["Check engine light on","EGR stays inactive because the intake sensor never becomes ready","Possible companion code for the sensor signal"],2,1,["P2B8C","P2B8D","P2B8E","P2B88"],"גוף חימום חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח (בנק 1)"],P2B8C:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Heater Control Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1","P2B8C is not about broken wires: the heater of the bank 1 intake oxygen sensor is electrically intact, yet the element does not reach or hold its temperature as expected, or the heater needs power that does not fit the conditions. Mounted right after the intercooler, this sensor gets hit by condensate.",["Water from the charge air cooler reaching the hot sensor element","Heater aged with increased resistance, sensor slow to warm up","Corroded pins or high resistance in the heater supply","Low system voltage limiting heater power"],["Check engine light on","Fault often appears in humid or cold weather and with high boost","EGR temporarily reduced"],2,1,["P2B8B","P2B8D","P2B8E","P2AC0"],"גוף חימום חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2B8D:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Heater Control Circuit Low Bank 1","P2B8D means the voltage the module sees on the heater control wire of bank 1's intake oxygen sensor is lower than the module expects for the commanded state, usually because the line is shorted to ground. Many engine modules switch such heaters on the ground side; there a control wire chafed against the body can keep the heater running even when it should be off, which overheats the ceramic and can crack it.",["Heater control wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Heater coil with shorted turns inside the sensor","Water bridging the heater pins in the connector","Heater output stage in the engine module defective"],["Check engine light on","Heater switched off by the module, EGR feedback unavailable","Repeated sensor failure if the short is not repaired"],2,1,["P2B8B","P2B8C","P2B8E","P0031"],"גוף חימום חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2B8E:["Intake Air O2 Sensor Heater Control Circuit High Bank 1","With P2B8E, bank 1's intake O2 heater control wire shows more voltage than expected, as when it is shorted to battery voltage or when the driver cannot pull it down. If the module switches the heater on its ground side, such a short means the heater never receives current, the element stays cold and the sensor is never released for measuring.",["Heater control wire shorted to battery voltage","Heater with too low resistance tripping the driver's overcurrent protection","Damaged connector with pins touching each other","Heater output stage in the engine module defective"],["Check engine light on","Intake oxygen sensor stays cold and not ready","EGR inactive"],2,1,["P2B8B","P2B8C","P2B8D","P0032"],"גוף חימום חיישן חמצן אוויר יניקה — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה (בנק 1)"],P2B8F:["Turbocharger/Supercharger B Temperature Sensor Circuit","P2B8F is the general circuit fault for temperature sensor B, the second sensor of this kind on a charged engine, often belonging to a second turbocharger. Which spot it watches is left to the manufacturer, and none documents this code publicly. The engine computer sets it when the signal is lost or unusable without clearly sitting below or above its range, for example during short interruptions.",["Loose or heat-damaged connector with intermittent contact","Wiring chafed or brittle near hot exhaust parts","Temperature sensor B failed internally"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Sensor B value missing or jumping in live data"],2,1,["P2B90","P2B91","P2B92","P2B6E","U0689"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2B90:["Turbocharger/Supercharger B Temperature Sensor Circuit Low","P2B90 means the signal of temperature sensor B has dropped below the lowest value the engine computer accepts. What that says about temperature depends on the element: an NTC thermistor loses resistance when hot, so a low signal reads as extreme heat, whereas a platinum resistor of the kind Heraeus patented for turbo protection (US8328419B2) gains resistance with heat, so a low signal reads as extreme cold.",["Signal wire shorted to ground, for example melted insulation","Sensor element shorted internally","Faulty input stage in the engine computer"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Sensor B shows a fixed extreme value even on a cold engine"],2,1,["P2B8F","P2B91","P2B92","P2B6F"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2B91:["Turbocharger/Supercharger B Temperature Sensor Circuit High","P2B91 is stored when temperature sensor B delivers a signal above its permitted window. By far the most frequent reason is a broken current path: an unplugged or corroded connector, a cracked wire or an element that has burned open, which pulls the input up to its reference voltage. A short to the 5 V supply or to battery voltage has the same effect.",["Signal or ground wire open, connector unplugged or corroded","Sensor element or its lead wires broken by heat cycling","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or battery voltage"],["Warning lamp with stored code","Sensor B stuck at an end value in live data"],2,1,["P2B8F","P2B90","P2B92","P2B70"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2B92:["Turbocharger/Supercharger B Temperature Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","P2B92 says that temperature sensor B delivers a plausible voltage whose content is wrong: it may hang at one value, follow load changes too slowly or disagree with its partner sensor A on an engine with two chargers. A sensor that sits in a soot-coated or oil-wetted spot reacts sluggishly and is a classic trigger.",["Sensor tip coated with soot or oil, responds sluggishly","Sensor element aged and reading off","Contact resistance in connector or wiring"],["Warning lamp, usually without drivability change","Sensor B lags behind or contradicts sensor A in live data","Boost may be limited as a precaution"],2,1,["P2B8F","P2B90","P2B91","P2B71","U0689"],"חיישן טמפרטורת מגדש‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2B93:["Wastegate Position Sensor A Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B93 concerns the learned closed position of electric wastegate A. The computer periodically drives the valve onto its seat and stores the sensor value found there; Ford's patent US9243553B2 explains why: linkage length drifts with temperature and the reference must be refreshed.",["Wastegate linkage bent, stretched or wrongly adjusted","Wastegate flap or seat worn so the valve travels too far","Turbocharger or actuator replaced and relearn not completed"],["MIL in the first trip","Boost slightly low because the valve does not fully close"],3,3,["P2B94","P2B81","P003A","P2AB7","P0244"],""],P2B94:["Wastegate Position Sensor B Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B94 is set when the learned end position of electric wastegate B falls outside the window the engine computer accepts. Stellantis documents it on the 2025 Ram 1500 with the 3.0L Hurricane twin-turbo: bulletin 09-008-25 (Rev. B) lists P2B94 together with P0248 and a MIL, with weak turbo response, caused by wastegate rod retention clips installed incorrectly at the factory.",["Wastegate rod retention clips incorrectly installed (Stellantis 09-008-25)","Play or bending in the wastegate B linkage","Charger or actuator B replaced without completed relearn"],["MIL on, often together with P0248","Lack of acceleration from the turbo"],2,3,["P2B93","P2B82","P0248","P003B","P2ABA"],""],P2B95:["Cold Start Injection Pulse Performance","P2B95 belongs to the cold-start strategy of petrol direct-injection engines: while the catalyst is heated, each injection is split into two or more small pulses, and the module checks via the injector coil voltage that every pulse really opened the injector. Unlike P2B08 to P2B0F, which name a cylinder, P2B95 is the engine-wide verdict.",["Engine software setting the code falsely (GM and Stellantis reflash bulletins)","Injector opening sluggishly when cold due to deposits or wear","High resistance or chafing in injector wiring","Rail pressure outside the expected range during cold start"],["Check engine light after two cold starts with the fault","Usually no noticeable effect on driving","Possibly rough running in the first seconds after a cold start"],2,1,["P2B96","P2B08","P2B09","P2B0A","P2B0B"],"פולס הזרקת התנעה קרה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B96:["Injection Pulse Performance","P2B96 is the engine-wide check, outside the cold-start phase, that injectors on a direct-injection petrol engine really open when commanded. The module digitises the voltage across each injector and looks for the small kink the moving armature leaves; if commanded pulses repeatedly show no opening, it assumes fuel was not delivered.",["Engine harness chafed against underhood parts (GM 2.7 l L3B)","Engine software detecting falsely, fixed by reprogramming","Injector armature sticking or injector worn","High resistance in an injector circuit or connector"],["Check engine light after two drives with the fault","Misfire or rough running if fuel is really missing","Often other codes from the same harness or injector fault"],3,1,["P2B95","P2B00","P2B01","P2B03","P0300"],"פולס הזרקה — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2B97:["Exhaust Pressure Control Valve A Position Exceeded Learning Limit","P2B97 concerns the electrically driven exhaust back-pressure flap of GM's 3.0-litre Duramax diesel. After key-off the module moves the flap to its fully closed and fully open stops and stores what the SENT position sensor reports there.",["Flap travel blocked by welding slag, soot or corrosion","Position sensor in the actuator drifted","Actuator gear or motor worn so the stops are not reached","Weak battery during the key-off learn"],["Check engine light after one drive","Slower warm-up or reduced exhaust heating for aftertreatment","Possibly reduced engine power"],3,3,["P2B98","P2B99","P0476","P048B","P047F"],""],P2B98:["Exhaust Pressure Control Valve A Supply Low","P2B98 says the motor of exhaust pressure control valve A is not getting enough supply voltage. On GM's 3.0-litre Duramax, whose 2025 table 25OBDG04B documents the code, the H-bridge that drives the exhaust flap reports undervoltage below 6 V; 240 failed out of 300 samples taken every 12.5 ms set it, outside cranking and with the powertrain relay delivering more than 11 V. Type A, MIL after one trip.",["Blown fuse or interrupted feed to the valve actuator","Engine harness chafed and shorted (GM 21-NA-149)","Corroded connector or poor ground at the actuator","Weak battery or charging fault causing voltage dips"],["Check engine light after one drive","Exhaust flap without function, slower warm-up","Further codes for the same fuse or harness"],2,3,["P2B97","P2B99","P0475","P0477"],"אספקת שסתום בקרת לחץ פליטה‏ A — ערך נמוך"],P2B99:["Exhaust Pressure Control Valve A Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P2B99 reports that the output stage driving exhaust pressure control valve A is running too hot or carrying too much current. In GM's 2025 diesel table 25OBDG04B for the 3.0-litre Duramax, the H-bridge driver temperature has to exceed 170 °C in 240 of 300 samples at 12.5 ms intervals, outside cranking and with more than 11 V on the powertrain relay; Type A, one trip.",["Valve motor with internal fault such as shorted windings","Flap binding from soot or corrosion so the motor stalls","Short in the actuator wiring (GM 21-NA-149)","Defective driver stage in the control module"],["Check engine light after one drive","Exhaust flap no longer controlled","Possibly reduced power or longer warm-up"],3,3,["P2B98","P2B97","P0475","P0478"],"שסתום בקרת לחץ פליטה‏ A — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר"],P2B9A:["Reductant Quality Sensor Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2B9A covers a DEF quality sensor whose signal drops out now and then or jumps between values, rather than sitting permanently too low or too high. The sensor in the tank module usually gauges urea concentration by timing an ultrasonic echo and passes the result on digitally.",["Loose, corroded or water-damaged connector at the DEF tank module","Air bubbles or sloshing DEF disturbing the ultrasonic echo","Quality sensor beginning to fail","Urea crystals or deposits on the sensor face"],["Check engine light on","DEF warning message, possibly a countdown to reduced speed or no restart","Fault comes and goes, often after refilling or on rough roads"],2,3,["P206A","P206B","P206C","P206D","P207F"],"חיישן איכות אוריאה (AdBlue) — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2B9B:["Vehicle Conditions Incorrect for Particulate Matter Sensor Regeneration","P2B9B is a status code of the particulate matter sensor behind the diesel particulate filter: the sensor needs to burn its electrodes clean before the next measurement, but operating conditions do not allow it. Heating the ceramic to around 780 °C is only safe once the exhaust is dry.",["Short trips and long idling keeping exhaust below the dew point","Faulty exhaust temperature signal misjudging dew point conditions","Low supply voltage to the sensor control unit preventing heating","Engine software setting the enable conditions too narrowly"],["Usually no change in driving","Particulate filter monitor shown as not complete","Code disappears after a longer drive at steady speed"],1,0,["P24D1","P24AF","P24B3","P24B7","P2002"],""],P2B9C:["Coolant Pump A Stuck/Stalled","P2B9C signals that coolant pump A is powered and commanded but its rotor does not turn, or stops. Ford uses the code in its 2024 gasoline OBD summary as fault type 71 (actuator stuck) under P2600, where pump A is the auxiliary pump in the high-temperature loop for cabin heating; the check runs continuously above 11 V battery voltage over 5 seconds.",["Seized bearing or rotor in the auxiliary pump","Sludge, sealant residue or debris jamming the impeller","Coolant frozen in the pump due to weak antifreeze","Burnt motor winding or failed drive electronics"],["Little or no cabin heat","Check engine light","Pump silent when it should run"],2,1,["P2B9D","P2B9E","P2B87","P2B63","P2B6A","P26F8"],""],P2B9D:["Coolant Pump A Supply Voltage Circuit","P2B9D means the power feed of coolant pump A is outside its usable range, as opposed to the command line covered by P2600 to P2603. Ford names it in the 2024 gasoline OBD summary as fault type 1C (feed voltage outside its window) of the cabin-heating auxiliary pump, monitored all the time from 11 V battery voltage with a 5-second window.",["Blown fuse or faulty relay in the pump supply","Corroded connector or poor ground at the pump","Weak battery or charging system voltage too low","Chafed or broken supply wire"],["Cabin heat weak or missing","Check engine light","Fault comes and goes with battery condition or electrical load"],2,1,["P2B9C","P2B9E","P2B62","P2B69","P26F7","P2600"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ A — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2B9E:["Coolant Pump A Control Module Overtemperature","P2B9E is raised by the electronics built into coolant pump A when their temperature gets too high; the pump then derates or shuts down to protect itself. Ford's 2024 OBD summary for gasoline engines lists it as fault type 98 (system over temperature) of the cabin-heating auxiliary pump, monitored continuously once the battery supplies 11 V or more.",["Low coolant or air at the pump, so the electronics lose cooling","Stiff bearing or impeller raising motor load","Heat from nearby exhaust parts or damaged heat shield","Ageing power stage in the pump electronics"],["Cabin heat drops off after some time of driving","Check engine light","Pump stops and restarts after cooling down"],2,1,["P2B9C","P2B9D","P2B86","P2B64","P2B6B","P26F9"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור‏ A — חום יתר"],P2B9F:["Coolant Pump B Underspeed","P2B9F means coolant pump B turns slower than requested. Ford's 2024 gasoline OBD summary places it as underspeed type B2 in the block of base code P261A, where pump B is the auxiliary pump of the high-temperature loop for component cooling no. 1; the check runs continuously from 11 V with a 5-second window.",["Worn bearing or dragging impeller in pump B","Debris or sludge slowing the impeller","Low supply voltage or poor ground at the pump","Weak motor or drive electronics in the pump"],["Check engine light","Temperature warning for the cooled component under load","Possible power reduction to protect hot parts"],2,3,["P2B63","P2B65","P261B","P2B87","P2BA0","P2BA1"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ B — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2BA0:["Coolant Pump C Underspeed","P2BA0 reports that coolant pump C does not reach its speed. GM names the code Low Temperature Coolant Loop Pump Underspeed in its diesel ECM tables and treats it as a low out-of-range speed reading: in 2020 (20OBDG04) the printed limit is below -100 rpm in 5 of 8 one-second samples, in 2025 (25OBDG04A) below -50 rpm in 4 of 5; enable conditions are an active pump, 11 V or more at the relay and no cranking.",["Engine harness chafed against brackets, shorting pump circuits","Worn or partly seized low-temperature loop pump","Air or low coolant in the low-temperature loop","Low supply voltage at the pump relay"],["Check engine light after the second faulty trip","Parts on the low-temperature loop cooled less, reduced power possible","Further electrical codes when the harness is damaged"],2,3,["P2C48","P26F4","P26F8","P26FA","P2B9F","P2BA1"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ C — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2BA1:["Coolant Pump D Underspeed","P2BA1 is set when coolant pump D, a further electric pump in the manufacturer's thermal management, turns slower than its command. No manufacturer documents this code publicly, so which circuit pump D serves and which limits apply is unknown.",["Worn bearing or dragging impeller in pump D","Debris or deposits slowing the impeller","Low supply voltage or high resistance in power or ground","Weak motor or drive electronics in the pump"],["Check engine light or cooling warning, depending on the vehicle","Rising temperature of the part cooled by pump D"],2,3,["P2B6A","P2B6C","P2B69","P2B66","P2B9F","P2BA0"],"משאבת נוזל קירור‏ D — מהירות נמוכה מדי"],P2BA2:["Engine Coolant Pump Stuck/Stalled","P2BA2 belongs to the electric main water pump. GM uses it in a way the title does not suggest: on the 2.7-litre L3B (table 19OBDG03D) and in the 2025 table 25OBDG03B the test runs while the pump should be switched off – pump disabled or a request of 0–4 rpm for at least 3 s – and fails if the pump still reports 10 rpm or more for 8 of 10 seconds with over 11 V on board.",["Pump electronics ignoring the off command","Implausible speed feedback from the pump","Impeller turned by coolant flow from another pump","Command or enable line fault keeping the pump on"],["Check engine light after two trips","Engine takes longer to reach operating temperature","Pump audible after the engine is switched off"],3,1,["P2B85","P26CE","P26CB","P26CA","P26D2"],""],P2BA3:["Starter/Generator Mechanical Performance","P2BA3 concerns the belt-driven starter-generator of mild-hybrid and stop-start engines: the controller has concluded that the machine does not turn the crankshaft or take torque from it as it should, although its electrics seem healthy. The exact detection rule is not published.",["Weak or defective belt tensioner or tensioner damper letting the belt slip","Worn, misaligned or thrown poly-V belt","Damaged idler or tensioner rollers","Mechanical damage in the starter-generator (bearing, pulley)"],["Squealing, chirping or grinding from the belt drive, often at start","Engine fails to restart after an automatic stop","Battery runs flat because the machine no longer charges","Electrical system warning or MIL on the instrument panel"],2,3,["P0A92","P0A1E","P2DC7","P2DCC"],"מכני מתנע/גנרטור — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2BA4:["Catalyst Feedgas Performance","Many diesel SCR systems rely on the oxidation catalyst ahead of them to turn part of the NO into NO2, because a mix near half NO2 lets the SCR reaction run fast at low temperature. P2BA4 reports that this catalyst no longer delivers the needed gas mix. CARB 13 CCR 1968.2 (f)(1.2.3)(B) requires this check for 2015 and later diesels, but lets a maker cover it with the regular NMHC efficiency monitor;",["Oxidation catalyst thermally aged or poisoned (sulphur, oil ash), little NO2 produced","Catalyst inlet face coated with soot or unburnt fuel after injector or EGR problems","Faulty NOx or exhaust temperature sensor distorting the evaluation","Exhaust leak upstream of the catalyst diluting the measured gas"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","SCR efficiency codes such as P20EE set as well","Usually no noticeable change in driving behaviour"],3,1,["P2BA5","P0420","P20EE","P2BA6"],""],P2BA5:["Particulate Filter Feedgas Performance","Some diesel particulate filters carry a precious-metal coating that, besides helping burn soot, oxidises NO to NO2 for the SCR catalyst further down. P2BA5 says this coated filter fails to supply enough NO2.",["Filter coating thermally aged, e.g. after very hot or uncontrolled regenerations","Ash or oil additives covering the catalytic layer","Weak upstream oxidation catalyst in a combined evaluation","Exhaust temperature or NOx sensor reading wrongly"],["Malfunction indicator lamp on","More frequent active regenerations","SCR efficiency codes may follow"],3,1,["P2BA4","P2002","P20EE","P24A2"],""],P2BA6:["NOx Exceedance - SCR NOx Catalyst Performance","P2BA6 opens the group of NOx exceedance codes that grew out of the European rules on reagent-based NOx control. Each code names why tailpipe NOx has climbed above the diagnostic limit; here the blame lies with the SCR catalyst itself, while dosing, reagent and EGR still look plausible.",["SCR catalyst aged, overheated or chemically poisoned","Urea crystal deposits on mixer or catalyst face","Downstream NOx sensor drifting high","Too little NO2 from upstream oxidation catalyst"],["MIL and emission system warning in the cluster","Countdown to speed limit or no restart after some distance","Higher DEF consumption without better NOx reduction"],3,3,["P20EE","P2BAD","P2BA9","P2BAE","P2BA4"],""],P2BA7:["NOx Exceedence - Empty Reagent Tank","P2BA7 records that NOx control has been lost because the DEF or AdBlue tank has run dry, so no reagent can be dosed. Regulation (EU) 2017/1151 Annex XVI requires a level warning no later than 2,400 km ahead of an empty tank and an inducement that keeps the vehicle from operating with an empty tank, typically by blocking the next engine start after a countdown.",["DEF tank simply not refilled despite level warnings","Level sensor reading empty although fluid is present (fault, ice, deposits)","Leaking DEF tank or line emptying the system","Only a small amount refilled, below the quantity the system needs to recognise a refill"],["DEF empty message with restart countdown","Engine will not restart once countdown expires","MIL or emission warning on"],1,3,["P203F","P2BA8","P2BAF","P241D"],""],P2BA8:["NOx Exceedence - Interruption of Reagent Dosing Activity","With P2BA8 the controller states that NOx went up because reagent dosing stopped although the engine needed it. Regulation (EU) 2017/1151 Annex XVI, point 5.5, treats such an interruption as a case for the driver warning, unless the system paused dosing on purpose in conditions the maker declared to the authority; if dosing is not restored within 50 km, inducement starts.",["DEF injector clogged or stuck by crystals","Pump failure or pressure not built up","Frozen fluid because tank or line heater fails","Wiring or SCR control unit fault stopping dosing"],["DEF dosing malfunction message with distance countdown","MIL on, further SCR component codes stored","Reduced power or no restart if not repaired"],2,3,["P208B","P20E8","P2047","P2BA7","P2BAA"],""],P2BA9:["NOx Exceedence - Insufficient Reagent Quality","P2BA9 blames high NOx on reagent that falls short of the specified quality, e.g. diluted or contaminated DEF. EU Annex XVI wants a wrong-fluid warning and inducement if not fixed within 50 km; CARB asks for improper reductant detection.",["DEF diluted with water, aged or replaced by the wrong fluid","Contaminated tank or lines (also from production, FCA 25-003-15)","Air leak after the MAF sensor or at EGR cooler joints misleading the NOx model (JLR)","Outdated engine software or faulty NOx sensor"],["Incorrect DEF quality message with restart countdown","MIL on, often with P2BAE and P2BAF","Speed or power limit if the countdown runs out"],2,3,["P207F","P2B9A","P2BAE","P2BAF","P20EE"],""],P2BAA:["NOx Exceedence - Low Reagent Consumption","P2BAA means less reagent is actually reaching the exhaust than the dosing strategy asks for, so NOx stays too high. EU Annex XVI sets the frame: actual and demanded consumption are compared, and a gap above 50 % over 30 minutes triggers the warning.",["Partially blocked DEF injector delivering too little","Weak DEF pump or clogged pump filter","Calibration error setting the code without a fault (GM 25-NA-042)","Leak in the pressure line returning fluid before the injector"],["Service emission or exhaust fluid system message","MIL on after one trip","DEF level falls more slowly than usual"],2,3,["P249D","P20E8","P2BA8","P2BA9","P208B"],""],P2BAB:["NOx Exceedence - Incorrect EGR Flow","P2BAB attributes excess NOx to exhaust gas recirculation that delivers the wrong amount of gas, so combustion temperature and raw NOx rise. It belongs to the European NOx control rules: Regulation (EU) No 582/2011, Annex XIII, handles tampering-related monitoring through UN Regulation 49 and keeps an EGR valve counter, so an impeded valve leads to warning and inducement.",["EGR valve sooted up or sticking","EGR cooler or pipe partly blocked","Faulty EGR position sensor or air mass meter distorting flow estimate","Leak in the intake or EGR path"],["MIL on, EGR flow codes stored","Rough running or sooting with too much EGR","Power reduction possible if not repaired"],2,3,["P0400","P0401","P0402","P2BAC"],""],P2BAC:["NOx Exceedence - Deactivation of EGR","P2BAC is reserved for the case where exhaust gas recirculation is not just off target but shut down altogether, whether by an unplugged valve, a blocked path, an unauthorised software change or a defect that leaves the valve closed. The European rules treat this as a typical tampering scenario: Regulation (EU) No 582/2011, Annex XIII, carries an EGR valve counter that ends first in a warning and then in inducement.",["EGR valve unplugged, blanked off or disabled","EGR valve stuck closed or actuator failed","Modified engine software with EGR switched off","Open or short in the EGR valve circuit"],["MIL and NOx warning, later inducement","Harder, louder combustion","EGR circuit or position codes stored as well"],2,3,["P2BAB","P0400","P0401"],""],P2BAD:["NOx Exceedence - Root Cause Unknown","P2BAD is the catch-all of the series: NOx after the SCR is measured too high, yet none of the specific causes from P2BA6 to P2BAC can be pinned down. GM uses it on the 2014 Duramax 6.6 L LML as Exhaust NOx Concentration High - Unknown Reason: the measured SCR efficiency, minus an offset-corrected model value, is filtered over time and fails once the difference drops below zero, with both NOx sensors active for over…",["Poor DEF quality or partly blocked dosing without a specific code","Aged or deposit-covered SCR catalyst","Upstream or downstream NOx sensor drifting","Engine control software needing an update (Nissan Titan XD)"],["Exhaust fluid quality poor or emission warning","MIL on after the first failed run","Speed limit countdown if the condition persists"],3,3,["P20EE","P207F","P2BA6","P2BAE"],""],P2BAE:["NOx Exceedence - NOx Control Monitoring System","P2BAE is tied to the system that watches NOx control itself, typically the NOx sensors and the logic that compares measured emissions with the permitted level. Regulation (EU) 2017/1151 Annex XVI allows exhaust NOx sensors to replace separate quality and consumption checks, with warning and inducement once the NOx OBD limit is passed; the heavy-duty rules keep counters for monitoring system faults.",["Underlying SCR fault such as poor DEF quality or dosing pressure deviation","NOx sensor damaged, badly mounted or contaminated","Air trapped in the DEF system","Outdated engine software"],["MIL with DEF dosing malfunction message","No-restart countdown in the cluster","Stored together with P2BAF and a root cause code"],3,3,["P2BAF","P2200","P2BAD","P249C","P2BA9"],""],P2BAF:["NOx System Driver Inducement Active","P2BAF does not name a faulty part; it states that the driver inducement of the NOx control system has been activated. Regulation (EU) 2017/1151 Annex XVI requires such an inducement once reagent is lacking, of wrong quality, under-consumed or not dosed, typically counting down to a blocked engine restart; the reason and the distance driven with it go into non-erasable records kept for 30,000 km or 800 days.",["Active SCR fault (DEF quality, dosing, level) that started the inducement","DEF tank run empty","Control module software fault, e.g. BCM on Jeep Compass (FCA 08-103-19)","Root cause fixed but the clearing monitor has not yet run"],["Countdown message until no restart","MIL and DEF system warning on","Speed or power limited, engine may not restart"],2,3,["P2BAE","P241D","P2BA9","P208B","P2BA7"],""],P2BB0:["Alternative Fuel Consumption Too Low","On engines that burn compressed natural gas, LPG or another fuel besides petrol or diesel, the controller can estimate how much gas it has injected and compare that with how fast the tank actually empties, judged by tank pressure or level. P2BB0 means the tank drains noticeably more slowly than the injection quantity implies.",["Alternative fuel tank pressure or temperature sensor reading wrong","Gas injectors or filter restricted, less gas delivered than commanded","Pressure regulator supplying too little pressure","Fuel mode or control software not matching actual operation"],["MIL on, sometimes together with lean mixture codes","Gas range or gauge reading implausible","Engine switches to petrol more often than usual"],4,1,["P2BB1","P2BB2","P01A8","P019E","P01AA"],"צריכת דלק חלופי — ערך נמוך מדי"],P2BB1:["Alternative Fuel Consumption Too High","P2BB1 is set when the alternative fuel store, typically a CNG cylinder, loses more gas than the injected quantity can account for. The main suspicion is a leak between tank and injectors, which is why this check doubles as a safety monitor.",["Gas leak at fittings, lines, regulator or tank valve","Gas injector leaking or sticking open","Tank pressure or temperature sensor exaggerating the pressure drop"],["Gas range much shorter than usual","Gas smell around the vehicle","MIL on, gas mode may be locked out"],4,1,["P2BB0","P2BB2","P01A9","P019E","P01AA"],"צריכת דלק חלופי — ערך גבוה מדי"],P2BB2:["Alternative Fuel Tank Empty","P2BB2 reports that the tank for the second fuel, mostly CNG or LPG, has been drawn down to its usable minimum. It is a status message rather than a component fault: a bi-fuel vehicle simply goes back to petrol.",["Gas tank actually used up to its reserve","Tank pressure or level sensor reading too low","Tank shutoff valve closed or not opening"],["Engine runs on petrol only, gas mode cannot be selected","Gas gauge shows empty or low-level warning"],1,0,["P2BB0","P2BB1","P019E","P01AF","P224C"],""],P2BB3:["Fuel Pump Secondary Circuit Performance","Where a separate driver module powers the fuel pump, the ECM sends a duty-cycle command and the module reports what it actually applies. P2BB3 means these two values disagree beyond a tolerance, so the pump is not running at the requested speed although no open or short has been found.",["Fuel pump driver or tank zone module not delivering the commanded output","High resistance in the pump supply or ground connection","Worn or binding fuel pump drawing abnormal current","Disturbed data link between ECM and pump module"],["MIL on","Hesitation or power loss under load","Long cranking or stalling"],2,3,["P0231","P0232","P023F","P0233","P064A","P0087"],"משני משאבת דלק — ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2BB4:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 4 Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","This code covers jumps in the signal of the fourth coolant temperature sensor that coolant cannot physically make. GM explains the method in the 2019 edition of its engine tables for the L3B and related engines (19OBDG03D): from each reading and the sensor's time constant the software predicts an upper and a lower bound for the next sample, and a step beyond either counts as erratic;",["Loose or corroded terminal at the sensor 4 connector","Engine harness chafed, wire making intermittent contact","Internal intermittent break in the sensor element"],["MIL on after two drives","Jumping temperature value in live data","Cooling fans or thermal management reacting erratically"],2,1,["P2AFC","P2AFD","P2AFE","P2AFF","P2BB5","P01E7"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 4 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2BB5:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 5 Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2BB5 is the erratic-signal code for coolant sensor 5. Unlike the hard circuit faults P2B2D and P2B2E, the reading here stays within the valid range but changes faster than the sensor's thermal inertia allows, which betrays a contact that briefly opens or shorts.",["Chafed engine harness with intermittent contact in the sensor 5 wires","Loose, spread or corroded connector terminal","Sensor element breaking intermittently"],["MIL on after the second trip","Sensor 5 value spikes in live data","Often stored together with other harness-related codes"],2,1,["P2B2B","P2B2C","P2B2D","P2B2E","P2BB4","P2BBA"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 5 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2BB6:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 6 Circuit","P2BB6 is the general circuit code for a sixth coolant temperature sensor, intended for control units that only know that the circuit is faulty and do not distinguish a grounded from an open or shorted-high line. Six or more coolant sensors appear on engines with split cooling, rotary coolant valves or separate branches for head, block, radiator and heater;",["Sensor 6 connector unplugged, damaged or corroded","Open or shorted wire between sensor 6 and the ECM","Failed NTC element in sensor 6"],["MIL on","Sensor 6 shows a fixed substitute or implausible value","Fans may run continuously as a precaution"],2,1,["P2BB7","P2BB8","P2BB9","P2BBA","P2B2B","P2AFC"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 6 — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2BB7:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 6 Circuit Range/Performance","With P2BB7 the sixth coolant sensor delivers an electrically valid value that nevertheless makes no sense. Plausibility tests of this kind compare the sensor with the other engine temperatures after a long cold soak, expect a clear rise once the engine warms up, and flag a value that never moves. CARB requires such rationality monitoring for coolant temperature inputs on which emission functions depend.",["Sensor 6 element drifted out of its characteristic curve","No coolant flow at sensor 6 due to failed pump, valve or air pocket","Contact resistance at connector or terminals"],["MIL on, usually only after a cold start and warm-up","Sensor 6 value lags or stays flat compared with the other coolant sensors"],2,1,["P2BB6","P2BB8","P2BB9","P2BBA","P2B2C","P2AFD"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 6 — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2BB8:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 6 Circuit Low","Coolant sensors are NTC thermistors, so a low signal from sensor 6 means a very small resistance that the ECM would have to read as extreme heat; in practice a signal wire touching ground or a shorted element.",["Sensor 6 signal wire shorted to ground, e.g. chafed harness","Internally shorted sensor element","Moisture or coolant in the connector bridging the pins"],["MIL on after two trips","Sensor 6 shows an implausibly high temperature","Radiator fans running at high speed"],2,1,["P2BB9","P2BB6","P2BB7","P2B2D","P2AFE","P01E5"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 6 — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2BB9:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 6 Circuit High","A high signal from coolant sensor 6 corresponds to a resistance so large that only an interrupted circuit, a disconnected plug or a wire shorted to a voltage source explains it; read as temperature it would be colder than −60 °C. GM's tables check for this once the engine has run more than 10 s or intake air is warmer than −20 °C.",["Sensor 6 connector unplugged or not latched","Broken signal or ground wire, or signal shorted to voltage","Open sensor element"],["MIL on after the second trip","Sensor 6 shows about −40 °C or lower","Fans may run continuously"],2,1,["P2BB8","P2BB6","P2BB7","P2B2E","P2AFF","P01E6"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 6 — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2BBA:["Engine Coolant Temperature Sensor 6 Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","P2BBA catches short dropouts or spikes in the sixth coolant sensor signal that never last long enough to count as a steady low or high fault. GM includes it in its 2019 L3B/common ECM tables (19OBDG03D) and in the 2025 edition (25OBDG03B): based on the last reading and the sensor time constant, the software allows only a limited change per sample, and if the signal leaps past that window for 5 s within 6 s the code…",["Chafed engine harness with intermittent contact","Loose or corroded terminal at sensor 6 or the ECM","Sensor element with intermittent internal break"],["MIL on after two trips, may go out again","Sensor 6 value jumps in live data","Other harness-related codes stored at the same time"],2,1,["P2BB6","P2BB8","P2BB9","P2BB5","P2BB4","P01E7"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור מנוע‏ 6 — אות לא יציב במעגל"],P2BBB:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit","P2BBB is the general fault of the position feedback from bypass valve A, the electrically driven valve that lets boosted air flow back from the compressor outlet to its inlet when the throttle closes or boost has to be trimmed. It is not the wastegate on the exhaust side. The engine module reads the sensor as a share of its 5 V reference; this code covers an open line or a signal it cannot sort into low or high.",["Loose, corroded or unplugged connector at the bypass valve position sensor","Chafed or broken signal, reference or ground wire in the harness near the compressor","Internal fault of the position sensor in the valve actuator","Faulty sensor input or 5 V reference inside the engine control module"],["Check engine light","Reduced boost and noticeably less power","Whoosh or flutter noise when lifting off the throttle"],2,3,["P2BBC","P2BBD","P2BBE","P23AA","P0033","U0657","P2C2A"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2BBC:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit Low","P2BBC sets when the position signal of the bypass valve A sensor sits too low – usually an open signal wire, a short to ground or a lost 5 V supply to the sensor. GM uses the code on the 2019 Corvette ZR1 with the supercharged LT5, whose electronic compressor recirculation valve (eCRV) reports its position as a share of the reference voltage: a raw value under 10 % in 10 of 14 samples taken every 100 ms counts as a…",["Signal wire shorted to ground or chafed against the engine","Open 5 V reference wire or reference shorted by another sensor on the same supply","Pushed-out or corroded terminal in the valve connector","Defective position sensor in the valve actuator"],["Check engine light on in the first trip","Limited boost and weaker acceleration","Possibly further 5 V reference codes if the supply is shorted"],2,3,["P2BBB","P2BBD","P2BBE","P23AA","P2C2B"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2BBD:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve A Position Sensor Circuit High","P2BBD is the high-side counterpart: the position signal from bypass valve A rises toward the full reference voltage. That points to a short to the 5 V supply or to battery voltage, a broken sensor ground – the signal then floats upward – or a defective sensor.",["Open sensor ground wire or corroded ground terminal","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or to battery voltage","Defective position sensor in the valve actuator","Moisture in the valve connector creating a leakage path"],["Check engine light on immediately","Reduced power because boost is limited","Unusual noise when lifting off the throttle"],2,3,["P2BBB","P2BBC","P2BBE","P23AA","P2C2C"],"חיישן מצב שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2BBE:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve A Position Exceeded Learning Limit","P2BBE is not a wiring fault but a failed end-stop learn. GM's 2019 tables for the LT5 Corvette ZR1 describe how the electronic recirculation valve is taught after each engine shutdown: the module first drives it to the closed stop and stores the sensor value, then repeats this for the open stop.",["Oil or carbon deposits keeping the valve from reaching its stops","Bent flap or shaft, or worn actuator gear","Position sensor shifted or drifted after a repair or with age","Non-matching replacement valve with a different travel range"],["Check engine light after the engine has been switched off and restarted","Boost limited or erratic on lift-off"],3,3,["P2BBB","P2BBC","P2BBD","P23AA","P2261","P2C2D"],""],P2BBF:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve A Supply Voltage Low","P2BBF concerns the power side of bypass valve A rather than its position feedback. Electric recirculation valves are moved by a small DC motor fed through an H-bridge in the engine module, and the bridge chip itself flags when its supply drops too far.",["High resistance in the engine module feed, fuse or ground connection","Weak battery or charging fault causing voltage dips","Corroded pins at the engine module or valve connector","Internal fault of the H-bridge driver in the engine module"],["Check engine light on immediately","Valve no longer moves, boost limited or surging on lift-off","Often accompanied by other low-voltage codes"],2,3,["P2BC0","P0033","P0034","P0035","P2C2E"],"אספקת שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ A — מתח נמוך"],P2BC0:["Turbocharger/Supercharger Bypass Valve A Driver Current/Temperature Too High","P2BC0 sets when the output stage that drives bypass valve A reports too much current or overheating. GM applies it to the electric recirculation valve of the LT5-powered 2019 Corvette ZR1: when the H-bridge raises its flag in 80 out of 100 checks spaced 12.5 ms apart, with relay voltage of 11 V or more and no cranking, a Type A fault with immediate MIL results.",["Sticking or jammed valve making the motor draw high current","Shorted winding in the valve actuator motor","Motor leads shorted to each other or to ground in the harness","Overheated or damaged H-bridge driver in the engine module"],["Check engine light on immediately","Reduced boost and less power","Compressor surge noise when lifting off"],2,3,["P2BBF","P00D7","P23AA","P2261","P2C2F"],"שסתום מעקף מגדש‏ A — זרם או חום גבוהים מדי בדרייבר"],P2BC1:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump A Stuck/Stalled","P2BC1 means the electric pump that circulates coolant through the charge air cooler loop is powered, but its rotor will not turn or stops under load; the pump electronics see high current at little or no speed and report this to the engine module.",["Rotor stuck after a long standstill (Audi bulletin 2080825)","Debris, deposits or a worn bearing blocking the impeller","Engine module software needing an update (FCA bulletins for Giulia/Stelvio)","Ice in the loop due to insufficient antifreeze"],["Check engine light, often with a reduced-power message","Hot charge air and less power under load","No running noise from the pump during an actuator test"],2,3,["P2B83","P2B84","P026E","P023A","P2BC2","P2BC3","P2CB3"],""],P2BC2:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump A Supply Voltage Circuit","P2BC2 points to the power feed of charge air cooler pump A: the pump or its controller sees a supply that is missing or outside its working window. Typical causes are a blown fuse, a relay with burnt contacts, a broken or corroded feed or ground wire, or a water-damaged plug; a weak battery can contribute. No manufacturer documents P2BC2 publicly.",["Blown fuse or faulty relay in the pump feed","Broken or corroded supply or ground wire","Water ingress or corrosion in the pump connector","Weak battery or charging fault"],["Check engine light or engine warning message","Pump does not run, charge air temperature rises","Reduced power in hot conditions or under load"],2,3,["P2BC1","P2BC3","P023A","P2B84","P2CB4","U02A9"],"משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ A — תקלה במעגל מתח האספקה"],P2BC3:["Charge Air Cooler Coolant Pump A Control Module Overtemperature","The control electronics of an electric coolant pump sit inside the pump body and are cooled by the liquid flowing through it. P2BC3 means the electronics of charge air cooler pump A report a temperature above their limit.",["Low coolant level or air trapped in the low-temperature loop","Partly blocked impeller or worn bearing raising motor current","Fault in the pump's integrated electronics","Missing heat shield or pump placed close to hot engine parts"],["Check engine light or engine warning message","Pump runs slower or switches off, especially in hot weather","Hot charge air and reduced power"],2,3,["P2BC1","P2BC2","P2B83","P026E","P2CB5"],"מודול בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור מצנן אוויר (אינטרקולר)‏ A — חום יתר"],P2BC4:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor B Circuit","P2BC4 is the catch-all electrical code for positive contactor B of the charging system, the second charging switch on the plus side next to contactor A (P0D07). Which charging path B serves is up to the maker: Mercedes-Benz files its B codes under the DC charge connection unit of its plug-in hybrids, EQB and eSprinter, Mazda under the on-board charger branch of its two large plug-in SUVs, and Audi calls it charging…",["Coil of positive contactor B open or shorted","Wiring or connector fault in the contactor B branch","Fault or software issue in the controlling module"],["DC fast charging or on-board charger charging (depending on design) refused","Charging fault message in the cluster or app","Driving usually still possible"],4,0,["P2BC5","P2BC6","P2BC7","P2BCB","P0D07"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2BC5:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor B Stuck Closed","P2BC5 reports that positive charging contactor B still conducts after the open command, normally because its contacts have fused. Mercedes-Benz stores it, often with P2BCC, in the DC charge connection unit (N116/5, on the eSprinter N24/6) of GLE, E- and S-Class plug-in hybrids, the EQB and the eSprinter; after a DC session the vehicle refuses to start.",["Contacts of positive contactor B welded, e.g. after current peaks at the end of charging","Software of the charging module judges the contactor state wrongly (Mercedes update)","Ripple, overcurrent or overvoltage from the charging station","Coil driver does not switch off"],["Vehicle will not start after DC charging (Mercedes)","High-voltage or hybrid system warning in the cluster","Further charging blocked"],4,2,["P2BC4","P2BC6","P2BCC","P0E89","P0D08"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2BC6:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor B Stuck Open","P2BC6 means positive charging contactor B does not close when commanded, so the plus side of that charging branch stays dead and the session aborts or never starts. The only maker documenting it publicly is Mazda: on the 2024–2026 CX-90 and 2025–2026 CX-70 plug-in hybrids it reads OBC contactor (+) stuck off, listed with the welded cases P2BC5 and P2BCC.",["Contactor B damaged inside and no longer closing (Mazda junction box)","Coil supply or drive line interrupted","Charging control software misjudging the closing check"],["Charging session stops or does not start","Hybrid system malfunction message (Mazda)","Driving usually unaffected"],4,0,["P2BC4","P2BC5","P2BC7","P2BCD","P0D09"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2BC7:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor B Control Circuit/Open","P2BC7 concerns the coil drive line of positive charging contactor B, not its main contacts: the module compares its command with the voltage and current it measures on that line and sets the code when the line is broken or the driver that does not follow. No manufacturer documents P2BC7 publicly.",["Control wire or connector to contactor B interrupted","Coil of positive contactor B open","Driver stage in the control module defective"],["Charging via the contactor B path not possible","Charging fault indication"],4,0,["P2BC4","P2BC8","P2BC9","P2BCA","P2BCE","P0D0A"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2BC8:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor B Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2BC8 flags a control circuit of positive charging contactor B that is connected but behaves implausibly: the coil draws a current that does not fit the command, the line voltage lies in an unexpected band, or pulling in takes too long. No manufacturer documents P2BC8 publicly. CARB demands rationality checks in addition to circuit checks for the charging components of plug-in vehicles.",["Contact resistance at connectors of the control line","Coil resistance of contactor B outside specification","Driver stage in the module degraded"],["Charging works only now and then","Charging aborts with a fault message"],4,0,["P2BC7","P2BC9","P2BCA","P2BCF","P0D0B"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2BC9:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor B Control Circuit Low","P2BC9 is the low-signal fault on the coil feed of plus-side charging contactor B: the module measures less voltage on that wire than its command calls for, most often because the wire touches ground or the output stage is being dragged down. With a high-side feed the coil is then starved and the contactor never pulls in, or the output stage trips its own protection. No manufacturer documents P2BC9 publicly.",["Control wire of contactor B shorted to ground","Moisture or corrosion in a connector","Coil of contactor B internally shorted"],["Charging session does not start","Charging fault message"],4,0,["P2BC7","P2BC8","P2BCA","P2BD0","P0D0C"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2BCA:["Battery Charging System Positive Contactor B Control Circuit High","P2BCA means the wire energising the coil of positive charging contactor B shows too much voltage, caused by contact with battery voltage or an output stage stuck in the on state; the contactor could then pull in uncommanded. Audi documents the code as charging contactor 2, short to positive, in the hybrid battery management module (address 008C) of the 2024 Q8 and SQ8 e-tron, including Sportback.",["Over-sensitive diagnostic software (Audi Q8 e-tron)","Control wire of contactor B shorted to supply voltage","Driver stage does not switch off"],["Drive system cannot be activated after charging (Audi)","Drive system and electrical system fault warnings","Charging blocked"],4,2,["P2BC7","P2BC9","P2BD1","P0ADC","P0AE0","P0D0D"],"מגען חיובי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2BCB:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor B Circuit","P2BCB is the general electrical code for negative contactor B of the charging system, which closes the return path of the second charging branch to the traction battery. No manufacturer documents P2BCB publicly. Where B serves DC fast charging, each pole usually has its own contactor so the inlet is isolated from the pack whenever no charger is connected;",["Coil of negative contactor B open or shorted","Wiring or connector fault on the return-side contactor","Fault in the module that drives contactor B"],["Charging in the affected mode refused","Charging fault message","Driving usually still possible"],4,0,["P2BC4","P2BCC","P2BCD","P2BCE","P0D0E"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2BCC:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor B Stuck Closed","P2BCC says negative charging contactor B is still closed although the module ordered it open – in practice fused contacts on the return side. Mercedes-Benz lists it in the DC charge connection unit next to P2BC5 and P0E8929 (DC input current too high); the plug-in hybrid, EQB or eSprinter then cannot be started after DC charging.",["Contacts of negative contactor B welded at the end of charging","Charging module software (Mercedes update)","Current ripple or overvoltage from the DC station"],["Vehicle will not start after DC charging (Mercedes)","High-voltage system warning","Charging blocked"],4,2,["P2BCB","P2BCD","P2BC5","P0E89","P0D0F"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — תקוע במצב סגור"],P2BCD:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor B Stuck Open","P2BCD is set when negative charging contactor B fails to close, so the charging branch lacks its return path and no current can flow even with the plus side connected. No manufacturer documents P2BCD publicly; Mazda lists the welded minus case P2BCC and the non-closing plus case P2BC6 for the CX-90 PHEV, but not this one.",["Negative contactor B burnt or mechanically not closing","Coil supply too weak or interrupted","Charging control software misjudging the check"],["Charging stops or never starts","Charging fault message"],4,0,["P2BCB","P2BCC","P2BCE","P2BC6","P0D10"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — תקוע במצב פתוח"],P2BCE:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor B Control Circuit/Open","P2BCE watches the coil drive of negative charging contactor B for an open line or a driver whose real state differs from its command. No manufacturer documents P2BCE publicly. The closest published test is GM's P0D11 for minus contactor A in the Volt and the ELR: an output above 4 V with the driver off, a voltage close to supply, or a coil current under 57 mA with the driver on all count as faults, and the status of…",["Control wire or terminal of negative contactor B open","Coil of negative contactor B open","Driver stage in the module defective"],["Charging via the contactor B path not possible","Charging fault indication"],4,0,["P2BCB","P2BCF","P2BD0","P2BD1","P2BC7","P0D11"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2BCF:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor B Control Circuit Range/Performance","P2BCF points to a control circuit on negative charging contactor B that is neither open nor shorted yet still implausible: coil current, line voltage or switching time fall outside the window that belongs to the commanded state. No manufacturer documents P2BCF publicly, and no published GM table has such a check for a charging contactor coil.",["Corrosion or contact resistance in the control connector","Coil resistance of negative contactor B shifted","Poor ground of the controlling module"],["Charging drops out or will not begin","Charging fault message from time to time"],4,0,["P2BCE","P2BD0","P2BD1","P2BC8","P0D12"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל הבקרה"],P2BD0:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor B Control Circuit Low","With P2BD0 the coil drive line of minus-side charging contactor B is too low – usually insulation damage letting the wire touch the body, or an output stage stuck low. Starved of current, the coil leaves the return path of that charging branch open. No manufacturer documents P2BD0 publicly.",["Control wire of negative contactor B shorted to ground","Moisture in a connector of the control line","Coil of negative contactor B internally shorted"],["Charging session will not start","Charging fault message"],4,0,["P2BCE","P2BCF","P2BD1","P2BC9","P0D13"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2BD1:["Battery Charging System Negative Contactor B Control Circuit High","P2BD1 flags excess voltage on the coil feed of minus-side charging contactor B, for instance from contact with a 12 V wire or an output stage that will not turn off. The risk is a coil that stays energised and keeps the return pole connected while the module believes it is open, so the module normally blocks charging. No manufacturer documents P2BD1 publicly.",["Control wire of negative contactor B shorted to supply voltage","Driver stage stuck on","Over-sensitive diagnostic software"],["Charging blocked","High-voltage or charging fault warning"],4,0,["P2BCE","P2BCF","P2BD0","P2BCA","P0D14"],"מגען שלילי מערכת טעינת סוללה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2BD2:["Exhaust Aftertreatment System A Leak","P2BD2 reports that the first aftertreatment line, or the only one, is not gas-tight, so exhaust escapes between engine and tailpipe or false air enters. A leak upstream of the catalysts lets untreated NOx and soot out and also confuses sensors: Foton Cummins patented a check that compares the measured aftertreatment pressure with a model value from exhaust back pressure and flags a leak beyond a limit, noting that…",["Loose V-band clamp or failed gasket between aftertreatment modules","Cracked exhaust pipe, flex joint or catalyst housing","Leak at a sensor, DEF injector or pressure tap mounting","Pressure sensor hose cracked, making the system look leaky"],["MIL on","Exhaust smell, soot marks or ticking at a joint","Follow-up SCR or particulate filter codes"],2,1,["P2BD3","P2453","P20EE"],"דליפת מערכת טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ A"],P2BD3:["Exhaust Aftertreatment System B Leak","P2BD3 is the twin of P2BD2 for a second aftertreatment line, found on engines with two parallel exhaust paths, each with its own catalysts and filter. Which physical line is B is up to the maker; in practice it is usually the path of the second cylinder bank.",["Loose clamp or leaking gasket in line B","Crack in pipe, flex joint or housing on side B","Leaking sensor or injector mounting on line B","Faulty pressure sensor or hose shared by both lines"],["MIL on","Exhaust noise or smell on one side","Uneven readings between the two lines"],2,1,["P2BD2","P2453","P20EE"],"דליפת מערכת טיפול בגזי הפליטה פליטה‏ B"],P2BD4:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C Control Circuit/Open","Hybrid and electric drives cool the inverter, DC/DC converter and motor with one or more electric pumps; J2012 labels them A, B and C. P2BD4 means the controlling module has found an open circuit or an unclassified fault on the control line of pump C. No manufacturer documents P2BD4, or a third pump of this kind, publicly.",["Unplugged, loose or corroded connector at pump C","Broken control or signal wire between module and pump","Failed electronics inside the pump","Faulty output or input stage in the controlling module"],["Hybrid or drive system warning, often with the check engine light","Reduced drive power when the electronics heat up","Pump C silent during an actuator test"],2,3,["P2BD5","P2BD6","P2BD7","P2D0A","P2D0D","U0648","P0A05","P0B38"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2BD5:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C Control Circuit Low","P2BD5 flags the command line of the third electric coolant pump in the inverter and motor electronics loop as sitting at too low a level. With a low-side or PWM driver this usually means the wire or the pump input is shorted to ground, so the pump either runs unchecked or not at all. No manufacturer documents P2BD5 publicly.",["Pump C control wire chafed through and touching ground","Water or corrosion in the pump connector bridging the signal pin to ground","Shorted input stage inside pump C","Faulty output driver in the controlling module"],["Warning for the hybrid or drive system, often with the check engine light","Pump C runs constantly or stays silent regardless of command","Reduced drive power once the electronics warm up"],2,3,["P2BD4","P2BD6","P2BD7","P2D0D","P0A06","P0B39"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2BD6:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C Control Circuit High","P2BD6 is stored when the control circuit of motor electronics coolant pump C reads higher than the commanded state allows. A short to battery voltage, or a driver stage that reports overcurrent, are the usual triggers; the pump may then keep running or ignore commands. No manufacturer documents P2BD6 publicly.",["Control wire of pump C shorted to a supply wire in the harness","Pump C drawing excessive current because of an internal electrical fault","Bent or corroded pins in the pump C connector touching each other","Failed output stage in the controlling module"],["Hybrid system or check engine warning","Pump C keeps running after the vehicle is switched off, or does not respond at all","Power limitation during long climbs or fast driving"],2,3,["P2BD4","P2BD5","P2BD7","P2D0E","P0A07","P0B3A"],"משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2BD7:["Motor Electronics Coolant Pump C Control Performance","P2BD7 means pump C in the motor electronics cooling loop is electrically reachable but does not deliver what the controller asks for: wrong speed, a fault report from the pump itself or too little cooling effect. No manufacturer documents P2BD7 publicly. Ford's 2019 hybrids judge pump A this way under P0C73, set once the pump has reported a confirmed internal fault for more than 1.25 s.",["Air trapped in the electronics loop after a repair or coolant loss","Low coolant level in the electronics loop reservoir","Worn, sticking or debris-blocked pump C","Outdated software in the hybrid controller that misjudges the pump"],["Check engine or hybrid warning light","Cooling fan running at high speed more often than usual","Reduced electric drive or charging power when the loop gets warm"],2,3,["P2BD4","P2BD5","P2BD6","P2D0A","P2D0B","P2D0C","P0C73","P0C74"],"בקרת משאבת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2BD8:["Motor Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit","Some hybrid and electric drives measure the coolant in the inverter and motor electronics loop at more than one point; J2012 names these sensors A, B and C, and which spot each letter marks is left to the manufacturer. P2BD8 is the general circuit code for sensor B: the signal cannot be used, but none of the specific low, high or plausibility verdicts applies. No manufacturer documents P2BD8 publicly.",["Loose, unplugged or corroded connector at sensor B","Damaged signal or reference wire between sensor B and the module","Failed thermistor in sensor B","Faulty input circuit in the controlling module"],["Hybrid or drive system warning, often with the check engine light","Electronics coolant pump and fan running more than usual","Possible reduction of electric drive power"],2,3,["P2BD9","P2BDA","P2BDB","P2BDC","P0A00"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2BD9:["Motor Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance","P2BD9 means coolant temperature sensor B in the motor electronics loop delivers a voltage inside its electrical window, yet the temperature it reports does not fit the rest of the vehicle. The circuit itself is intact; a drifting thermistor, a sensor sitting in an air pocket or a value that stays frozen are typical. No manufacturer documents P2BD9 publicly.",["Sensor B thermistor drifted out of its characteristic","Air pocket or low coolant leaving sensor B partly dry","Added resistance from corroded terminals shifting the reading","Wrong value from a comparison sensor such as engine coolant or intake air temperature"],["Check engine light, usually without a noticeable driving issue at first","Cooling fan or electronics pump running at unexpected times","Occasional power limitation on hot days"],2,3,["P2BD8","P2BDA","P2BDB","P2BDD","P0A01"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2BDA:["Motor Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit Low","P2BDA is set when the sensor B signal in the electronics coolant loop falls below its valid window. These sensors are normally NTC thermistors, so a low voltage translates into an impossibly hot reading; a signal wire touching ground or a shorted sensor is the classic cause. No manufacturer documents P2BDA publicly.",["Signal wire of sensor B shorted to ground","Internally shorted sensor B","Moisture in the sensor connector creating a leakage path to ground","Faulty input stage in the evaluating module"],["Check engine light and hybrid system warning","Scan tool shows an implausibly high electronics coolant temperature","Power reduction even with a cold vehicle"],2,3,["P2BD8","P2BD9","P2BDB","P2BDE","P0A02"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2BDB:["Motor Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor B Circuit High","P2BDB tells that the signal of coolant temperature sensor B sits above its valid voltage range. With a thermistor fed from a 5 V reference through a pull-up resistor, a broken wire, an unplugged connector or a sensor gone open lets the voltage rise to almost the reference, which the module would read as extreme cold. No manufacturer documents P2BDB publicly.",["Sensor B connector unplugged, not latched or with a backed-out pin","Broken signal or ground wire of sensor B","Sensor B thermistor gone open","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source"],["Check engine light or hybrid warning","Scan tool shows an implausibly low electronics coolant temperature","Electronics coolant pump running at a fixed high speed"],2,3,["P2BD8","P2BD9","P2BDA","P2BDF","P0A03"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2BDC:["Motor Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit","P2BDC reports a general fault in the circuit of coolant temperature sensor C, a third measuring point that some drives use in the loop cooling the inverter, converter and motor. The code stands for a signal the module cannot use without assigning it to the low, high or plausibility codes P2BDE, P2BDF and P2BDD. No manufacturer documents P2BDC, or a third sensor of this kind, publicly.",["Poor contact at the sensor C connector","Chafed or broken wiring between sensor C and the module","Defective sensor C","Fault on a 5 V reference or sensor ground shared with other sensors"],["Warning lamp for the hybrid or drive system","Fan and electronics pump running at high output as a precaution","Possibly reduced electric power"],2,3,["P2BDD","P2BDE","P2BDF","P2BD8","P0CF0","P0CF1"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2BDD:["Motor Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P2BDD is the plausibility check of coolant temperature sensor C: electrically the signal looks fine, but the reported value cannot be right when set against other temperatures. No manufacturer documents P2BDD publicly. Two published approaches show how such a check can run while driving instead of after a cold soak.",["Sensor C reading drifted away from the true coolant temperature","Air or weak flow at the sensor C location, so it sees a local hot or cold spot","Corroded terminals adding resistance in the sensor C circuit","Faulty comparison temperature from another sensor in the system"],["Check engine light without an obvious drivability problem","Cooling fan behaviour that does not match the conditions","Power or charging limitation under heavy load"],2,3,["P2BDC","P2BDE","P2BDF","P2BD9","P0CEF"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2BDE:["Motor Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit Low","P2BDE reports that the voltage from coolant temperature sensor C has dropped below its lower limit. Low describes the voltage: for the usual NTC sensor it corresponds to a reading far hotter than the coolant can be, and the cause is mostly a grounded signal wire, a crushed pigtail or a sensor that has shorted internally. No manufacturer documents P2BDE publicly.",["Sensor C signal wire shorted to ground or to the sensor ground","Sensor C shorted internally","Crushed or melted sensor pigtail near hot components","Faulty analog input in the evaluating module"],["Hybrid warning or check engine light","Very high electronics coolant temperature shown in live data on a cold vehicle","Fan running at full speed shortly after start"],2,3,["P2BDC","P2BDD","P2BDF","P2BDA","P0CF0"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2BDF:["Motor Electronics Coolant Temperature Sensor C Circuit High","P2BDF is stored when the signal of coolant temperature sensor C climbs to nearly the full reference voltage. For the module this looks like coolant colder than any climate allows; in practice a pin that has backed out of the connector, a corroded or broken signal wire, or a short to a voltage source is behind it. No manufacturer documents P2BDF publicly.",["Backed-out or loose pin in the sensor C connector","Corroded or broken signal wire of sensor C","Open circuit inside sensor C","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V reference or another supply"],["Check engine or hybrid system warning","Live data shows the lowest possible temperature for sensor C","Pump and fan running in a fixed protective mode"],2,3,["P2BDC","P2BDD","P2BDE","P2BDB","P0CF1"],"חיישן טמפרטורת נוזל קירור אלקטרוניקת מנוע חשמלי‏ C — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2BE0:["Hybrid/EV Battery Coolant Level Sensor Circuit/Open","P2BE0 concerns the wiring of the level sensor in the coolant reservoir of the high-voltage battery loop: its signal is missing or the line is broken. Stellantis documents the code as P2BE0-00 on the 2021-22 Chrysler Pacifica Hybrid, where the cluster asks for hybrid system service;",["Battery coolant level actually low (leak or after service), bulletin asks to check first","Level sensor defective, e.g. internal solder joints (GM Volt)","Open signal wire or loose connector at the reservoir","Internal break in the sensor jumper harness"],["Service hybrid system message on the cluster","MIL on","Plug-in charging disabled on some models"],2,3,["P2BE1","P2BE2","P2BE3","P2B28","P0C4A"],"חיישן מפלס נוזל קירור סוללת מתח גבוה — מעגל תקול או פתוח"],P2BE1:["Hybrid/EV Battery Coolant Level Sensor Range/Performance","P2BE1 reports a battery coolant level signal that lies inside the electrical limits yet makes no sense, such as a value between the defined full and low states or one that flickers while the vehicle stands still. No manufacturer documents this code publicly.",["Level sensor with internal fault, e.g. cracked solder joints","Intermittent contact in connector or jumper harness","Coolant level near the switching point or air in the loop","Evaluation software in the battery or hybrid controller"],["Hybrid system warning, often intermittent","MIL on","Coolant level looks correct at the reservoir"],2,3,["P2BE0","P2BE2","P2BE3","P2B28"],"חיישן מפלס נוזל קירור סוללת מתח גבוה — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2BE2:["Hybrid/EV Battery Coolant Level Sensor Circuit Low","P2BE2 is stored when the voltage from the battery coolant level sensor falls below the lowest value the sensor can legitimately produce. That points to the signal touching ground or a sensor whose output collapses, not to a low coolant level, which normally reads inside the valid range. No manufacturer documents P2BE2 publicly.",["Signal wire chafed through and shorted to ground","Level sensor output stuck low","Sensor supply missing (connector, corrosion)"],["Hybrid system warning","MIL on","Charging possibly disabled"],2,3,["P2BE3","P2BE0","P2BE1"],"חיישן מפלס נוזל קירור סוללת מתח גבוה — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2BE3:["Hybrid/EV Battery Coolant Level Sensor Circuit High","P2BE3 means the level sensor signal of the battery coolant loop is above its valid range, typically from a short to the sensor supply or to 12 V, or from a lost sensor ground. No manufacturer documents P2BE3 publicly. GM's code P1FFD on the Chevrolet Volt shows the same test with numbers: above 4.0 V, 40 of 50 samples at 100 ms, Type A.",["Open sensor ground or open signal with pull-up (read as high)","Signal wire shorted to sensor supply or 12 V","Level sensor output stuck high"],["Hybrid system warning","MIL on","Charging possibly disabled"],2,3,["P2BE2","P2BE0","P2BE1"],"חיישן מפלס נוזל קירור סוללת מתח גבוה — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2BE4:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Current Sensor C Circuit","P2BE4 is the general circuit code for a third current measurement in the high-voltage battery, used where sensor A (P0ABF to P0AC3) and sensor B (P0B0E to P0B13) are already taken. What C measures depends on the design: a further Hall or shunt channel, or a sensor in a second current path; Continental patents a battery busbar with three independent current devices whose values are compared.",["Current sensor C defective","Wiring or connector fault between sensor and battery controller","Input stage or software of the battery controller"],["Hybrid or EV system warning","Reduced electric power or range","MIL on"],4,3,["P2BE5","P2BE6","P2BE7","U064C","P0ABF","P0B0E"],"חיישן זרם מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2BE5:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Current Sensor C Circuit Range/Performance","P2BE5 flags current sensor C as implausible although its signal is electrically valid, for instance an offset with no current flowing or a value at odds with the other readings. Stellantis lists it, worded as current sensor C circuit performance, in bulletins 08-047-20 and 08-130-21 for the 2017-18 Chrysler Pacifica plug-in hybrid with the 3.6 litre engine: the MIL comes on, and the remedy is new software for the…",["Battery controller software (Stellantis Pacifica PHEV, reflash per bulletin)","Sensor offset or gain drift","High resistance at connector or sensor ground"],["MIL on","Hybrid system warning","Inaccurate state of charge or reduced electric range"],4,3,["P2BE4","P2BE6","P2BE7","P0AC0","P0B0F","P0B13"],"חיישן זרם מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2BE6:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Current Sensor C Low","P2BE6 is set when the output of current sensor C drops below the lowest value it can deliver in normal service. Unlike its A and B siblings, the official title omits the word circuit, but the meaning is the same out-of-range low check. No manufacturer documents P2BE6 publicly.",["Signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor supply voltage missing","Current sensor C defective"],["MIL and hybrid or EV warning on","Reduced power, possibly no ready mode"],4,3,["P2BE7","P2BE4","P2BE5","P0AC1","P0B10"],"חיישן זרם מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — ערך נמוך"],P2BE7:["Hybrid/EV Battery Pack Current Sensor C High","With P2BE7 the signal of current sensor C sits above its usable range, which after conversion would be an impossibly large current. As with P2BE6, the official wording drops the word circuit. No manufacturer documents P2BE7 publicly. GM's coarse-channel check for sensor A (P0AC2) shows typical numbers: above 303 A (ADC count over 4013) during 1.6 s out of every 2 s, Type A, MIL on the first trip.",["Open sensor ground","Signal wire shorted to the 5 V supply or 12 V","Current sensor C defective"],["MIL and hybrid or EV warning on","Battery power limited"],4,3,["P2BE6","P2BE4","P2BE5","P0AC2","P0B11"],"חיישן זרם מארז סוללת מתח גבוה‏ C — ערך גבוה"],P2BE8:["Hybrid/EV Battery Precharge Contactor Control Circuit B Open","P2BE8 reports an open in control circuit B of the battery precharge function, i.e. the coil drive of a second precharge contactor. Note the wording: the letter follows circuit, while the A codes P0AE4 to P0AE7 name contactor A.",["Open control wire or loose connector at contactor B","Coil of precharge contactor B open internally","Driver stage in the battery controller defective"],["Vehicle does not become ready to drive","MIL and hybrid or EV warning on","Charging not possible"],4,3,["P2BE9","P2BEA","P2BEB","P0AE4","P0C78"],"מעגל בקרת מגען טעינה מוקדמת סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — נתק"],P2BE9:["Hybrid/EV Battery Precharge Contactor Control Circuit B Range/Performance","P2BE9 says control circuit B of the precharge function is connected but behaves implausibly: the coil current, the feedback voltage or the effect of switching does not match the command. No manufacturer documents P2BE9 publicly.",["Coil resistance out of tolerance or sluggish armature","High-voltage load or resistor fault keeping the bus from rising during precharge","Corrosion or high resistance in the control circuit","Battery controller software or driver stage"],["Vehicle sometimes does not become ready","MIL and hybrid or EV warning on"],4,3,["P2BE8","P2BEA","P2BEB","P0AE5","P0C78"],"מעגל בקרת מגען טעינה מוקדמת סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2BEA:["Hybrid/EV Battery Precharge Contactor Control Circuit B Low","P2BEA is stored when control circuit B of the precharge function carries less voltage than its state requires, mostly because the coil feed touches ground or the output is pulled down. With a high-side driver the coil then gets no current and the second precharge path stays open. No manufacturer documents P2BEA publicly.",["Coil feed chafed and shorted to ground","Coil of precharge contactor B shorted internally","Driver stage of the battery controller pulled low"],["Vehicle does not become ready to drive","MIL and hybrid or EV warning on"],4,3,["P2BEB","P2BE8","P2BE9","P0AE6"],"מעגל בקרת מגען טעינה מוקדמת סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — ערך נמוך"],P2BEB:["Hybrid/EV Battery Precharge Contactor Control Circuit B High","P2BEB reports too much voltage on control circuit B of the precharge function while it should be off, usually a short to 12 V or a driver that does not switch off. The risk is a second precharge path closing on its own; the resistor can overheat if it stays in circuit. No manufacturer documents P2BEB publicly.",["Coil feed shorted to 12 V","Driver stage stuck on in the battery controller","Damaged insulation between adjacent wires in the harness"],["MIL and hybrid or EV warning on","High-voltage system blocked as a precaution"],4,3,["P2BEA","P2BE8","P2BE9","P0AE7","P0AE2"],"מעגל בקרת מגען טעינה מוקדמת סוללת מתח גבוה‏ B — ערך גבוה"],P2BEC:["Fuel Control System A Too Lean Bank 1","Engines that combine port and direct injection keep separate fuel trim adaptations for each injection mode. Ford, which uses this code on its PFDI engines such as the 2.7 L EcoBoost and 5.0 L V8 of the F-150, assigns system A to the direct-injection mode.",["PCM software fault on affected Ford models, fixed by reprogramming","High-pressure pump or its volume regulator delivering too little rail pressure","Direct injectors on bank 1 restricted or coked","Bank 1 upstream oxygen sensor reading skewed"],["Check engine light on","Hesitation under acceleration, when the engine relies on direct injection","Often no noticeable change in drivability"],2,1,["P2BED","P2BEE","P2BF0","P0171","P0087"],"מערכת בקרת דלק‏ A — תערובת ענייה מדי (בנק 1)"],P2BED:["Fuel Control System A Too Rich Bank 1","P2BED is the rich counterpart of P2BEC: bank 1 has to remove fuel, but only while the engine is fed by direct injection, which Ford calls fuel system A on its port-plus-direct engines. The Ford monitor runs continuously in closed loop and reacts when long-term trim has pulled more than 25 percent and short-term trim keeps pulling beyond 1 percent for 2 seconds;",["Direct injector leaking or dribbling on bank 1","PCM software fault, Ford reprogramming bulletins","Rail pressure above target because of a faulty volume regulator or pressure sensor"],["Check engine light on","Long cranking or rough running right after a hot start","Fuel smell from the exhaust, higher consumption","Misfire codes on the same bank in some cases"],3,1,["P2BEC","P2BEF","P2BF1","P0172","P0088"],"מערכת בקרת דלק‏ A — תערובת עשירה מדי (בנק 1)"],P2BEE:["Fuel Control System A Too Lean Bank 2","Here the lean correction concerns bank 2, the cylinder row without cylinder 1, and again only the direct-injection operating mode (fuel system A in Ford terms). Ford applies the same monitor as on bank 1: closed loop, warm engine, purge off, long-term trim above plus 25 percent combined with short-term trim above plus 1 percent for 2 seconds. Comparing banks narrows the search.",["Direct injectors on bank 2 restricted","PCM software requiring a Ford update","Bank 2 upstream oxygen sensor reading skewed","Low rail pressure, usually with P2BEC on bank 1 too"],["Check engine light on","Slight hesitation under load","Often no other complaint"],2,1,["P2BEC","P2BEF","P2BF2","P0174"],"מערכת בקרת דלק‏ A — תערובת ענייה מדי (בנק 2)"],P2BEF:["Fuel Control System A Too Rich Bank 2","P2BEF says that the engine module has had to take away a lot of fuel on bank 2 while direct injection alone was supplying the cylinders. Ford sets it on port-plus-direct engines when long-term trim on that bank drops past minus 25 percent while short-term trim keeps subtracting more than 1 percent; two seconds in closed loop are enough.",["Known PCM software issue on 2019-2020 F-150 2.7 L","Direct injector on bank 2 sticking open or seeping","Rail pressure sensor reading too low, pressure actually too high"],["Check engine light on","Rough running after a hot restart","Increased fuel use"],2,1,["P2BED","P2BEE","P2BF3","P0175"],"מערכת בקרת דלק‏ A — תערובת עשירה מדי (בנק 2)"],P2BF0:["Fuel Control System B Too Lean Bank 1","Fuel system B is, in Ford's monitor documents, the port fuel injection mode of engines that also have direct injectors. P2BF0 therefore means bank 1 runs lean only when the port injectors do the work. The decision rule matches the DI codes: long-term trim past plus 25 percent, short-term trim past plus 1 percent, held for 2 seconds during closed-loop operation with purge off. The suspects differ, though.",["Low-pressure fuel pump or supply pressure too weak for the port injectors","Port injector on bank 1 clogged","Air leak at a port injector O-ring or intake manifold gasket","PCM software, Ford reprogramming bulletins"],["Check engine light on","Uneven idle or surging at light load","Hesitation when pulling away"],2,1,["P2BF1","P2BF2","P2BEC","P0171","P2187"],"מערכת בקרת דלק‏ B — תערובת ענייה מדי (בנק 1)"],P2BF1:["Fuel Control System B Too Rich Bank 1","With P2BF1 the PCM has seen bank 1 too rich while fuel came through the port injectors, Ford's fuel system B. Ford flags it when the long-term value sits beyond minus 25 percent and the short-term value still takes away above 1 percent, for a 2 second window in closed loop. Since this monitor only runs with the canister purge valve closed, vapour from the evaporative system cannot explain the result;",["Port injector on bank 1 leaking or dribbling","PCM software, Ford reprogramming bulletins","Low-side fuel pressure above specification","Mass air flow sensor under-reporting"],["Check engine light on","Fuel smell, black exhaust deposits","Rough idle when warm"],2,1,["P2BF0","P2BF3","P2BED","P0172","P2188"],"מערכת בקרת דלק‏ B — תערובת עשירה מדי (בנק 1)"],P2BF2:["Fuel Control System B Too Lean Bank 2","P2BF2 combines two restrictions: the lean correction is on bank 2, and it only occurs in the port injection mode that Ford designates fuel system B. The Ford threshold is identical to the other trim codes of this family, more than 25 percent added by long-term trim plus over 1 percent by short-term trim for 2 seconds. Using both letters and both banks together helps the diagnosis.",["PCM software, Ford reprogramming bulletins","Port injector on bank 2 clogged","Air leak at the bank 2 intake gasket or injector O-ring","Weak low-pressure supply, usually with P2BF0 as well"],["Check engine light on","Uneven idle","Mild hesitation at part throttle"],2,1,["P2BF0","P2BF3","P2BEE","P0174","P2189"],"מערכת בקרת דלק‏ B — תערובת ענייה מדי (בנק 2)"],P2BF3:["Fuel Control System B Too Rich Bank 2","The last of the eight mode-specific trim codes: bank 2 is too rich while the port injectors (Ford fuel system B) are active. Ford triggers it when long-term trim has gone below minus 25 percent and short-term trim continues to subtract over 1 percent for 2 seconds, with the engine warm and purge disabled.",["Port injector on bank 2 not sealing","PCM software, Ford reprogramming bulletins","Bank 2 upstream oxygen sensor biased lean"],["Check engine light on","Fuel smell at idle","Higher consumption"],2,1,["P2BF1","P2BF2","P2BEF","P0175","P2190"],"מערכת בקרת דלק‏ B — תערובת עשירה מדי (בנק 2)"],P2BF4:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Position Circuit","Many electrically driven exhaust flaps report their actual angle back to the engine computer, either as an analog voltage or as a PWM duty cycle from a smart actuator. P2BF4 is the umbrella fault for that feedback path on valve A: the signal is missing, unusable or cannot be classed as clearly too low or too high. No manufacturer documents P2BF4 itself in public material.",["Actuator connector loose, wet or corroded by road salt","Feedback or ground wire broken or heat-damaged near the exhaust","Position sensor inside the flap actuator failed"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust flap no longer switched, sound stays in one mode"],2,1,["P2BF5","P2BF6","P2BF7","P2BFC","P26C5","P2D11"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ A — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2BF5:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Position Circuit Range/Performance","Here the position signal of exhaust valve A is electrically fine, yet its value does not fit: the reported angle disagrees with the command, the end stops are not where the learned values say, or the signal jumps. Ford lists P2BF5 in its active exhaust bulletins for the 2018-2023 Mustang (21-2011 for the 2020 GT500, later 23-2132 and 25-2146), together with the matching valve B code P2BFD and the drive codes.",["Muffler or tailpipe not fully seated in its clamps, straining the actuator","Actuator bracket bent or not welded flush to the tailpipe","Pinched actuator harness giving an unstable signal","Flap shaft binding from corrosion or soot"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust mode or drive mode not available message","Exhaust tone does not change between modes"],2,1,["P2BF4","P2BF6","P2BF7","P2BFD","P26FE","P2D11"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ A — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2BF6:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Position Circuit Low","P2BF6 means the position feedback of exhaust valve A sits below its valid range, as with a signal shorted to ground or a lost sensor supply. Mazda is the best documented user: its 2.5 litre Skyactiv-G with cylinder deactivation carries an exhaust shutter valve that Mazda patents describe as closing partly in two-cylinder mode to damp exhaust pulsation noise.",["PCM software misjudging the sensor (Mazda bulletin 01-004/20)","Position signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor supply open or connector not latched","Position sensor in the shutter valve failed"],["Master warning or check engine light on","Reduced engine power"],2,3,["P2BF4","P2BF5","P2BF7","P2BFE","P26C6"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ A — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2BF7:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve A Position Circuit High","P2BF7 is set when the position feedback of exhaust valve A rises above its plausible maximum. Electrically that points to the signal line touching the sensor reference or battery voltage, or to a lost sensor ground, which lets the input float up to its pull-up level.",["Open sensor ground letting the signal float high","Signal wire shorted to reference or battery voltage","Position sensor in the valve assembly failed"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust flap held in its default position","Exhaust sound no longer changes as expected"],2,3,["P2BF4","P2BF5","P2BF6","P2BFF","P26C7"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ A — אות גבוה במעגל"],P2BF8:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve B Control Circuit/Open","Valve B is the second exhaust flap; Ford's gasoline OBD summaries 2020-2024 put it on bank 2, while valve A (P26C5) serves bank 1. P2BF8 reports that the drive circuit for flap B is open or unusable. On Ford a smart driver checks the output continuously and flags it within about 5 seconds; the 2024 summary files the open circuit as subtype 13.",["Broken or unplugged harness to the bank 2 flap actuator","Open circuit inside the flap actuator","Actuator not aligned after replacement or outdated PCM software (subtype 78)"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust mode not available message","One tailpipe flap no longer moves"],2,1,["P2BF9","P2BFA","P2BFB","P26C5","P2D12"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ B — מעגל הבקרה תקול או פתוח"],P2BF9:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve B Control Circuit Low","With P2BF9 the control line of exhaust flap B is pulled toward ground. A bare spot rubbing on the body or exhaust, or a shorted actuator, is the classic cause, which is why the code tends to appear after exhaust work or with a sagging harness. Ford's 2024 OBD summary treats it as subtype 11 of the bank 2 flap check, run continuously over 5 seconds by the smart driver.",["Control wire chafed through and touching ground","Harness pinched at the actuator bracket","Internal short in the flap B actuator"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust mode cannot be changed","Bank 2 flap stuck, uneven sound left and right"],2,1,["P2BF8","P2BFA","P2BFB","P26C6"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל הבקרה"],P2BFA:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve B Control Circuit High","P2BFA reports too high a level on the control line of exhaust flap B. Either the wire has contact with a powered circuit, or the actuator electronics feed voltage back, so the driver cannot pull the line down when it should. Ford's 2024 OBD summary lists it as subtype 12 of the bank 2 check, monitored continuously with a 5 second window.",["Control wire shorted to a powered circuit","Flap B actuator electronics feeding voltage back","Damaged tailpipe actuator harness, Ford service part 14A411"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust mode warning in the cluster","Bank 2 flap in wrong position for the selected mode"],2,1,["P2BF8","P2BF9","P2BFB","P26C7"],"שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל הבקרה"],P2BFB:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve B Control Performance","P2BFB is the functional fault of flap B: wiring checks pass, but the flap does not reach or hold the commanded angle. Ford runs two tests on its bank 2 flap. The smart driver reports a stuck valve over its PWM feedback line, and a rationality check compares measured with commanded position, its duration depending on ambient conditions.",["Flap B binding from corrosion, soot or ice","Exhaust or actuator bracket not seated correctly","Actuator not aligned or outdated PCM calibration","Worn or overheated flap actuator"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust mode not available message","No audible difference between exhaust modes"],2,1,["P2BF8","P2BF9","P2BFA","P2BFD","P26FE","P2D12"],"בקרת שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ B — ביצועים לא תקינים"],P2BFC:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve B Position Circuit","P2BFC covers a general fault in the feedback path that tells the engine computer where exhaust flap B is. It applies only to systems with a second position-monitored flap, such as one per tailpipe, so on single-flap vehicles it cannot occur. No manufacturer documents P2BFC in public material. Ford defines valve B as its bank 2 flap and reads its state through the smart driver's PWM line;",["Flap B connector loose, wet or corroded","Feedback wire to flap B broken or heat-damaged","Position sensing in actuator B failed"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust mode selection limited or unavailable"],2,1,["P2BFD","P2BFE","P2BFF","P2BF4","P2BF8","P2D12"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ B — תקלה במעגל החשמלי"],P2BFD:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve B Position Circuit Range/Performance","P2BFD flags a position signal from exhaust flap B that is electrically valid but implausible, for instance an angle that lags the command, end points that drifted from the learned values, or a reading that wanders while the flap should rest. Ford is the public user.",["Muffler and tailpipe not fully engaged in the clamps","Actuator bracket not welded flush to the tailpipe","Pinched harness at actuator B"],["Check engine light on","Drive mode or exhaust mode not available message","Exhaust tone stays the same in every mode"],2,1,["P2BFC","P2BFE","P2BFF","P2BF5","P2BFB","P2D12"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ B — טווח/ביצועים לא תקינים במעגל"],P2BFE:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve B Position Circuit Low","The position feedback of exhaust flap B reads below its lowest valid value. For an analog sensor that means a signal at or near 0 V, typically a short to ground or a missing 5 V supply; for a PWM feedback it means a duty cycle stuck near zero. No manufacturer publishes P2BFE.",["Flap B signal wire shorted to ground","Sensor reference supply open or shorted","Position sensor in actuator B failed"],["Check engine light on","Flap B no longer adjusted, exhaust sound unchanged"],2,1,["P2BFC","P2BFD","P2BFF","P2BF6","P2BF9"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ B — אות נמוך במעגל"],P2BFF:["Exhaust Flow Control Valve B Position Circuit High","P2BFF is the upper limit fault for the position feedback of exhaust flap B. An analog signal pinned near supply voltage, or a PWM feedback stuck near 100 percent, usually comes from a lost sensor ground, a signal wire touching voltage, or water bridging the connector pins. No manufacturer documents P2BFF publicly.",["Open ground at the flap B position sensor","Water or salt bridging the actuator B connector pins","Signal wire shorted to a voltage source"],["Check engine light on","Exhaust mode warning, flap B held in default position"],2,1,["P2BFC","P2BFD","P2BFE","P2BF7","P2BFA"],"מצב שסתום בקרת זרימת פליטה‏ B — אות גבוה במעגל"]};export{e as default};
